the game. Because...well, shit. That's absolutely horrifying. The idea that the Blossoming effectively gives you the power to make your dreams a reality at the cost of hollowing you out definitly paints the &quot;Inner Light&quot; in a waaaay more sinister manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T03:42:09-07:00","id":1075061,"title":"","content":"Well.... I think it's still canon somewhat, but it's more uncomfortable than really a a torture from what I understood, and Wisps are fairly easy to recover fortunately, so Princesses will rarely fall into this situation. But, yeah, this does raises some creepy implications, right?<br /> <br /> Also, if you want access to the current version of the doc, I'll need your mails so I can share it with you. You can send them in private obviously.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T07:27:19-07:00","id":1075115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1075024#post1075024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Woot! Glad the name was a success. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, reading past the part that describes Whisps and I have to ask: is the part about a Princess having her emotions and feeling muted to the point of feeling empty if they are low or out of Whisps still a thing in the later or most updated version of the game. Because...well, shit. That's absolutely horrifying. The idea that the Blossoming effectively gives you the power to make your dreams a reality at the cost of hollowing you out definitly paints the &amp;quot;Inner Light&amp;quot; in a waaaay more sinister manner.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the link is to the latest version.<br /> <br /> But, yeah, when you use your dreams and emotions as fuel, running out has... consequences.<br /> <br /> What about Alhambra *stealing* wisps?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T07:52:09-07:00","id":1075128,"title":"","content":"I always thought the hyper-empathy symptoms of Sensitivity was the worst part of being a Noble. Hyper-empathy is pretty exhausting and draining and P:tH does not skimp on acknowledging that fact, especially when you literally do have a duty to try to solve as many of those problems as you can.<br /> <br /> Giving a literal child mental illness symptoms and telling them that they can't just try to cope with them the normal way is a pretty sinister thing to do for the Queens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 04-08-2017, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T07:58:47-07:00","id":1075129,"title":"","content":"Actually, just thought of another potential name for the supplement<br /> <br /> Hunter: the Vigil - The Candle and The Light<br /> <br /> It highlights both the similarities and differences between these two metaphorical lights in the darkness","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T13:11:36-07:00","id":1075222,"title":"","content":"I wonder about the Starlight Guardians' attitude regarding Princesses, assuming both groups have ever met.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T15:09:44-07:00","id":1075262,"title":"","content":"Starlight who now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T15:45:50-07:00","id":1075277,"title":"","content":"Hey there, everybody. I came as quickly as I could after the call for help went out. My most prominent skills are writing and editing (especially editing), and I'd love to provide assistance.<br /> <br /> I have read both of the P:tH corebooks and the existing supplement, but my knowledge of H:tV is very limited. I have gleaned the personalities of the compacts and conspiracies from various sources online (this thread included), but I am clueless about their systems.<br /> <br /> I'm going to be busy for the next three or four days, but once I'm available I'll blaze a path of edits through any material sent my way. As for mechanical stuff, I may need some things explained to me (like what Dread Powers are and how they tend to be designed), but I'll throw out any decent ideas I come up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13233-rougemephilesclone","name":"RougeMephilesClone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T15:54:12-07:00","id":1075285,"title":"","content":"Alright^^ Give me your mail in private if you want access to the supplement. As for the informations for Hunter, I'm sure there are plenty of people here who could explain to you better than me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T18:42:56-07:00","id":1075318,"title":"","content":"Do you still want me to edit too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"htt