.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T02:28:54-07:00","id":1075412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1075262#post1075262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Starlight who now?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://vindae.tumblr.com/post/123476195745/magicalgirls\" target=\"_blank\">https://vindae.tumblr.com/post/12347...5/magicalgirls</a><br /> <br /> Basically, fae contracted hunters with a magical girl theme specialized in (but no exclusive to) rogue changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 04-09-2017, 06:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T02:44:30-07:00","id":1075416,"title":"","content":"Ah, I see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you still want me to edit too? </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T04:10:54-07:00","id":1075429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1075318#post1075318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you still want me to edit too?</div> </div> </div> </div>When it comes to editing, more cooks can make the soup better, if not just finished sooner. Jump on in. If you feel hesitant to make a permanent change, switch your editing permissions to the &quot;Suggestion&quot; mode by clicking on the &quot;Editing&quot; button in the top right corner. I'll be using it for more complicated revisions, so additional input will be necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13233-rougemephilesclone","name":"RougeMephilesClone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T08:36:08-07:00","id":1075489,"title":"","content":"Thanks. And always great to be a collaborator with someone more experienced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T16:24:47-07:00","id":1075622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1072394#post1072394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, how I longed for this day to come.<br /> <br /> In my own honest and possibly uninformed opinion, there is kinda a general sentiment that magical girls, and in turn Princesses, cannot be portrayed in a negative light; after all, their powers are always used for the greater good and how could they possibly be antagonistic when they talk about love and friendship, having the confidence to fight against the darkness, never giving in to despair, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not the case in Princess at all. The three Twilight Queens (my favourite of the antaognist splats) each represent a moral failing that all Princesses are prone too.<br /> <br /> Tears represents putting the people closest to you first, even to the extent of hurting others.<br /> Storms represents letting your anger at the monsters you fight turn into self-destructive hate.<br /> Mirrors represents clinging to your ideals even in denial of reality.<br /> <br /> However those are flaws that the Radiant Princesses are aware of and make efforts to avoid; they're just not always successful.<br /> <br /> <br /> A lot of the recent series that play with the idea of magical girls not nessacarally being good hinge on a shocking twist that changes the fundamental nature of Magical Girls, Madoka being an obvious example. For Princess I'm trying to avoid that, and I'm trying to avoid anything that makes it inevitable that a Princess will go bad. In Princess magical girls are good by nature, but they have a <i>very</i> hard job to do and some of them crack under the pressure, but others of them manage to live up to their potential.<br /> <br /> In other words. You don't need to change the fundamental nature of magical girls Madoka Style to do a darker take on the magical girl story. You have young people fighting monsters, portray that realistically and it's automatically dark.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1075024#post1075024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, reading past the part that describes Whisps and I have to ask: is the part about a Princess having her emotions and feeling muted to the point of feeling empty if they are low or out of Whisps still a thing in the later or most updated version of the game. Because...well, shit. That's absolutely horrifying. The idea that the Blossoming effectively gives you the power to make your dreams a reality at the cost of hollowing you out definitly paints the &quot;Inner Light&quot; in a waaaay more sinister manner.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's still there in the latest Dream version. There's a specific condition for it.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say it has sinister implications though. Thematically it represents &quot;exhaustion&quot;. If a Princess is careful about managing her risks she need never experience this drawback. However if life throws problem after problem at her until she's out of Wisps then the Condition gives a little mechanical weight to how hard it is to balance school, social life, and fighting evil by moonlight. But you can't really blame the Light for the fact the world doesn't give Princesses the time they need to refuel; and it's not like the Light cursed Princesses with this drawback, any more than I would &quot;curse&quot; you to have to regularly by gas if I gave you a car.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1075128#post1075128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Giving a literal child mental illness symptoms and telling them that they can't just try to cope with them the normal way is a pretty sinister thing to do for the Queens.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Queens don't create Princesses or otherwise choose who becomes a Princess.<br /> <br /> They do however teach Princesses how to cope with their symptoms. I always saw them taking a genre savvy approach. I want to tell this 14 year old Champion to stay home, train and let older Princesses handle it until she's 18 but I <u><i>know</i></u> nothing I say will stop her hunting monsters, so I better make sure she knows how to fight and has emotional coping skills.<br /> <br /> (Not least because somebody is going to want to play Sailor Moon and she's 14).<br /> <br /> P.S. the Darkness has a weakness to jade; that rule exists specifically for the benefit of Hunters.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T16:45:02-07:00","id":1075627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A lot of the recent series that play with the idea of magical girls not nessacarally being good hinge on a shocking twist that changes the fundamental nature of Magical Girls, Madoka being an obvious example. For Princess I'm trying to avoid that, and I'm trying to avoid anything that makes it inevitable that a Princess will go bad. In Princess magical girls are good by nature, but they have a <i>very</i> hard job to do and some of them crack under the pressure, but others of them manage to live up to their potential. </div> </div> </div>And <i>that</i>, right here, is why I fell in love with your game. I never could get in shows like Madoka precisely because of the pessimistic tone and how it treated Magical Girls. You avoided that and put straight Magical Girls in a horrible setting to live in, without holding back punch, yet still made sure they had decent chances to win.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> P.S. the Darkness has a weakness to jade; that rule exists specifically for the benefit of Hunters. </div> </div> </div>Don't worry, I remember that^^<br /> <br /> On a note, since you're here, might as well ask you: do you want access to the current draft of this supplement, or would you rather wait until it's complete?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T17:09:21-07:00","id":1075637,"title":"","content":"Just finished reading through the current HtV: Darkness &amp; Light document. Love what I've read so far, my only two recommendations is for the material to not short change some of the other supernatural creatures (in particular a witch isn't just a &quot;human with weird powers&quot; when those powers include giving you the clap forever or literally stealing your soul and putting it into a cursed medallion) and emphasize a more scientific explanation for some of the Nobles (I think the word Empath could be floated around more and that a Princess' armor should be difficult to distinguish between a psychic projection or a magical ability.)<br /> <br /> In regards to my thoughts on the sinister nature of the Light, I don't think the gasoline reference is quite appt for what happens when a Princess loses Whisps below a certain point (especially since the threshold rises the more powerful they become) simply because acquiring a car normally comes with an acceptance of the fact that a cost must be given in order to use said car, while the Blossoming (from what I've read so far) isn't an active choice. It's something that occurse naturally when certain circumstances are met, and the Princess doesn't really have a grasp of the consiquences of it until after the fact. I could be wrong and will amend this post once I get more information (a lot of stuff to read, but loving every minute of it) but so far the way Nobles are described tend to pain the picture of a supernatural force/phenomena of positivity that transforms a human into a psychic conduit from which it wages a subtle and active war against another opposit force/phenomena. And that's fantastic, because it allows a discussion about the nature of a Princess' condition both within and outside of the game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 04-09-2017, 08:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T17:50:49-07:00","id":1075652,"title":"","content":"Oh, don't get me wrong, I know what Mages really are; I read Mage the Awakening. But thing is, I am trying to write the book from the Hunters' perspective from the most part. And based on what I read in H:tV and its various supplements, as far as hunters are concerned, &quot;witches&quot; is just a term used to design at the same time any form of human being (as in not completely supernatural like vampires and werewolves) who have supernatural powers. Usually believed to have gained their powers through a deal with the devil. I know that's not true obviously, but I get the impression that's what Hunters believe when reading the books. I gotta admit, though, I REALLY like the suggestions for more sicentific explanations and mentionning Empathy/psychic projection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T18:38:02-07:00","id":1075663,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a> Us readers of Princess know the Radiant Queens don't choose them, but do the Hunters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T21:03:01-07:00","id":1075708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1075024#post1075024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, reading past the part that describes Whisps and I have to ask: is the part about a Princess having her emotions and feeling muted to the point of feeling empty if they are low or out of Whisps still a thing in the later or most updated version of the game. Because...well, shit. That's absolutely horrifying. The idea that the Blossoming effectively gives you the power to make your dreams a reality at the cost of hollowing you out definitly paints the &quot;Inner Light&quot; in a waaaay more sinister manner.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's only in the Dream version, at least as a mechanic. In Vocation running out of Wisps just locks away transformation and the powers that depend on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T00:03:19-07:00","id":1075759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1075627#post1075627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And <i>that</i>, right here, is why I fell in love with your game. I never could get in shows like Madoka precisely because of the pessimistic tone and how it treated Magical Girls. You avoided that and put straight Magical Girls in a horrible setting to live in, without holding back punch, yet still made sure they had decent chances to win.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1075627#post1075627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a note, since you're here, might as well ask you: do you want access to the current draft of this supplement, or would you rather wait until it's complete?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were you I'd make the early draft public, there's no such thing as too much constructive feedback.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1075637#post1075637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Blossoming (from what I've read so far) isn't an active choice. It's something that occurse naturally when certain circumstances are met, and the Princess doesn't really have a grasp of the consiquences of it until after the fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much, however the requirements for being a Princess inlcude that the charachter was acting like a Princess already. So while Blossoming increases the risks of draining your Wisps dry it decreases risks like getting eaten by monsters since you're more likely to win the fight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1075663#post1075663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a> Us readers of Princess know the Radiant Queens don't choose them, but do the Hunters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-10-2017, 03:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T03:38:26-07:00","id":1075824,"title":"","content":"@The Kings Raven,<br /> <br /> If it were just the drawbacks to having Whisps as a power source then yes, the Blossoming and condition of being a Noble would be extraordinarily beneficial compared to other forms of supernatural adaptations. However, I think we can both agree that it gets much more dangerous and sinister once you add both Sensitivity AND Belief to the mix. Then it becomes gaining emotional hypersensitivity along with emotional drainage and the threat of going crippling depressed or transforming into a slathering monstrosity should your self-esteem drop low enough. (To be fair, it is more complicated than that. But damn, I didn't expect the Blossoming to be more akin to the First Change rather than an Awakening.)<br /> <br /> Also, I noticed that the text in the PDF that was sent to me mentions the Hopefull's &quot;Purpose on Earth&quot; quite often. Enought that it's starting to sound really similar to how in Beast: the Primordial it's constantly mentioned that the Begotten's &quot;purpose&quot; is to teach humanity hard lessons. That get's me wondering, just like for the Begotten how much of that is cultural traditions and dialogue? The HtV: Darkness &amp; Light does a good job of making that question nebulous since it's an outsider perspective, but how much is confirmable in the PtH core game? (I ask this mainly because what I've read so far indicates that the Hopefull's desire to help others is very much a Need rather than a Want. It's not an overpowering need, but what dubious questions arise when helping others becomes more about preventing one's own pain rather than ending another's. Especially when failure to do so means very real torment for yourself.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T04:22:42-07:00","id":1075832,"title":"","content":"Okay, following King Raven's advice, I am now making the draft open to public for reading. You can find the link in the first post^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T06:17:01-07:00","id":1075854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1075824#post1075824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I think we can both agree that it gets much more dangerous and sinister once you add both Sensitivity AND Belief to the mix.</div> </div> </div> </div> Dangerous sure, but to me sinister is casting a question upon the Light's motivation or ethics. For that to be true would first require that the Light has enough conciousness to possess either motivations or ethics, and secondally it would require that the Light had the ability to design the Princess' powerset and chose to include Sensitivity.<br /> <br /> Neither of those two requirements are confirmed. The Light might just be a natural force with no conciousness whatsoever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1075824#post1075824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That get's me wondering, just like for the Begotten how much of that is cultural traditions and dialogue?</div> </div> </div> </div>For Princesses it's <i>all</i> cultural traditions. If a bunch of Princesses decided to retreat into the mountains and build a utopian secret village they'd have a very easy time of it. They aren't going to start getting painful cravings to go out and do good, nor will they set of an eternal winter, or have the &quot;Light Mother&quot; turn up to scold them. The only reason hidden Princess only utopias aren't a common thing is that the kind of person who would choose a hidden utopia instead of sticking around to make the world better is not likely to Blossom.<br /> <br /> In other words, you Blossom because you've found and followed a Calling. Blossoming does not force a Calling upon you. The distinction is most obvious with Onceborn where the requirements for Blossoming are much stricter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-10-2017, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T07:22:25-07:00","id":1075869,"title":"","content":"Once again, this stuff could also be what the Hunters believe","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T07:41:53-07:00","id":1075878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1075759#post1075759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much, however the requirements for being a Princess inlcude that the charachter was acting like a Princess already. So while Blossoming increases the risks of draining your Wisps dry it decreases risks like getting eaten by monsters since you're more likely to win the fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Come to think of it, that means there is probably a fair number of Hunters who might Blossom. That could be interesting, especially if they Blossom from Compacts or Conspiracies that have...less-than-good relationships with the Nobility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T08:52:03-07:00","id":1075916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1075878#post1075878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. <br /> <br /> Huh. Come to think of it, that means there is probably a fair number of Hunters who might Blossom. That could be interesting, especially if they Blossom from Compacts or Conspiracies that have...less-than-good relationships with the Nobility.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think they blossom younger than many conspiracies recruit. But that could be interesting","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T10:05:01-07:00","id":1075938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1075622#post1075622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of the recent series that play with the idea of magical girls not nessacarally being good hinge on a shocking twist that changes the fundamental nature of Magical Girls, Madoka being an obvious example. For Princess I'm trying to avoid that, and I'm trying to avoid anything that makes it inevitable that a Princess will go bad. In Princess magical girls are good by nature, but they have a <i>very</i> hard job to do and some of them crack under the pressure, but others of them manage to live up to their potential.<br /> <br /> In other words. You don't need to change the fundamental nature of magical girls Madoka Style to do a darker take on the magical girl story. You have young people fighting monsters, portray that realistically and it's automatically dark.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><i>I walk in waving a flag made out of a long cardboard tube and a &quot;Magical Girl Raising Project&quot; poster. Several security guards grab me and dropkick me into the Punishment Hole. As I fall out of sight, I scream &quot;It was alriiiiiiight!&quot;.</i><br /> <br /> I concur that having a large group of magical girls acting under different codes of ethics and desires is a much more interesting character-driven story than a rehash of Madoka's plot. It did its thing, it was fresh the first time, and if the next season ever comes out, it seems posed to do something a bit more grounded in character conflict. According to someone earlier in this thread, some of the side stories have shown a preference for using actively villainous Magical Girls instead of just showing the characters learn about the mechanics of the Contract.<br /> <br /> And regarding Raising Project, I have heard that the first novel (which was adapted into the anime) was the weakest point, and the rest of the series gives more attention the Magical World and criminals who escape from it. There are Demons of varying threat levels, but the primary villains are people. And hey, there's even a Mage faction of normal humans learning how to use magic! I'm keen on seeing more from that franchise.<br /> <br /> <i>Anyways.</i><br /> <br /> I can't do my editing sweep for a couple more days, and as I have mentioned earlier, I will be utilizing the Suggestion feature to present possible edits for anything larger than a grammatical error.<br /> <br /> I have read over the document, however, and it looks good so far. It's clearly focused on getting the world building set up before mechanical details are considered, though I have to question how Cheiron managed to get anything out of researching Princesses. Like\u2026 they run on emotions and beliefs. How did they even find principles to imitate? Are transformations predicated upon holding a certain mood over their durations?<br /> <br /> And for nicknames for the Court of Diamonds, how about &quot;Brains&quot;, &quot;Spies&quot;, or &quot;Voyeurs&quot;? They play up how annoyed a Cell would get with someone consistently one step ahead of them when it comes to occult research.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13233-rougemephilesclone","user":"RougeMephilesClone","date":". 04-10-2017, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13233-rougemephilesclone","name":"RougeMephilesClone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T11:56:07-07:00","id":1076014,"title":"","content":"@The Kings Raven,<br /> <br /> Good point. Sinister in retrospect is definitly not the right words to describe the Light, but I am very pleased that it does possess some level of amorality. Just like with Beast (one of my favorite gamelines) I'm truly glad that it's the player character's active choice to do good, and how. Even if it is supernaturally motivated, it still allows the level of agency that I've found very few other games have that the Chronicles possess in spades. <br /> <br /> This line of thinking is all towards a common purpose though: working out potential Tactics that Hunters may utilize in their conflicts with either the Nobles or the Darkness. And in that vein I have two ideas solidifying right now.<br /> <br /> ~ Knight of Mirror's Tactic: Otherwise known as Empath Preservation Tactics or the &quot;Don Kehote Tactic&quot;, this technique is the improved upon methods that led to the disasterous attempt to rid one of the Hopeful of their self-destructive delusions about a &quot;Purpose on Earth.&quot; While the first time it was used led to the revelation about what a Noble becomes when their delusions progress to psychosis, it has since been modified by [insert name of anti child soldier compact] in order to at least ground the Noble's delusions about saving the world with the very real danger and trauma that fighting the supernaturals bring. This tactic is risky, and difficult because in order for it to succeed the Hunters will need to discover a Noble's true identity, and confront their family or circle of friends with this revelation before confronting the Noble themselves. If successful, then the Noble's Empathic powers will turn against her as their desire to end the suffering of others will conflict with their family and friend's desire for their loved one to not be in danger any more or risk their lives for their sake. While this doesn't necessarily take away a Noble's powers, if successful it will weaken them enought that they won't be able to endanger themselves for a good deal of time. And that just might be what the Hunter needs in order to either capture the Noble themselves, or target and eliminate the supernatural threat that the Noble themselves were going to confront. <br /> <br /> ~ Beacon of Hope Tactic: Often mockingly referred to as the &quot;Bat Signal&quot; this tactic solely involves the Hunters putting out a noticeable coded message to an unidenrified Noble in the area for assistance. This is primarily used when the Hunter Cell realizes they're out matched by the supernatural force they fight against and are either unable to contact the Noble for a more formal request for assistance, the Cell is too prideful or prejudice to ask so instead they rely upon plausibly deniable assistance from an unknown Noble, or (most dastardly) when the Cell wants to set a trap for the Noble themselves. Success results in a Noble of the ST's choosing arriving at either a critical moment of a combat encounter, or for the Hunter's trap. The danger, of course, is even when the call is genuine and sincere, there is no guarentee which Noble shows up, or even if they will take the Hunter's side of the fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T12:15:04-07:00","id":1076029,"title":"","content":"On the subject of tactics, something to get past Defence would be a good one to have, Nobles have high Defence and often apply it to ranged attacks as easily as they do in melee; as is tradition from magical girl shows<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1075916#post1075916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they blossom younger than many conspiracies recruit. But that could be interesting</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no hard limits on age, but reincarnated Princesses have a very low threshold to trigger a Blossoming so they tend to Blossom young.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-10-2017, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T12:16:56-07:00","id":1076031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1076029#post1076029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no hard limits on age, but reincarnated Princesses have a very low threshold to trigger a Blossoming so they tend to Blossom young.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is there a hard limit on lowest age tied to the development of empathy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T12:22:54-07:00","id":1076037,"title":"","content":"Despite all, I think Hunters in general would be more agreeable to work alongside Princesses than with, for example, Heroes, given the choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T13:08:50-07:00","id":1076062,"title":"","content":"Hmm...do you have any suggestions Tactics wise for overcoming their Defense. So far the logic has been around either weakening their powers (via weakining their Belief with Tactics like Mirror Knight) or to just get the jump them (via settings traps from Beacon of Hope.) In the spirit of the gameline I've tried to tie the tactics to originally beneficent purposes (helping Nobles realize that their families and friends don't want them to endanger themselves on their behalf or out right asking for help against a more dangerous foe) but always add the option for those purposes to be subverted towards personal ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T14:12:30-07:00","id":1076101,"title":"","content":"Explosives, fire, suppression fire?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T14:22:36-07:00","id":1076110,"title":"","content":"Don't we already have those though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T14:34:28-07:00","id":1076116,"title":"","content":"EDIT: never mind, read further","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T14:36:05-07:00","id":1076117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have to question how Cheiron managed to get anything out of researching Princesses. Like\u2026 they run on emotions and beliefs. How did they even find principles to imitate? Are transformations predicated upon holding a certain mood over their durations? </div> </div> </div>Well, they somehow figured out how to make implants based on werewolves despite the fact Uratha turned back to human after death and have their powers from being half-spirit. And based on what I read in Tooth and Nails, they somehow found a way to make stuff from Beasts, whose powers come from having a Nightmare as a soul. I figured they'd find a way.<br /> <br /> As for the nicknames for Diamonds, I like these^^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ~ Knight of Mirror's Tactic: Otherwise known as Empath Preservation Tactics or the &quot;Don Kehote Tactic&quot;, this technique is the improved upon methods that led to the disasterous attempt to rid one of the Hopeful of their self-destructive delusions about a &quot;Purpose on Earth.&quot; While the first time it was used led to the revelation about what a Noble becomes when their delusions progress to psychosis, it has since been modified by [insert name of anti child soldier compact] in order to at least ground the Noble's delusions about saving the world with the very real danger and trauma that fighting the supernaturals bring. This tactic is risky, and difficult because in order for it to succeed the Hunters will need to discover a Noble's true identity, and confront their family or circle of friends with this revelation before confronting the Noble themselves. If successful, then the Noble's Empathic powers will turn against her as their desire to end the suffering of others will conflict with their family and friend's desire for their loved one to not be in danger any more or risk their lives for their sake. While this doesn't necessarily take away a Noble's powers, if successful it will weaken them enought that they won't be able to endanger themselves for a good deal of time. And that just might be what the Hunter needs in order to either capture the Noble themselves, or target and eliminate the supernatural threat that the Noble themselves were going to confront.<br /> <br /> ~ Beacon of Hope Tactic: Often mockingly referred to as the &quot;Bat Signal&quot; this tactic solely involves the Hunters putting out a noticeable coded message to an unidenrified Noble in the area for assistance. This is primarily used when the Hunter Cell realizes they're out matched by the supernatural force they fight against and are either unable to contact the Noble for a more formal request for assistance, the Cell is too prideful or prejudice to ask so instead they rely upon plausibly deniable assistance from an unknown Noble, or (most dastardly) when the Cell wants to set a trap for the Noble themselves. Success results in a Noble of the ST's choosing arriving at either a critical moment of a combat encounter, or for the Hunter's trap. The danger, of course, is even when the call is genuine and sincere, there is no guarentee which Noble shows up, or even if they will take the Hunter's side of the fight. </div> </div> </div>Both of these are great. I am adding them^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 04-10-2017, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T15:37:48-07:00","id":1076157,"title":"","content":"*bows* Thank you. I thought those would be cool ways for Hunters to use Tactics to explore some of Princess' themes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for the big guns, those would be effective tactics I would assume since besides their latent magic they perish to bullets and explosions just like any other mortal character. The trouble is finding tactics that a) don't have the potential to leave child corpses behind just in case the Jone of Arc fire-starter turns out to be a 14 year old school girl with a dream. And b) from what I've read more firepower is effective but only once you get the Noble's Whisps (or Willpower in their Hunter Template) sufficiently below a certain point so they'll be unable to use their powers, and that would both cost the Hunters a pretty penny and lack the subtle that most Hunters need to rely on.<br /> <br /> That being said, I think it would be good to reference some Tactics from the other Supplements as methods used in addition to the ones unique to Princesses &amp; the Darkness. For instance, a nice alternative to Mirror Knight would be Going to Groups from Tooth &amp; Nail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 04-10-2017, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T15:50:46-07:00","id":1076163,"title":"","content":"ok, two questions about Princess stuff in general: <br /> <br /> 1) What exactly is the adult to teenager to child ratio for initial blossoming? Everyone's acting like they're largely kids, but I don't see pre-teens having the same rules on stats as adults.<br /> <br /> 2) What's up with the Darkness and the sites of major, prolonged atrocities? I feel like those places, such as sites of genocide should have major tainted stuff going on, but visitors to the Auschwitz memorial (for example) don't seem to be going evil-crazy or that would probably break the masquerade pretty quick, or at least slow down visiting. I can understand why you might want to avoid talking about real-world atrocities, but I always like in-universe stuff<br /> <br /> Also question about the Union. How old is the group, exactly? I got this feeling from reading about them that they kinda grew up with the internet, even if they drew on earlier traditions. If that's true, they might not know about the Twilight Princesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T16:08:10-07:00","id":1076170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *bows* Thank you. I thought those would be cool ways for Hunters to use Tactics to explore some of Princess' themes. </div> </div> </div>You're welcome^^ and I appreciate that you actually used that Dethroned anecdote I put in the story section.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What exactly is the adult to teenager to child ratio for initial blossoming? Everyone's acting like they're largely kids, but I don't see pre-teens having the same rules on stats as adults. </div> </div> </div>Well, the book isn't clear on that part, though it does mention Blossom tend to happen in a period of change, which is often teenage or growing up. In term of rules, child nobles don't really have unique rules aside from adult supervision.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What's up with the Darkness and the sites of major, prolonged atrocities? I feel like those places, such as sites of genocide should have major tainted stuff going on, but visitors to the Auschwitz memorial (for example) don't seem to be going evil-crazy or that would probably break the masquerade pretty quick, or at least slow down visiting. I can understand why you might want to avoid talking about real-world atrocities, but I always like in-universe stuff </div> </div> </div>You only get corrupt by staying in Tainted places for extended periods of time (as in several days) or comitting atrocities inside them; if you stay for short amount of times and avoid doing things that would cause a Breaking Point, you usually are fine. Moreover, becoming Darkened doesn't turn you evil on the spot: it's a gradual transformation causing your morality to slowly decay further while your body is warped by the darkness, and if you manage to get your Integrity two dot higher than it was before you got corrupt, you're cured.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also question about the Union. How old is the group, exactly? I got this feeling from reading about them that they kinda grew up with the internet, even if they drew on earlier traditions. If that's true, they might not know about the Twilight Princesses. </div> </div> </div>... Good point. I am not sure about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T16:28:10-07:00","id":1076176,"title":"","content":"You know what, I actually think the section detailing the Darkness should be greatly increased to the same length as the information presented about the Nobility themselves. The part about it in the document so far can be easily summed up as: &quot;It's really really bad, no exceptions. Destroy it at all costs.&quot; I think a good deal more can be explored by examining it from the Hunter's perspective, especially since honestly Hunters will see more of the Supernatural world than most splats (maybe with the exception of Mage or Beast) albeit in thousands of small fragments. This could allow a much wider examination about exactly what tainted locations are, what and how Darkspawn form, and of course a further examination about the Dethroned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 04-10-2017, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T16:34:37-07:00","id":1076179,"title":"","content":"Obviously, &quot;the Darkness&quot; is a mutagenic virus or fungus. It lingers in some areas, affecting long term residents and warping them as the infection progresses. There is a noticeable effect upon the subjects' brain, reducing empathy and increasing sociopathic tendencies, as well. Perhaps more troubling, it appears to be another &quot;reanimator&quot; infection, capable of resuscitating hosts as mobile infection vectors even after they have expired.<br /> -Dr. William Cole, Null Mysteriis","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-10-2017, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T17:12:14-07:00","id":1076191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You know what, I actually think the section detailing the Darkness should be greatly increased to the same length as the information presented about the Nobility themselves. The part about it in the document so far can be easily summed up as: &quot;It's really really bad, no exceptions. Destroy it at all costs.&quot; I think a good deal more can be explored by examining it from the Hunter's perspective, especially since honestly Hunters will see more of the Supernatural world than most splats (maybe with the exception of Mage or Beast) albeit in thousands of small fragments. This could allow a much wider examination about exactly what tainted locations are, what and how Darkspawn form, and of course a further examination about the Dethroned. </div> </div> </div>You probably are right, but I couldn't find that much to say about the Darkness. Just felt like there was much more to say about Princesses. Of course, if you have ideas of what to add, you are welcome to write it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Obviously, &quot;the Darkness&quot; is a mutagenic virus or fungus. It lingers in some areas, affecting long term residents and warping them as the infection progresses. There is a noticeable effect upon the subjects' brain, reducing empathy and increasing sociopathic tendencies, as well. Perhaps more troubling, it appears to be another &quot;reanimator&quot; infection, capable of resuscitating hosts as mobile infection vectors even after they have expired.<br /> -Dr. William Cole, Null Mysteriis </div> </div> </div>I dig that^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T17:12:33-07:00","id":1076192,"title":"","content":"From the doc (which I am just now reading)<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Overall, Princesses have only recently been identified as a separate kind of creature than witches, and some cells still don\u2019t really recognize them as such; after all, how else would you call a person who appears human in every way, only with occult powers?&quot;<br /> -Might want to mention the 'Familiar'-like aspect of Shikigami as well.</span></span><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Second, while they are biologically human, their magic appears to be an integral part of their being, rather than something acquired through deals with entities or occult practices.&quot;<br /> -Would most Hunters know this? It's not like they'd really be able to tell. After all, some Witches don't need incantations (either Mage not using the Yantras, or a Psychic) or say they never made a deal for their powers.<br /> <br /> Will add more later. In general, I'd be sparse with any Princess terms and references, throwing in the occasional deliberate inaccuracy to keep things vague.<br /> (Of course, if any Splat is likely to talk about themselves, it is Princesses)</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T17:17:43-07:00","id":1076194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1076163#post1076163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok, two questions about Princess stuff in general:<br /> <br /> 1) What exactly is the adult to teenager to child ratio for initial blossoming? Everyone's acting like they're largely kids, but I don't see pre-teens having the same rules on stats as adults.</div> </div> </div> </div>True children (pre-puberty) almost never Blossom. Teenagers are probably the commonest, closely followed by college-age adults. However, age is less important than stress and adversity.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, the Vocation version does have a sidebar about adjusting character creation for teenaged PCs, in the section for transformation rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1076163#post1076163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) What's up with the Darkness and the sites of major, prolonged atrocities? I feel like those places, such as sites of genocide should have major tainted stuff going on, but visitors to the Auschwitz memorial (for example) don't seem to be going evil-crazy or that would probably break the masquerade pretty quick, or at least slow down visiting. I can understand why you might want to avoid talking about real-world atrocities, but I always like in-universe stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11745_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11745\" data-vbnamecard=\"11745\">Darinas</a> said, it takes time for a Tainted area to corrupt people. Also, destroying the structures where atrocities happened, or performing exorcisms and purifying rituals at the sites, usually clears out most of the Taint there. You can assume that the Auschwitz memorial is clean of Taint by now (though what it was like when the death camp was operating doesn't bear thinking about.)<br /> <br /> The really dangerous Tainted areas are ones where the original crimes that seeded them have been successfully concealed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T17:33:59-07:00","id":1076198,"title":"","content":"The other day, a colleague floated a troubling hypothesis regarding the connection between the Darkness infection and these &quot;Princesses&quot; - the later are carriers. She pointed out the figures showing that concentrations of these &quot;Nobles&quot; correlated to more &quot;Darkspawn&quot; incidents, and brought up the reports of some Nobles even undergoing catastrophic mutation. As if their immunity suddenly gave out against a massive infection. There are still too many variables left unknown to be certain, but the thought of these individuals, frequently only mere teenagers, acting as &quot;Typhoid Marys&quot; to the very people they claim to protect is... unnerving.<br /> -Dr. William Cole, Null Mysteriis","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T17:39:41-07:00","id":1076199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Might want to mention the 'Familiar'-like aspect of Shikigami as well.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>I did. It's mentioned in &quot;Fighting a Noble&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Would most Hunters know this? It's not like they'd really be able to tell. After all, some Witches don't need incantations (either Mage not using the Yantras, or a Psychic) or say they never made a deal for their powers.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>The ones who make deeper analysis of magic and how it works, like the Cheiron Group, would have figured out. It's said in the Charm A Magical Girl's Eye's description that a Princess in her transformed state is entirely made of magic, which I figured would be visible on TFV's sensors for that sort of thing. And of course, there's the fact Princesses turn into nightmarish clearly non-human abominations when their Belief is broken. It's subtle, but there are a lot of small details indicating their magic is part of their being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Will add more later. In general, I'd be sparse with any Princess terms and references, throwing in the occasional deliberate inaccuracy to keep things vague.<br /> (Of course, if any Splat is likely to talk about themselves, it is Princesses)</span></span> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. I admit, my initial idea was to have Hunters use a specific term to design them, like how they use &quot;Ghostwalkers&quot; for Sin-Eaters, but I couldn't figure out anything good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T17:45:46-07:00","id":1076202,"title":"","content":"A few cursory opinions on the darkness beyond &quot;aaaa, it's evil, kill it&quot;<br /> <br /> Ashwood Abbey- a lot of Ashwood Abbey might well be darkened, and in some of the worst chapters full-fledged Mnemosynes might be able to fit in. This can leave the Abbey in the unfortunate situation of having to defend creatures of darkness. Of course, the Abbey isn't populated entirely by monsters, and the risk of civil war if a particularly influential member turns to the dark is enough to ensure that these kind of situations are often &quot;dealt with&quot; before they become a nuisance.<br /> <br /> The Long Night- There was a perfect world, and then a shadowy force came, manipulated the people there into sin and cursed the world with darkness. Sound familiar? The Darkness is the curse lain on the earth by the fall of eden, still manifesting to this day. Does this mean the compact should leave it to wreck judgement, or fight it as an aspect of sin? Opinions vary. Of course, an alternate reading is it's not the curse, but the Serpent- that is, Satan. The implications of the adversary manifesting and turning people into monsters are... worrying, to say the least.<br /> <br /> The Cheiron Group- sadly, implants from &quot;creatures of darkness&quot; are not very useful. They're easy to transplant (almost suspiciously so, some of the more paranoid surgeons say) and provide impressive amounts of power, but the people with them tend to go weird. Then murderous. Then their skin falls off and they become knife-monsters. Analysis of the bodies isn't hugely useful- it seems most of the damage is more metaphysical then physical. This goes against everything cheiron believes, and they keep trying in the hope of finding out what is causing the reaction.<br /> <br /> The Union- The union isn't as opposed to the darkness as many people are. Sure, the skeletal things that eat children's minds, they need to go away. But a lot of the so-called &quot;darkened&quot; are just members of the community. Assholes, sure, but not monsters. Likewise tainted places, which are just as often someone's house as underground torture bunkers. While the union has been told by the nobles that these darkened will become monsters, and many do, they're still a bit leery about massacring people or burning down blocks based only on the word of strange magic ladies. While this hasn't been enough to break any alliances yet, in areas with a lot of tainted places it has started causing significant tensions.<br /> <br /> The Lucifuge- sin leads to hell. Sin enough in one place, and hell draws closer. To the Lucifuge, tainted places are, if not portals to hell, places where the inferno is a lot closer to earth then normal. The darkspawn are either demons or a strange form of possession. To this end, the Lucifuge work with princesses to erase these areas- although a few of the more fanatical members wander if finding a way to blow these thin areas open might be a way to finally take the fight to the demons. Doing so would presumably require committing horrific sins in an already tainted place. Something no member of the Lucifuge would ever condone, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T18:00:34-07:00","id":1076208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1076199#post1076199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did. It's mentioned in &quot;Fighting a Noble&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just got to that point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1076199#post1076199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ones who make deeper analysis of magic and how it works, like the Cheiron Group, would have figured out. It's said in the Charm A Magical Girl's Eye's description that a Princess in her transformed state is entirely made of magic, which I figured would be visible on TFV's sensors for that sort of thing. And of course, there's the fact Princesses turn into nightmarish clearly non-human abominations when their Belief is broken. It's subtle, but there are a lot of small details indicating their magic is part of their being.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think TFV has &quot;magic sensors&quot;, but I could have missed something. And, really, what separates a Princesses' &quot;made of magic&quot; from a Changeling? Or a Promethean? Or, heck, a Mage with the right Legacy? Plenty of critters have magic laced through their being. As for Dethroned - is it their magic turning on them, or some creature they keep contained getting out or showing its true form?<br /> <br /> Hunters don't seem properly equipped to determine the exact details. All they have is an outsider's perspective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1076199#post1076199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. I admit, my initial idea was to have Hunters use a specific term to design them, like how they use &quot;Ghostwalkers&quot; for Sin-Eaters, but I couldn't figure out anything good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Twinks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T18:03:51-07:00","id":1076211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1076199#post1076199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed. I admit, my initial idea was to have Hunters use a specific term to design them, like how they use &quot;Ghostwalkers&quot; for Sin-Eaters, but I couldn't figure out anything good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lightbringers? Works both for those who support and oppose them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T18:26:32-07:00","id":1076225,"title":"","content":"Eeeeh, that's a term for the devil so while deliciously loaded I don't think it would be good based on the current themes in the doc. I would just a blanket term like Purifiers. That way we can use different regions of the world's terminology for what's closest. <br /> <br /> Also, haven't reached that point in the Princes doc yet. But what are the catagories of Darkspawn? If any?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T18:36:57-07:00","id":1076230,"title":"","content":"From least to most powerful:<br /> <br /> Darkened- humans who are influenced by the darkness, with soem powers, but have not yet actually become supernatural creatures yet. <br /> <br /> Darkspawn- Darkened twisted into feral monsters. They lack any aspect of their human lives and are very rarely sentient.<br /> <br /> Mnemosynes- Darkened totally corrupted by the darkness who can can still pass for human. They have magic-style powers and are fully sentient.<br /> <br /> Cataphractoi- Copies of people who die filled with despair. They have the physical mutations of the darkspawn and the magic of the mnemosynes, and work to emulate the life of the person they copied in horrifying ways. Can control lesser darkspawn<br /> <br /> Dethroned- Princesses who have fallen to the Darkness. Have massive magic powers and twist reality around them into reflections of their broken psyche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T18:40:22-07:00","id":1076233,"title":"","content":"Ignore. - <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12109\" data-vbnamecard=\"12109\">Urbenmyth</a> summarizes it better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":".  Ninja'd 04-10-2017, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T19:02:23-07:00","id":1076238,"title":"","content":"Cataphractoi can also perform Transformations of their own. These vary wildly, but are always bad news.<br /> <br /> Just want to give a couple reminders about falling to Belief 0 and the Dethroned:<br /> <br /> First of all, while a Princess that hits Belief 0 due to Hunter meddling is likely to be reminded of her former supernatural status and attempt a Transformation, this isn't a certainty. While a Belief 0 Princess almost always invites trouble (apparently, Light and Dark-attuned characters are drawn to them), they can also just be zombie-like versions of themselves, and will default to either doing nothing or making token efforts to uphold her mundane life until her Willpower hits 0. A Dethroned is merely a possibility (though, again, an admittedly likely one with Hunters involved).<br /> <br /> Secondly, not all Dethroned are giant monsters. In fact, the example Dethroned from the corebooks has a detailed enough &quot;script&quot; to pass as a normal old woman. Sure, they lash out like monsters without a care in the world and act like fake people when they have enough of a &quot;script&quot; to act, but much like their lesser brethren, they are a varied bunch.<br /> <br /> Finally, Dethroned are mostly passive. They spend the majority of their time just sitting in their Fortress of Regrets in the Dark World and moping. Therefore, a Hunter would only be likely to encounter a Dethroned in two situations. The first is at ground zero before a new Dethroned realizes that the Dark World hurts a bit less and retreats there. This is usually the Hunter's fault, but it certainly hasn't done much good for the reputation of the Hopeful. The second occasion is if a Dethroned exits the Dark World through a hijacked Tainted Place, usually at the urging of some desperate Creatures of Darkness. The Vocation Version goes into the different kinds of interactions a Dethroned's abilities can have on reality, but the Dream Version assumes that when a Dethroned strays close to reality, they tend to pop in for a short visit. This\u2026 can be disastrous. If Hunters don't make it to the attack in time, they'll probably be called in to help with the cleanup. Some Dethroned are uncanny people, but others are small Kaiju, and they are far past the point of caring who sees them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13233-rougemephilesclone","user":"RougeMephilesClone","date":". 04-11-2017, 06:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13233-rougemephilesclone","name":"RougeMephilesClone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T20:21:47-07:00","id":1076260,"title":"","content":"Interesting, so the Dethroned are more of a parallel to the Suankshen rather than the Deceived from Mummy: the Curse? Beings who are mere shells of their former selves an range from nasty beasts to dangerous masterminds?<br /> <br /> Also, what on earth is the Dark World? Is that like what the Primordial Dream is to the Bright Dream in regards to the Dreamlands? Or is it something more other like Arcadia or one of the Lower Depths?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 04-10-2017, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T02:59:50-07:00","id":1076385,"title":"","content":"Even in-universe, nobody is sure what exactly the Dark World is, aside from the fact the Darkness came from this place (even though ironically even creatures of the Darkness have trouble staying active inside it when they get too far away from Tainted Areas). What is known about it is that it looks like a dark reflection of the real world (as in everything is destroyed or trying to kill you, buildings are in ruins, the moon is a black hole, the sun is red....), and Tainted Areas are places where it &quot;leaks&quot; into the real world. Because of this, creatures of the Darkness (and Princesses with the right Lacrima Charms) can use Tainted Areas as portals to travel to the Dark World and vice-versa the same way werewolves use Loci to travel to the Shadow.<br /> <br /> Also, since we're at it, I'd like to clarify a few more things regarding the Darkness:<br /> <br /> Darkened, being still human for the most part, aren't systematically evil; many of them don't even realize they have been corrupt until their &quot;Umbrae&quot; (the mutations provoked by their conditions) get too blatant to not notice (many earlier Umbrae actually are pretty subtle). There can even be people who who are looking for a cure or a mean to use these powers well (though the latter rarely goes well). Princesses are aware of this, so with the exception of Stormites, they don't usually shoot Darkened on sight and would rather try to cure the innocent ones when it is still possible. Only Mnemosyne, Darkspawns are Cataphracoi are ireedeemably evil.<br /> <br /> Many Darkened and Mnemosyne organize in Dark Cults intended to recruit and corrupt more people, usually by baiting them first and then by locking them in Tainted Areas if they are too reluctant. These cults rarely last long, however -- most of the time their blatantly evil attitude means the police will end up taking care of them even if a Princess doesn't show up. Only the really smart ones survive.<br /> <br /> When a Darkened reaches Integrity 0 with even one Umbrae (he has a chance of getting one each time his Integrity lowers), he dies in his sleep and rises as a Darkspawn later. Darkened who somehow managed to get to Integrity 0 without a single Umbrae become Mnemosyne instead. Cataphractoi, meanwhile, are born when someone reach a level of dispair where she is convinced there's nothing good in the world and dies in that state (frequently but not always suicide), resulting in her body rising as a Cataphract.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 04-11-2017, 06:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T04:20:52-07:00","id":1076406,"title":"","content":"On the subject of Dethroned. They tend to be very passive and it's very very rare to see one outside of the Dark World. Very few Hunters will know of them. Only truely old and widespread groups like the Ascending Ones and the Aegis Kai Doru are likely to have met a Dethroned and recorded it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1076194#post1076194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can assume that the Auschwitz memorial is clean of Taint by now (though what it was like when the death camp was operating doesn't bear thinking about.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine the opposite. In my World of Darkness there is no Auschwitz memorial, the sites of old concentration camps are avoided like the plague. Either Princesses, The Malleus Malificarum, or Sin-Eaters (depending on what suits the story) have set up powerful magical wards to keep the monsters infesting the sites from escaping, and occasionally launch raids to cull the monsters when they get too numerous and look like they might escape.<br /> <br /> Alternatively the concentration camps were burnt to the ground decades ago to sterilize the area. Which of course feeds into holocaust denial conspiracy theories.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1076179#post1076179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously, &quot;the Darkness&quot; is a mutagenic virus or fungus. It lingers in some areas, affecting long term residents and warping them as the infection progresses. There is a noticeable effect upon the subjects' brain, reducing empathy and increasing sociopathic tendencies, as well. Perhaps more troubling, it appears to be another &quot;reanimator&quot; infection, capable of resuscitating hosts as mobile infection vectors even after they have expired.<br /> -Dr. William Cole, Null Mysteriis</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1076198#post1076198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other day, a colleague floated a troubling hypothesis regarding the connection between the Darkness infection and these &quot;Princesses&quot; - the later are carriers. She pointed out the figures showing that concentrations of these &quot;Nobles&quot; correlated to more &quot;Darkspawn&quot; incidents, and brought up the reports of some Nobles even undergoing catastrophic mutation. As if their immunity suddenly gave out against a massive infection. There are still too many variables left unknown to be certain, but the thought of these individuals, frequently only mere teenagers, acting as &quot;Typhoid Marys&quot; to the very people they claim to protect is... unnerving.<br /> -Dr. William Cole, Null Mysteriis</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Null Mysteriis one of the most important things is to write them as competent scientists. Not what TvTropes calls <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/AgentScully\" target=\"_blank\">Agent Scully</a>. One of the first things you learn in science class is that correlation does not imply causation, so an NM doctor is not likely to consider Nobles and Darkspawn in the same place as evidence that one causes the other, especially not when there's a far simple explenation that they both seek each other out.<br /> <br /> Even the open minds aren't likely to make basic mistakes, rather they'd have elabourate self-consistant theories that are mostly impossible to disprove.<br /> <br /> That said, there probably is such a thing as &quot;dark fungus.&quot; There's already precedent that the Darkness can corrupt animals (Duskhounds might be animals, which strongly implies it's non-controvercial among Princesses to say the Darkness can courupt animals. Also I'm just going to flat out state it can <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) so why can't it corrupt fungus? If the NM autopsies a dead Darkspawn and sees that it's full of various Tainted spores and moulds from living in a Tainted Place then assuming the moulds spread corruption is a reasonable evidence based hypothosis. And helpfully you can't just pump someone full of Tainted fungus and see if it disproves your theory because that would be unethical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T04:55:55-07:00","id":1076413,"title":"","content":"The task force Valkyrie stuff, while making perfect sense... Makes me want to take them over my knee, ideas why?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T07:16:52-07:00","id":1076466,"title":"","content":"because it's kinda nationalistic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T07:22:00-07:00","id":1076469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1076406#post1076406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine the opposite. In my World of Darkness there is no Auschwitz memorial, the sites of old concentration camps are avoided like the plague. Either Princesses, The Malleus Malificarum, or Sin-Eaters (depending on what suits the story) have set up powerful magical wards to keep the monsters infesting the sites from escaping, and occasionally launch raids to cull the monsters when they get too numerous and look like they might escape.<br /> <br /> Alternatively the concentration camps were burnt to the ground decades ago to sterilize the area. Which of course feeds into holocaust denial conspiracy theories.</div> </div> </div> </div>that is an ...interesting idea. How does that work for places that can't be burned to the ground though? like mass graves and killing fields? For example, My Lai 101 or Khmer Rouge sites. This also brings up another question. How does the Darkness interact with the negative spirits that feed on these sites, and even the Wound spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 04-11-2017, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T07:51:21-07:00","id":1076488,"title":"","content":"oh if you read some of the &quot;Crystal tokyo dystopia&quot; sailor Moon Fanfics... you might see more thinking that would allow rationalizing opposition to magical girls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T09:09:13-07:00","id":1076529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1076469#post1076469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This also brings up another question. How does the Darkness interact with the negative spirits that feed on these sites, and even the Wound spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not well? They feed on the same prey and aren't exactly creatures prone to co-operation. That might actually be what's stopping places like that spilling into reality- the monsters are too busy fighting each other to make any serious plans.<br /> <br /> Although, if you are giving Princess primacy, maybe a wound is what happens when the Darkness infests a spiritual location, just like a tainted place is when it infests a physical one. Maybe wound-spirits, or even infernal demons, are spirit darkspawn. Maybe drauger and broken souls and the Mad and pandorans and insatiables and all those always-evil groups, maybe they're all just what happens when the darkness gets its claws in a super. Maybe monsters are only <i>monsters</i> because long ago the Darkness worked its way into entire species so deeply that now they just call it &quot;the beast&quot; or &quot;hunger&quot; or &quot;Kuruth&quot; or &quot;torment&quot;, and they never even think that maybe it it wasn't meant to be there.<br /> <br /> It's a theory, at least, and one people who know of the Darkness and what it does might come up. It'd be kind of interesting to see a hunter/princess group who belives that- like storms, but they think <i>every</i> non-princess supernatural is darkened at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T10:29:16-07:00","id":1076572,"title":"","content":"One of the more recent additions to the Vocation edition of Princess is a Caligo that pulls spirits out of the Shadow reflection of a Tainted area. It's there so you can play with Dark cults that use Wound-spirits, or bargain with the Inferno.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T13:52:19-07:00","id":1076654,"title":"","content":"Alright, I think I've got enought to write up a simplified catagorizarion for the Darkness and it's many spawn. What each Cell, Compact, or Conspiracy may believe about the Darkness or these creatures will vary, but the commonalities are enought among all of them for any one Cell who's fought Darkspawn before to recognize. <br /> <br /> ~ Lurkers: Horribly twisted and loathsome creatures that seem to almost feed on the suffering they cause to humanity. While most instances report that they are entirely bestial, some appear to possess a dangerous cunning when it comes to spreading misery and chaos. These are the most common kinds of Spawn, and while monstrous they are also the easiest to eliminate since all that's necessary is either enough firepower or just the right kind of Bane. Sadly though, these creatures are just the simptom of a much greater problem that Hunters are faced with, and worse very few Hunter are aware of that and thus miss critical opportunities to eliminate the problem wholesale. <br /> <br /> ~ Infiltrators: A far more advanced and dangerous Spawn than a Lurker. Infiltrators are dangerous because they're completely indistinguishable from an ordinary human. They still appear to feed off misery and chaos, but they possess enough intelligence (although many argue whether or not they are sentient or just cunning enough to fake it) to be subtle in their predation and careful enough to avoid outright detection like their Lurker cousins. In fact, some Compacts &amp; Conspiracies theorize Infultrators to have once been humans themselves before being infected and transformed into something...else. Whatever the case, Infultrators are definitively not human any more (if they ever were) and often naive Hunters underestimate their danger and powers compared to their Lurker cousins. Those who do usually don't survive the confrontation. <br /> <br /> ~ Nests: Often confused for haunted locations or the equally rare Institutional Demon, Nests are the true threat that all Hunters must inevitably face when Spawn are involved. They are physical locations where tragedy or atrocities took place that seem to take on a life of their own and actively gestate and birth Spawn into the world to act as worker drones to collect the misery and suffering it needs in order to grow and expand. Unlike spirit haunted locations or Institutional Demons, Nests are definitively not sentient and act with an almost animalistic instinct when spreading and creating Spawn. If Lurkers or Infultrators are present, then without question a Nest is near by and must be taken care of if the Spawn problem is to ever be completely taken care of. Luckily for Hunters and Mortal Mediums, Nests seem to be effected by exorcisms and other purification rituals. Unfortunatly, humans who enter a Nest are beset by traumatic flashbacks and mental assaults by the Nest itself, as well as having to confront any Spawn that are at the Nest or rush back to defent it. The most curious part about Nests though is that they are exceedingly rare, and seem to generally appear (or are &quot;birthed&quot;) when the supernatural creatures known as Nobles are within the general region. Many Hunters debate to this day whether or not Nobles are just numerous where there are Nests because they are creatures who universally oppose the Spawn, or if the Nest and Spawn themselves are drawn to areas with high Noble activity and seed themselves nearby in order to feed off the misery they bring to the Empaths themselves. <br /> <br /> That being said, many Cells, Conpacts, and Conspiracies don't even acknowledge the existence of Spawn and simply see other supernatural monsters that just share similar characteristics. Truly, how many monsters exist in the world who were once human but are now beasts that feed upon their former friends and family? How many &quot;cursed&quot; locations reach out and twist a population against itself? And why should thousands of years of history and research be put aside for some fable that Nobles tell amongst themselves to easily explain why they are good and every other creature of the night is evil? These are questions all Hunters must face sooner or later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 04-11-2017, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T14:48:51-07:00","id":1076667,"title":"","content":"Wait, they only appear near Nobles?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T15:05:25-07:00","id":1076672,"title":"","content":"From the Hunter's point of view. Without the Noble lens what's the real difference between a Wound, God Machine Infrastructure, Abyssal Verge, Haunted House, Tainted Location, or any of the thousand of terrors that go bump in the night?<br /> <br /> Plus remember, this is meant to examine and dissect some of the lore and beliefs from Princess itself. Nobles spend their entire lives fighting the Darkness, and from what I've read have an almost WoD Garu mentality involving their necessity to save humanity from the forces of the Darkness. Calling into question if the Darkness truly exists as a cosmic force (or if the Light even does as well), questioning mortal compotence in fighting Darkspawn, and all around examining a Princess' relationship to the Darkspawn could prove very fruitful in a Hunter the Vigil Chronicle as well as a Princess: the Hopeful one.<br /> <br /> And besides, mortal lore involving the supernatural almost exclusively deals in falsehoods and half-truths. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":"Polish 04-11-2017, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T15:06:33-07:00","id":1076674,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7920_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7920\" data-vbnamecard=\"7920\">Master Aquatosic</a> No, but since they can feed on Light in the place of normal food, Darkspawn prefer to go where Tainted Places (Light can't get a foothold in them and leaks into the Dark World) and Nobles (DINNER SERVED WITH DESSERT\u2026 and they're ancient enemies to boot!) are plentiful.<br /> <br /> Darkspawn can feel the Light leaking out of a Light-attuned character, whether it be from a Beacon, a Sworn with a bit of Queen-inspired Inner Light, or a Noble with their Inner Light gradually growing. This doesn't mean they will automatically hunt down Light-attuned characters and kill them, just that they are subconsciously compelled to occupy the same general area and oppose the Light's influence.<br /> <br /> The rules for Tainting an area are what they are, and with this taking place in the World of Darkness where evil is more common, they could appear anywhere. If the Light instinctually opposes the Darkness, a place with a lot of existing Tainted Places may see more Blossomings in response. From what I can gather, that might be why San Francisco is PtH's primary location. Of course, this is mostly speculation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13233-rougemephilesclone","user":"RougeMephilesClone","date":". 04-11-2017, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13233-rougemephilesclone","name":"RougeMephilesClone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T23:59:20-07:00","id":1076834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1076469#post1076469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that is an ...interesting idea. How does that work for places that can't be burned to the ground though? like mass graves and killing fields? For example, My Lai 101 or Khmer Rouge sites. This also brings up another question. How does the Darkness interact with the negative spirits that feed on these sites, and even the Wound spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way Tainted Places work means that there's always one or more physical lynchpins, a single bone or spent bullet in a mass grave for example, so throwing enough napalm or explosives at a Tainted Place will work. The Purgation Charm is especially powerful because it starts a fire that can feed on anything Tainted. Damp soil over a mass grave included.<br /> <br /> As for Wound Spirits. IMO Wounds and Tainted Places are so similar thematically that I wouldn't use them both in the same game; not the most useful answer for crossover I know.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T03:11:39-07:00","id":1076884,"title":"","content":"Well, the crossover section on the wiki DOES mention Tainted Areas and Wounds frequently overlap with each others, leading to occasional collaboration between Nobles and Uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T07:39:19-07:00","id":1076962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1076834#post1076834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Wound Spirits. IMO Wounds and Tainted Places are so similar thematically that I wouldn't use them both in the same game; not the most useful answer for crossover I know.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I would, but that's mostly because I like to screw with and confuse people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T07:57:17-07:00","id":1076971,"title":"","content":"Not all tainted places would have had enough or bad enough crimes to become Wounds, I think, considering that just a sour enough social atmosphere of envy and oneupsmanship is enough to make a neighborhood lightly tainted it sounds like","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T12:59:23-07:00","id":1077148,"title":"","content":"Alright, I've finished skimming through the Princess PDF (I'm assuming it's the 2nd Edition Dream version by what I've read) and after everything I've read and despite how profoundly contemptuous some of the writing is (seriously, having a social narrative of killing creatures in order to &quot;save them&quot; amongst the Nobility really doesn't sit well with me, but then again I could already be completely corrupted by the Darkness <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) I can honestly say that this is the best fanmade gameline I've ever read. The game knows exactly what it wants to be and makes room for both fans of the inspirational material and for more subtle interpretations for those who don't. The systems are solid, and there's a lot of creativity and love that went into it's making and it really shows. I tip my hat to the creators of such an interesting fangame. <br /> <br /> It's given me some great ideas about new tactics for fighting creatures of the Darkness and maybe one more for Nobles, and I'd like to advocate again for a section near the beginning that takes some time to explore morality in Hunter the Vigil just a little more closer since the &quot;battle of the Light vs. the Darkness&quot; is such a core theme of Princess the Hopeful. By examining a Hunter's own beliefs (*wink*) we can examine strengths and dangers of conviction as well as examine how social narratives are made to justify the Hunt amongst certain Hunter families and organizations. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T13:56:08-07:00","id":1077193,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1077148#post1077148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and despite how profoundly contemptuous some of the writing is (seriously, having a social narrative of killing creatures in order to &quot;save them&quot; amongst the Nobility really doesn't sit well with me, but then again I could already be completely corrupted by the Darkness <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )...</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm not exactly certain about where in the document you picked that up from. By default, killing Darkened people is greatly frowned upon by everyone except the Court of Storms, mainly due to the fact that they can be redeemed at that point. In general, the only beings that Princesses will always try to kill on principle are Darkspawn, Mnemosynes, Cataphractoi, and Dethroned, and even then (according to the Dream version, at least) they need to do it with noble intentions (or Tempesta Charms) to actually reduce the sum of Darkness in the world. Once something becomes a creature of Darkness, the person they used to be is functionally (and almost always literally) dead. At that point, murder isn't the best solution, it's the only one that works.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13233-rougemephilesclone","name":"RougeMephilesClone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:27:16-07:00","id":1077273,"title":"","content":"Yeah I don't remember anything about killing Darkened to save them either, and I read the Dream version. But regardless, glad you agree about how good this game is^^ Glad as well that it gave you new ideas. Feel free to add them.<br /> <br /> I am not sure I understand. What would this section be about?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T16:24:49-07:00","id":1077323,"title":"","content":"Well, to give a bit of context: if you want your protagonists to be sympathetic and still claim that it's possible to &quot;nobly kill&quot; anything, let alone something that was basically irradiated into a sadistic mutant monster, in order to decrease the total about of evil in the world than you either need them to a) be either fanatical or deluded or b) write up said mutant monsters as so irredeemably evil that it might as well turn them into baby eating Nazi's. But that's sort of the buy-in for Princess the Hopeful though, it's a dark fantasy game at heart. Not a horror game. And that puts it at odds with all of the core CofD gamelines since even Inferno acknoledges that Demons on their own are shallow and empty characters, but their interactions with regular humans is what makes them interesting and gives depth to stories of faustian bargains and good intentions leading to a descent into hell.<br /> <br /> But I digress, I'd probably write the morality play section as sort of a primer before the supplement goes into the Nobility proper. Spend a few sections discussing how individual Hunters beliefs are effected and shaped by their experience with the Vigil, and how their personal interactions with the supernatural shapes their morality. Then slowly go larger in scale until you get to how Conspiracies like the Aegis Kai Doru develop their own mythology to justify their Hunting practices and how personal experiences can call into question those beliefs and how that could potentially be both good and bad for Hunters in the field. Something like that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T16:42:00-07:00","id":1077334,"title":"","content":"Well, thing is, Darkspawns are not really mutants as much as they are monsters made out of corpses (and not even retaining a sentience or the living person's personnality like with vampires). Killing them really IS a mercy kill at best. And really, I fail to see how this contracticts the other games, since most do have at least one faction or species that can be killed without feeling bad about it. I mean, can you tell me with a straight face you would feel sorry about killing a True Fae? Or a Strix? Or an Indigam? Or an Insatiable? Again, Darkened are usually not killed as the first option, and all other creatures of the Darkness are causing pain and suffering remorselessly (not to mention that in the case of Dethroned, they are basically in a permanent state of pain). Princesses kill creatures of the Darkness less for what they are and more for all the horror they inflict.<br /> <br /> But yeah, digression.<br /> <br /> Okay... well be my guest, I guess. Not sure how such a section would have something to do with the topic of the supplement, but I'll wait to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T17:14:54-07:00","id":1077345,"title":"","content":"Feel sorry about? Definitively no. In all cases my success would amount to mostly luck I'd imagine.<br /> <br /> Justified though...well that depends. If it was personal then yes. A Kindred setting fire to their shadowy tormentor or a Changeling kicking in the teeth of their Keeper can be very powerful scenes. But feeling justified about the destruction of another creature is a very dangerous spiral to fall down. Coincidently that very line of logic is primarily what Hunter the Vigil is about, but even then the game clearly realizes that this line of thinking is what transforms ordinary people into monsters. <br /> <br /> That downward spiral only tangentially exists in Princess. Any Noble can feel completely justified in slaying all the Darkspawn they want without consiquences. The only cause for pause involve collateral damage, or slaying people who are dark but not &quot;fully tainted.&quot; It just...strikes me as sort of fiat to allow players to guilt free butcher semi-human creatures that are often metamorphosise against their own will. And that turns to contempt when said game's player character culture swears it's for their own good.<br /> <br /> I'm not the only one who sees this as kinda fucked up right? Maybe that's even the point? It just...it's kinda weird, really the only problem I have with the game. But then again, maybe that just how the genre is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T17:29:13-07:00","id":1077351,"title":"","content":"Trying to avoid turning this thread into a long morality debate, I got the impression that darkspawn are probably not meant to be common. The Nobles aren't meant to keep killing darkspawn, they're meant to make the world such that it stops spawning darkspawn. Killing darkspawn is meant to be a tragic case of having to do something terrible because no-one else stepped in when things could still be saved. <br /> <br /> There's a reason that the faction whose defining purpose is &quot;kill darkspawn&quot; are one of the villains. If you're slaughtering darkspawn wholesale, then somethings gone wrong. What you should be doing is redeeming darkened, purifying tainted areas and making the world a place that doesn't spawn darkspawn.<br /> <br /> At least, that's what I got and how I'd play it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T17:33:56-07:00","id":1077353,"title":"","content":"I'll admit, at least a mention of some, perhaps misguided, attempts to rehabilitate full-on Darkspawn would be nice. trying to cure Dark Taint sounds like something the Ascending Ones, Les Mysteres or Null Mysteres might try","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T17:36:14-07:00","id":1077358,"title":"","content":"(although, it's a interesting position for a hunter group to take. Hunters only really have the Princess's word for it that darkspawn are irredemable and incurable. Indeed, with their comparatively young age, the Princess don't necessarily <i>know</i> that, only that none have been cured so far. They're relying on the information of Storms and Tears, neither of which are necessarily good guides. A group dedicated to finding out whether darkspawn can be cured- and whether the Nobles have a vested interest in ensuring they aren't- could be a interesting idea, if maybe too narrow for a full compact)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T17:37:48-07:00","id":1077359,"title":"","content":"Perhaps even make it hard but possible to save the once-human ones. <br /> <br /> That said, do remember that becoming Darkspawn does require you to commit various horrific breaking point worthy acts. Sure, you are nudged along by the nature of the place, but the responsibility is still on you ultimately. At the very least, Darkspawn were those who stood by and did not nng to stop others from doing horrible things","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T17:42:42-07:00","id":1077360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1077353#post1077353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit, at least a mention of some, perhaps misguided, attempts to rehabilitate full-on Darkspawn would be nice. trying to cure Dark Taint sounds like something the Ascending Ones, Les Mysteres or Null Mysteres might try</div> </div> </div> </div> If there's some kind of story seed section, one of those groups making some actual progress would be very interesting, on both sides. The reaction of the Twilight Courts to the knowledge that the creatures they've been destroying/surrendering to/hiding from could have been cured if they'd just tried harder would be devestating- perhaps enough for them to try and cover it up before anyone found out.<br /> <br /> Then there's the more powerful darkness creatures getting worried they might lose their minions, the more willing ones worrying they'd lose their powers, the more aware ones trying to find the cure but lacking the capacity to do so safely, the radient princesses torn between hope and an &quot;is it too good to be true&quot; worry, other hunters thinking this might be the breakthrough to curing all monsters (and thus either promoting or destroying it based on their interests)...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T17:47:09-07:00","id":1077361,"title":"","content":"Well said @Urbenmyth,<br /> <br /> This is all nitpicks anyways for me (although I could go on about my frustrations with how Belief is written up...), but ultimately the game is just fine as is. <br /> <br /> As for the morality discussion for Darkness &amp; Light, I'll see how much I can write up by later tonight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T17:52:01-07:00","id":1077364,"title":"","content":"Yeah, best not turn this section into a moral debate. I do see where you're coming from, Duskage, in that I consider genocide should never be considered a &quot;good&quot; thing in my mind and I don't believe in things such as an entirely evil species (though in Darkspawns' case, they aren't exactly a species, but more Darkened who are too far gone-- much like vampires with zero humanity). But yeah, I think Urbenmyth sums it up well; Princesses aren't meant to JUST kill Darkspawns, and in fact this is more meant as a last resort, like killing an enemy soldier in war. When the game talks about &quot;nobly&quot; killing creatures of the Darkness, it's more to understand as killing them for a justified reason -- like to protect the weak. There is a reason the fighting class is called Champion, and not slayer. Also, one nice thing is that Princess actually shows there are many ways to bring the light other than killing Darkspawns, like healing and inspiring people with music.<br /> <br /> Now, I suggest we get back on topic^^ I can't wait to see what you'll do, Duskage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:10:06-07:00","id":1077414,"title":"","content":"To tack on one last bit about generic Darkspawn, some of them are just Darkness given form, like the ones who are usually sleeping in the Dark World and any that are directly created by a Dethroned. Their resemblance to normal ex-living creatures is likely just the All-Consuming Darkness recycling some of the forms it has already stolen from the world. The Vocation version has a few Alhambra-specific Darkspawn who embody this, right down to using limited speech just to screw with people. Taking that into consideration, some Darkspawn may be totally resistant to rehabilitation due to having been created in their current state, so the whole idea is pretty much a crapshoot.<br /> <br /> Like, there is a bit on Dethroned that notes that anyone can be redeemed if someone loves them enough, and since that's not what Hunters <i>do,</i> their experiments will be predisposed towards failure. Of course, if Cheiron can enslave Promethean bees, then I guess the sky is the limit. What the Storyteller says goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13233-rougemephilesclone","name":"RougeMephilesClone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T20:10:11-07:00","id":1077461,"title":"","content":"Potential opinions on the darkness from the other main Compacts:<br /> <br /> <b>Network Zero</b>- As much as they'd hate to admit it, lurkers are really useful for the secret frequency. They're obviously supernatural, leave behind huge amounts of evidence and barely try to hide. Finding one in the area is usually cause to try and get as much footage as possible before someone smashes it.<br /> This, however, leads to another thought- unlike most supernatural creatures, you can make a lurker. Not with complex rituals or rare cosmic coincidences, but just by hurting people. You can do it by accident. Of course, almost everyone in the compact finds the idea abhorrent...but the thought keeps coming up in the more extreme fringes. Final and undeniable proof of the supernatural, at the cost of one person's soul. Might that not be worth it?<br /> <br /> <b>Null Mysteris</b>- Serious studies into the Darkness are running into problems. Not just because it seemingly lacks any kind of biological, chemical or energy-based vector- at this point the scientists of the compact are pretty used to that- but because of the ethical difficulties studying it. Pretty much any serious investigation into the outer darkness violates every experimental ethics guideline at best and is outright scientific atrocity at worst.<br /> Among those members of the compact who know of the Darkness, two sides are forming. One argues it should be left for now- knowledge isn't worth your humanity. Others say that the need to study this potentially apocalyptic force justifies overriding some normal restraints. The debate is rapidly getting less academic, and if left to grow may soon spill out into the wider compact.<br /> <br /> <b>The Loyalists of Thule</b>- The Loyalists hate the darkness. Lurkers, infiltrators, nests- they all need to go. They say this is because of its danger and evil, and that's certainly true. But also, with their knowledge of the occult, they are one of the few groups who know of the Darkened. The idea that the worst among might not have committed their crimes alone, then responsibility might lie in the hands of some shadowy alien force rather then the human heart- to the Indebted, it's both psychologically and ideologically horrific. Better to destroy the darkness before people get ideas.<br /> <br /> <b>Ageis Kai Doru</b>- the Agies Kai Doru are worried by the darkness. They know how paradise fell, and it wasn't the outer darkness. Is it some dark force the mages of Atlantis drew on to power corrupt arts? Then why don't the tales of atlantis sound anything like the powers infiltrators wield?<br /> Were the Mistress of Honey and Asterion children of the dark? Then why aren't shapeshifters affected by jade in any way, or darkspawn by silver?<br /> Was the fall of atlantis not the first time mankind lost paradise? Then why don't any of the records of Atlantis mention that?<br /> Practically, of course, it doesn't matter- they're monsters and must be stopped. But try as they might, the Guardians can't fit the Darkness into their mythology, and more and more, that worries them.<br /> <br /> <b>Ascending Ones</b>- The ascending ones are frustrated by the Darkness. Their role as diplomats fail before them- even the smartest Darkspawn refuses to co-operate or bargain except as prelude to attack, and their presence brings chaos to both mundane and supernatural communities.<br /> The easiest answer is to wipe them out, of course, and most ascending ones do. But on faction have started trying to capture them, in the hope of redeeming them. If they can take even these monsters and make them good- or at least reasonable- that would be a significant practical and moral accomplishment. If it leads to anything but slaughter on both sides, that is.<br /> <br /> <b>Mallus Malificeruim</b>. They're demons. Demons from hell, send them back. Easy right? Well, no. Most demons, they need to tempt. They manipulate or lie or bribe, but they can't just make you sin. They can possess, yes, but that doesn't stain your soul. Not the Darkness. The Darkness just makes you a worse person, overrides your free will and makes you turn away from God. If some theories about what happens with darkspawn is correct it might even destroy your soul outright. The idea of the devil being able to do that is horrifying on an almost unimaginable level to the Hammer of Witches.<br /> Naturally, the higher ups write long theological papers explaining why that isn't the case- the victim must have subconsciously listened to the darkness, or only the body was controlled, or the soul goes straight to hell- but even the possibility is devastating to Catholicism. A good reason to kill the whole thing now just in case.<br /> <br /> <b>TF:V</b>- TF:V doesn't care a huge amount about the darkness- they're monsters, kill them, boom. Job done. But there's a secret. People in power- politicians, businessmen, generals- there is a lot of darkened among them. A few infiltrators, even. You don't reach those heights without doing something, and often it has consequences. And TF:V knows exactly who they are and how integral they are to the power structure of the nation.<br /> Naturally, if this was revealed would be deeply damaging to the USA's authority, so the grunts aren't told about this. As long as they think the darkness is just monsters they can shoot that's great. Another devil dealt with by TF:V.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","user":"Urbenmyth","date":". 04-12-2017, 11:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T02:42:33-07:00","id":1077590,"title":"","content":"On the subject of saving Darkspawn. It's very intentionally impossible. Princess (at least Dream) is designed to be a toolbox style. If you want to play an all Troubadour game along the lines of <i>Jem and the Holograms</i> where the only antagonists are: mortal paparazzi, muckraking gossip magazines, and record company executives, you can do that. If you want to play a Sailor Moon inspired game where you fight your way through progressively more powerful Darkspawn every session then you can do that too.<br /> <br /> In line with that design philosophy there <u>has</u> to be at least one antagonist type where violence is the unambiguously correct solution for players who want to play in the style of classical magical girl warriors, lots of magic lasers, no moral issues with using them. Thus, apart from Darkened and Dethroned, there's no curing Creatures of the Darkness.<br /> <br /> Of course Hunters might not know that. (Though Hunters being more concerned about monster rights than Princesses does seem a tad athematic to me)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1076654#post1076654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That being said, many Cells, Conpacts, and Conspiracies don't even acknowledge the existence of Spawn and simply see other supernatural monsters that just share similar characteristics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, Hunters would be very keen to document which monsters are vulnerable to a jade bullet, and which monsters are vulnerable to holy water.<br /> <br /> Getting the two mixed up could be fatal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1077148#post1077148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can honestly say that this is the best fanmade gameline I've ever read. The game knows exactly what it wants to be and makes room for both fans of the inspirational material and for more subtle interpretations for those who don't. The systems are solid, and there's a lot of creativity and love that went into it's making and it really shows. I tip my hat to the creators of such an interesting fangame.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-13-2017, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T12:31:56-07:00","id":1078474,"title":"","content":"Ok, I succeed from writing a morality section in the supplement. I've been a it for days and nothing's really coming. :/<br /> <br /> Good idea on paper but I'm definitly falling short of the mark, so I'm moving on to something else. How are the write ups for the Compacts/Conspiracies for HtV: Darkness &amp; Light coming along?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T14:54:52-07:00","id":1078551,"title":"","content":"Not that easy, I guess...<br /> <br /> Well, making good progress overall, albeit slow. After some days thinking about it I am finally writing something for the Lucifuge section. The Ascending one on the other hand are giving me some trouble. I would also appreciate any ideas for the followings:<br /> <br /> * Suggestions to start developping the new Conspiracies/Compacts ideas<br /> * New Endowments for each Conspiracy<br /> * More new Tactics<br /> * Rules to build Princesses and Creatures of the Darkness as antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T15:18:21-07:00","id":1078574,"title":"","content":"What's the etiquette on editing? Just go in there and delete errors, or just make comments?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T15:21:06-07:00","id":1078576,"title":"","content":"For the Luciferge, maybe something that fills someone with images of the sins of the world? Demoralising for anyone but potentially devestating for a princess. (it would also be wise to say whether luciferge powers that affect demons affect darkspawn- I'd lean towards not, as they're not extradimensional but hey). <br /> <br /> For a benediction, something that shows people their true self in the eyes of god (at least that's what the MM say it does). Damages those with lower then 4 morality, temporarily paralyses darkspawn (and, I guess, draugr and insatiables and stuff) as they briefly remember the person they used to be.<br /> <br /> Advanced armory thing that temporarily disrupts a Noble's perception filter, so you can see who they are? You could probably come up with a vauge sciency explanation<br /> <br /> A implanted shard of a Storm Princesses' Phylactery that lets the agent cover weapons in acid<br /> <br /> An elixer that shuts off your inner light (making it near imposssible to move you with appeals to guilt or morality) or hyperboosts it (making it naer impossible to tempt you with your vice)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T15:24:06-07:00","id":1078578,"title":"","content":"A &quot;figure out who the princess is&quot; tactic would make sense.<br /> <br /> A &quot;convince them to give up hope&quot; one would also work for more anti-princess factions.<br /> <br /> On the darkspawn side, a tactic for convincing a darkened to return to the light makes thematic sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T15:24:57-07:00","id":1078579,"title":"","content":"may I suggest moving a lot of the stuff that is past tense to the present tense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T15:26:38-07:00","id":1078581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1078578#post1078578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A &quot;figure out who the princess is&quot; tactic would make sense.<br /> <br /> A &quot;convince them to give up hope&quot; one would also work for more anti-princess factions.<br /> <br /> On the darkspawn side, a tactic for convincing a darkened to return to the light makes thematic sense.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I feel like the deprogramming tactic would not work. it would have to be more sincere and less morally ambiguous","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T15:30:14-07:00","id":1078585,"title":"","content":"do Compacts even have Endowments?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T15:36:11-07:00","id":1078588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1078581#post1078581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I feel like the deprogramming tactic would not work. it would have to be more sincere and less morally ambiguous</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe something that involves exposing the darkened to people/things they love from their human life? Trying to ground them back in the idea there are good things in the world.<br /> <br /> (also, compacts having endownments in as optional rule in Compacts and Conspiracies, I don't know how widely accepted it is though)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T15:43:15-07:00","id":1078596,"title":"","content":"(although a tactic for outright brainwashing people into joining the light might be a good sign of the different tones of Hunter and Princess. And a fourth twilight court, now I think about it. Fallen Clubs or Hearts, maybe? But I digress)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T15:59:45-07:00","id":1078605,"title":"","content":"Alright, this is more my fort\u00e9.<br /> <br /> Love the ideas floating around for Tactics. I think the Mirror Knight one already is used to attack a Princess' Belief by forcing them to have to Compromise with reality. I particularly like the idea of a Tactic that tries to catch a Princess in Transformation. Something maybe involving invasive journalism or luring a Spawn into an area with hidden cameras?<br /> <br /> And you know what? Mirror Knight might actually work on Spawn that have a shred of their humanity left! By forcing them to confront the reality of their own twisted transformation (forcing them to Compromise in the poisonous &quot;Belief&quot; that infects them from the Dead World) and if not open the possibility of redeeming them, then at least make them go docile so the Hunter can put them down in a humane manner. In a way that hauntingly mirror what happens to a Princess who goes to Belief 0. What do you all think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Brain Blast! 04-14-2017, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T16:38:05-07:00","id":1078632,"title":"","content":"You know, your second idea made me think... how would sound the idea of a Conspiracy using Darkspawns as familiars?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T17:12:31-07:00","id":1078647,"title":"","content":"If that's a thing, then some kind of tactic to deliberately taint someone/something might exist (although you would have to be careful in the description to avoid it just being unpleasant)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T17:17:47-07:00","id":1078652,"title":"","content":"I'll keep the idea in a corner for now. Best develop the ideas for new Compacts and Conspiracies we already have before starting new ones.<br /> <br /> I'd welcome any good ideas of names for the Stormwracked Compact and the Anti-Child Soldier group. Or ideas for any of these new groups' backstories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T17:40:49-07:00","id":1078666,"title":"","content":"I am not great with names, but<br /> <br /> Imagine you're a parent. And your young daughter, she starts talking about how she has superpowers and fights monsters. You shrug it off as playing. Her school work begins to suffer and she starts sneaking out to hang around these strange people and she starts to show signs of stress. You assume bullying, maybe, or depression. Until her body turns up torn apart. A wild animal, they say, but you remember how fervent she was that she <i>really was</i> fighting monsters.<br /> <br /> You start looking on the internet, and there are more parents with the signs. Some always knew something was up, some only saw it when you pointed it out. The child starts off enthusiastic, then starts getting grimmer, then they vanish or die. You start finding parents whose children haven't vanished yet, and this is what you learn- the magic powers are real. The monsters are real. And so are the Queens. They give the children magic items and send them to fight monsters. And the children, being unwitting child soldiers, die.<br /> <br /> The Queens say they are trying to create utopia. You don't know if they genuinely believe that or if it's a front for some nefarious purpose, and frankly you don't care. They're brainwashing your children, they're sending them to fight terrible things and they're moving on to the next child once they're done. Maybe they do think they're doing the right thing, but the world is full of people who commit atrocities in the name of the right thing.<br /> <br /> So you get together. Some of these parents have connections. Some have money. Some have combat skills or organisational experience or knowledge of the occult. you work closer and closer, and eventually you form a secret society. You don't blame the adult &quot;princesses&quot;- they've been brainwashed since they were children. You don't even blame the lurkers- if someone pushes a child into an alligator pit, you don't blame the alligator for what happens. No, it's the Queens who are responsible for this whole thing. And with the support of over a hundred grieving parents now, you will take down these Queens before they can recruit one more child into their private army.<br /> <br /> (While the group primarily focuses on the queens, they will fight against any monster that preys on children, and will recruit from anyone who lost or almost lost a child to the supernatural. But as far as they know, most of these monsters are individual horrors. The Queens are the ones organising this manipulate-brainwash-exploit-discard-repeat thing on a large scale, and thus they're the threat the group focuses on)<br /> <br /> (Also this seems to have evolved into a save-the-children group rather then an anti-child-soilder specifically. Sorry)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","user":"Urbenmyth","date":". 04-14-2017, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T17:46:17-07:00","id":1078669,"title":"","content":"Don't be sorry. This is actually pretty good, and does give them a believable, defendable motivation. Even knowing the Princesses' point of view, I admit it's hard to say these people are wrong.<br /> <br /> I'm adding it to the doc^^ Will flesh it out later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T18:05:08-07:00","id":1078678,"title":"","content":"(fyi- I have removed various typos from the post, if that helps)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T18:09:56-07:00","id":1078681,"title":"","content":"Holy crap! That's fantastic Urbenmyth! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The first name that pops into my head for that organization is something like: The Polaris Foundation. Also, perhaps they gear most to hunting the creatures of the Dreamlands that influence the child and adult Princesses. They could also have developed a decent understanding of the &quot;Sensitive's&quot; powers and mental needs (they don't use the word Noble or Princess to describe the Sensitives because that just reinforces the propaganda the &quot;Queen's&quot; use to recruit) and develop Tactics to try and change a Sensitive's Beliefs to gear more towards non-violent methods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T18:22:06-07:00","id":1078686,"title":"","content":"If they're mostly hunting dream creatures, they might have some interesting interactions with the Merrick Institute. <i>Especially</i> if they ever find out their true origins.<br /> <br /> They discover that there was a government programme to exploit the dream realm to make child soldiers out of kids with powers, and now there are godlike dream creatures giving children powers to fight a war- there's a lot of possible conclusions you can draw from that, and none of them bode well for either side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","user":"Urbenmyth","date":". 04-14-2017, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T19:03:30-07:00","id":1078704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1078666#post1078666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not great with names, but<br /> <br /> Imagine you're a parent. And your young daughter, she starts talking about how she has superpowers and fights monsters. You shrug it off as playing. Her school work begins to suffer and she starts sneaking out to hang around these strange people and she starts to show signs of stress. You assume bullying, maybe, or depression. Until her body turns up torn apart. A wild animal, they say, but you remember how fervent she was that she <i>really was</i> fighting monsters...<br /> <br /> (Also this seems to have evolved into a save-the-children group rather then an anti-child-soilder specifically. Sorry)</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes perfect sense.<br /> <br /> For a name - how about Millstone? It's a Biblical allusion - to one of Jesus' statements, that &quot;But whoever causes one of these little ones who believe in Me to stumble, it would be better for him if a millstone were hung around his neck, and he were thrown into the sea.&quot; (Matthew 18:6, Luke 17:2, or Mark 9:42.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T20:54:14-07:00","id":1078743,"title":"","content":"Alright, I'm so inspired I think I'll take a crack at writing up a Conspiracy idea I've had knocking around for a while. Be noted that like the True Fae...and now that I think about it the Darkness too...I'm not that original, but I can make meeeean homage content. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> The Cold Guard: The Watchers of the Darkness<br /> <br /> &quot;The Nobles love to tell a common tale about the origins of their society and the righteousness of their mission. Well, let me share with you a tale explaining the origins of our order: The Cold Guard was founded by a single woman from such a long time ago it no longer exists in recorded history. Back then there were eight citystates that were near constantly at war with one another, and each was ruled over by a sorcerer who wielded powerful magic relating to the human soul. Now, these citystates warred with each other so much that a fissure opened up within the earth itself and from it pored forth a horde of monstrosities that slaughtered all in their path. The horde grew so great that each of the citystates were forced to join forces, and yet even with their combined might the monsters couldn't be completely destroyed before more came poring through the deep fissure. This is where our founder comes into the story. She was a simple woodsman's daughter who lived far from the walled citystates and despite her good nature she and her family were no strangers to hardships. They looked out for each other and their small community, but were always willing to do what was necessary in order keep the community alive. All of this changed when the monsters appeared and slaughtered all of the villagers save for her, and only because she was covered in the viscera of the monster who almost killed her and thus the creatures couldn't recognize her from one of their own. Heartbroken but determined to avenge her family and prevent such destruction from befalling any other villages she drank of the blood of the creatures, a deadly poison that would do worse than kill her in time but cloak her from most of the horde, and followed the horde back to the deep fissure from which they arrived. Down into the dark she climbed until she climbed so far down that she arrived at...nothing. A great and infinite void from which the monsters must have come but was so still, cold, and empty that no other life could possibly live there. She knew she would not survive this journey, but when confronted with the void she knew fear like she'd only felt once before. And deep inside she cried out for something to be there, even if it was a monster. And from that fear, that desperate need, the Emissary was created from the void and emerged with the full knowledge of it's creation and the scope of the void so that it may answer the woman's questions and comfort her. It spoke of how the void is given shape and warmth by the essence of what humans call the soul, and how since humanity is covetous by nature only the essence that a human doesn't want to keep within themselves escapes to shine like distant starlight upon the void. Thus, when the citystates made war upon another to claim imperium and the sorcerers delved deep into the magic of the soul, hope, joy, love, friendship, and all that humans deem good was hoarded, while pain, sorrow, fear, despair, and doubt were cast out until it became a dim red sun that finally pierced the wall between worlds and allowed the void given shape by what humanity wishes to avoid to journey to the other side and consume the sweet warmth that had been denied to them. It spoke of how in time the sorcerers would discover the void and use it to become immortal monarchs over realms carved out of the human soul itself. It spoke of a time when the void would become Darkness, and actively seep into the souls or humans in a desperate hunger for warmth. It spoke of betrayal among the monarchs and a time one would come to rule over the Darkness itself. It spoke of the day humanity gains the power to destroy itself, and of the day humanity will first walk among the stars, how each will shape the void made Darkness. The woman listened to all of this, and deep in her heart knew it to be true. Thus, did she refuse to die there in the void. Instead she began to climb, as the Emissary watched from deep below. Near death, but never more determined she climbed back towards her world with the knowledge of what must be done to prevent suffering like she had endured. And at last she collapsed upon the soil of the world she was born into, and began the work that needed to be done. She let the citystates fall to the monsters, for nothing would stop the sorcerer's ambitions for godhood. Instead she gathered together those who were like herself, survivors who knew grief but accepted it as a part of who they are. She taught them all she knew, until at last she no longer cared about humanity and hungered for the sweet warmth hidden beneath supple flesh. That is when her fellows finally killed her, as she wished. The most dedicated among them drank her blood, and continue to do so to this day. Is any of this true...really? What do you think. Does any of this matter? Look at the world around you today and tell me that it doesn't...&quot;<br /> <br /> The Cold Guard is a conspiracy of monster hunters and humanists who know very well what the Darkness is, and why that no matter what the Nobility tries to do it will always remain. The Darkness is shaped by the failings of humanity itself, and until humanity can accept those failing there will always be Nests and Spawn cropping up to feed on the warmth of human beliefs and emotions. The Watchers have three primary duties that they strive to fulfill, called the Three Fronts. The First Front is the humanitarian front. The world will not become a better place unless people start treating others like people. Hunters on this front work to undo the damage wrought by Nests, as well as combat the influence of other social or supernatural predators. Often this front is used to either temper the fires of some of the more zealous trainees or to help veteran Hunter who are starting to feel the corruption of the Penumbrae setting in and want to prolong their lives and selves for as long as possible. This latter scenario can lead to some...less than desirable problems, but giving a veteran the potential to face their Fading with dignity while giving back something positive to the community is worth the risk as far as most of the Conspiracy is concerned. The Second Front is the Cold World front, where Hunters cut their teeth on the creatures of the Darkness. It's this front where trainees become official Hunters of the Conspiracy, and where the Cold Guard acquires the necessary components to create Penumbrae. Of all of the Fronts it's this one that sees the most combat, as well as the obvious higher turn over rate. Their expertise really shows though, for there's few mortal organizations that can match the Cold Guard's knowledge about Spawn and the Cold World. The final, and most controversial, front is the Third Front, the Sorcerer Queen front. This is also the most dangerous and morally reprehensible task that the Watchers must perform. The hunt of the Nobility, not &quot;contain&quot; or &quot;reform&quot; but hunt. They kill Princesses, because someone must show mercy to those poor souls. To the Cold Guard a Noble is just another kind of Spawn, one made for the most cruelest of purposes. They are human who contain a shard of the Sorcerer Queens soul and feed their immortal appetite for hope and joy by leeching out the light and belief of their vessel. The Watchers look no further than when a Noble's human self finally collapses under the weight of the Queen's power and reveals the Queen's connection to the Cold Realm, and how they claimed immortality. By killing these poor creatures they save them from such a doomed state, or at leasts that's what they tell themselves to sleep better at night. <br /> <br /> New Endowment: Penumbrae. <br /> ~ The Cold Guard takes in the otherworldly darkness of the Spawn in a ritually diluted manner in order to manifest lesser variants of the same powers the Spawn themselves utilize. The cost is a dire one, for the only end a Watcher can look forward to after the First Ritual is complete is either a painful death or eternal suffering as a Spawn themselves. The rewards are potent though, for not only do the Hunters become inured to the worst effects of a Nest, but also gain partial transformations that allow them strength in battle not seen in mortals except in the Nobility themselves. For each dot in Penumbrae a Hunter gains bonus dots to add to their Physical Attributes as they see fit when they manifest a partial transformation. They can spread them out however they wish, and lose the extra dots at the end of a scene. For every dot of Penumbrae they also receive a [Still coming up with name] that grants them a passive bonus just for having, but also an activated bonus that they can use during partial transformations. The major draw back is that once they possess a single dot of Penumbrae they register and count as Tainted creatures for all instances in which that would be pertinent. In addition, they also gain the potential to drop from Integrity 1 to 0, upon which the character is automatically retired as a Spawn as all of their experience points and merits liquidate for use in their next character [at the ST's discretion of course.] It should be noted though, that not all members of the Conspiracy possess Penumbrae. To undergo the First Ritual is a personal death sentence for the recipient, and special honors (and precautions) are taken involving said Hunter hence forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 04-15-2017, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T22:53:45-07:00","id":1078775,"title":"","content":"I came up with an outline for a compact a while ago from talking to Kings Raven. A newspaper company who believe Nobles feed upon humanity's emotional connections due to run-ins with Alhambra a few centuries back, they seek to sever all of a noble's mortal connections before killing. Their endowment is essentially the psychic paper from Dr Who and can convince people of non-existent credentials. <br /> <br /> Due to real life concerns I won't have time to add anything more this month but I hope I can help inspire someone with this. Also, I feel it necessary to mention that the Darkness is the Walmart of forbidden sorcery; really cheap with a wide variety but rather low quality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12243-dreaming-cat","name":"Dreaming Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T03:20:57-07:00","id":1078816,"title":"","content":"For the save the children group- you could combine the names. The Polaris Foundation sounds like a more official name, maybe a cover as a children's rights charity or grief consoling group, with Millstone being an internal name used by those &quot;In the know&quot; about the group's real purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T04:29:51-07:00","id":1078831,"title":"","content":"Then we need to define exactly why it's called the Polaris Foundation.<br /> <br /> @Duskage:Interesting idea... might need some organization, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T05:55:20-07:00","id":1078848,"title":"","content":"@Dusksage<br /> Dude. There's some real merit in that write-up. The point about there being only eight city states may need to be changed, as the corebooks imply that nobody really knows the real number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13233-rougemephilesclone","name":"RougeMephilesClone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T08:17:57-07:00","id":1078894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RougeMephilesClone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1078848#post1078848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Dusksage<br /> Dude. There's some real merit in that write-up. The point about there being only eight city states may need to be changed, as the corebooks imply that nobody really knows the real number.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'd say &quot;exactly&quot;. No one knows the real number so 8 is as good a number as any for the Cold's myth.<br /> <br /> Can Penumbrae users also pick up Caligines?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T09:23:11-07:00","id":1078918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1078894#post1078894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I'd say &amp;quot;exactly&amp;quot;. No one knows the real number so 8 is as good a number as any for the Cold's myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ack. I realized that, forgot about it, and wrote the post in a weird tone. The description Dusksage gave for the backstory <i>is</i> far enough removed from what the corebooks say to be perfectly acceptable in a Hunter context.<br /> <br /> As for Calignes, my understanding is that anyone can perform a ritual to gain a Caligo, but doing so and using one are both Breaking Points. To reiterate something Dreaming Cat said, the Darkness offers a wide variety of easy dark magic, it just kind of sucks compared to what other WoD magic users can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13233-rougemephilesclone","name":"RougeMephilesClone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T10:30:10-07:00","id":1078952,"title":"","content":"I'd say that it's very possible for Watchers with Penumbrae to learn Calignes, perhaps as some form of further initiation into the Second Front. I'd also say that it's forbidden for anyone without Penumbrae to learn them though, because that means when they inevitably fall to the Fading they become an Infiltrator rather than a Lurker, and those are much harder to detect. That being said...when has any Hunter played soley by the book when the Vigil is at stake? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (Also should be noted, any time a Hunter with Umbrae gains a dot in it or uses a partial transformation then they must make a Breaking Point roll. That's how they inevitably get eroded away until they either need to take time away from the hunt to regain control of themselves, or find a Gate to the Cold World and charge in and take out as many Spawn as possible until their they transform or they perish.)<br /> <br /> As for the story, like the unnamed narrator implied the story is more of an allegory to help explain why the Cold Guard exists and why they must use the Darkness to contain the &quot;Cold World&quot; and fight against the Sorcerer Queens. If there is any truth in that story, it's up to the player characters to discover. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (I'll work on a formal organization set up for the Conspiracy today. I'm leaning towards setting them up like an army/masonic order.)<br /> <br /> In regards to the Polaris Foundation's namesake, I though of the organization using this as a symbol of hope and their purpose. A guiding star to lead their indoctrinated loved ones back home where they will be welcomed. Personally I love the idea of the Millstones being their informal name. The Polaris Foundation: The Millstone Wielders (or just Millstones for short.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 04-15-2017, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T11:59:12-07:00","id":1078992,"title":"","content":"The Cold Guard have a solid concept, it's relatively close to Tears but I wouldn't worry about that. The thematic contrast that makes a good Princess focused Hunter Conspiracy is the exact same contrast that makes a good Twilight Court, so it's not surprising or a problem if there's overlap.<br /> <br /> I wasn't too sold on them Hunting Princesses though. In a situation like this any good argument they can make to Princesses about the cosmology will be overshadowed by the fact they're trying to kill Princesses; from the Princess POV the fact the Cold Guard are trying to kill them is a ready made justification to ignore anything they say.<br /> <br /> On a similar vein parts came across as acting to much like Princesses rather than an an expression of their thematic contrast. The humanitarians, for example, could use a touch up to include more of the guard's ideology: So where as a Princess might see a junkie and try and help them overcome their addiction and improve their life; the Cold Guard would see a junkie and tell them that they'll always be a junkie and trying to fight it only makes things worse but they'd try to make them comfortable until the drugs kill them (or recruit them). Where as Princesses like to kill Darkspawn and cleanse Taint; the Cold Guard might try and trap Spawn inside Nests but at the same time they'd protect the nests from destruction. If there's always going to be Spawn and Nests; then why not keep them where you can see them rather than destroy them and have a replacement appear who-knows-where?<br /> <br /> <br /> But I'd say my most important piece of advice: More paragraph breaks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T13:27:21-07:00","id":1079023,"title":"","content":"Well, the similarities between the Princesses and the Cold Guard is completely intentional. They are Princesses without the proper lighting, makeup, and inherint supernatural advantage and are ment to have all the right intentions in the world despite the fact their methods are naturally self-destructive. If the Nobles are Belief without Compromise then the Cold Guard is Compromise as their Belief. They are trying to help humanity, they want humans to have the strength and agency to face reality in all of it's darkness and beauty. They tell the junky that if they want to be clean they will help, but it will hurt and they mustn't give up on themselves. That they are beautiful and human, and all they've done wrong is make some bad choices. They Hunt Princesses for the same reason they Hunt Spawn, because despite what a Princes themselves believe their Belief is fragile and they will either die horribly or they will transform into a nightmarish Spawn reflecting the selfishness that lies inherent in all Utopian Ideology. To them the Dethoned are what all Princesses really are, only the one's who've yet to transform still retain the person who became the unwitting vessel of a greedy immortal god-monster. <br /> <br /> I mean, they are blatantly based off the Grey Wardens from Dragon Age: Origins. They can range from noble to selfish, but they are humans who choose to try and fight the darkness given the only tools they're allowed while still retaining their agency as humans. They are antagonists for Princesses and many other Hunters, they are allies to many other Hunters and even some creatures of the night. They are meant to be morally grey protagonists or antagonists who force the players to confront the themes that are presented and make informed decisions for themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T14:22:07-07:00","id":1079043,"title":"","content":"Actually, I thought of a way to make the Stormite Compact their own thing distinct from normal Stormwracked:<br /> <br /> They're not really radical. Okay, in a sense they are, they want to tear apart every single instance of Taint they can find, and piss on the remnants, but what turned them from a normal group of Queen-touched berserks into a functioning Compact was suddenly realizing how much collateral damage they were inflicting. Perhaps, once, the original members grew so ruthless that Tempestra wasn't enough to sterilize the Nest <i>their own actions </i>were forming, and they had a massive wakeup call. Of course, Storms rejected the lily-livered weaklings as soon as she realized their hearts weren't completely sunken in it anymore-but they still believe in her cause. They're just smarter and more cautious about it-and in a sense, more total. They've realized to really kill the Dark, you <i>starve </i>it.<br /> <br /> Thus, what was once a terrorist cell became a hacktivist group. Since their proper leader is/was a fanatical Egyptophile, they call themselves #Ammit, after the demon who eats the hearts of the wicked. Much like the Devourer of the Dead herself, they don't really think of themselves as judges, but as executioners of those deemed by others to be evil, to have been already found &quot;dead inside&quot;-they just make that death total, so as to not pollute the world anymore. And they're <i>very serious </i>about this; if you can't convince at least a large minority of the community that your target is a source of the Dark and still launch a hunt, they will censure you, and you will not like it. As several now incarcerated racist trolls discovered (and keep on discovering, to the point where ferreting out the 3edgy5me &quot;heroes of free speech&quot; to drop the banhammer on is regarded as sport among the accepted members-their infraction forum is called the &quot;Whack-A-Mole Scorecard&quot;), this in particular includes &quot;judgements&quot; that are primarily based on conspiracy theory and prejudice; the reason Ammit is their mascot is that her mix-n-match nature of being a hippo, a lion, and a crocodile echoes the ethnic mishmash of the founders, and the people they recruit; Cults of the Dark prey on the weak, and the weak are often minorities desperate to escape their situations. Once you've convinced them though, the gloves come off and the inner Seraphim come out; #Ammit doesn't just want to stop you, they want to <i>break </i>you. Not kill, although that's usually on the table-fire does wonders for purifying Spawn. But it's not really the Nest themselves they focus on, but the &quot;Children of Apophis&quot;-people whose actions have contributed to Taint, continue to contribute, and will contribute in the future. To really make sure punishment is effective, you need to make them <i>examples.</i> They will find everything there is to an Apophite, and they will slowly, methodically undo everything about them, drag them down, publicize the slow destruction, and with any luck scare any potential Apophites back onto the straight and narrow. &quot;This heart is something the world knows is heavy&quot;, they say. &quot;We are the flooding Nile. Heavy things sink.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ironically, this also means they're relatively pacifist when it comes to monsters. If you're not an Apophite, that means you're innocent until proven guilty. They look up to most Princesses in general, even if they have to suppress a snort at how naive many of them are. This means they often play moderator between the Nobility and other hunters, or other monsters-especially Beasts, since they don't see what the big deal is with the nicer ones (the Princess usually starts listing them, but by that point the Princess is on the ignore list for a while). Of course, the problem with them is, once they've decided you are an Apophite, you're dead to them-it takes a lot of effort to calm their rage, and even then they will never, ever trust you. Compound that with complete derision of people who they see as obstacles of justice (the Polaris Movement has absolutely no sympathy from them-they view concerned parents as a bunch of cowards afraid their little angels get hurt, sort of like actual human beings; better take away their consoles too, there might be violent video games!), and one has a recipe for a group that has no real neutral parties-they are your friends, or they are some type of enemy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T14:39:22-07:00","id":1079050,"title":"","content":"This ^ <br /> <br /> This all the way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Honestly the Stormwracked Compact was the one I was the least interested in, but I think I might have fallen in love with #Ammit. It really helps show in contrast to the Polaris Foundation (and if greenlit as the supplement Conspiracy the Cold Guard) just how divided the Hunter community is regarding the Empaths and Spawn. Excellent work <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar180_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"180\" data-vbnamecard=\"180\">Leliel</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 04-15-2017, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T14:50:52-07:00","id":1079058,"title":"","content":"stormites as Egyptian-themed Anonymous. Me likey","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T14:58:42-07:00","id":1079062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly the Stormwracked Compact was the one I was the least interested in </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I suspected so^^' Nobody exactly rushed to write anything about that one or the Crown Jewels.<br /> <br /> Okay, I'll adopt it then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T16:09:00-07:00","id":1079099,"title":"","content":"Okay, since the Stormwracked are a huge part of #Ammit's backstory, I'll need to add a section for them in the supplement. What needs to be decided, should the hunters actually call them Stormwracked, or use a different term?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T16:51:50-07:00","id":1079115,"title":"","content":"I'd say they're mistaken for Slashers a lot. Like Avengers and Brutes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T17:02:23-07:00","id":1079120,"title":"","content":"Good idea, but I still feel like it might be a good idea to give them a name by Hunters. How about Berserkers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T18:14:17-07:00","id":1079139,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'd have to argue against this. Hunters have a vague understanding of the supernatural creatures at best, and the fact that the Stormwrecked are too close to being just regular humans (just like Sworn) means that most wouldn't register them as anything more than zealous hunters at best and dangerous extremists at worst.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm still riding high on the inspiration right now so I'm working on a Compact and an alternate contender for the Conspiracy slot that's a play on the Crown Jewels idea mentioned. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 04-15-2017, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T18:22:05-07:00","id":1079145,"title":"","content":"Well, I'd say you might be right, but again: the fact #Ammit started out as a Stormwracked Cell kinda forces us to adress what Stormwracked, and by extension Sworns, are. Plus, Hunters do know about ghouls and wolf-blooded, don't they? And finally, I feel there is good potential for paranoia in the Stormwracked from the Hunters' perspective, in that they have to be on the lookout for themselves, for some people among them, or even entire cells, might turn into psychotic vigilantes with radio-active powers...<br /> <br /> <br /> Sooooo I guess the Crown Jewels aren't a popular idea either, then?^^' Still, nice to see you got inspiration. I look forward to see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 04-15-2017, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T18:41:04-07:00","id":1079153,"title":"","content":"For the sworn- maybe just Lesser Princesses? In the same way that Cainites see ghouls as Lesser Vampires? After all the (greater?) Princess apparently get their power from Queens, it's perfectly reasonable to assume it's the same process just with less power behind it.<br /> <br /> (also, unrelated, for a what works and what doesn't- do you think the True Sight of Saint Able could detect a princesses in her human form? I would be inclined to say yes- if it can break through the disguises of the True Fae and the Exarchs/Abyss it can break through that of the Queens- but I am unsure)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","user":"Urbenmyth","date":". 04-15-2017, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T18:49:45-07:00","id":1079158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1079145#post1079145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'd say you might be right, but again: the fact #Ammit started out as a Stormwracked Cell kinda forces us to adress what Stormwracked, and by extension Sworns, are. Plus, Hunters do know about ghouls and wolf-blooded, don't they? And finally, I feel there is good potential for paranoia in the Stormwracked from the Hunters' perspective, in that they have to be on the lookout for themselves, for some people among them, or even entire cells, might turn into psychotic vigilantes with radio-active powers...<br /> <br /> <br /> Sooooo I guess the Crown Jewels aren't a popular idea either, then?^^' Still, nice to see you got inspiration. I look forward to see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That, and the Queen can channel her powers through Stormwracked occasionally, and they have prophetic dreams of her.<br /> <br /> Maybe Vectors? They are essentially hosts for her power to be transferred out into the world after they were &quot;infected&quot; by her essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T18:58:18-07:00","id":1079161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (also, unrelated, for a what works and what doesn't- do you think the True Sight of Saint Able could detect a princesses in her human form? I would be inclined to say yes- if it can break through the disguises of the True Fae and the Exarchs/Abyss it can break through that of the Queens- but I am unsure) </div> </div> </div>Sorry, never read about that Benediction. Could you tell me which book it is from, so I can check by myself?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That, and the Queen can channel her powers through Stormwracked occasionally, and they have prophetic dreams of her.<br /> <br /> Maybe Vectors? They are essentially hosts for her power to be transferred out into the world after they were &quot;infected&quot; by her essence. </div> </div> </div>Aye, pretty hard to miss that.<br /> <br /> That could be a good idea too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T19:03:06-07:00","id":1079165,"title":"","content":"It's in the core book, page 162 (it's actually abel, sorry). In short, it lets a hunter roll to detect whether a given person is supernatural and renders them immune to inbuilt concealment effects of the supernatural, like the sleeping curse, lunacy, the mask, etc (Maybe cover? I honestly don't know. Hmm.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T19:37:28-07:00","id":1079179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1079165#post1079165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's in the core book, page 162 (it's actually abel, sorry). In short, it lets a hunter roll to detect whether a given person is supernatural and renders them immune to inbuilt concealment effects of the supernatural, like the sleeping curse, lunacy, the mask, etc (Maybe cover? I honestly don't know. Hmm.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Princesses have an inherent protection against being identified, but not one from being detected; so True Sight of St. Abel should detect a Princess in her mundane form as supernatural. In fact, given the Benediction's text, it would reveal her type as well. But it wouldn't reveal her transformed identity - it's not designed to do that. At most it could justify an identification attempt, comparing this girl's face to that of known Hopeful in the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T21:30:11-07:00","id":1079219,"title":"","content":"Two ideas: 1 Compact &amp; 1 Conspiracy. Both inspired by the idea that both were created by the Nobility but either quickly or slowly spin out of control and took on a life of their own. <br /> <br /> Excalibur: the Hand of the Crown<br /> <br /> &quot;Don't you see? People like you are the keys to humanity's future. You aren't enemies, you're separate pieces of a puzzle that unlocks the hidden potential in all of us. The enemy is the contagion that would degenerate us all into monstrosities, not each other...&quot;<br /> <br /> Excalibur, or Project: Excalibur, was created by a team of scientists who all had first hand experience with the Nobility in some form. Some were psychically linked to the Empaths in the form of some knightly vow, while others were witnesses or bystandards to some of the tremendous feats of superhuman powers the Nobility are known for. All of them came away from the experience with the same conclusion: these Empaths are the future of humankind, but their own human development and culture is hindering their growth into the perfect humans. <br /> And so, the scientists set out to properly examine and codify the methods and powers of the Nobility in an attempt to discover how a normal human can develop such intricate psychic abilities and deep empathy. But to do that the scientists needed to play to the social ques that Noble society uses to explain their empathetic drive and justify the violence necessary to lessen the psychic trauma from experiencing humany's shared suffering. <br /> So, Excalibur came up with a plan: they would become the advisors and knight errants of the Nobility themselves. Working as one part method spy and one other part field researcher, the Hands would seek out Nobles, earn their trust, and work within their society to discover their secrets and the full extent of their latent powers.<br /> Sounds easy enought right? Well, sadly the project turned out to be far more complicated than that. And surprisingly not from the sheer amount of violence a Noble must become accustomed too either, but instead from said Noble's own society. Apparently the &quot;Courts&quot; are far more fractious and splintered than the Hands originally anticipated. With each &quot;Court&quot; having a code of beliefs that they are unwilling to compromise on and many &quot;Courts&quot; being openly hostile towards one another (three particular one's specifically) it became apparent very quickly that if something wasn't done then the Nobles would spend all of their energy bickering with eachother. <br /> Luckily a solution presented itself fairly quickly, although it was a step that only the most dedicated of the Project could commit too and would shape the nascent Compact to these very night. Something needed to unite the Nobles together in a common cause, and that cause was the threat of the Spawn. So, Excalibur began the heinous but necessary task of cultivating Nests in areas where the Empaths gather together. Then, they would go undercover to offer their services to the Nobility so they could then study them while they fought against the Spawn that they helped cultivate. All in the name of human progress. <br /> <br /> <br /> Magister United: The Merchants of Dreams<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm going to spell this out for you plainly: I'm a rich philanthropist who donates thousands of dollars to cancer research. You're an angst ridden teenager with the power to destroy a small neghborhood. I'm the hero of this story. You're the monster.&quot;<br /> <br /> If there are two emotions that define the human condition, then they must be envy and want. Or, at leasts that's what the Hunters of Magister United believe, and they make it their buisness to provide for those who both covet and desire.<br /> Originally an organization called the Magisters of the Crystal Crown, their entire purpose was to serve as guardians and councilors to a young Noble who believed himself to be the heir to an ancient Queen of Queens. His powers were great but he was so certain of his abilities and divine providence that he was eventually confronted with a threat he couldn't overcome by himself (a vampire lord began converting monetary assets that were originally the Noble's) and rather than compromise with his selfish beliefs he fled like a coward as his servants were fell upon by the vampire's minions. Few Magisters survived that fateful night, but one inparticular who did came to a revelation: a Noble for all their might was bound by the mantle of nobility and were punished on high for breaking said code of ethics, but a human was not. If a human could somehow acquire a Noble's power without the empathetic connection that can cripple a Noble then that human would have the power to change the world...or, make a shit-load of money.<br /> And thus, did that Magister set out to find a way to steal the powers a Noble. And afte years of searching through esoteric texts and occult manuscripts he finally found his answer. He tracked down the Noble who he served so long ago and over drinks he played upon the Noble's vanity and easily re-earned his trust (as the Hunter suspected, the Noble had not changed in any recognizable way beyond simple age.) Over a final toast the Magister drugged the Noble and brought his body to a glass coffins and locked it in golden chains. That night, the Dream Spider came to him and thanked the Magister for returning the &quot;Missing Ward&quot; to her custody. Since he had returned the Noble just as the grimoire had instructed the Dream Spider gave him the Noble's ornate mirrored scepter, and upon awakening the Magister didn't find the magical token but could feel it's power none the less from within himself. Just waiting to be called upon. And thus did the Magister use his new found powers to become filthy rich, and founded the Hunter group that would continue to grow into the Conspiracy that it is to this very night. <br /> Hunters of Magister United are buisness savy men and women who mingle with the rich, make strong political connections, become founders of charity's and other philanthropic ventures, and oh yes...they kidnap Nobles and sell them to the Wardens of the Dreamlands in exchange for a sliver of their Inner Light. <br /> To a Merchant of Dreams the Hunt is both a buisness venture and a means to achieve godhood. To them, the divine powers of the Queens should belong to the merchant class, not spoiled Nobles who are more likely to crash and burn rather than create anything real or long lasting. They are doing humanity a service by stealing the Light for themselves, they're making dreams actually happen. Or, at leasts that what they tell themselves. Either way, the Merchants can wield tremendous political and financial power when on the hunt. And while they primarily hunt the Nobility they are well aware of the other threats in the night and more often than not take action to rid the community of them...unless of course they stand to make a profit by having them around...<br /> <br /> <br /> New Endowment: Usurpation <br /> ~ The Merchants broker with otherworldly dream entities in order to steal the magical powers of the Nobility. By successfully captureing, sedateing, and performing the Rite of Somnus they may being to purches dots in Usurpation. By gaining dots in Usurpation the Hunter also gains a Dread Power related to the Noble they bound and delivered to the Dream Spiders equal or below the total number of dots they possess in Usurpation. These powers are all tied to a Regalia that manifests whenever the Hunter activates the power, although this Regalia is always malformed or twisted in often dream-like ways. Multiple Nobles may be captured by a single Hunter with Usurpation, and for each they may potentially add new Dread Powers whenever they increase their Usurpation dots or when next they perform the Rite of Somnus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T00:48:09-07:00","id":1079281,"title":"","content":"I like where you're going with the Magesters. It reminds me of a scene early in Netflix's Iron Fist where there's a debate about the morality of drug pricing. I particularly liked that the corporate executives weren't portrayed as heartless strawmen but made good points, though I actually felt that Danny could have been given better arguments; maybe a spiritualistic/dentological argument to contrast with the executives consequentialism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1079023#post1079023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the similarities between the Princesses and the Cold Guard is completely intentional.</div> </div> </div> </div> In that case, what are a few examples of the practical differences in the way a Cold Guard and a Princess will act? That needs to be as clearly defined as the similarities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1079023#post1079023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are meant to be morally grey protagonists or antagonists who force the players to confront the themes that are presented and make informed decisions for themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said; it's hard to force players to confront themes with an antagonist who tries to kill them. At first the player would be distracted by trying to survive. Afterwords the antagonist will be dead or imprisoned and unable to force the player to confront anything.<br /> <br /> If the Cold Guard were willing to work alongside Princesses (in a teeth clenthed teamwork situatoin) that would give them a lot more oppotunities to force the Princess' player to confront ideas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1079145#post1079145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'd say you might be right, but again: the fact #Ammit started out as a Stormwracked Cell kinda forces us to adress what Stormwracked, and by extension Sworns, are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait a second. Were Ammit supposed to be Stormwracked or founded by ex-Stormwracked? In interpereted it as the latter, as the Queen of Storms wouldn't convert members of Ammit into Stormwracked if they weren't going out and fighting Darkspawn personally. Also because Sworn of Storms don't gain any powers that are useful outside of combat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1079153#post1079153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(also, unrelated, for a what works and what doesn't- do you think the True Sight of Saint Able could detect a princesses in her human form? I would be inclined to say yes- if it can break through the disguises of the True Fae and the Exarchs/Abyss it can break through that of the Queens- but I am unsure)</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're playing a Princess game - absolutely not. The Dual Identity is a contract between the player and the storyteller: Antagonists cannot go after your mundane life, friends or family, unless you screw up and reveal your identity somehow.<br /> <br /> In a Hunter game: Sure it can.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-16-2017, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T04:11:05-07:00","id":1079320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1079281#post1079281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait a second. Were Ammit supposed to be Stormwracked or founded by ex-Stormwracked? In interpereted it as the latter, as the Queen of Storms wouldn't convert members of Ammit into Stormwracked if they weren't going out and fighting Darkspawn personally. Also because Sworn of Storms don't gain any powers that are useful outside of combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought of them as ex-Stormwracked, as part of the reason they aren't a generic Stormite cell is that they <i>did </i>&quot;compromise&quot;, in her mind-they stopped finding collateral damage acceptable, and started worrying about the solution being worse than the problem (mostly because they realized they could generate Taint, but that's hardly new for humans to only put the breaks on when they realize they're making more problems for themselves). It's also because, as mentioned, #Ammit is mostly a cabal of hackers, community organizers, and occasionally information brokers if they really need the mystical big guns. They don't really engage in fisticuffs.<br /> <br /> Yes, this is a quiet lambasting of how self-destructive Storms is.<br /> <br /> EDIT: They are, however, a stone's throw away from the rage of the Queen herself-I wouldn't be surprised if they have quite a few members with Supernatural Merits, both because of their own Astral proximity to the living storm quietly agitating their own hidden powers and because Cults of the Dark target the kind of people exiled for their power, and #Ammit tends to recruit those victimized by Dark Cults, including ex-members. I don't think that tendency is reliable enough to figure into their Status progression (it's a side effect, not a mystic gift-they'd probably be working on turning into an Endowment if it happened reliably), but it does figure into their more open attitude towards monsters; they know how close they are to being monsters themselves, and that a lot of the time, &quot;monsters&quot; are just people with strange powers and strange needs. That's part of why I noted why they have a low opinion of Stormfront types who want to corrupt their community into yet another facet of the Internet Hate Machine, and why they have a neutral opinion on Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 04-16-2017, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T04:35:28-07:00","id":1079327,"title":"","content":"Jesus.... there have been a lot of posts while I was asleep. Let me see if I can answer them...<br /> <br /> @Duskage: Soooo, are Excalibur meant to replace the Crown Jewels, or be a separate faction? I'm still not sure about that part.<br /> <br /> I gotta admit, the Merchant of Dreams are a creepy and great idea. Involving the Wardens actually is a good way to make use of elements from Princesses. Congratulation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wait a second. Were Ammit supposed to be Stormwracked or founded by ex-Stormwracked? In interpereted it as the latter, as the Queen of Storms wouldn't convert members of Ammit into Stormwracked if they weren't going out and fighting Darkspawn personally. Also because Sworn of Storms don't gain any powers that are useful outside of combat. </div> </div> </div>... I admit I am not really sure anymore at this point. The orginal idea was to make them just a Stormwracked group who happens to be better organized than most, but the whole #Ammit thing seems to have gone for making them founded by former Stormwracked instead. Which I admit makes them more interesting and their own thing compared to Stormwracked, but at the same time, if they aren't Stormwracked anymore, then what will their Status advantages/possible Endowments be?<br /> <br /> But my point still stand: weither #Ammit started out as defecting Stormwracked or still are Stormwracked, in either case the existence of Sworns needs to be adressed.<br /> <br /> Though since you bring up the topic, I admit I always got confused about that part in the game: <i>what</i> powers do Sworn have, exactly? My understanding based on the book is, they have access to Wisps, Practical Magic and Invocations, but not Charms. But thing is, what can they use their Invocation for if they don't have Charms? Or does this mean their Invocation only becomes useful when they have Bequests?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you're playing a Princess game - absolutely not. The Dual Identity is a contract between the player and the storyteller: Antagonists cannot go after your mundane life, friends or family, unless you screw up and reveal your identity somehow.<br /> <br /> In a Hunter game: Sure it can. </div> </div> </div>How about a compromise? The power DOES kinda works, but for starter it causes a Clash of Will. Moreover, from what I understand, none of the two forms a Princess has actually are a disguise, but rather two different identities, both being very real. Maybe it allows to recognize a Princess' mundane form as having supernatural potential, but not to identitfy her as the same person without the usual roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 04-16-2017, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T04:48:47-07:00","id":1079329,"title":"","content":"I think the Anti Child soldier group, might do better, with something Similar to advanced armory.with advanced pharmacuticals etc, then using the powers of darkness...<br /> <br /> just my 2 cents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T05:53:05-07:00","id":1079340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I admit I am not really sure anymore at this point. The orginal idea was to make them just a Stormwracked group who happens to be better organized than most, but the whole #Ammit thing seems to have gone for making them founded by former Stormwracked instead. Which I admit makes them more interesting and their own thing compared to Stormwracked, but at the same time, if they aren't Stormwracked anymore, then what will their Status advantages/possible Endowments be?<br /> <br /> But my point still stand: weither #Ammit started out as defecting Stormwracked or still are Stormwracked, in either case the existence of Sworns needs to be adressed.<br /> <br /> Though since you bring up the topic, I admit I always got confused about that part in the game: <i>what</i> powers do Sworn have, exactly? My understanding based on the book is, they have access to Wisps, Practical Magic and Invocations, but not Charms. But thing is, what can they use their Invocation for if they don't have Charms? Or does this mean their Invocation only becomes useful when they have Bequests?</div> </div> </div> </div>Weren't they a Compact, and don't really have an Endowment to start with?<br /> <br /> Nevermind. From my reading, Sworn Invocations are largely mute points without their Bequests, but Invocations have one other trait you missed-they are a potential Willpower source. If your actions during a scene are in line with one of your Invocations, and have not broken the Ban, you can roll your dots-every success is a Willpower point refreshed. Admittedly, Sworn don't have many dots, but it's not completely useless for them.<br /> <br /> Stormwracked get the short end of the stick-because so many of them are Sworn to the Queen Herself, it's not uncommon for them to lack Bequests, since she has a hard time making those, and her Princesses can't keep up with the demand. They have their Mystery Cult Initiation, the ability to channel the Queen (at a significant hazard to their health) and Golneau patronage instead.<br /> <br /> Of course, that doesn't mean there isn't a market for paranoia horror caused by realizing the Lady of Cleansing Fires whispers to people who are <i>just that angry.</i> She doesn't tempt-she promises. All she wants you to do is continue pursuing revenge, continue to purge the Dark-and to make sure your unenlightened brethren don't get in the way of justice. Falling to her influence isn't a drop, it's a sideways step, and nobody notices-not until the clay cyborg is tearing through their flesh because the proper cell the Stormwracked is a part of has become an obstacle, and the Golneau needs a body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T06:49:08-07:00","id":1079350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1079320#post1079320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, this is a quiet lambasting of how self-destructive Storms is.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, it's not like self-destructive isn't the core theme and mechanical drawback to Storms <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Though Storms are a very effective at taking down Taint and Darkspawn, because magic. In the real world their attitude usually does more harm than good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1079320#post1079320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's part of why I noted why they have a low opinion of Stormfront types who want to corrupt their community into yet another facet of the Internet Hate Machine, and why they have a neutral opinion on Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't they already be part of the Internet Hate Machine. They specialise in tearing down and destroying people's lives, there's not much you can do to sugar coat that. Besides, Hate is a signature emotion of Storms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1079327#post1079327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But thing is, what can they use their Invocation for if they don't have Charms? Or does this mean their Invocation only becomes useful when they have Bequests?</div> </div> </div> </div> Leliel has it right. Sworn's use their Invocations for Bequests and Willpower. (And for generating Wisps if you're Sworn of Storms)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1079327#post1079327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">from what I understand, none of the two forms a Princess has actually are a disguise, but rather two different identities, both being very real.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. Think of them as having identical nature but different nurture. The Transformed identitiy is who the Princess would have been if she grew up in different circumstances.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T09:51:59-07:00","id":1079415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1079350#post1079350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't they already be part of the Internet Hate Machine. They specialise in tearing down and destroying people's lives, there's not much you can do to sugar coat that. Besides, Hate is a signature emotion of Storms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said they weren't. They're just self-aware about it-and terrified of becoming a subset of Stormfront, 8chan, and all the other communities founded largely on prejudice, rather than the right things to be angry about. Because racism (and sexism-this is a group that used to work for the <i>Queen </i>of Storms) sucks.<br /> <br /> Also, if they do have an Endowment, I have a suggestion-they remember how Golneau Grafts work, and while they can't use those anymore lest their new arms start shooting everything that moves due to having just given up on the Ban, they did figure out the occult engineering behind how flesh and clay can be merged. More importantly, how they can use ritually sanctified information technology instead of Golneau Numina. Yes, most of it isn't a part of <i>them, </i>but #Ammit has learned how those three traits working as one can make them capable of hacking reality instead of just computers. Actual hacking, mind, so they can't just play around with a laptop and set all doors to &quot;open sez me&quot;-they need a &quot;password&quot;, occult permission to do so, and that usually requires social engineering (ie, calling the superintendent and pretending to be a lost guard looking for a key). But beyond that? They can install spyware in a mundane window, spoof being a friend of their target to disguise themselves, make a protest into a metaphysical DDOS attack that imposes a penalty anything that was protested working right, and link their minds into a telepathic botnet. In game terms, Chimeric Hacking is based around Preparation-they have to scheme and nudge to even set up their powers, but once that happens, #Ammit is essentially capable of reality warping. Think Unknown Armies with how adepts need mundane things to charge up and release their spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 04-16-2017, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T10:16:13-07:00","id":1079423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1079415#post1079415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never said they weren't. They're just self-aware about it-and terrified of becoming a subset of Stormfront, 8chan, and all the other communities founded largely on prejudice, rather than the right things to be angry about. Because racism (and sexism-this is a group that used to work for the <i>Queen </i>of Storms) sucks.<br /> <br /> Also, if they do have an Endowment, I have a suggestion-they remember how Golneau Grafts work, and while they can't use those anymore lest their new arms start shooting everything that moves due to having just given up on the Ban, they did figure out the occult engineering behind how flesh and clay can be merged. More importantly, how they can use ritually sanctified information technology instead of Golneau Numina. Yes, most of it isn't a part of <i>them, </i>but #Ammit has learned how those three traits working as one can make them capable of hacking reality instead of just computers. Actual hacking, mind, so they can't just play around with a laptop and set all doors to &quot;open sez me&quot;-they need a &quot;password&quot;, occult permission to do so, and that usually requires social engineering (ie, calling the superintendent and pretending to be a lost guard looking for a key). But beyond that? They can install spyware in a mundane window, spoof being a friend of their target to disguise themselves, make a protest into a metaphysical DDOS attack that imposes a penalty anything that was protested working right, and link their minds into a telepathic botnet. In game terms, Chimeric Hacking is based around Preparation-they have to scheme and nudge to even set up their powers, but once that happens, #Ammit is essentially capable of reality warping. Think Unknown Armies with how adepts need mundane things to charge up and release their spells.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very nice, though that sounds more Demon, or perhaps Mage, themed than Princess. How are you deriving the powers from the Princess (especially Storms) based source?<br /> <br /> What about limiting it to various on the Aggressive Meme Numina, and derivatives of the concept of &quot;Infectious Hate&quot;? They can make viewers of their messages/meme's into an impromptu protest/angry mob, and possibly even extend that into technology itself &quot;hating&quot; the target?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-16-2017, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T10:34:08-07:00","id":1079428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1079423#post1079423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Very nice, though that sounds more Demon, or perhaps Mage, themed than Princess. How are you deriving the powers from the Princess (especially Storms) based source?<br /> <br /> What about limiting it to various on the Aggressive Meme Numina, and derivatives of the concept of &quot;Infectious Hate&quot;? They can make viewers of their messages/meme's into an impromptu protest/angry mob, and possibly even extend that into technology itself &quot;hating&quot; the target?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Much better plan. I was trying to figure out how Tempestra's theme of destructive artifice could be translated to a more computer-based form. The original idea was emphasizing the anarchist bit, but manipulating memes? Much better plan.<br /> <br /> New idea: #Ammit's Endowment is based around &quot;reality viruses&quot;, infectious memes and the like. The core ability is to plant an idea that something is Wrong and Should Be Opposed and watch it grow, but other power ideas are getting technology itself to turn against the target (it shares in #Ammit's opinion of you), preternatural skill with research (the beginning and end of hacking, really), and the aforementioned Protest DDOS attack. I can even think of names: Sekhmet's Roar (infectious meme), Scorn of Ptah (tech hates you), Thoth Macro (research buff), Denial of Set (protest DDOS-he's the god of outsiders, and the idea behind Denial of Service is a bunch of outsiders getting in the way of business) and Meretseger Firewall (misleads investigators away from their real identities-the very fact they developed that is a sign they're not pure Stormwracked).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 04-16-2017, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T10:45:25-07:00","id":1079430,"title":"","content":"Several things.<br /> <br /> 1) Thanks for the complements about Magister United. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> They've quickly grown to tie my love of the Cold Guard, so now I'm not sure what to focus on. <br /> <br /> 2) In regards to the Cold Guard you make some good points <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a>, I still think they should hunt Princesses as part of their twisted belief that all Princesses are already Dethroned, most are just time bombs waiting to go off, but they should be very self aware of what they are doing. I think they can be altered to first try and turn the Princesses away from the service of their Court, appearing as allies that want to preserve their humanity and agency for as long as possible. It only when they refuse, or slip too far down the rabbit hole that they actively hunt them. The former should be nightmarish from the Princesses' point of view, while the latter is darkly rememicent of when they mercy kill their own members when the Fading grows too great and there's no longer a chance of them recovering. <br /> <br /> 3) Both Excalibur and Magister United were inspired by the Crown Jewels but evolved into something else entirely. Honestly Magister United is much more solid than Excalibur in my own opinion.<br /> <br /> 4) If I put my two cents in for #Ammit, I'd say they work best as a Compact without an Endowment. Giving them a superpower kinda takes away the sheer horror of what they can do to you just with a laptop and your address.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 04-16-2017, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T10:48:40-07:00","id":1079431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1079430#post1079430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) If I put my two cents in for #Ammit, I'd say they work best as a Compact without an Endowment. Giving them a superpower kinda takes away the sheer horror of what they can do to you just with a laptop and your address.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I agree with you. They're not combat monsters, they're a bunch of researchers with a grudge-and all the fury of the world wide web behind them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T11:13:06-07:00","id":1079439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1079430#post1079430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) If I put my two cents in for #Ammit, I'd say they work best as a Compact without an Endowment. Giving them a superpower kinda takes away the sheer horror of what they can do to you just with a laptop and your address.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Though I usually like to give Compacts something, even if not a full Endowment (such as Rituals that they have access to, or specialized equipment, but others might acquire as well - nothing as fully fleshed out as an Endowment, just a little something in-theme to give them an edge).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar180_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"180\" data-vbnamecard=\"180\">Leliel</a> Maybe convert those &quot;hacks&quot; into Tactics? Such as Sekhmet's Roar being group members doing some psychological profiling upon a &quot;target&quot; group, then the rest seeding memes, reports, and &quot;fake news&quot; designed to trigger said group's rage-button (and get them angry toward another target in question). Technically any Internet-savvy group of Hunters could pull it off, but it is one of #Ammit's specialty Tactics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":".  Example 04-16-2017, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T11:14:58-07:00","id":1079440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1079439#post1079439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True. Though I usually like to give Compacts something, even if not a full Endowment (such as Rituals that they have access to, or specialized equipment, but others might acquire as well - nothing as fully fleshed out as an Endowment, just a little something in-theme to give them an edge).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar180_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"180\" data-vbnamecard=\"180\">Leliel</a> Maybe convert those &quot;hacks&quot; into Tactics?</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't a bad plan-of course, it's mundane social engineering then, but that's the point-with the occasional Open Rite (Mummy term, refers to magic anyone can do like exorcisms).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T11:26:50-07:00","id":1079445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1079440#post1079440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That isn't a bad plan-of course, it's mundane social engineering then, but that's the point-with the occasional Open Rite (Mummy term, refers to magic anyone can do like exorcisms).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sure. #Ammit might use that old Golneau lore to craft a special server (one component to an Open Rite) that simply lets them perform Social Maneuvering against target Technology Spirits (not that they'd know exactly what it is doing, merely that it works). The mechanics, obviously, would be simplified to a mere Condition or Tilts, though. No need to make things too complicated (I just like coming up with plausible in-universe explanations).<br /> <br /> Hmm. On that note... Maybe Denial of Set invokes the Ghosts of all those wronged by the target, making their electronics (at least) Open to a mass haunting. Heh, try tracing those IP addresses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-16-2017, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T13:21:40-07:00","id":1079485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Leliel has it right. Sworn's use their Invocations for Bequests and Willpower. (And for generating Wisps if you're Sworn of Storms) </div> </div> </div>Wait, you can use your Invocations for willpower?! I don't remember reading anything about this in the Dream version...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T13:40:42-07:00","id":1079496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1079485#post1079485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, you can use your Invocations for willpower?! I don't remember reading anything about this in the Dream version...</div> </div> </div> </div>It is under the &quot;Invocations&quot; section of Chapter 3, on page 102 of the Dream version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13233-rougemephilesclone","name":"RougeMephilesClone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T14:07:15-07:00","id":1079509,"title":"","content":"Ah, yes, just found the section. Thanks^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T17:52:07-07:00","id":1079590,"title":"","content":"Well, the Crown Jewels now have their full entry, with only their Endowment missing. We are now at 3 new Compacts and 2 New Conspiracies. Not to mention I started the mechanics to play Princesses and Creatures of the Darkness in Hunter rules. This week has really been productive^^<br /> <br /> The Merchant of Dream entry still needs to be completed and prepared, but after that, I would say the new Compact and Conspiracies part of the Supplement is pretty complete, meaning we will be able to start focusing on the rest.<br /> <br /> On a note, I can't help but wonder: are the Merchant of Dream inspired from the Promethean Brotherhood in Witchfinders?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T18:22:02-07:00","id":1079601,"title":"","content":"So, what simplified mechanics encapsulate Princess abilities? The generic toughness Dread Powers should cover Holy Shield. What others? The powers are somewhat diverse...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T18:35:21-07:00","id":1079606,"title":"","content":"I already started writing down these mechanics. You can go check them on the document^^ So far I tried creating Dread Powers primarly for the basics, like Levinbolt or Kensai.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T18:42:36-07:00","id":1079608,"title":"","content":"Though, you know what we need for Philly's own monstrous foes, because the city is a goddamned death trap in the CofD?<br /> <br /> A Hunter Cataphract. With special traits, to show this is something outside the Nobility's expertise.<br /> <br /> <b>Ben Vold, the Delaware Draug</b><br /> <br /> Quote: <i>You face the rage of the betrayed, little candle. Let my ship through, or be trawled in the dark seas it sails, as your body joins its crew.</i><br /> <br /> Hunters in Philly's ports, for the past two years, have increasingly three bits of advice for any peer nearby the two rivers-if you happen to be sailing the Delaware at night, keep an eye out for a towboat, painted black and blue with rusted paint, with two lights on either side, one flickering white, one solid blue, on each side, lighting the river like four eyes. If you see no boats, keep at least one buddy on watch at all times, because that's when it sneaks up on you, not emerging from the gap between the living world and the dead until it's nearly too late-if not completely too late, because you were stupid enough to not rig your boat for speed. This contemporary ghost ship, the <i>Ran, </i>is from the modern day, but her captain certainly isn't, nor is her crew. They say that a cell of amateur hunters, high on cocaine and too many pirate movies, got it into their heads to be Vigilant pirates, cutting the seas in search of monsters and various treasures the sea-going beasts had to have. Their first target was fossilized longship with a ghostly Viking spirit attached that they were sure had to be the source of several sea-based nightmares around its native museum, and so when it was being transported for demonstration on a cargo ship, the brave, stupid crew of the <i>Ran </i>struck, using speedboats launched from their houseboat/base to strike at a poor ship filled with people who had no fucking clue why all these pirates were ransacking something from a university. As one might imagine, they killed the crew to cover their tracks-which ended up awakening the formerly sleeping spirit of an ancient Norse nobleman who was peacefully dozing the eons away-as well as his entire cohort of warriors. Enraged at the dishonorable curs who dared called themselves warriors of justice, he and his men possessed the bodies of the cargo tanker's crew and slaughtered the hunters to a man, before commandeering their ship and sailing back to their home to ensure no kin of those cowards would disgrace the name of bravery again. If they catch you, say the hunters, they won't listen to your protestations of bravery, thinking it just a cowardly attempt at pleading for your life; if you're very stalwart, and very lucky, they <i>might </i>instead merely test you, letting you go free with merely a warning to never sail again and blaspheme the gods with your presence on the sea. If you fail, or you're not, well there aren't any stories from those survivors, shall we say.<br /> <br /> As one might imagine, this takes a real thing and attaches a story which is complete and total dreck, and the fact that people are alive to tell it is probably proof of its bullshit, given how it makes several assumptions about Old Icelandic culture the undead jarl would probably find very offensive. There <i>is </i>a rusty old towboat sailing the Delaware, but it's not Twilight it dips in and out of-it's the Dark World. And it's captain is indeed a monstrous warrior of the sea, but he's just as modern as the <i>Ran </i>itself, and he <i>was </i>the original hunter captain. And while he did fall to his own recklessness, it wasn't some irate medieval warrior which did him in, but his own grief.<br /> <br /> Before he became the Delaware Draug, Ben Vold (which is itself an alias-he neither remembers nor cares for his original name) was a captain in a more terrestrial sense, the CO of several Task Force VALKYRIE cells near Philadelphia. He was, by all accounts, a stand-up, brave, and competent officer who his subordinates respected, though not to the point of love. Really, he was more a specialist in logistics than anything, making sure all the Advanced Armory requests arrived reasonably late and that all the ammo was stocked. Still, he was no coward, and he could fight on the frontlines as well as any of his subordinates. But it wasn't his first choice, not the least because unlike far too many hunters, he had a happy home life, not the least because his family was aware of him working on dangerous, long-term missions for the government that he couldn't really talk about. His children were fine sorts too, all very involved with the world and with their father's boundless idealism well-represented.<br /> <br /> The story of how the future Vold ended up killing his family is heavily classified and spun as far as VALKYRIE can while still not verging on total lie. The basic gist though, is that Vold was assigned to the grim duty of neutralizing a Noble in service to their well-intentioned invasion, this one a Hearts witch attempting to enforce her Queen's decrees on local politics. Due to a series of tragic mistakes, misadventures, a broken cell phone and sheer laziness from unrelated building inspectors, the college dorm where said Princess was staying was completely destroyed in a fireball as Vold looked on in horror as his wife and other two children sat down with his eldest daughter for Easter dinner. VALKYRIE's legion of shrinks tried all they could to put the captain's mind back together, but by that point, he had lost all faith in his comrades, his country, or himself. While he seemed to recover some will to live, this was an illusion-what the psychologists thought was him becoming functional was really just the fires of hate giving him enough will to snap himself out of catatonia long enough to lure every one of his men and the support apparatus for said mission onto a then-normal towboat, before blowing the boiler and locking all of them inside the flooding cabins. The last person to meet the churning waves was himself, a sound that could have been laughter, screaming, or sobbing escaping his throat as the waters of the Delaware washed in.<br /> <br /> <i>Something </i>came with the waters. The researchers into the Dark Spawn's origins, should they find out about his origin, would be divided as to whether this was raw Dark drawn by his despair and madness to swamp what little remained of sanity in his soul and weaponize his rage, an alien parasite born of the same and performing one last indignity on his corpse, or something in between. Whatever the case is, the newly-rechristened <i>Ran </i>somehow, impossibly, sank in reverse a few nights later, the bodies of the people killed in that initial drowning merged and mixed in every unclean manner with examples of life at the bottom of lakebeds and the deep sea, all giving ululating praise to their captain-the only one among them that remained somewhat humanlike, at least on the outside. Inside, the Delaware Draug's mind has been twisted into something almost completely unrecognizable as having once been a human, a mishmash of the man he was, the Darkness incarnate he is, and half-remembered gargles of Norse mythology, born from idle curiosity of how VALKYRIE named its weapons leading to a minor hobby. To what passes for Ben Vold's mind, he is the hand of Hel, sent to gather the dishonored dead to make war on the living-and from there, the Aesir themselves on the fields of Ragnarok to smother the new world in its crib, and that all may remain dead and free of grief of being alive when those loved are not.<br /> <br /> The reason he choses hunters to make into the dishonored dead is far more personal, however; Vold has not forgotten the recklessness of the Vigil that led to his creation, and so he hates his former peers for that reason-but really, it's because he can't stand to be reminded of what he lost. The &quot;tests&quot; have nothing to do with worthiness-in fact, he's looking for people that <i>fail</i>, and in so doing, lose things that force them to understand his pain. Everyone else reminds him too bitterly of the nobility and bravery he once had before that fatal Easter, and how they might have been stronger than he was, or luckier, or smarter, or a thousand other things. These hunters must be dragged down to his level, to be forced into dishonorable death, in the same way-he drowns them, pincers and fin-hands holding them in a specialized compartment of the <i>Ran </i>that fills with gallons and gallons of river-water on command.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately for everyone, he's right on one particular thing-those who drowns and buries in silt, he finds, do indeed rise again, and join his darkling crew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 04-16-2017, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T18:57:39-07:00","id":1079620,"title":"","content":".... Love it. Again, I love the fact it creates a connection between Princess and Hunters, and take advantage on the fact TFV has bad relationships with Nobles. Plus, it's ambiguous enough that Princess fans can recognize a Cataphract while Hunter fans will see it as some mysterious Dark entity.<br /> <br /> Now all we need is a profile for him gameplay-wise...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T19:52:56-07:00","id":1079643,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar180_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"180\" data-vbnamecard=\"180\">Leliel</a> Nailed it.<br /> <br /> However, there's one last lore question before we can really move on to the mechanical nitty-gritty.<br /> <br /> What's his Transformation?<br /> <br /> The Draug seems pretty well stocked up on minions, and he has a clear Homefield Advantage if he can get you inside <i>Ran</i>. So... perhaps, to gain more power in a pinch, he needs to sacrifice all of it, fusing with at least his entire current crew and/or part of his boat to pound his most hated enemies into sand with devastating blows.<br /> <br /> Or he could just turn into a big ol' demonic sea monster thing. Probably with tentacles, as he dragged his crew down with him in life.<br /> <br /> Either way, any cells taking on this guy are in for a big surprise if they think all they're getting is Davy Jones. Cataphractoi are always dangerous, but that's a dial they can turn up to eleven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13233-rougemephilesclone","user":"RougeMephilesClone","date":". 04-16-2017, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13233-rougemephilesclone","name":"RougeMephilesClone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T21:58:43-07:00","id":1079679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RougeMephilesClone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1079643#post1079643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar180_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"180\" data-vbnamecard=\"180\">Leliel</a> Nailed it.<br /> <br /> However, there's one last lore question before we can really move on to the mechanical nitty-gritty.<br /> <br /> What's his Transformation?<br /> <br /> The Draug seems pretty well stocked up on minions, and he has a clear Homefield Advantage if he can get you inside <i>Ran</i>. So... perhaps, to gain more power in a pinch, he needs to sacrifice all of it, fusing with at least his entire current crew and/or part of his boat to pound his most hated enemies into sand with devastating blows.<br /> <br /> Or he could just turn into a big ol' demonic sea monster thing. Probably with tentacles, as he dragged his crew down with him in life.<br /> <br /> Either way, any cells taking on this guy are in for a big surprise if they think all they're getting is Davy Jones. Cataphractoi are always dangerous, but that's a dial they can turn up to eleven.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, the first idea (devour minions to Transform) is better-it fits with his theme of murder-suicide and the fundamental contempt he actually feels towards the people who he makes his crew from. <br /> <br /> It also explains why people haven't noticed he turns into a fish-ship-crab-Cthulhu-thingy; even beyond the loss of ego, he has to start drowning people all over again to recoup his losses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T06:49:15-07:00","id":1079771,"title":"","content":"On a note, I came up with this quote for the supplement. Mind to give an opinion?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>You know, many people I met thought these so-called \u201cNobles\u201d were a joke. I get it, I really do. In fact, I used to think like this. After all, when you have faced blood-sucking corpses, men who turn into cannibalistic wolf-men, or walking nightmares disguised as people, how are you supposed to take sparkly little girls in superhero suits seriously? That just doesn\u2019t sound as scary\u2026</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>But then I actually met one.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>It all started like any other day, as we were interrogating some guy about one of his friends we suspected of being a vampire. Our leader was in a bad mood, and getting paranoid, so he started beating him up.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>And then, she shew up. She look young, barely than seventeen. She was wearing a flashy, red and pink dress with laces, and her hair were dyed to look like flames. At first, the others thought she was just some kid who got lost, and tried to make her leave nicely. They completely changed their attitude when she raised her hand, and a longsword appeared out of nowhere between her fingers.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The guys panicked, and started to shoot. She began moving so fast we could barely see her, dodging the bullets without breaking a sweat. When a few lucky shot actually got her, she would defect them with some sort of shiny barrier. Then she lighted that friggin\u2019 sword on fire and started slashing through us. None of us died, weirdly, but it barely took her more than a few seconds to make all of us bite the dust. Twelve trained men with guns and kevlar vests, taken down by a teenage girl in a mini-dress with an oversized knife.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>When we woke up, we found our leader beaten to a pulp with severe burnt, and the prisoner gone. All she left behind was a message, written on the wall of our safehouse with the edge of her blade: \u201cStay away from my friends\u201d. We went to check everyone in the guy\u2019s inner circle, his girlfriend, his sister, anyone in the neighborhood, but we couldn\u2019t find who she was.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>That was how I learnt to not underestimate Nobles. They might look all rainbow and sunshine, but that Light they keep rambling about? Yeah, it really gives them power. And when you give them reason to unleash that power on you, they are fuckin\u2019 terrifying.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>-Samuel Stone, veteran Hunter.</i></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T14:29:45-07:00","id":1080558,"title":"","content":"Well, no answer, but judging by the likes, at least some persons enjoyed it^^'<br /> <br /> Anyway, the Magister United (renamed Magister of the Economie) entry is completed.<br /> <br /> I'm planning to add your character to the doc with your permission, Lelial. Would you rather let us design his profile, or take care of it yourself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T14:34:07-07:00","id":1080560,"title":"","content":"Oh, will definitely check out the write up (not sure how I feel about the name change but I'll reserve my opinions until I see the full write up.)<br /> <br /> In retrospect I did subconsciously draw from the Promethean Brotherhood a little, so rewriting the exact process of how they bargain with the Wardens might be the right way to go with that.<br /> <br /> EDIT: No, it's perfect. Just finished reading through the Compacts and Conspiracies section and...it all perfect. Not only are the ideas presented in a refined and polished manner, but they all have plot points and hooks that drives the reader's imagination into overdrive. There is nothing more I can add that hasn't already been either added or refined. All I can say is...to all contributors and to our project leader, thank you and it's a privilege to work on this project with you all. :,)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  So...beautiful... 04-18-2017, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T18:03:55-07:00","id":1080666,"title":"","content":"I am glad you like it so much^^ I have always been a big fan of World-building, so I put a lot of effort into making this supplement a mean to marry the two gamelines in a way that would integrate the Nobles to the larger New World of Darkness. I am glad my efforts paid off, especially since some of the entries were difficult to do^^<br /> <br /> If you still wish to help, though, #Ammit doesn't have subfactions nor a Status merit. If you got any idea for that, feel free to suggest^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T19:10:28-07:00","id":1080700,"title":"","content":"I think I'll leave #Ammit to Leliel since they got that Compact super down. I did come up with an idea for a Tactic based around targeting and decreasing a Nest's power through community and combined mourning (might be good to use against Hauntings and Wounds too, will come up with a proper write up later.)<br /> <br /> Also, special shout out to the contributor who perfected the Cold Guard. It's final version is everything I wanted out of the Conspiracy and more. I tip my hat to you. *tips hat*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T19:48:30-07:00","id":1080708,"title":"","content":"An Advanced Armory! What do people think?<br /> <br /> <b>The Sunna Box (3 dots)</b><br /> <br /> While the equaliser grenade deals with the physically shape-shifting, not all creatures need to physically change to hide. Princesses are impossible to identify, Changelings and Prometheans look human and demons wear lives like masks. To counter these potentially devastating powers, R&amp;D created the Sunna Box. A metallic cube of classified nature, the device emits carefully modulated light beams that &quot;interface with human brainwaves, countering paranormal effects that hide information&quot;. It sounds handwavey, and the grunts are fairly sure the higher-ups are hiding something. But it works, and if there are any side-effects no-one's complained yet.<br /> <br /> Once activated, the Sunna Boxes' oddly-hued flickering light fills around 60ft. Anything under that light loses any passive powers that hide their identity. Most notably, Princesses no longer have the mental block that keeps others from connecting their two identities. Any action under the light is seen can be remembered as the mundane identity's doing (assuming the hunters know the mundane identity, of course). In addition, promethean deformities and changeling miens are visible, and a demon's true mechanical form can be seen*. Other monsters are affected in similar ways. Active attempts to supernaturally hide a monsters identity, such as The Familiar Stranger or Contracts of the Mirror, take a -2 penalty in the area and must be rerolled upon entering.<br /> <br /> The power only works on illusions and mental effects- it does nothing to stop physical transformation, nor does it stop mundane disguise attempts.<br /> <br /> *note the demon still <i>has</i> cover- they just look like their demonic form. They have neither the penalties nor benefits of going loud, and if they decide to so while in the light they can do so normally.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T19:59:12-07:00","id":1080712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1080708#post1080708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Advanced Armory! What do people think?<br /> <br /> <b>The Sunna Box (3 dots)</b><br /> <br /> While the equaliser grenade deals with the physically shape-shifting, not all creatures need to physically change to hide. Princesses are impossible to identify, Changelings and Prometheans look human and demons wear lives like masks. To counter these potentially devastating powers, R&amp;D created the Sunna Box. A metallic cube of classified nature, the device emits carefully modulated light beams that &quot;interface with human brainwaves, countering paranormal effects that hide information&quot;. It sounds handwavey, and the grunts are fairly sure the higher-ups are hiding something. But it works, and if there are any side-effects no-one's complained yet.<br /> <br /> Once activated, the Sunna Boxes' oddly-hued flickering light fills around 60ft. Anything under that light loses any passive powers that hide their identity. Most notably, Princesses no longer have the mental block that keeps others from connecting their two identities. Any action under the light is seen can be remembered as the mundane identity's doing (assuming the hunters know the mundane identity, of course). In addition, promethean deformities and changeling miens are visible, and a demon's true mechanical form can be seen*. Other monsters are affected in similar ways. Active attempts to supernaturally hide a monsters identity, such as The Familiar Stranger or Contracts of the Mirror, take a -2 penalty in the area and must be rerolled upon entering.<br /> <br /> The power only works on illusions and mental effects- it does nothing to stop physical transformation, nor does it stop mundane disguise attempts.<br /> <br /> *note the demon still <i>has</i> cover- they just look like their demonic form. They have neither the penalties nor benefits of going loud, and if they decide to so while in the light they can do so normally.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Cover breach might be a bit much. At least Bear Mace needs to hit the correct target - it isn't a field.<br /> <br /> What about a field that reacts with current supernatural effects (including disguise powers) like a blacklight. Maybe it reacts to spent fuel stats?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-18-2017, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T20:09:42-07:00","id":1080715,"title":"","content":"The point of the cover breach is that it's only apparent to humans- to the G-M the demon's still in their human cover- but I get your point, I was worried it was a little too powerful. I was thinking of making it so, as a light, it is affected by other sources of light (i.e. use it in the dakr it works perfectly, use it at midday it does nothing because it's blocked out) but I was unsure how to implement that? Probably giving the monster a saving throw","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T20:11:17-07:00","id":1080716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1080712#post1080712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about a field that reacts with current supernatural effects (including disguise powers) like a blacklight. Maybe it reacts to spent fuel stats?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is probably a better plan, actually, although it would need some help to get through the princess' dual identity, which was the original purpose.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T20:12:23-07:00","id":1080717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1080700#post1080700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'll leave #Ammit to Leliel since they got that Compact super down. I did come up with an idea for a Tactic based around targeting and decreasing a Nest's power through community and combined mourning (might be good to use against Hauntings and Wounds too, will come up with a proper write up later.)<br /> <br /> Also, special shout out to the contributor who perfected the Cold Guard. It's final version is everything I wanted out of the Conspiracy and more. I tip my hat to you. *tips hat*</div> </div> </div> </div>First, I'm a guy, but thanks for the gender-neutral things.<br /> <br /> Second, off the top of my head, #Ammit Status is less of increasing initiation and more like a very specialized Fame Merit; it's gained by, when it comes down to it, showing off your Mad Skillz (tm) in a competently spectacular manner. Humiliating and discrediting an Apophite by publishing how he cheated on his wife? Good. Revealing said information via a music video/sex tape replacing the gallery of memories at the wedding anniversary, and the mistress is wearing a costume that blatantly resembles the Apophite's biological sister? Much better. Videotape all of that and then show the reaction anonymously to the board of directors thinking about buying his company from him, derailing the deal and ensuring he gets bankrupt? The question is not whether they'll trip over themselves buying you drinks, the question is, given how gender-and-sexuality-open #Ammit prides itself on being, &quot;When you said 'have my babies', how many of you were being serious?&quot;<br /> <br /> A set of benefits might go:<br /> <br /> * You've convinced the moderators that you believe in the cause, and you hate the Darkness as much as they do. As a sign of their faith in you, they've taught you some of their tricks when it comes to hacking, and put you in contact with a couple of your more exoerienced peers. You gain a free Specialty in Computers or Crafts relating to modifying or hacking into information technology, and a one dot Contact (#Ammit) Merit.<br /> <br /> *** &quot;We are the flood&quot; is the motto of #Ammit, and someone at this level of trust, authority, and chutzpah knows how to irrigate it. You gain the Sekhmet's Roar Tactic free of charge, or have your Experience refunded if you already know it. Furthermore, you are enlisted as a moderator of the groups' many forums, and your authority gives you a lot of sway among not only #Ammit, but grey hat and shadowy subcultures in general. You gain four dots to distribute among Allies (Hacktivists), and Allies (Occultists) but you can only apply these to enlisting help for anti-Apophite operations; #Ammit is honorable like that, and dishonorable people don't last long.<br /> <br /> ***** Maybe it's some lingering wisp of the Purifying Storm guiding them, maybe it's simple experience combined with the not-small amount of occult lore they retain, but a true rock star among #Ammit's merry band has a knack for finding more...special sympathizers with the cause. Once per session, an administrator of #Ammit may get in contact with a supernatural enemy (or at least a supernatural being that can become an enemy with a little convincing) of a particular Child of Apophis with an hour's investigation and an Intelligence + (higher of Computer of Occult) roll. While said entity is unlikely to be the end-all be-all of the hunt, they invariably have powers that make them very useful surprises and alternative ways of getting useful information that social engineering and research can't do on its own. Of course, aid of the shadowy world does not come free, and it's likely that they'll ask a commiserate favor of their own, but it's hardly the worst sacrifice an administrator has made at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T20:18:08-07:00","id":1080719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1080716#post1080716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is probably a better plan, actually, although it would need some help to get through the princess' dual identity, which was the original purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if the &quot;radiation&quot; sticks, they should be trackable for a time even after they transform.<br /> <br /> I just don't think there should be an auto-win reveal. It hard-stops uncertainty, and thus potential stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T20:19:39-07:00","id":1080720,"title":"","content":"Yeah, fair point. I am going to bed but will try rewriting it in the morning (or if other people want to do it)!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T21:18:30-07:00","id":1080733,"title":"","content":"Here's the tactic idea, could use a bit of refinement but I think it will work given the themes so far:<br /> <br /> <br /> Candlelit Vigil: Some Hunters and occultists become painfully aware of how certain locations take on a life of their own under often horrific circumstances. Hauntings, Possessions, and especially Nests can be created when pain, suffering, or hate grows to a boiling point and a location becomes a corrupted creature all it's own. This is where this Tactic owes it's origins, for sometimes the only way to fight such horrific tragedy is with love, understanding, and closure. All of which is few and far between amongst those who take up the Hunter's Vigil...but humans may use another kind of Vigil to give the Hunter's just the right kind of power they need. Often used by religious or community driven Cells, this Tactic calls upon the local or regional community to gather and either pay their respects or morn a specific person or event that's connected to a spiritually poisonous location. The community puts forth it's faith, sorrow, or friendship and it weakens the tainted emotions that many haunted locations feed upon. While the Candlelit Vigil might not be enough to dispel the corruption from the location, having so many people sending forth their own positive emotions often gives the cell just the opening they need to move in and either properly purify it or at least destroy the dark-beating heat that gives foul life to the evil of the place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 04-19-2017, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T23:58:06-07:00","id":1080765,"title":"","content":"Candlelit Vigil is a good idea. The Sauna Box is definitely over powered, and I would say its also un-fun since tracking down monsters and discovering their secret identity is part of the fun; you don't want to skip past it.<br /> <br /> For TF:V might I suggest some sort of big brother related power where you file a request with the geeks back at HQ to dig through social media accounts looking for a monster. Roll Status * 2 - the monster's Anonymity merit (if they have one).<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: You're given a list of NPCs. 40% are red herrings, the remaining 60% are people of interest: ex-victims, unwitting pawns, loyal ghouls/sworn/etc, and of course the monster itself.<br /> Success: As above, but none of the characters on your list is the monster. Just red herrings or people close to them.<br /> Failure: Your request gets suck in a queue behind higher priority items. You get the results of a success, at the start of the next session.<br /> Dramatic Failure: 80% are red herrings, 20% of the list are legitimately people of interest. If the monster has appropriate abilities (like a Princess' visionary dreams or a Genius with an AI watching for spies) they also learn about your social media scan.<br /> <br /> Make it one use per session and require a target like a school or a sherrif's department, so players should do a bit of investigation first to avoid pointing it at somewhere without any monsters in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-19-2017, 04:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T04:18:14-07:00","id":1080813,"title":"","content":"Thank you, Leliel^^ Integrated that to the #Ammit page.<br /> <br /> The Candlelit Vigil indeed is pretty good. Starting to place it as well.<br /> <br /> I however have to agree with King Raven here. The Sauna Box is a bit overpowered; plus it kinda takes away the paranoia involved with Dual Identity, and would be completely Game-Breaking in a game with Princess players. Sorry, Urbenmyth, but that one I won't be able to keep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T04:49:25-07:00","id":1080827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1080813#post1080813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you, Leliel^^ Integrated that to the #Ammit page.<br /> <br /> The Candlelit Vigil indeed is pretty good. Starting to place it as well.<br /> <br /> I however have to agree with King Raven here. The Sauna Box is a bit overpowered; plus it kinda takes away the paranoia involved with Dual Identity, and would be completely Game-Breaking in a game with Princess players. Sorry, Urbenmyth, but that one I won't be able to keep.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the reactive, radiation based marker alternative?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T05:24:36-07:00","id":1080839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1080827#post1080827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about the reactive, radiation based marker alternative?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dual Identity would probably put a stop to most things\u2026<br /> <br /> So, perhaps we're going about this the wrong way.<br /> <br /> You can't reliably track a Princess because the universe registers her as two different people. But could you track her phylactery?<br /> <br /> It would be be considerably more difficult for a Hunter to get his hands on a Princess phylactery than just shooting her with a(n ultimately useless) tracing marker, but it could be more effective.<br /> <br /> I don't have a name for this technology or tactic, but it would require physical possession of a phylactery for a short period of time. This would need to be covert, as a Princess destroying and reforming it immediately foils this method. However, if it is a success, then the next time the phylactery is used to transform, the precise location it was used can be pinpointed. If a pattern can be established from this, then a Hunter is at least one step closer to finding a Noble's true identity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13233-rougemephilesclone","user":"RougeMephilesClone","date":". 04-19-2017, 08:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13233-rougemephilesclone","name":"RougeMephilesClone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T05:35:23-07:00","id":1080843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RougeMephilesClone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1080839#post1080839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dual Identity would probably put a stop to most things\u2026<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you aren't tracking *her* you are tracking a radiation signature. If you lose the Princess, and come across a girl (though &quot;obviously&quot; not the one you were tailing) with that signature, well, there are some questions that should be asked, right?<br /> <br /> And (in my proposal) it only reacts when fuel is spent - no wisps used, no reaction to track. It is foilable, and far from fool-proof.<br /> <br /> It is basically throwing meta-physical flour everywhere and watching for footprints.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-19-2017, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T06:14:49-07:00","id":1080860,"title":"","content":"Welp, in an attempt to redeem myself, one of my other endowment ideas!<br /> <br /> <b>Infernal Archives</b> (Castigation)<br /> <br /> Hell contains all sins and all atrocities in itself, every ugly part of humanity put in sharp relief. To gaze upon this litany of darkness would shatter the human soul. The Lurciferge, with their demonic bloodline, can do just that<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1 willpowe<br /> <b>Action</b>: Contested<br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: Presence + intimidation vs Resolve<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure</b>- the Luciferge sees hell, and is reminded of their own damnation. They lose the ability to spend willpower for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure</b>- Nothing happens except the Luciferge looks a bit silly<br /> <br /> <b>Success- </b>the victim sees the greatest horrors of human history in a terrifying instant. On a human target, or any monster with an integrity equivalent, the victim loses the ability to spend willpower for the scene and will attempt to leave the area as soon as possible. This isn't an overwhelming compulsion- they won't jump through windows or leave a dying friend- but they will do so as soon as an opportunity arises.<br /> A Noble has a bigger reaction. As well as the above effects, they immediately suffer a Hyper-Empathy Roll. If the roll succeeds it cannot be resolved until the end of this scene.<br /> (The ST may rule some particularly empathetic, kind or innocent humans may have a similar reaction. If so, they make the roll using their integrity as a dice poll. They cannot suffer the shadowed condition and lose 2 willpower on an exceptional success)<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional success-</b> Victims also lose the ability to gain willpower. If a noble is affected, their hyper-empathy roll has a bonus equal to the hunter's castiagation rating.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback </b>- Not all creatures fear sin. If used near a being that feeds on or embodies sin (creatures of the Darkness and the Inferno, definitely, others at the ST's discretion) the creature gains willpower equal to the hunter's castigation rating. If used <i>on </i>one of these creatures, it regains twice the hunters castigation rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T06:54:56-07:00","id":1080869,"title":"","content":"Random R&amp;D ideas:<ul><li>Something that acts as metaphysical insulation - nothing covered in it can truly touch another thing, rendering touch powers ineffective, and prevent use of magic items that must be &quot;on&quot; or &quot;held&quot; by the user to activate.</li> <li>Dream journey boosting stuff. I can see a Thaumatech Implant based on those hijacked by Amanojaku, or some Elixirs that take you on an empowered dream trip.</li> <li>A Relic (severed Darkspawn head?) that leeches wisps from the area when it's mouth/eyes open. Good for demoralizing others, too.</li> <li>Castigation that creates a false shell of &quot;sin&quot; around themselves/a target, letting them avoid Nest curses, and throw Darkspawn off the trail or toward something?</li> <li>Maybe a Castigation that simply grants access to Caligines without the usually Integrity degrading side-effects (limited, of course).</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T07:32:48-07:00","id":1080877,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12109\" data-vbnamecard=\"12109\">Urbenmyth</a> Mhm... okay, that Castigation idea is good^^ a bit counterproductive, since I established the Lucifuge try to keep good relationships with the Hopeful, but I do have an idea of how to take advantage on this^^ I'm including it to the doc.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Something that acts as metaphysical insulation - nothing covered in it can truly touch another thing, rendering touch powers ineffective, and prevent use of magic items that must be &quot;on&quot; or &quot;held&quot; by the user to activate. </div> </div> </div>I am... not sure I understand that one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ul><li>Dream journey boosting stuff. I can see a Thaumatech Implant based on those hijacked by Amanojaku, or some Elixirs that take you on an empowered dream trip.</li> <li>A Relic (severed Darkspawn head?) that leeches wisps from the area when it's mouth/eyes open. Good for demoralizing others, too.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>Both really good ideas, though I wonder if the latter one isn't a bit overpowered? I guess it depends how its effect works mechanic-wise. But I really like the idea of a Darkspawn's severed head as a relic. Also, the Elixir alread exists in Tooth and Nails^^'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Castigation that creates a false shell of &quot;sin&quot; around themselves/a target, letting them avoid Nest curses, and throw Darkspawn off the trail or toward something? </div> </div> </div>Good idea^^ Here's my try at adapting this idea:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shield of Sins</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Lucifuge have the blood of demons in their vein, and just like them, they have power over sin. This include the ability to tempt people into committing them, but also to shield them from others influences who would try to urge them toward it. By channeling Hell\u2019s authority, this rite allows to cast a false \u201cshell\u201d of sin around the innocents and the virtuous, making them appear as sinners in the eyes of forces who would want to corrupt or destroy them.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Lucifuge must slightly cut himself, and place some of his blood on the intended subjects. This typically translates as 1 bashing damage per subjects.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Extended; each turn represents one minute of preparation. The threshold is 2 successes per person.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice pool:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Resolve + Castigation</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The hunter unwillingly corrupts the subjects with his blood. All characters who should have benefited from this rite immediately suffer a Breaking Point penalized by the hunter\u2019s dots in Castigation.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Nothing happens.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The hunter makes progress toward invoking the rite.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Extraordinary progress is made.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once the threshold is reached, all people targeted by this rite are now wrapped in a protection made of false \u201csins\u201d, causing them to appear as more corrupt than they really are and protecting against any corrupting influence. Any ability intended to jauger their Integrity Rating, such as Sense Integrity, will identify it as Castigation dots lower than it actually is. Moverover, should they visit a Nest, its Curses won\u2019t affect them even if they behave with good intention: the Darkness will be tricked into believe they are acting with some sinister ulterior motif.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 04-19-2017, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T07:58:48-07:00","id":1080897,"title":"","content":"I feel like Archives of Hell should definitely work on Beacons","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T08:16:16-07:00","id":1080907,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> Sorry about the weird tone of my last post. I was trying to write in some sort of character, but it came out looking dismissive of your idea.<br /> <br /> In retrospect, those two concepts are different enough to work as two separate technologies. Yours is a signature that appears on people who have already used magic and must be found after its application, and mine is a signal that pings upon phylactery usage. Both are fallible (I would imagine that a Veiled Palace would jam the signal of my idea, in addition to all its other potential failings up to that point), and yours parallels the Charm &quot;Reflected Light&quot; nicely.<br /> <br /> Just a question: the signature probably appears on Nobles and Sworn who use Wisps on Bequests. Can this technology pick up Bequests at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13233-rougemephilesclone","name":"RougeMephilesClone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T08:52:33-07:00","id":1080921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1080877#post1080877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am... not sure I understand that one.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, it basically works like an air gap, but only for supernatural purposes. Like, if you are covered in it, touch powers can't reach you. If something requires it to be on your person to be used, and you have this stuff between you, it doesn't even matter if it is in your (gloved) hand - you don't &quot;have&quot; it. It doesn't prevent touch, it prevents the concept of ownership required for certain magical effects. A princess in a full body suit wouldn't &quot;have&quot; her phylactrey on her to transform (even if she were holding it through the material).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T09:03:56-07:00","id":1080927,"title":"","content":"And another one! I can't think of a name or much fluff but it is an level 4 elixir!<br /> <br /> <b>Action</b>- instant<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic failure</b>- Poison, probably! I am away from book and can't remember how much poison level 4s usually give but that much poison.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure</b>- nothing happens<br /> <br /> <b>Success</b>- for the next 24 hours, the hunter has their inner light either put out or flared up.<br /> <br /> <i>More inner light</i>- The hunter has their dark side temporarily repressed- any attempt to socially exploit their vice or make them directly harm others automatically fail. They also get +2 to empathy rolls and rolls that heal people. Lastly, they count as a being of the light for any effects that interact with that, and they suffer from hyper-empathy. Their dice-poll is their integrity, their wisps for exceptional success is their permanent willpower, and the shadowed condition applies to elixir rolls (and any other supernatural powers, should the hunter have any) <br /> <br /> <i>Less inner light- </i>The hunter has their better nature erased. Any attempt to appeal to the hunter's virtue or sense of guilt and shame automatically fail. They also get +2 to intimidation and rolls to hurt people (just combat doesn't work- the attack has to be in some sense overly cruel or vicious). They count as a creature of darkness for any effects that interact with that, and suffer aggravated damage from jade.<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Success</b>- Once per scene, the hunter can switch which half of the power they are using.<br /> <br /> Opinions? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T09:11:26-07:00","id":1080932,"title":"","content":"Needs a slight rewrite to be adapted to the rules presented in the supplement, but pretty good^^ I am taking it, with your permission.<br /> <br /> Though a name is needed obviously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T09:14:56-07:00","id":1080934,"title":"","content":"No I am posting ideas just to ensure no-one can use them<br /> <br /> (I am perfectly fine with my ideas being in the document!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T09:20:58-07:00","id":1080936,"title":"","content":"Potion of the Heart and Feather, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T09:23:34-07:00","id":1080938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No I am posting ideas just to ensure no-one can use them<br /> <br /> (I am perfectly fine with my ideas being in the document!) </div> </div> </div>... Sorry, that was a really dumb question^^'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Potion of the Heart and Feather, maybe? </div> </div> </div>As a reference to Maat, I suppose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T09:26:39-07:00","id":1080939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1080938#post1080938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a reference to Maat, I suppose?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed! It could also help with fluff I guess","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T14:27:06-07:00","id":1081076,"title":"","content":"Okay, added it to the doc^^ Now I am trying to do something with the severed Darkspawn head idea. Here's what I got so far:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Head of the Black Devil (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The creature known as the Black Devil, nowaday believed to have some form of advanced Lurker, was a strange but very powerful monster who once lived deep inside a cavern, in some middle-eastern country. Tells say it had the ability to drain its victims\u2019 will to live just by his stare, gradually turning them more and more depressed until they wouldn\u2019t even fight back when he devoured them. The fiend eventually was slayed by a blind hero, who feigned being affected by its power, then, guided by his hearing, stroke as it was getting close. His severed head, however, retained part of its power, and as such the Aegis Kai Doru has been keeping it ever since. The hideous face\u2019s eyes usually are kept shut, but whenever they are open, all people who can see them start to suffer the creature\u2019s infamous power -- especially Nobles.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 3 Willpower</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Benefit:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> By spending the required Willpower points, the hunter can causes the head\u2019s eyes to open, unleashing its power. Any mortal character who meets the head\u2019s eyes immediately suffers a Breaking Point; if he fails at the roll, he loses 1 Willpower in addition to the Integrity dot. Not only that, but he now also automatically loses 1 Willpower per turn, which lasts even after he took his eyes away from the head. The effect can only be stopped by either the victim surrendering, or closing the head\u2019s eyes, which can be done reflexively, but requires to be able to touch it.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Princesses are even more vulnerable to this effect. When confronted by the head, they suffer a Hyper-Empathy roll in addition to the Breaking Point; the number of Willpower they lose per turn equals their success on the Hyper-Empathy. If you use the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Princess: the Hopeful</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> rules, you can have them lose Wisps instead of Willpower.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The hunter using the head </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>isn\u2019t</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> immune to its hypnotic gaze. Whenever he opens its eyes, he must be careful to never actually face it directly, or the effect will start affecting him as well. This also means its power can be turned against him if his victims act fast enough.<br /> <br /> Opinions?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T14:30:06-07:00","id":1081079,"title":"","content":"I know I should know this, but what is the Hyper-Empathy roll?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T14:32:29-07:00","id":1081081,"title":"","content":"Well, you know how all these supplements about hunters hunting other supernaturals offer their own simplified rules for the supernatural in question, sometimes with different names entirely? Hyper-Empathy is the name Sensitivity in these rules for Nobles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T14:41:58-07:00","id":1081085,"title":"","content":"I like it. Also, I don't know why, but I get the feeling the Black Devil wasn't a Lurker but a Beast who developed Kinship Nightmares from a Lurker.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T14:45:45-07:00","id":1081087,"title":"","content":"Thanks^^ And interesting theory^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T14:50:04-07:00","id":1081091,"title":"","content":"Does anyone mind if I use my work on this project as an editing creit on my resume?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T14:53:06-07:00","id":1081095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1081081#post1081081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you know how all these supplements about hunters hunting other supernaturals offer their own simplified rules for the supernatural in question, sometimes with different names entirely? Hyper-Empathy is the name Sensitivity in these rules for Nobles.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ah, thanks for clearing that up. Could someone remind me what a Sensitivity roll entails though? Something to do with Shadows, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T14:57:17-07:00","id":1081099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does anyone mind if I use my work on this project as an editing creit on my resume? </div> </div> </div>I don't. I am not sure how it'll help, since that project isn't exactly finished, but if you think that can look good on your resume, be my guest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ah, thanks for clearing that up. Could someone remind me what a Sensitivity roll entails though? Something to do with Shadows, right? </div> </div> </div>You're welcome. And yes, that's basically it. Whenever a Princess sees something particularly horrible and cruel, she must roll Sensitivity, whose dice pool is determined by her Inner Light. If she gets more success than she has Shadows, she gains a new dot of Shadow. And Shadows cause penalties for her roll to transform and regain Wisps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T15:18:38-07:00","id":1081114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1081099#post1081099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't. I am not sure how it'll help, since that project isn't exactly finished, but if you think that can look good on your resume, be my guest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously I'll put it on when it's finished <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Thanks for the permission.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T15:45:23-07:00","id":1081129,"title":"","content":"You're welcome^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T16:02:43-07:00","id":1081139,"title":"","content":"Here's another idea that was suggested a few post ago for a Relic and which I tried to adapt. I am afraid that one might be overpowered, though. Mind giving me an opinion again?<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shard of Storm (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Court of Storm sometimes incorporates among its ranks strange golem-like creatures, made from a bizarre mixture of flesh, clay and this green fire they seem to get their power from. Their body, when damaged, can leave behind fragment glowing with the destructive power inhabiting them. The Aegis Kai Doru has quickly learnt to recover these shards and incorporate them in their weapons, allowing them to channel this power.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1 Willpower</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Benefit:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The shard can be incorporated in some fashion in a regular weapon, which can be either melee or long range. Whenever the hunter uses the weapon, he call upon its power to coat its blade or projectiles into green, acidic fire, giving it the ability to inflict Aggravated damages to Spawns of the Darkness of any kind.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T16:08:00-07:00","id":1081143,"title":"","content":"Maybe give it some kind of self-destructive effect? It would fit in thematically as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T16:10:34-07:00","id":1081145,"title":"","content":"I thought about it. Maybe causing it to inflict 1 Aggravated damage as a cost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T16:12:07-07:00","id":1081146,"title":"","content":"Sounds fairly reasonable, I would say<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T18:43:14-07:00","id":1081221,"title":"","content":"So, any thought about doing an expansion doc (or two - the latter, being for Fan ones) to cover the non-Core Compacts and Conspiracies?<br /> <br /> The Cainite Heresy, being very... focused, probably doesn't have much input. Hababti Ma, though (Especially with Millstone)? The Keepers of the Source?<br /> <br /> Though the Faithful of Shulpae entry is going to be a bit... hard to write.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T18:46:22-07:00","id":1081222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1081221#post1081221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Though the Faithful of Shulpae entry is going to be a bit... hard to write.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Grossness aside, how are they not a Dark Cult already if Princess is canon at the same time as them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T19:02:05-07:00","id":1081226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1081222#post1081222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. Grossness aside, how are they not a Dark Cult already if Princess is canon at the same time as them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because what they do is Holy? You are, after all, what you eat...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T19:04:23-07:00","id":1081228,"title":"","content":"Maybe they are, who knows how the ritual actually works. Certainly every princess will think they are.<br /> <br /> Hm. In terms of enemies, The Night Watch and the Barrett Commission are probably both quite suspicious- both those in the worst parts of the city and those in the halls of power have experience with privileged idealists trying to fix the world, and neither of those experiences are good. Idealistic fools at best, hiding an agenda at worst. The Talbot Group admit this spirit may be doing more benevolent things with its host, but it's still possession. The Promethean Brotherhood is lining up with knifes to see if this new type of mage will be last key in making the rite work. The Reckoning see them as far too close to heroes for their liking. VASCU are sympathetic to their motives, but vigilantes are vigilantes however magic they are<br /> <br /> Allies, The Maiden's Blood Sisterhood move in the same circles as the average noble, and get one well. Utopia Now sees them as kindred spirits, although the princesses may disagree. The Illuminated Brotherhood have stumbled to the dreamlands once or twice, and mostly like what they see. The Bear Lodge see darkspawn as great prey and will team up with princesses for the hunt. Les Mysteres have plenty of room for those that channel the light in their belief systems, although they wish they would lake their spiritual responsibilities more seriously.<br /> <br /> Opinons? Sorry, that is a lot of them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T03:17:57-07:00","id":1081365,"title":"","content":"I did consider doing parts for these, but I felt it was best to primarily focus on the core Compacts and Conspiracies like most books like this do. I allowed an exception with the Merrick Institute because their dream theme was something that would likely get them involved with Princesses. That said, if you guys want to give it a try, go ahead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah. Grossness aside, how are they not a Dark Cult already if Princess is canon at the same time as them? </div> </div> </div>I don't think just doing something horrible like this is enough to become a Dark Cult, though it certainly helps. From what I read in the Faithful of Schulpae's entry, many of them are perfectly nice and functional people in every other aspect than their disgusting cannibalistic practices. Maybe that protects them from the Darkness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T05:43:47-07:00","id":1081400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1081085#post1081085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it. Also, I don't know why, but I get the feeling the Black Devil wasn't a Lurker but a Beast who developed Kinship Nightmares from a Lurker.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. A fan theory about a fan supplement to a fan game. I think we've hit peak meta.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T05:55:03-07:00","id":1081402,"title":"","content":"XD Good point.<br /> <br /> Anyway, here is my attempt to adapt the idea suggested by King Raven for the TFV database:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Eye of Odin (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While the Equaliser Grenade deals with the physically shape-shifting, not all creatures need to physically change to hide. Princesses are impossible to identify thanks to the strange magic covering their identity, Changelings and Prometheans have near-perfect human disguises, and Demons steal people\u2019s lives to wear them like masks. While TFV has yet to figure out any efficient way to pierce through these disguises, they can take advantage on the government surveillance over social medias and the internet in general to look for any clue suggesting someone might be an ENE. All the informations collected are then placed inside a larger database known as the Eye of Odin, whose access is sometimes given to field agents to help them investigate. This won\u2019t actually tell them who is the ENE, but it can narrow down the list of suspects, and make the job easier for them.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Function:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Once per session, a character with this Endowment can connect himself to the Eye of Odin and request a list of all the potential ENEs in a specific area. The area can be a school, a sheriff department, a small town or anything, similar, as long as it covers a specific area. Agents are expected to have already done some investigation of their own to justify their suspicions, as it\u2019s frown upon to waste the government resources on an area without any known supernatural being.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once the area has been chosen, roll the character\u2019s TVF Status * 2. If the monster they are looking for has the Anonymity Merit, apply the merit\u2019s dots as a penalty to the roll. Regardless of what you get, the character will receive a list of NPCs suspected to be ENEs in the area; the result merely serves to decide how accurate and useful said list will be:</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Roll Results:</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 80% of the people on the list are red herrings, while 20% of the list are legitimately people of interest. Moreover, if the targeted monster has an appropriate ability (such as a Princess\u2019 prophetic dreams or a mad scientist with an AI watching for spies), they become aware of your social media scan.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Your request gets stuck in a queue behind higher priority items. You get the results of a success, at the start of the next session.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 40% of the people on your list are red herring, while the remaining 60% are people of interest: unwitting pawns, loyal ghouls and Sworns, wolf-blooded or equivalent. None of them is the monster, however.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Same than success, but one of the people on the list is the monster you are looking for.<br /> <br /> I would also like to remind you guys #Ammit is still in need for a section of sample Hunters and on the various Divisions they have. If any of you feels inspired regarding this, be my guests and bring your ideas on the table.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 04-20-2017, 09:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T06:52:30-07:00","id":1081420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1081402#post1081402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also like to remind you guys #Ammit is still in need for a section of sample Hunters and on the various Divisions they have. If any of you feels inspired regarding this, be my guests and bring your ideas on the table.[/FONT][/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div>Divisions? Maybe, Research (finding Apophites or validating suspected targets), Outreach (forming alliances with other hacktavist groups and potentially useful Hunter - and supernatural - factions), and Onsite (the more personally capable hunters, either physically, or socially - sometimes you need muscle, or in-person social engineering).<br /> <hr /><br /> Rereading through the doc:<br /> <br /> Another potential nickname for Storms: Punishers<br /> <br /> For some of the Dread Powers (and a few Endowments), could we make them a little less locked into just affecting or being linked to the Light or Darkness? One of the nice things with new Dread Powers (or Endowments) is that you can use them for other things/targets. I'll list some more examples when I have more time - For the Shard of Storms, maybe make it 1 Aggravated damage per hit (rest Lethal) to most targets, and full Aggravated damage to Darkspawn?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T07:04:21-07:00","id":1081424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1081365#post1081365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think just doing something horrible like this is enough to become a Dark Cult, though it certainly helps. From what I read in the Faithful of Schulpae's entry, many of them are perfectly nice and functional people in every other aspect than their disgusting cannibalistic practices. Maybe that protects them from the Darkness?</div> </div> </div> </div>To qualify as a Dark Cult members have to specifically worship the Darkness, simply being an evil cult isn't enough.<br /> <br /> If an Anakim Tyrant convinces a bunch of people he's a god and should be worshipped through bullying minorities with ambitions of climbing the soceo-ecconomic ladder, but that's evil but it's not a Dark Cult and due to the way Taint works (specifically it's location based and it's going to form in the dark alleyways where they commit the crimes, not their homes) there's a fairly good chance they'll even avoid becoming Darkened.<br /> <br /> However if the victims start congregating in the Tainted alleys and performing sacrafices to the Darkness to acquire supernatural powers that they can use to defend themselves that would be a Dark Cult, despite the fact it's significantly more justified than the first group.<br /> <br /> <br /> Life isn't fair, the World of Darkness is less so, and the moral of the story is that no matter how horrible the situation you're trapped in is; making deals with the metaphysical embodyment of evil is going to make it worse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1081402#post1081402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once per session, a character with this Endowment can connect himself to the Eye of Odin and request a list of all the potential ENEs in a specific area.</div> </div> </div> </div>One point; there was a reason I phrased it that the tech geeks back at HQ recieve your request and start doing research; that was to justify the once per session rule. If you just log in and search then there's no reason why you can't use it again and again, but if humans are involved that's a limited resource<br /> <br /> Mind if I take a crack at that:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While the Equaliser Grenade deals with the physically shape-shifting, not all creatures need to physically change to hide. Princesses are impossible to identify thanks to the strange magic covering their identity, Changelings and Prometheans have near-perfect human disguises, and Demons steal people\u2019s lives to wear them like masks. While TFV has yet to figure out a reliable way to pierce through these disguises, you don't need to see through a disguise to notice the ENE wearing it is acting unusually. VALKARIE operates a vast automated system called the Eye of Odin which piggybacks on government survelence over social media, financial transations, phones, and the internet in general to flag anything which might indicate ENE activity. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Function:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Once per session, a character with this Endowment can contact headquarters and ask for a report on a specific area. The area can be a school, a sheriff department, a small town or anything, similar. Upon recieving a request a team of specially trained analyists will begin combing through flagged material to identify persons of interest. Even if a Princess fusditiously avoids using social media, the Eye of Odin might still flag a suspicious spike in accademic achievements and positive sentiments on social media </span></span>which when cross referenced with debit card that purchased a bulk order of socks at 11pm next to a homeless shelter suggests someone is either a Princess or inspired to follow a Noble's example.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once the area has been chosen, roll the character\u2019s TVF Status * 2 to requisition a report. If the monster they are looking for has the Anonymity Merit, apply the merit\u2019s dots as a penalty to the roll. Regardless of what you get, headquarters will present your character a list of charachters suspected to be ENEs in the area; the result merely serves to decide how accurate and useful said list will be:</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Roll Results:</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 80% of the people on the list are red herrings, while 20% of the list are legitimately people of interest. Moreover, if the targeted monster has an appropriate ability (such as a Princess\u2019 prophetic dreams or a mad scientist with an AI watching for spies), they become aware that you are looking for them.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Your request gets stuck in a queue behind higher priority items. You get the results of a success, at the start of the next session.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 40% of the people on your list are red herring, while the remaining 60% are people of interest: unwitting pawns, loyal ghouls, Sworn, wolf-blooded or equivalent. None of them is the monster, however.</span></span> Alternatively you learn that there is no monster present.<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Same than success, but one of the people on the list is the monster you are looking for.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T09:20:52-07:00","id":1081464,"title":"","content":"Well, I was afraid the geek part might make it a bit too close to Network Zero rather than TFV, but... yeah, you've got a point here. I'll add your modifications to the doc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Divisions? Maybe, Research (finding Apophites or validating suspected targets), Outreach (forming alliances with other hacktavist groups and potentially useful Hunter - and supernatural - factions), and Onsite (the more personally capable hunters, either physically, or socially - sometimes you need muscle, or in-person social engineering). </div> </div> </div>That'll do as a good base. Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For some of the Dread Powers (and a few Endowments), could we make them a little less locked into just affecting or being linked to the Light or Darkness? One of the nice things with new Dread Powers (or Endowments) is that you can use them for other things/targets. I'll list some more examples when I have more time - For the Shard of Storms, maybe make it 1 Aggravated damage per hit (rest Lethal) to most targets, and full Aggravated damage to Darkspawn? </div> </div> </div>I am not really sure what you mean by that, I precisely tried to not make most of them too locked on these. The Head of the Black Devil can be used on pretty much anything, it's just more effective on Nobles; same for Infernal Archives. Heart and Feather of Maat can be useful in plenty of situations. Shield of Sin can be used against demons with the ability to sense sins, and the Eye of Odin is explicitly said to be useful against a large variety of supernaturals. The only Endowments I can think of that are really focused on them are the Christ's Benediction and Astral Implants. Your idea for Shard of Storm is good, though.<br /> <br /> As for Dread Powers, well... okay, looking back at them, maybe they ARE a bit too focused on Nobles and Darkspawns. What would you suggest to change?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T11:56:16-07:00","id":1081520,"title":"","content":"First thing I suggest? Go through the existing Dread Powers in Hunter books looking for similarities to Noble and Dark abilities.<br /> <br /> For instance, I'm looking at the Hunter core. &quot;Dread Attack&quot; is pretty close to the Kensai Charm (close enough for Hunter-only campaigns) - the only critical aspect it leaves out is the ability to deal either bashing or lethal damage. &quot;Impress&quot; has no single match in Princess, but several Charms do things like it.<br /> <br /> Mortal Remains has several more suitable Dread Powers. &quot;Dead Flesh&quot; should be automatic for Nobles - despite its description, its effect is very nearly that of Holy Shield. &quot;Blast&quot; is to Levinbolt what &quot;Dread Attack&quot; is to Kensai. &quot;Cloak of Authority&quot; represents another family of Noble social influencers. &quot;Flicker and Flash&quot; or &quot;Uncanny Reflexes&quot; can stand in for dodging and speedster Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T12:00:09-07:00","id":1081523,"title":"","content":"I already did that. That's the reason I didn't put a Loathsome Weapon Dread Power. The reason I made a Dread Power matching Kensai was because Dread Attack wouldn't allow to apply an Invocation/Enhancement to it. In fact, if you check my Dread Power section, I did put a list of already existing Dread Powers to use when building Princesses. I tried to create new ones only for abilities that didn't have any match in the already existing Dread Powers, like the Mirrors Charms allowing them to manipulate reflective surfaces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T12:31:37-07:00","id":1081538,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I passed that list by because it's broken down by Queens. I was looking for Dread Powers which are universal among Nobles.<br /> <br /> As a tangent, I'm a bit surprised that there isn't an official Dread Power for intrinsic Armor, when practically every supernatural type has a power for just that purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T12:40:41-07:00","id":1081540,"title":"","content":"yeah, that can happen.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I find this weird as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T13:57:38-07:00","id":1081570,"title":"","content":"A few more no-core group's opinions, because hey why not?<br /> <br /> Yuri's group is torn. On the one hand, they can't deny that the Nobles do good work and help a lot of the same people they do. On the other, they're intrinsically suspicious of creatures that set themselves up as moral authorities over humans. The Queens and their nobles are less openly hostile in their &quot;lessons&quot; then the beasts, but are they <i>different</i>? Yuri's group isn't sure, and keeps an eye on them for now.<br /> <br /> The Cainite Heresy doesn't care. Darkness? Nobles? They're not vampires. Vampires are the problem. Let's focus on those. We can deal with the dregs of the supernatural world once the vampires are ash.<br /> <br /> The Knights of Saint George are firm. Witches are witches. However good their intentions are, they pose a threat to the world and must be put down. When they get a Noble as a target (usually when she's looking into the same few businesses and organisations,oddly enough) Division Six agrees.<br /> <br /> Ahl al-Jabal are suspicious. They are dedicated to preventing the monsters that stop human progress, but what about the ones that support it? Are the Nobles allies, or simply a more appealing plan to lure humanity off track? Opinions vary- for now, the group waits until more information is available before making a stance one way or another.<br /> <br /> The Faithful of Shulpae... as mentioned, best not to go into details. Suffice to say, a god's essence is unchanged by its mortal shell, and eating it has the same benefits however harmless it looks. Also, they are on every courts &quot;destroy&quot; list and every dark creature's &quot;make into cult&quot; list, so there's that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T14:02:39-07:00","id":1081572,"title":"","content":"What's Yuri's Group?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T14:04:20-07:00","id":1081573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1081570#post1081570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Faithful of Shulpae... are [on] every dark creature's &quot;make into cult&quot; list, so there's that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like that would go badly for the Darkness, considering what The Faithful do to the things they venerate","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T14:15:44-07:00","id":1081574,"title":"","content":"Yuri's group are from Tooth and Nail, the beast hunter supplement. They're therapists who fight Beasts on the grounds they are abusers using talk of &quot;lessons&quot; to justify their actions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1081573#post1081573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like that would go badly for the Darkness, considering what The Faithful do to the things they venerate</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point, but on the other hand, if there's one force in the world of darkness willing to risk everything to spread pain and destruction...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T14:17:56-07:00","id":1081576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What's Yuri's Group? </div> </div> </div>A Compact introduced in Tooth and Nails, the supplement about hunting Beasts. Basically, they are an support group for people who suffered at the hand of the supernaturals, and especially from Beasts. Though they also sometimes try to redeem monsters by giving them group Therapy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T14:31:13-07:00","id":1081584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1081523#post1081523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I already did that. That's the reason I didn't put a Loathsome Weapon Dread Power. The reason I made a Dread Power matching Kensai was because Dread Attack wouldn't allow to apply an Invocation/Enhancement to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then what about making a that a quality of Enhancement, or add a Dread Power that let them deal Bashing damage instead (call it Merciful?). I could see some Horrors who prefer live prey using it as well for capture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T14:36:32-07:00","id":1081587,"title":"","content":"Seems like a good compromise I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T14:45:09-07:00","id":1081589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1081574#post1081574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yuri's group are from Tooth and Nail, the beast hunter supplement. They're therapists who fight Beasts on the grounds they are abusers using talk of &quot;lessons&quot; to justify their actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, basically the B:tP detractors who weren't whining about &quot;otherkin bait&quot;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T14:50:14-07:00","id":1081591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, basically the B:tP detractors who weren't whining about &quot;otherkin bait&quot;<img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> </div> </div> </div>XD yeah pretty much. I personally wonder if they weren't created just to adress this criticism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T14:53:45-07:00","id":1081592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1081591#post1081591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> XD yeah pretty much. I personally wonder if they weren't created just to adress this criticism.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> oooooh, they <i>undoubtedly</i> were","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T15:44:29-07:00","id":1081607,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=888823#post888823\">Yeah... about that</a><br /> <br /> More seriously, Dave's opening to the Yuri's group thread strongly implies that it was a case of multiple people having the idea so I don't think I can claim credit. I can say I did suggest it specifically on the grounds that those criticisms had a point and it should be addressed. Same story behind <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/691410-compact-ride-to-damascus-the-beastcrafters\">Ride to Damascus</a> (who I consider to be my best Hunter work. Fun fact: They were actually a spin off from a conversation I had with PenDragon about Princess/Beast)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-20-2017, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T15:44:36-07:00","id":1081608,"title":"","content":"Well, then they did a good job, because Yuri's Group are portrayed as sympathetic rather than Strawmen. Personally, they are among my favourite Compacts.<br /> <br /> Anyway, back on topic, I got this idea for a Tactic, but I have trouble deciding some of the dicepools. Mind helping again, please?<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Divide to Reign</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (all participant) Resolve 2, (secondary actors) Stamina 2, Athletic 3, (primary actor) Resolve 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Requires:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 3; each participant above 3 grants a +1 bonus to the primary actor\u2019s dice pool</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Dice pool:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Secondary Dice pools:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Stamina + Athletic</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Description:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Hunters who survived enough confrontations with intelligent Spawns capable of controlling Lurkers have come to realize their control over their repulsive servants tend to wear out after a while away from them. This Tactic was invented to take advantage of this weakness. Using part of their members as willing baits, the Cell tries its best to lure the creatures as far away as possible from their masters, then resort to traps and ambush to make sure he won\u2019t be able to approach them until the effect of his power ceases.This is risky, as a Spawn powerful enough to posses such an ability rarely is harmless, but when used well, this can break an organized force of Spawns into small groups of mindless monsters much easier to dispose of.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Tactic is meant to be used against Spawns with the Monster Lord Dread Power, and works in two phases; during the first one, the hunters split up, with the secondary actors doing their best to attract the Lurkers\u2019 attention and bring them out of range of their master\u2019s power. This part is particularly risky, as they take the risk of having the monsters catch up with them; any secondary actor who fail his roll ends up having to fight the targeted Lurkers. Fortunately, a larger number of hunters can lessen this problem: the number of Lurkers he has to fight is divided by the number of secondary actors taking part in this Tactic.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For the second phase, the primary actor confronts the Lurkers\u2019 master if he shows up, and does everything he can to prevent him from getting to his minions, hopefully with help from any secondary actor who could make it back. Each success on the primary actor means the Spawn is hold back for one hour; if he\u2019s hold back long enough for Monster Lord to wear off, he loses his control over his Lurkers.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Tactic is equally effective against any creature using some form of mind control or compelling effect to keep a hold over its minions, as long as you can keep them away the needed time, such as vampire thralls, or people under the effect of a mad scientist\u2019s mind control device. If the mind manipulating power\u2019s effect is based on range rather than duration, replace the hours gained for each success by yards.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Organizations:</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T07:11:24-07:00","id":1081822,"title":"","content":"Well, I guess no one has any suggestion for that one.<br /> <br /> Anyway, currently trying to build the profile for Ben Vold (that Sample Cataphractoi <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar180_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"180\" data-vbnamecard=\"180\">Leliel</a> suggested). But I am running into a small problem... how much do Dread Powers cost to buy with experience/creation point, please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T07:47:03-07:00","id":1081837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1081822#post1081822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I guess no one has any suggestion for that one.<br /> <br /> Anyway, currently trying to build the profile for Ben Vold (that Sample Cataphractoi <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar180_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"180\" data-vbnamecard=\"180\">Leliel</a> suggested). But I am running into a small problem... how much do Dread Powers cost to buy with experience/creation point, please?</div> </div> </div> </div>It usually doesn't list, since they are (mostly) Antagonist material. You give the critter what fits and don't worry about XP costs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T07:52:05-07:00","id":1081838,"title":"","content":"Mortal Remains suggests (p. 164) a cost of two Experiences for each dot of Dread Powers. That's for the 2ed experience system, of course. If you're using 1ed, that's the same price as a Skill dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T11:47:56-07:00","id":1082330,"title":"","content":"Thank you. If you have any advice regarding the kind of abilities this guy should have, I am all ears.<br /> <br /> So far, I am thinking Dead Flesh (to go with the whole Draugr thing) and Strange Form (though Biomechanical Nightmare might work as well if we go with the idea he merges with his boat).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 04-22-2017, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T13:14:00-07:00","id":1082368,"title":"","content":"Well, the big thing mentioned in Vold's description is how he seeks out hunters and dishonors them, then locks them into his tugboat's bilge so they'll drown and turn into Darkspawn. A quick scan suggests Damnation and Judgement of Guilt from the HtV core as useful for that purpose. Eye for Desire from Mortal Remains is just as good for a hanging judge as a tempter.<br /> <br /> Merging with his boat ... actually, I'd run with Lord of the Manor in Mortal Remains for that. And since Vold <i>is</i> a sailor, using Tempest to surround his boat with violent weather and wreck other boats would be in theme.<br /> <br /> Strange Form is a requirement for any Cataphract, and Vold's water-creature motif justifies Tendrils when he transforms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T16:06:17-07:00","id":1082420,"title":"","content":"Sounds good. Thank you.<br /> <br /> Here's what I got so far. Any opinion? Did I make him overpowered?<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Vice:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Envy- as noted above, Ben Vold hates hunters because they remind him of what he lost.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Virtue:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Dutiful- Vold was a responsible man in his life, even though his ideas of serving the Aesir is little more than delusion, he still takes this task seriously.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mental Attributes:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Physical Attributes:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Strength 2(5), Dexterity 3 (4), Stamina 2(6)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Social Attributes:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mental Skills:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Academics 2, Computer 2, Investigation 3, Occult 2, Politics 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Physical Skills:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Athletic 2, Brawl 3, Drive 3 (the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Ran</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">), Firearms 2, Survival 2 (Sea)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Social Skills:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Empathy 4, Intimidation 4, Persuasion 2 (Break Spirit), Subterfuge 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Merits:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Small Unit Tactics, Good Time Management, Fast Reflexes 2, Safe Place 3 (the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Ran</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Health:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 7(11)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dread Powers (both forms):</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Contagion 2, Damnation 3 Dead Flesh 3, Dread Attack 2, Eye for Desire 2, Judgment of Guilt 5, Monster Lord 4, Sense Integrity 1, Strange Form 4, Tempest 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dread Powers (Strange Form only):</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Tendrils 3 (Tentacles), Lord of the Manor 5 (Permanent, the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Ran</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Potency/Shadows:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Aspirations:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Recruit more people in his crew, break hunters, </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Willpower:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Size:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Speed:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 10 (14)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Defense:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 5 (6)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Initiative:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 4 (5)<br /> <br /> Also, I would appreciate if someone could give me a reference to base the Ran's profile on. I do have the Armory book, but I am not sure which sample boat I should pick.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 04-22-2017, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T00:12:43-07:00","id":1082531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1082420#post1082420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I would appreciate if someone could give me a reference to base the Ran's profile on. I do have the Armory book, but I am not sure which sample boat I should pick.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd take the houseboat listed on Armory p.146, cut the safe and max speed in half and add 3 points to durability, since tugboats are slow and somewhat tough even without the use of magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T04:56:55-07:00","id":1082560,"title":"","content":"Okay, here's the current version:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Vice:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Envy- as noted above, Ben Vold hates hunters because they remind him of what he lost.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Virtue:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Dutiful- Vold was a responsible man in his life, even though his ideas of serving the Aesir is little more than delusion, he still takes this task seriously.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mental Attributes:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Physical Attributes:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Strength 2(5), Dexterity 3 (4), Stamina 2(6)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Social Attributes:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mental Skills:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Academics 2, Computer 2, Investigation 3, Occult 2, Politics 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Physical Skills:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Athletic 2, Brawl 3, Drive 3 (the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Ran</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">), Firearms 2, Survival 2 (Sea)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Social Skills:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Empathy 4, Intimidation 4, Persuasion 2 (Break Spirit), Subterfuge 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Merits:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Small Unit Tactics, Good Time Management, Fast Reflexes 2, Safe Place 3 (the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Ran</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Health:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 7(11)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dread Powers (both forms):</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Contagion 2, Damnation 3 Dead Flesh 3, Dread Attack 2, Eye for Desire 2, Judgment of Guilt 5, Monster Lord 4, Sense Integrity 1, Strange Form 4, Tempest 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dread Powers (Strange Form only):</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Tendrils 3 (Tentacles), Lord of the Manor 5 (Permanent, the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Ran</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Potency/Shadows:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Aspirations:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Recruit more people in his crew, break hunters, defend his boat</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Willpower:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Size:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Speed:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 10 (14)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Defense:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 5 (6)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Initiative:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 4 (5)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Notes:</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Ran</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> is a modified Houseboat (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Armory p. 146</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">), with the following modification: Safe Speed and Max Speed cut by half, +3 Durability. For those lacking the book, here\u2019s the resulting profile:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Durability 6, Size 23, Structure 29, Acceleration 2, Safe Speed 12, Max Speed 22, Handling -1, Occupant 1+7.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">On the inside, it counts as a Nest of Size 3 with a Corruption level of 10, with the following Curses: Corruption, Dominance (+3), Resistance (-2), Speed (-2), Willpower (-1), Defense (-1). The Foci is an old lighter in the boiler room, which Vold used to commit his murder-suicide.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Vold is rarely seen without his crew, which mostly consists in Lurkers, with possibly a few Infiltrators as his most faithful lieutenants. The Storyteller should build them himself, ideally with at least Dead Flesh and Dread Attack, but they can have any other Dread Power. While in Strange Form, Vold can sacrifice any member of his crew to recover from wounds, healing lethal damages equal to the sacrificed crew member\u2019s health boxes. This takes 1 Instant action per crew member.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While in Strange Form, Ben Vold merges with the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Ran</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, becoming a monstrous fusion between a boat and a kraken. In term of game, this means he cannot be killed nor knocked out while in this state unless the boat itself is destroyed; the players can still attack him and inflict him damages, but should they feel his last health box with lethal or Aggravated damages, he will merely use Lord of the Mansion to retreat his \u201cmain\u201d body (actually the organic part of him) to a different area of the ship, where he can heal himself by sacrificing crew members. He cannot, however, return to harass the players until his health boxes have been fully healed, giving them some delay to act. If out of crew member, his wounds will heal naturally at the same rate than a human. Should the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Ran</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> be destroyed or purified, he would die.</span></span></li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 04-23-2017, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T14:42:52-07:00","id":1082774,"title":"","content":"So, let me see if I understand this. When Vold fuses with his ship, he turns into a Size 5 humanoid with his legs/lower tentacles connected to his ship (or something like that). He can move around normally, and automatically teleports to a location not occupied by players upon &quot;death&quot;. The requirement of the <i>Ran</i> being destroyed to truly defeat him if he transforms sets up something of an equipment gate for players. That said, I can see a Storyteller urging their players to initiate a tactical retreat after a successful fight, leading to a more conclusive round two later.<br /> <br /> A few questions: how many mooks can be expected to participate in any given encounter? Would they be on deck with Vold, or below deck until called? About how large of a crew can players expect to run into?<br /> <br /> I also have one nitpick: because this runs on Hunter rules, Vold uses Willpower to perform Dread Powers, and lacks a Shadows stat. Now, I can't claim to know how Hunter stats work, but from what I can gather, this guy seems to have a lot of abilities and not much Willpower to use them. I don't know if this is a normal statline or not, so I yield to the opinions of those more experienced than I.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13233-rougemephilesclone","user":"RougeMephilesClone","date":". 04-23-2017, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13233-rougemephilesclone","name":"RougeMephilesClone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T15:39:19-07:00","id":1082795,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's more or less it. I admit it's probably not the best mechanics, but I figured that if he actually became one with the ship as in the ship became fully his body, the players would have absolutely no chance defeating it. So I thought giving the players a mean to temporarly stop his attacks would balance it somewhat.<br /> <br /> I... am not sure for his crewmen's number. As for where they would be, I imagine they would walk around the ship with some below deck and others on deck depending on the situation.<br /> <br /> Well, in the rules I wrote to use Darkspawns in a Hunter campaign, Shadow became the equivalent of Potency instead of what it is in Princess. But yeah, you're right about his Willpower; I'll fix that right away.<br /> <br /> Done. I also raised his Potency slightly, so he actually has 10 Willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 04-23-2017, 06:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T15:51:27-07:00","id":1082802,"title":"","content":"Does Hunter usually use the source monster's power stat? I thought they just converted it to Potency","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T15:53:52-07:00","id":1082804,"title":"","content":"Well, Mortal Remains does call them all Potency but also has a section where it gives them individual names and effect, so... yeah, I don't know for sure. And Tooth and Nail calls it Lair for Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T16:03:41-07:00","id":1082809,"title":"","content":"In the main three (spirit slayers, night stalkers, witch hunters) it gave them blood potency/primal urge/gnosis, albeit with different simplified rules. SO it's probably ok to use inner light/shadows here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T16:08:42-07:00","id":1082810,"title":"","content":"Well, at least that's what I am doing.<br /> <br /> Regardless, how many crewmen would you say Ben Vold should have? Six? Ten? A dozen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T16:36:30-07:00","id":1082821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1082810#post1082810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless, how many crewmen would you say Ben Vold should have? Six? Ten? A dozen?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a recommended range of 6-12 is sufficient, with a note that they shouldn't all be in the same location. Storytellers already have a wide berth when it comes to Darkspawn, so they can make the crew as large and powerful as they want. It all hinges on what the players can handle when they reach the encounter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13233-rougemephilesclone","name":"RougeMephilesClone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T17:09:27-07:00","id":1082837,"title":"","content":"That will do. Thanks.<br /> <br /> Soooo since we now have at least 1 sample Creature of the Darkness, I feel like it's only fair to make a sample Noble as well. Right now, I do have an idea, of my own if you guys wanna hear, but I am open to suggestions as usual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T18:38:06-07:00","id":1082862,"title":"","content":"How about one from Alhambra or Storms and one Radiant one as an Antagonist for Hunters in the shadier Conspiracies like Cheiron or Faithful of Shulpae?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T18:52:21-07:00","id":1082868,"title":"","content":"I would put at least one radiant &quot;ally&quot; (that is, one that will help the hunters) and one radiant &quot;enemy&quot; (one that will stand in the way of hunters- protecting the monsters, for example)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T18:56:21-07:00","id":1082870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1082868#post1082868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would put at least one radiant &amp;quot;ally&amp;quot; (that is, one that will help the hunters) and one radiant &amp;quot;enemy&amp;quot; (one that will stand in the way of hunters- protecting the monsters, for example)</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't even need to be a &quot;protect the monsters&quot; deal with some Hunters","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T05:59:26-07:00","id":1082984,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but I like the protect monster angle personally. Here's my try at it. Feel free to comment:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cheryl Wilson, the Monster Keeper</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cI don\u2019t care if he is a monster. That doesn\u2019t give you the right to kill him.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">An unfortunate truth many Hunters aren\u2019t comfortable with, but usually end up learning, is that not all monsters are pure evil. While many of them certainly are irredeemable fiends, there are just as many who really just want to be left alone, or even are trying to do good. These are the ones the Noble known as the Monster Keeper makes her duty of protecting.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Originally a young girl named Cheryl Wilson, this particular Princess grew up in a small, but reasonably happy family, with loving parents and a little brother named Lee. She was a good-hearted kid, and got along pretty fine with him, often acting protective; they had their arguments, like any sibling, but overall they were rather close.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At some point when they were teenagers, however, something changed with Lee. The boy went through a Devouring, and became a Beast. Cheryl was confused about what had happened to her little brother, who was suddenly talking about a hungry monster living inside his mind and urging him to hurt people. To make things worse, when he tried to resist, the entire family started having nightmares about being chased by a hideous dragon-like creature, which always ended with them awakening and finding Lee in tears, repeating he didn\u2019t want to hurt anyone.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Then came the day where a man came to the home and tried to murder Lee, insisting the boy was a monster. When she saw this lunatic trying to kill her beloved little brother she had seen crying for weeks, something inside Cheryl snapped, and she went through a transformation of her own, becoming a Noble. With her newfound power, she was able to defeat the man and save her brother. Soon after, she found out not only could she now gather the energy to feed her powers by helping people around her, but doing so actually seemed to feed whatever creature was inside Lee, diminishing its urge to hurt people. In a matter of days, the nightmares ended, and the kid could more or less resume a normal life.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ever since, the two siblings have become even more inseparable than they already were, and regularly travel, looking for other supernatural beings like them who get hunted down like animals. Whenever they find one, they observe from a distance, trying to figure out if they are dealing with a real monster who needs to be stopped, or a victim of the consequences. If he proves the former, they let the local hunters do their job, and might even give them tips in the case of really bad seed. If the latter, however, the Princess does everything in her power to defend the creature. She will usually try diplomacy first, but should the hunters prove impossible to reason with, or worse, not care, she will unleash all her power on them.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T06:41:44-07:00","id":1082993,"title":"","content":"I love it. We gonna do stats for her brother, too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T06:58:14-07:00","id":1082997,"title":"","content":"Glad you like it^^' I was a bit concerned with how people would react to it, since portraying Beasts sympathetically seems to raise some controversy among fans, but it seems that one works.<br /> <br /> As for doing stats on her brother... I admit I am not sure. On one hand, it would only make sense, seeing how the two are rarely without each other. But on the other hand, the book is supposed to be about Princesses, not Beasts, and the Beast rules already are in Tooth and Nails. Maybe give him stats but make them optional by saying he might stay aside to let her do the job?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T07:45:40-07:00","id":1083013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1082997#post1082997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glad you like it^^' I was a bit concerned with how people would react to it, since portraying Beasts sympathetically seems to raise some controversy among fans, but it seems that one works.<br /> <br /> As for doing stats on her brother... I admit I am not sure. On one hand, it would only make sense, seeing how the two are rarely without each other. But on the other hand, the book is supposed to be about Princesses, not Beasts, and the Beast rules already are in Tooth and Nails. Maybe give him stats but make them optional by saying he might stay aside to let her do the job?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say they might split up occasionally, but Lee seems a bit dependent upon his sister for decent feeding.<br /> <br /> Maybe he was killed (either instead of being saved from the Hero/Hunter, or later)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T07:52:09-07:00","id":1083015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1082997#post1082997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was a bit concerned with how people would react to it, since portraying Beasts sympathetically seems to raise some controversy among fans, but it seems that one works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, her brother is a Beast in name only, at least by what's written there. He doesn't feed upon human fears, he doesn't teach lessons. Maybe you just didn't get to that, but I'm guessing he uses Family Dinner to feed. (A mechanic I feel makes it way to easy for Beasts to just avoid Hunger)<br /> <br /> Incidently that's probably half the reason Princesses and Beasts usually don't get along. A Beast can't exactly justify their feeding as necessity if assisting a Princess with good works is a viable alternative. The other half is that Princesses would agree that lessons and emotions are super important, which is why they can't stand Beasts who &quot;are doing it wrong!&quot;. With some justification, see Yuri's Group, also nothing Atavisms &amp; Nightmares can do come close to Passion's Light &amp; You Must Remember This for teaching an effective lesson; and that's before you get to the high level Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think there is an issue though: Conflict between Cheryl and hunters is too black and white. Either the hunter are fanatics (or Chiron) and want to hurt the innocent monsters she protects, or there is some contrived misunderstanding, or there is no conflict. I won't lie, this is a fundamentally hard character to write, because if the monsters she protects are bad enough to justify players hunting them then she comes across as a bad parody of magical girl, stupid good in TvTropes terms. If the monsters are not bad enough then you hit the problem you have now: A narrow concept that only works when players are intentionally playing fanatics.<br /> <br /> My thought would be for the Princess to be trying to save a monster who's harmless now, but with the potential to level a city (pity Deviant isn't out yet). Then you could have a conflict based on &quot;it's too dangerous to leave alive&quot; vs &quot;saving a life is worth a risk&quot; (with the added complications that starting a fight might set the Deviant off so you really want to use non-violent means to get the Princess away before going in for the kill).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T07:55:37-07:00","id":1083016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe he was killed (either instead of being saved from the Hero/Hunter, or later)? </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I kinda feel like the character works better as a pair with her sibling... maybe leave that option open to the storyteller?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly, her brother is a Beast in name only, at least by what's written there. He doesn't feed upon human fears, he doesn't teach lessons. Maybe you just didn't get to that, but I'm guessing he uses Family Dinner to feed. (A mechanic I feel makes it way to easy for Beasts to just avoid Hunger) </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what he is doing, yes. I kinda get the feeling fans tend to think ALL Beasts either revel in harming people to feed, or justify what they are doing with teaching lessons -- even though my impression reading the final version of the Beast book is that only parts of them go for these options, and it's perfectly possible for Beasts to be people who just wish to have a life while harming as little people as possible. I designed Lee to be like this. And it's not like this is a unique case: Conquering Heroes mentions a Beast who didn't know about his inheritance and refused to feed much like Lee does here (he was less lucky however and ended up killed by Hero Gracia Teller). I just thought it'd be interesting to make a Beast character who handles his condition by feeding primarily through Family Dinner.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think there is an issue though: Conflict between Cheryl and hunters is too black and white. Either the hunter are fanatics (or Chiron) and want to hurt the innocent monsters she protects, or there is some contrived misunderstanding, or there is no conflict. I won't lie, this is a fundamentally hard character to write, because if the monsters she protects are bad enough to justify players hunting them then she comes across as a bad parody of magical girl, stupid good in TvTropes terms. If the monsters are not bad enough then you hit the problem you have now: A narrow concept that only works when players are intentionally playing fanatics.<br /> <br /> My thought would be for the Princess to be trying to save a monster who's harmless now, but with the potential to level a city (pity Deviant isn't out yet). Then you could have a conflict based on &quot;it's too dangerous to leave alive&quot; vs &quot;saving a life is worth a risk&quot; (with the added complications that starting a fight might set the Deviant off so you really want to use non-violent means to get the Princess away before going in for the kill). </div> </div> </div>Well, I thought she might be used both as an antagonist and a supporting character, or a character that would force players to question how right they are in what they are doing. But yeah, I see your point. I'll try integrating your suggestion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 04-24-2017, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T08:29:42-07:00","id":1083024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1083016#post1083016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, I kinda feel like the character works better as a pair with her sibling... maybe leave that option open to the storyteller?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but it involves Beast, which isn't really needed. You could also leave what happened to him vague (instead of purposefully calling out Beast). Basically - something happened, Lee became a &quot;monster&quot;, tries to handle it as best he can (with help from his sister), but it still stalked by people who just see him as a monster. Could be a Beast, Vampire, unique Horror, etc. <i>His</i> details aren't important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1083016#post1083016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's exactly what he is doing, yes. I kinda get the feeling fans tend to think ALL Beasts either revel in harming people to feed, or justify what they are doing with teaching lessons -- even though my impression reading the final version of the Beast book is that only parts of them go for these options, and it's perfectly possible for Beasts to be people who just wish to have a life while harming as little people as possible. I designed Lee to be like this. And it's not like this is a unique case: Conquering Heroes mentions a Beast who didn't know about his inheritance and refused to feed much like Lee does here (he was less lucky however and ended up killed by Hero Gracia Teller). I just thought it'd be interesting to make a Beast character who handles his condition by feeding primarily through Family Dinner.</div> </div> </div> </div>Family Dinner working with a Princess seems both anti-thematic, and raising serious questions about how any other Beast feeds morally. It kills the drama of &quot;Doing the best one can as a monster&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1083016#post1083016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I thought she might be used both as an antagonist and a supporting character, or a character that would force players to question how right they are in what they are doing. But yeah, I see your point. I'll try integrating your suggestion.</div> </div> </div> </div>She could either be naive, defending monster because even they &quot;deserve a chance&quot; when the monsters are either using her, or beyond saving (even if they themselves can't admit that). Or she could realize they are a danger, but thinks they don't deserve summary execution either.<br /> <br /> Have you seen season 2 of Daredevil (Netflix)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T09:13:18-07:00","id":1083042,"title":"","content":"I think it's perfectly reasonable for there to be genuine moral conflict- monsters can be dangerous but still worthy of life. Monsters can be rehabilitated- a beast or vampire can feed with only minor harm and a demon could make fair and equitable deals. Even a spirit could gain essence in helpful, or at least harmless, ways. Do the hunters have the right to just write them off as abominations and shoot them?<br /> <br /> Some monsters are dangerous through no fault of their own- a promethean's disquiet, torment and wasteland are dangerous, but does the promethean deserve to die for them? Possessed, changelings and deviants are ultimately victims in their own right- can we ethically kill them for the crime of being in the wrong place at the wrong time, however dangerous they are now?<br /> <br /> Even on a deeper level, do monsters even have human moral obligations? Can a pain-spirit be blamed for being what it is? Is a vampire eating a human really any more evil then a human eating a cow? Why <i>should</i> we expect a millennia-old mummy to abide by modern western ethics?<br /> <br /> And even if monsters are genuinely evil and destructive, so are many people- do we want death squads going around killing them with no trial or accountability?<br /> <br /> There are more then enough questions in hunting to allow a genuine moral discussion around the ethics of killing genuinely dangerous monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T09:18:00-07:00","id":1083045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1083016#post1083016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's exactly what he is doing, yes. I kinda get the feeling fans tend to think ALL Beasts either revel in harming people to feed, or justify what they are doing with teaching lessons</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's probably because once you've taken away both the reveiling and the lessons; there's not much left that's distinctly Beast.<br /> <br /> To use Princess as a counter example. If you take away their hope and their striving to make the world better (the closest equiviliants to hunger &amp; lessons) then you'd probably get the Court of Tears (or maybe a Courtless Princess who aligns with Lacrima but stays away from Alhambra) that's a clear attention grabbing archetype for a Princess who's rejected the core premise of the game, and one that you could easily play or use as an antagonist.<br /> <br /> If you take away hunger and lessons for a Beast you get a guy who follows other supernaturals and feeds from Family Dinner; but that's not a clear and distinct Beast archetype. It doesn't have a splat page with it's own mechanics. It gets pulled in dozens of directions by other game lines. And ultimately it becomes overlooked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1083024#post1083024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Family Dinner working with a Princess seems both anti-thematic, and raising serious questions about how any other Beast feeds morally. It kills the drama of &quot;Doing the best one can as a monster&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but you could say the same about half the things a Beast could do to eat Family Dinner with a Spring Court Changeling. Romantic wingman while keeping everything safe, sane. and consensual? Driving an ice-cream truck and playing music on a hot summer day? Both let you feed on desire, both are morally sound.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T09:32:32-07:00","id":1083052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1083045#post1083045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but you could say the same about half the things a Beast could do to eat Family Dinner with a Spring Court Changeling. Romantic wingman while keeping everything safe, sane. and consensual? Driving an ice-cream truck and playing music on a hot summer day? Both let you feed on desire, both are morally sound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that simply illustrates another issue where Family Dinner can* conflict with the Drama behind a Beast's hungers.<br /> <br /> * = Family Dinner requires a certain amount of predation, I thought (contrasting a vampire's hunt vs feeding on a willing Blood Doll), and selling ice cream on a hot day doesn't really have much predatory about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T11:28:12-07:00","id":1083104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1083052#post1083052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* = Family Dinner requires a certain amount of predation, I thought (contrasting a vampire's hunt vs feeding on a willing Blood Doll), and selling ice cream on a hot day doesn't really have much predatory about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that a rule? Still, the wingman example should still qualify.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-24-2017, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T11:35:01-07:00","id":1083109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1083104#post1083104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that a rule? Still, the wingman example should still qualify.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If it's not, I'd definitely house-rule it in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T11:46:42-07:00","id":1083115,"title":"","content":"I have to agree that a Beast using Family Dinner on a Princess gathering Wisps doesn't really fit for either Beast or Princess - indeed, I've always said that the Hopeful shouldn't be within Beast Kinship at all. So Cheryl and Lee Wilson don't work as they stand. (A Sensitivity roll <i>is</i> the kind of event that qualifies as a shock AKA an opportunity for Beasts to feed ... but having Lee feed from Cheryl's moments of empathetic pain would be pretty creepy.)<br /> <br /> The better line of thought is - how can the characters be made to work? Lee doesn't actually need to be a Beast, just a monster who is inadvertently dangerous to others. Why not make him a werewolf without a tribe, a Ghost Wolf? The origin story works out almost the same way with a First Change instead of a Devouring, followed by the fanatic hunter showing up and getting Cheryl to Blossom. All that's lacking is the Family Tie effect where Cheryl's presence keeps Lee's hungers in check - and personally I'd rather see a story where the Noble has to figure out what will keep her brother sane than one where she does it just by being there and acting like herself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T12:16:45-07:00","id":1083129,"title":"","content":"I have two points to bring up since I like the idea for the sample Princess and her brother, and have a strong love for Beast the Primordial. <br /> <br /> 1) Family dinner is the safe bet for a Beast. It can be an easy way for them to manage hunger, but it NEEDS a second party's knowing (or creepily unknowing) participation. Unlike feeding regularly it gives less chance for Beasts to resolve their Hunger conditions and gain beats, and does very little to grow their Legend since they are essentially feeding off someone else's actions. For this particular character I feel it works since he's fundamentally rejected his new nature, or at least deeply mourns the metamorphosis that he's undergone. <br /> <br /> 2) If Beasts can feed off of Princesses, and consider them family, then what does that say about Princess the Hopeful? Beasts feed off of fear, loss, and revelations. Family Dinner is them supping off the residual fear inflicted upon others and the satisfaction of the ones feeding. It is not a pretty thing. It's dark, and ties into the primordial natures of the other supernaturals and their desperate needs. If anything, and hear me out, I'd argue that Beast can't feed off of the Nobility. Because Pricesses aren't family, either from their deep connection to what the Begotten call the Bright Dream, or from the unearthly alien entities that may reside within the souls of all the Nobility. Because if Princesses are kin to Beasts, then that sets a precident that can go for miles.<br /> <br /> In regards to the Monster Keeper, I would write that their brother can't feed off of them when they fulfill other's dreams. However, they can still feed off of the other supernatural denizens of the city, and by helping her brother find them she learns that just like her brother these &quot;monsters&quot; are still people. Their societies may be brutal, but that's because they're reflections of human society but with compromises made to allow them some sense of acceptance despite their new and unending hungers. It's from those interactions that she decided to champion the monsters who are just trying to get by. People who may have never even wanted to become monsters, but now must make the best of what they have. Just like her brother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 04-24-2017, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T12:34:39-07:00","id":1083138,"title":"","content":"Well, hoped too soon it seems. Didn't take long for my idea to cause issues after all. But if I may try to defend my point of view, here's the exact explanation for what needs to qualify for Family Dinner (taken directly from the book):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In order to use Family Dinner, a Beast must accompany a supernatural being as he hunts, feeds, or both. It doesn't matter whether it's a vampire thirsting after blood, a werewolf stalking an intruder in his territory, or a changeling feeding from human emotions, so long as he is actively tracking prey <b>And/Or</b> taking substenance from the hunt. The Storyteller has the final say on whether or not an activity counts, but it must involve a monster's supernatural nature or appetite directly; mundane hunting or feeding does not invoke Family Dinner. </div> </div> </div>Now, based on this description, collecting Wisps is the closest thing Princesses have from a &quot;supernatural appetite&quot; (in contrast with Sensitivity, which involves the Princess being hurt, NOT &quot;feeding&quot;), in that Princesses, from my understanding, need to keep a decent level of Wisps to feel comfortable (by avoiding the Running on Fume Condition). And unless hunting and slaying Darkspawns counts, I don't think princesses have an equivalent to hunting. So if my understanding is correct, I would say Beasts can feed from watching Princesses do good using Family Dinner, but the Satiety they would get from it would be weaker than if they were watching, say, a vampire or a werewolf.<br /> <br /> As for whether or not the Hopeful should be within Kinship or not... well, I would like to remind you we don't know for sure <i>what</i> Kinship is and how it works. The Begotten themselves believe this is because all supernaturals safe Demons are distant family members, but this explanation directly contradict the origins of other supernaturals (Father Wolf in particular), and the creators themselves have said they left intetionally ambiguous so that would be more up to interpretation. In the end, unless the creators of Princess actually have an opinion on the matter (which I don't exclude), my guess is, it's up to the Storyteller. And personally, I find it much more interesting to have Nobles <i>be</i> within Kinship, both because it makes for more interesting interactions and because it raises much more questions for a good story: what exactly is Kinship? How truly different from humans are Princesses? If Princesses really are ascended from the Dark Mother, then how did they turn out so different from the other family members?<br /> <br /> As for the fact this would give Beasts an easy way to feed morally and raise the question of why there aren't more of them doing that, even that can be made into an interesting story element: many Beasts genuinely feel its their duties to teach humanity lessons and the Dark Mother made them specifically for this purpose. How would they react to finding out there is a way to feed without that? Wouldn't they accuse the Beasts using this method to avoid their duties and be irresponsible? Wouldn't this raise conflict among Broods?<br /> <br /> I am just saying, if you look at it with the right angle, there is a lot more potential in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Now, that said, unless more than Duskage (thanks by the way^^) are in favour of my opinion, I probably will modify Cheryl's story to leave Lee's true nature ambiguous and leave it up to the Storyteller to decide what kind of monster he is. Offers more liberty, and will avoid causing controversy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 04-24-2017, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T13:10:14-07:00","id":1083147,"title":"","content":"Eeehhnn....well, while there is great story potential here there is one glaring issue that would need to be addressed. The themes of collecting Whisps just don't match &quot;actively tracking prey and/or taking sustenance from the hunt.&quot; Princesses don't hunt anything beyond Darkspawn (technically, not metaphorically.) Princesses aren't a emotional void waiting to be filled by the positivity of others (as The Kings Raven made very clear early on.) Princesses are without NEED beyond preventing themselves from being swallowed up by the pain and suffering of the world. The only monstrous thing about them (as written, not infered. There are many terrible things that are infered about Princess) is that if they doubt and compromise their ideology they may either wither away or turn into monstrosities. <br /> <br /> All I'm saying is that if you incorporate this, then it opens the doors for a lot of Princess fans to face very hard and morally grey questions pertaining to a gameline that is above all others primarily geared to be very straight forward morally. Family Dinner allows Begotten to feed off of other predators, what does that say when Princesses qualify for that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 04-24-2017, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T13:25:55-07:00","id":1083155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1083115#post1083115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to agree that a Beast using Family Dinner on a Princess gathering Wisps doesn't really fit for either Beast or Princess - indeed, I've always said that the Hopeful shouldn't be within Beast Kinship at all. So Cheryl and Lee Wilson don't work as they stand. (A Sensitivity roll <i>is</i> the kind of event that qualifies as a shock AKA an opportunity for Beasts to feed ... but having Lee feed from Cheryl's moments of empathetic pain would be pretty creepy.)</div> </div> </div> </div> While I agree that things get a little weird thematically if Beasts and Princesses are Kin* my policy for other interacting with gamelines is to take a strict &quot;what do the rules say&quot; approach, IMO it's not my place to tinker with other gamelines; that role belongs to the respective authors or individual storytellers. That said, we don't need to have rules for Beasts in a Princess/Hunter book, so the easiest solution here is to sweep the question under the rug.<br /> <br /> * Unique mechanics for some kind of antagonistic kinship on the other hand...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1083129#post1083129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">unearthly alien entities that may reside within the souls of all the Nobility</div> </div> </div> </div> Fun fact. One of my theories for why the Kingdom left no remains behind is that the origonal Kingdom wasn't on Earth at all. It was on an alien world (or possibly the moon) that's now a lifeless hunk of rock after the Darkness' victory. Spending so long trapped in the Dreamlands between reincarnations has meant that nobody except the Queen of Tears remembers this, and Tears doesn't think it's particularly important.<br /> <br /> They're really human aliens though; like the various alien-but-basically-human lands magical girls come to Earth from in Anime.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1083138#post1083138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">unless hunting and slaying Darkspawns counts</div> </div> </div> </div>It counts if you're a Champion or have dots in Tempesta. Hunting and <i>spying </i>on Darkspawn counts if you're a Seeker. &quot;Hunting&quot; for a front page story to put in your newspaper counts if you're a Seeker.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1083138#post1083138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In the end, unless the creators of Princess actually have an opinion on the matter (which I don't exclude), my guess is, it's up to the Storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well MB said above he thinks Princesses are not Kin. I think they're distant kin (like Mages) but <i>only</i> when Transformed. <br /> <br /> I also don't see any particular need to make crossover rules cannon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1083138#post1083138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If Princesses really are ascended from the Dark Mother, then how did they turn out so different from the other family members?</div> </div> </div> </div> Teenage girls have complicated relationships with their mothers; it's a law of nature.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T13:30:45-07:00","id":1083158,"title":"","content":"Again, <i>in this particular case</i>, I think leaving what Lee is ambiguous makes sense (this is about Hunters and Princesses - no need to include Beasts too, if it can be helped), and doesn't really detract form the story told or themes at all.<br /> <br /> So, next up, either a Tears or Storms Princess? Either cast a dark mirror upon many Hunters' motivations and methods. Tears for caring more about the goal, than the means - protection at any cost. Storms is about when killing the monsters makes you just as much of one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T13:31:01-07:00","id":1083159,"title":"","content":"Well, Princess <b>do</b> feel the need to act and help people because their Sensitivity makes them suffer when people are hurt, and as such urge them to react. They are not an emotional void, yes, but they do naturally feel a need to do good from my understand, and get satisfaction (through Wisps), AKA something that helps them endure despite the suffering, AKA arguably a form of substenance from it. Overall, it depend what you'd call substenance, I admit, but I feel that from a certain point of view, it does match. I mean, I didn't put it there, other examples of cases qualifying for Family Dinner include Mages collecting souls or making new discoveries; neither of these two things are something a Mage <i>needs</i> to survive, but it qualifies as substenance enough to fit for Family Dinner.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All I'm saying is that if you incorporate this, then it opens the doors for a lot of Princess fans to face very hard and morally grey questions pertaining to a gameline that is above all others primarily geared to be very straight forward morally. Family Dinner allows Begotten to feed off of other predators, what does that say when Princesses qualify for that? </div> </div> </div>Well, it doesn't bother me personally because I feel just because Princesses have some form of kinship with Beasts doesn't necessarly mean there is something wrong morally about them, even if it's a possibility raised. But yeah, I acknowledge that might be an issue. And that's why I probably will do like Vent says leave Lee's true nature ambiguous and up to the Storyteller in the end, so they can decide of their own what they want to do with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, next up, either a Tears or Storms Princess? Either cast a dark mirror upon many Hunters' motivations and methods. Tears for caring more about the goal, than the means - protection at any cost. Storms is about when killing the monsters makes you just as much of one. </div> </div> </div>Planning to do both, but need to find interesting concepts for them first.<br /> <br /> On a note, everyone agrees Cheryl should be all logic be a Sword?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T13:52:54-07:00","id":1083170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1083159#post1083159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Planning to do both, but need to find interesting concepts for them first.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Storms, just go Punisher, Magical Girl style. Stalks targets, sets up an ambush, the blows away all opposition, then de-Transforms and walks away in the chaos. Moves on to the next target, not caring about the power vacuum or secondary repercussions. She kills monsters, does deliberately target innocents - what more do Hunters want?<br /> <br /> Or... for a less obvious choice, maybe a more manipulative social provocateur? Whips up a mob, empowering them, then sets the monsters on fire while they are distracted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1083159#post1083159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a note, everyone agrees Cheryl should be all logic be a Sword?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-24-2017, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T14:03:48-07:00","id":1083172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1083159#post1083159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Princess <b>do</b> feel the need to act and help people because their Sensitivity makes them suffer when people are hurt, and as such urge them to react. They are not an emotional void, yes, but they do naturally feel a need to do good from my understand, and get satisfaction (through Wisps), AKA something that helps them endure despite the suffering, AKA arguably a form of substenance from it.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's not that being a Princess means that you feel a need to do good. It's that if you don't feel a need to do good you'll never become a Princess. Sensitivity only builds on what's already there, a pre-Blossoming Princess responds to seeing suffering by trying to help, Sensitivity just makes her much more aware of suffering.<br /> <br /> Same for Wisps. Wisps are literally a measure of the Princess' emotional batteries (for lack of a better word). They're pretty much the same as us real world humans' emotional batteries, except that Princesses' have bigger batteries and can use them to fuel magic. Have you ever felt excited before a contest, that excitement let you perform at your best, and then you felt drained afterwords? That's exactly how Wisps work, but rather than running faster a Princess might use her excitement fly or shoot fireballs and can dig deeper into their reserves.<br /> <br /> Consiqently things that recharge your emotional batteries also recharge wisps. Cheifly spending time with friends or achieving something and feeling good because those reward the player for acting in line with the games themes. So I guess you could say, it's not that recharging Wisps feels good, it's that feeling good recharges Wisps.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1083159#post1083159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a note, everyone agrees Cheryl should be all logic be a Sword?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can make a case for Clubs (monsters won't hurt anyone if they they and us find a way to exist in harmony), Hearts (We don't abandon traditions like due process just because someone isn't human), Swords (I'll follow my heart, even if it loves a monster), or even Courtless-favouring-Lacrima (I'll protect my brother, even if doing so hurts other people).<br /> <br /> It's always been my intent that Princesses would be a mixture of Courts to some extent.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T14:10:03-07:00","id":1083173,"title":"","content":"If no one else wants to do anything with the Tears I could do a write up of the one from the Union story hook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T14:21:12-07:00","id":1083176,"title":"","content":"Sure, go ahead^^ Right now I have no clear idea for the Court of Tears, though I might have one later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can make a case for Clubs (monsters won't hurt anyone if they they and us find a way to exist in harmony), Hearts (We don't abandon traditions like due process just because someone isn't human), Swords (I'll follow my heart, even if it loves a monster), or even Courtless-favouring-Lacrima (I'll protect my brother, even if doing so hurts other people).<br /> <br /> It's always been my intent that Princesses would be a mixture of Courts to some extent. </div> </div> </div>Thanks.<br /> <br /> Last thing to decide on Cheryl: should her brother still have stats? I mean, even if his template is unclear, it's possible to give him base stats and tell players to put whatever Template fits.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T14:25:10-07:00","id":1083180,"title":"","content":"I would avoid giving her brother stats- maybe a rough mention as to how powerful he should be, but the main story seed is about her, not him.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T14:43:59-07:00","id":1083190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1083180#post1083180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would avoid giving her brother stats- maybe a rough mention as to how powerful he should be, but the main story seed is about her, not him.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed - he's really just a background prop explaining how she got to be where she is. What he is, or even if he is still around, doesn't really matter. Heck, you could probably cut mention of his first name (and her last name), to make it easier for ST to slot in whatever monster the PCs might be pursuing as her brother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T15:17:23-07:00","id":1083202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1083190#post1083190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed - he's really just a background prop explaining how she got to be where she is. What he is, or even if he is still around, doesn't really matter. Heck, you could probably cut mention of his first name (and her last name), to make it easier for ST to slot in whatever monster the PCs might be pursuing as her brother.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oooo, I like that! Plot hooks are always fun. Especially if her brother has given in and become a true monster","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T06:02:15-07:00","id":1083423,"title":"","content":"Okay, got a new idea for a Noble character: a Princess with a split personality who doesn't realize her mundane and transformed states are the same person. But I am still hesitating on whether she should be Storm or Mirrors...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T06:14:44-07:00","id":1083432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1083423#post1083423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, got a new idea for a Noble character: a Princess with a split personality who doesn't realize her mundane and transformed states are the same person. But I am still hesitating on whether she should be Storm or Mirrors...</div> </div> </div> </div>Mirrors. Jekyll and Hyde split personalities are overdone. Mirrors are obstructive and egotistical, but not as lethally destructive as Storms","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T06:28:32-07:00","id":1083438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1083423#post1083423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, got a new idea for a Noble character: a Princess with a split personality who doesn't realize her mundane and transformed states are the same person. But I am still hesitating on whether she should be Storm or Mirrors...</div> </div> </div> </div>Mirrors. The side-effects of Specchio even lead to madness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T08:12:45-07:00","id":1083459,"title":"","content":"Cheryl's completed profile. Feel free to give opinions:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cheryl Wilson, the Monster Keeper</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cI don\u2019t care if he is a monster. That doesn\u2019t give you the right to kill him.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">An unfortunate truth many Hunters aren\u2019t comfortable with, but usually end up learning, is that not all monsters are pure evil. While many of them certainly are irredeemable fiends, there are just as many who really just want to be left alone, or even are trying to do good. These are the ones the Noble known as the Monster Keeper makes her duty of protecting.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Originally a young girl named Cheryl Wilson, this particular Princess grew up in a small, but reasonably happy family, with loving parents and a little brother named Lee. She was a good-hearted kid, and got along pretty fine with him, often acting protective; they had their arguments, like any sibling, but overall they were rather close.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At some point when they were teenagers, however, something changed with Lee. It\u2019s not clear what exactly happened to him, but the boy went through a transformation, and became a monster. Cheryl and her parents were confused about what happened to him, but they still tried to take care of him and live with his curse, as he would woke up crying at night and insisting he did not want to hurt anyone.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Then came the day where a man came to the home and tried to murder Lee, insisting the boy was a monster. When she saw this lunatic trying to kill her beloved little brother she had seen crying for weeks, something inside Cheryl snapped, and she went through a transformation of her own, becoming a Noble. With her newfound power, she was able to defeat the man and save her brother. Having herself gone through a supernatural transformation of her own, she grew even closer to him, and swore she would never let anyone ever hurt him for what he was.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ever since, the two siblings have become even more inseparable than they already were, and regularly travel, looking for other supernatural beings like them who get hunted down like animals. Whenever they find one, they observe from a distance, trying to figure out if they are dealing with a real monster who needs to be stopped, or a victim of the consequences. If he proves the former, they let the local hunters do their job, and might even give them tips in the case of really bad seed. If the latter, however, the Princess does everything in her power to defend the creature. She will usually try diplomacy first, but should the hunters prove impossible to reason with, or worse, not care, she will unleash all her power on them.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unfortunately for the two siblings, they often find out things aren\u2019t quite as simple and clear-cut as they wish it was. Lastly, Cheryl has found herself faced with a lot of situations where there was no clear innocent to defend: monsters who didn\u2019t mean to cause any harm but still were a threat to people despite their best efforts, or who did harm people but still had families they were trying to protect. As more and more cases like this show up, she finds it harder to pick a side.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Description:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> In her mundane form, Cheryl is a teenager or asian descent, going toward her late seventeenth. She looks attractive enough for her age, though unkempt, as she travels too often to concern herself with cosmetics. She usually dresses in male clothes, with preference for jeans and hoodies.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In her Transformed state, the Monster Keeper gains a slight tan to her skin, and her body becomes considerably more athletic. She wears a light armor reminiscent of an amazon armor, with red and gold colors and a flame motif. She is armed with a distinctive spear.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Storytelling Hints:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Cheryl is designed to push hunter players to question themselves, realize that some monsters are people and not just devilish abominations. Depending on the choices you make, she can play different roles, either as a supporting character or an antagonist. One should, however, avoid playing her as \u201cstupid good\u201d or naive- she does realize monsters can be dangerous, and understand the need for people to protect their family against them. Ideally, she is intended less as a physical opponent and more as one raising moral dilemmas for the players: she could, for example, take the defense of a monster who genuinely wishes to atone, but against whom the players have a personal vendetta due to him killing a loved one.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alternatively, if you do not wish to raise such questions, there is another use to the character; thanks to her history of helping supernaturals over her travels, Cheryl has a lot of contacts and allies among them, making her the ideal source of information if the players need something\u2026 as long as she is sure of their intentions.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Profile</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Virtue:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Just- Cheryl is aware many supernatural creatures are monsters and deserve to die, but she would rather preserve the ones who genuinely aspire to be better because she feels they deserve a second chance.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Vice:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Wrathful- while she is overall well-intentioned and nice, she is very hard to calm down once she actually get angry. Abusing her trust in particular is something she will have a hard time forgiving; should you bring her proof a supernatural has been using her kindness to deceive her, she will happily join you in slaughtering him.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Court:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Swords</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mental Attributes:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Physical Attributes:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Strength 2(3), Dexterity 2, Stamina 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Social Attributes:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mental Skills:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Investigation 3 (4), Medicine 1, Occult 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Physical Skills:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Athletic 3, Stealth 3, Survival 2 (Cities), Weaponry 3 (5)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Social Skills:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Empathy 2 (Sense motives), Persuasion 2 (3), Socialize 1 (Supernaturals), Streetwise 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Merits:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Contacts 5 (Vampires, Beasts, Prometheans, Werewolves, Sin-Eaters), Allies 2 (Changelings), Fast Reflexes 3 </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Health:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 8</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dread Powers:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Dread Attack 1, Mercyful 1, Armor of the Maiden 1, Elemental Form 2 (Fire)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Inner Light/Potency:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Enhancement:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Aspirations:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Protect innocent monsters, defend her brother, incite hunters to be more open-minded</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Integrity:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 7</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Willpower:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 7</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Size:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Speed:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 9 (10)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Defense:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Initiative:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 7</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Armor:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (1)</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Regarding Lee:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Lee\u2019s nature as a supernatural was intentionally left ambiguous in the story above, so the Storyteller could adapt him to what he wants for his story. He could be a vampire, a Beast, a werewolf, or even another unknown type of supernatural being that hasn\u2019t been identified yet. You should build him as whatever fits with the normal rules for creating a Monster in </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hunter the Vigil</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">; the key part of his character is that he is a creature of the night usually fought by hunters, who happen to have a very protective Noble for a sibling. Design him with a Potency of 2.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:10:13-07:00","id":1083556,"title":"","content":"Looks good.<br /> <br /> Regarding &quot;Generic-izing&quot; the Dread Powers, what about renaming &quot;Armor of the Maiden&quot; to Armor or Armored? <s>Just list in the description how some creatures have a hardened carapace, while others have it represented by actual armor (which covers Princesses)</s> -read the note. The notes on how Princesses only have access to most of their Dread Powers covers that it only appears when they Transform.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-25-2017, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:15:00-07:00","id":1083559,"title":"","content":"Absolutely love it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My only suggestion is to also add the plot elements that the supernatural soceties who often encourage the whole &quot;a beast I am lest a beast I become&quot; philosophy to be usually very antagonistic towards Cheryl and her brother. To them she is an interloper at best and a dangerous fire-starter at worst. For a few examples: the Lancea et Sanctum would see her as a sort of whore of babalyon, some Uratha would see her indoctrinating their Packmates from the tribes and into ghost wolves, some Prometheans would even see her as a spiritual dead end as her charges become dependent on her Inner Light rather than striving to undergo the transmutation to gain their own, and so on and so forth. That's not to say all supernaturals feel that way, but that just makes the story more interesting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 04-25-2017, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:44:28-07:00","id":1083581,"title":"","content":"Would it make sense to include an Amanojaku antagonist, or no, since they are very niche? Definitely ideal for the Merrick Institute, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:46:31-07:00","id":1083585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1083559#post1083559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutely love it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My only suggestion is to also add the plot elements that the supernatural soceties who often encourage the whole &quot;a beast I am lest a beast I become&quot; philosophy to be usually very antagonistic towards Cheryl and her brother. To them she is an interloper at best and a dangerous fire-starter at worst. For a few examples: the Lancea et Sanctum would see her as a sort of whore of babalyon, some Uratha would see her indoctrinating their Packmates from the tribes and into ghost wolves, some Prometheans would even see her as a spiritual dead end as her charges become dependent on her Inner Light rather than striving to undergo the transmutation to gain their own, and so on and so forth. That's not to say all supernaturals feel that way, but that just makes the story more interesting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure how many of them really see themselves like that outside of Vampires and Beasts. The rest have different agendas. Forsaken must hunt as part of their nature and try to act as a balance between spirit and flesh worlds.. Most Mages just see themselves as better humans rather than monsters. Changelings are trying to keep from going back to Arcadia and create new lives for themselves. The list goes on and on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T12:11:27-07:00","id":1083606,"title":"","content":"Can't comment on the doc, so adding in more comments here:<br /> <br /> For the Darkness Dread Powers:<br /> <b>Contagion:</b> looks good. Maybe make exact drawback more flexible, regarding what gets lost? Might not be needed, since it is follows a decent pattern.<br /> <b>Infectious Speech:</b> No changes necessary, since it leverages core Darkness mechanics. Might be able to made into a general Corruption power (I could see &quot;demons&quot; using a variant of it), with a little work.<br /> <b>Monster Lord:</b> This could be made more general by leaving what kind of create it can control open to definition. Darkness monsters would control Spawn, but Zombie Lords could control lesser Zombies, or Horror A control Horror Bs.<br /> <b>Poisonous Blood:</b> Great as is (maybe replace Spawn with creature, but that's just a text thing).<br /> <b>Sense Integrity:</b> Might have some overlap with Know Soul, but I'd need to check.<br /> <b>Shadow Walk:</b> Seems like it should be a generic power, but it leverages Nests (I'm probably just seeing the name and leaping to conclusions).<br /> <br /> Is there a generic &quot;Curse the Area&quot; power that Spawn could use to create a Nest? If not, what about making one? I could see powerful Wound Spirits doing something similar. Or would this just basically be the standard &quot;Ephemeral creates appropriate Resonance&quot; effect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T12:36:54-07:00","id":1083616,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Dreamland plot idea: the Wardens have somehow raised some kind of fortress increasing their local power in the Dreamlands, and are &quot;dream shaping&quot; the minds of local dreamers (using Gales?) into believing that the Dreamlands are their true home, and they are kept in the dismal &quot;dream land&quot; of the waking world by Princesses. Even some of the local Hunters have been affected, and are hunting down any Empath they can find to kill their &quot;Jailers&quot; so they can return to the &quot;real world&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T14:23:37-07:00","id":1083690,"title":"","content":"You can't comment? Weird. Did you ask me for the link to allow comments?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T18:01:54-07:00","id":1083766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1083585#post1083585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm not sure how many of them really see themselves like that outside of Vampires and Beasts. The rest have different agendas. Forsaken must hunt as part of their nature and try to act as a balance between spirit and flesh worlds.. Most Mages just see themselves as better humans rather than monsters. Changelings are trying to keep from going back to Arcadia and create new lives for themselves. The list goes on and on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I may have chosen my words poorely then. What I meant was that all supernatural societies are built around justifying their monstrous natures and necessities while trying to maintain some level of civility. As a universal rule all monsters who are a part of these societies tend to hold the &quot;holier than thou&quot; or &quot;humane monsters&quot; in contempt at best and social pariah's at worst.<br /> <br /> Forsaken look to humane ghost wolves as traitors to the cause when they're unwilling to make brutal choices to maintain the balance between flesh and shadow (too bad, if we don't sacrifice this child then the river spirit will rage out of control and hundred will die before it's bloodlust is satisfied.)<br /> <br /> Mages openly brand humane Willworkers as either Nameless or Banishers if they become to vocal about &quot;Awakened moral imperatives&quot; beyond self preservation and the preservation of Supernal magic.<br /> <br /> And Changelings...well, as you said they will do whatever it takes to remain free. Ultimately to be one of the Lost means that you must always be willing to throw those you haven't made oaths too under the bus if that's what's required to keep the Huntsmen off your trail. Even the most noble 2nd Edition Fairest may seriously consider taking that hit to Clarity if it ensures that they remain free of the grasp of the Gentle Lover of the Thousand Blades. Any Changeling who says they'd never make that choice is either lying, a unicorn amongst Changelings, or someone who's never had to make such a grim decision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellchek 04-25-2017, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T18:24:53-07:00","id":1083773,"title":"","content":"There's a difference between Holier than thou and just trying to hold on to your humanity. I don't think Changelings would hate her","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T18:35:25-07:00","id":1083775,"title":"","content":"I know well how bad Changelings can get, but I feel that they have the best chance of being &quot;humane monsters&quot;. Though yah, Nobles ain't big on the idea of &quot;necessary evils&quot;. and who knows, they could be right","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T19:07:04-07:00","id":1083780,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I definitely see Changelings and Nobles getting along surprisingly well once the veil of secrecy and paranoia has been passed. Glamour and Wisps are really similar (some might argue that Wisps are just more positively-aligned Glamour), and I think Changelings would very much appreciate having a person whose explicit stated goal is to prevent things like the Gentry from doing horrible things to people, and have the magical firepower to back some of it up. Conversely, a Princess with a few friends in the Freehold would be <i>very</i> hard to get the drop on, and could have a powerful ally or two under the right circumstances (especially if they can use their Charms to help with Catches in a pinch).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T20:10:30-07:00","id":1083792,"title":"","content":"Although I personally couldn't disagree more, my point was to encourage the avenue of play encouraging that Cheryl's enemies might prove to be more deadly to the potential players than technically she is once many supernaturals start getting wind of a monster missionary trying to get their former fellows to recant their evil ways and start hold hands and singing combaya (exaggerating.) Gives a bit more drama when all of the best intentions in the world lead her brother and family to being targeted by the angry lords of the monster societies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T20:22:25-07:00","id":1083793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1083690#post1083690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't comment? Weird. Did you ask me for the link to allow comments?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T20:34:53-07:00","id":1083799,"title":"","content":"Storms on Darklings: in a way, they get it, but only insomuch as a creature of Darkness can. Kill it anyways just to be safe","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T04:16:26-07:00","id":1083910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Probably not. </div> </div> </div>Then send me a request and I'll give you access.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T04:56:27-07:00","id":1084413,"title":"","content":"And now, I give you the concept for a Princess of Storm npc! Hope you enjoy:<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Carlin Sanders, the Green Knight</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Task Force Valkyrie is infamously known for putting special efforts in hunting down the Hopeful compared to most Conspiracies, but one thing not quite as well-known is that they have themselves the target of a Noble. A member of the Court of Storm, the ENE known as the Green Knight has been hunting down several high-rank members of the organization ever since their first appearance in Washington DC, a few years ago. The few who managed to get a good look at them describe an individual of unknown gender, fully dressed in a green and silver armor, taking down their target with military accuracy. While they have so far yet to inflict durable damages to TFV, their actions have still proven problematic, and several squads have been sent to take them down, in vain so far; to this day, the Green Knight\u2019s true identity remains a mystery, as does how they can access to restricted areas and informations most people couldn\u2019t possibly even know about.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Of course, the truth, which many people in Project Twilight have started to suspect but cannot prove yet, is that the Green Knight knows all these informations about TFV because they are working for them. Her real name is Carlin Sanders, and she is one of the main experts in charge of collecting informations for field agents through the Eye of Odin. Problem is, she did her job a little too well, and started making research on members of the Conspiracy itself. This led her to realize just how corrupt its hierarchy was; she discovered the majority of their budget was provided by vampires, and identified many Infiltrators among the higher ranks of the government. Initially, this left her in dismay and depression; she knew she couldn\u2019t just warn her superiors, as this would only get her in trouble. However, she refused to give up, and tried her best to figure out a solution. She personally believes it was this refusal to give in to despair that triggered her transformation into a Noble, granting her the power she needed to accomplish her goal.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">She immediately started using her free time to practice self-defense, get in shape and learn military Tactic, meticulously preparing herself for her quest. Once she thought herself ready, she started making a list. She knew she couldn\u2019t kill the vampires yet-- not without crippling the entire Conspiracy, but the Infiltrators could still be dealt with. And so, she started tracking down and assassinating the Infiltrators hidden among TFV\u2019s high ranks, building the reputation she got today.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To this date, thanks to Dual Identity and careful preparation from Carlin\u2019s part, nobody has yet been able to figure out she is the Green Knight. However, she knows any error of her part could break her cover, and more than likely people will find out eventually. But she doesn\u2019t care; all that matter is how much she can purify her group before this is found out.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T05:38:13-07:00","id":1084425,"title":"","content":"I'd trim the Vampire reference for Valkyrie's funding - it is contentious.<br /> <br /> How did Carlin first get involved with TF:V?<br /> <br /> Hmm. I'll need to review, but does Transformation cure/suppress personal Tilts or Conditions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-27-2017, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T05:38:45-07:00","id":1084426,"title":"","content":"What makes her a Storm though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T05:43:31-07:00","id":1084429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd trim the Vampire reference for Valkyrie's funding - it is contentious. </div> </div> </div>It is?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What makes her a Storm though? </div> </div> </div>... She is using military methods to kill Darkened with the intent to purify her Conspiracy from the Darkness, what else do you want?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T05:52:21-07:00","id":1084433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1084429#post1084429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ... She is using military methods to kill Darkened with the intent to purify her Conspiracy from the Darkness, what else do you want?</div> </div> </div> </div>More on why Radiant Princesses would disagree with her methods and on what she considers &quot;acceptable collateral damage&quot;. I feel that Storms isn't about reform, so much as hating the Darkness because it is the Darkness. They want to burn all Darkness, and consequences be dammed so long as they achieve their goal.<br /> <br /> Mx. Sanders' aspiration to reform rather than destroy TFV doesn't seem entirely like Storms. Sure, she is using military methods and killing people, but she could still just be low-Belief Radiant.<br /> <br /> but don't get me wrong, I love this character. So many plot hooks and rightly morally ambiguous. I just feel more emphasis on her fanaticism is necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T05:52:40-07:00","id":1084434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1084429#post1084429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... She is using military methods to kill Darkened with the intent to purify her Conspiracy from the Darkness, what else do you want?</div> </div> </div> </div>A lack of concern for collateral damage when taking out her targets, within reason.<br /> <br /> Example: bombing meetings/briefs Darkened officers are conducting, leaving their strung up corpses in public to send a message, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-27-2017, 08:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T05:57:32-07:00","id":1084436,"title":"","content":"Question about Dual Identity. Does it make fingerprints &amp; DNA unrecognizable","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T06:00:57-07:00","id":1084439,"title":"","content":"&quot;When an observer gets evidence that the two forms of a Princess are connected, he may try to identify her&quot;<br /> From the wiki<br /> <br /> So I would rule it makes DNA harder to recognise, but not totally impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T06:04:22-07:00","id":1084441,"title":"","content":"Oh, that. Well, I do intend to write she doesn't care about taking down innocents on the way, I just intend to put it in her description and storytelling hints. I wanted to focus on her background and motivations in that section. And I don't see her as trying to reform TFV as much as &quot;purify&quot; it (read: &quot;purify by fire&quot;). Though personally, I feel murdering people, even Darkened, without a second thought already is a reason most Radiants wouldn't agree with her methods...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Question about Dual Identity. Does it make fingerprints &amp; DNA unrecognizable ? </div> </div> </div>Probably. The description isn't clear, but it's define as making it impossible to figure out the two identities are the same person even if they have the same face, and it works even for Mages using Sympathy or Werewolves tracking them through smell, so I presume it extends to DNA and fingerprints too (especially since the Transformed state drastically changes the composition of a Princess' body to make her more of a magical being). Besides, Carlin wears a full-body armor in Transformed state and I trust she is smart enough to not put her traces everywhere anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T11:54:14-07:00","id":1084612,"title":"","content":"Is the vampiric higher-ups in TFV part of their expansion in the Compacts &amp; Conspiracies supplement? Because honestly I don't mind incorporating it if it is since that seems like a rather legitimate reason to go rouge. <br /> <br /> As for having her be Storms I'd argue that this fits perfectly because it builds a delicious parallel between Storms and TFV itself, since both are unwilling to compromise in their mission (the former being destroying the Darkness &amp; the latter being protecting the United States from supernatural threats.) Just like how TFV will accept civilian targets if they see no other alternatives and the threat is dire enough, so too do Storms see civilian casualties as a grim necessity when a clear path to victory can be achieved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T19:16:19-07:00","id":1084815,"title":"","content":"Side note, <br /> <br /> Was re-reading the Compacts &amp; Conspiracies section and something about the name for the Cold Guard's Endowment didn't quite set right with me.<br /> <br /> It's called Barring the Reservoir, and while it's effects are definitly barring magical powers the reservoir part didn't make much sense since it primarily targets the activation of Dread Powers and assists in Abjuration. I was thinking of perhaps changing it to at least Barring the Wellspring, but then more ideas came trough and wound up with a bunch of them. What are your thoughts on some of these, or should we just keep the name as is?<br /> <br /> ~ Barring the Wellspring<br /> <br /> ~ Fallow Field (or just Fallow since it's an adjective)<br /> <br /> ~ Banish Light<br /> <br /> ~ Nullify<br /> <br /> ~ Frostbite","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T19:25:17-07:00","id":1084823,"title":"","content":"Frostbite seems thematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T03:48:29-07:00","id":1084947,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Frostbite does fit with the &quot;Cold&quot; theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T07:06:06-07:00","id":1085007,"title":"","content":"Here is the current version of the Green Knight's profile. I trust you'll give me your opinions^^<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Carlin Sanders, the Green Knight</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Task Force Valkyrie is infamously known for putting special efforts in hunting down the Hopeful compared to most Conspiracies, but one thing not quite as well-known is that they have themselves become the target of a Noble. A member of the Court of Storm, the ENE known as the Green Knight has been hunting down several high-rank members of the organization ever since their first appearance in Washington DC, a few years ago. The few who managed to get a good look at them describe an individual of unknown gender, fully dressed in a green and silver armor, taking down their target with military accuracy and collateral damages worthy of a terrorist attack. While they have so far yet to inflict durable damages to TFV, their actions have still proven problematic, and several squads have been sent to take them down, in vain so far; to this day, the Green Knight\u2019s true identity remains a mystery, as does how they can access to restricted areas and informations most people couldn\u2019t possibly even know about.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Of course, the truth, which many people in Project Twilight have started to suspect but cannot prove yet, is that the Green Knight knows all these informations about TFV because they are- or rather </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>she is</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- working for them. Her real name is Carlin Sanders, and she is one of the main experts in charge of collecting informations for field agents through the Eye of Odin. Problem is, she did her job a little too well, and started making research on members of the Conspiracy itself. This led her to realize just how corrupt its hierarchy was; she discovered the majority of their budget was provided by vampires, and identified many Infiltrators among the higher ranks of the government. Initially, this left her in dismay and depression; she knew she couldn\u2019t just warn her superiors, as this would only get her in trouble. However, she refused to give up, and tried her best to figure out a solution. She personally believes it was this refusal to give in to despair that triggered her transformation into a Noble, granting her the power she needed to accomplish her goal.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">She immediately started using her free time to practice self-defense, get in shape and learn military Tactic, meticulously preparing herself for her quest. Once she thought herself ready, she started making a list. She knew she couldn\u2019t kill the vampires yet-- not without crippling the entire Conspiracy, but the Infiltrators could still be dealt with. And so, she started tracking down and assassinating the Infiltrators hidden among TFV\u2019s high ranks, building the reputation she got today.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To this date, thanks to Dual Identity and careful preparation from Carlin\u2019s part, nobody has yet been able to figure out she is the Green Knight. However, she knows any error of her part could break her cover, and more than likely people will find out eventually. But she doesn\u2019t care; all that matter is how much she can purify her group before this is found out.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Description:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> In her mundane form, Carlin is an indian woman in her thirties, with black hair she keeps into a bumb. She wears glasses and dresses in clothes too big for her, using them to hide the muscles she gained through her training and work-out; seemingly, she keeps the facade of a meek, introverted employee to hide the rage burning inside her mind.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As the Green Knight, she gets slightly taller, and wears a full-body green and silver armor hiding all her feature; the breastplate isn\u2019t even form-fitting, making it impossible to figure out her true gender, and the helmet covers the entirety of her face, with a visor covering the eyes. She avoids speaking while in this form, focusing on killing her quarries as fast possible, but should she still say something, her voice would come out as distorted, as if she was using a voice synthesizer. She is armed with a strange, spear-like gun, which she can use to shoot devastating bolts of green flames.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Storytelling Hints:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Make no mistake, Carlin might stick to her hope Task Force VALKYRIE can be brought back on track, but she is still a Princess of Storms at heart; at the end of the day, she cares more about purifying it than about purifying it. She has no problem slaughtering bystanders and field agents who get in her way on the Infiltrators, seeing them as necessary sacrifices, nor would she think twice before burning down TFV bases who have become Nests, even if this might cripple the entire Conspiracy. Part of her still would rather avoid useless victims, but she won\u2019t stop if she thinks it\u2019s necessary, because she knows her power will get weaker otherwise. She can still be reasoned with if the players are sufficiently good at social maneuvering and somehow find a way to discover her true idendity (she definitely isn\u2019t open to discussion on the battlefield), but this wouldn\u2019t be easy, and definitely would make her lose her Court. That said, trying to defeat her in combat isn\u2019t easy either- aside from her obvious powers and fighting skills, she is a cunning opponent who plays smart and knows most of the tactics used by Task Force VALKYRIE, including the ones used against Nobles.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Profile</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Virtue:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Faith- Carlin does believe in what Task Force VALKYRIE is doing, but feels the organization has to be purified in order to be brought back on tracks. She kills out of fanatical devotion more than anything else.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Vice:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Violent- she is good at hiding it behind her \u201cshy scientist\u201d persona, but Carlin has a lot of repressed aggressivity caused by her frustration over the corruption of her group, and she tends to express it as the Green Knight.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Court:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Storms</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mental Attributes:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Physical Attributes:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Strength 2(3), Dexterity 3, Stamina 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Social Attributes:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Presence 2, Manipulation 1, Composure 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mental Skills:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Computer 3, Investigation 3, Occult 3(4), Politics 2 (Task Force VALKYRIE)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Physical Skills:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Athletics 3, Brawl 2, Stealth 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Social Skills:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Subterfuge 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Merits:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Status 2 (Task Force VALKYRIE), Danger Sense 2, Fast Reflexes 3, Eidetic Memory 2, Area of Expertise (Task Force VALKYRIE)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Health:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 8</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dread Powers:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Blast 2 (Direct Damage), Armor of the Maiden 2, Dance Between the Bullets 1, Purgation 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Inner Light/Potency:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Enhancements:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Aspirations:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Kill all the Infiltrators in TFV, preserve her secret identity</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Integrity:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Willpower:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Size:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Speed:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 10(11)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Defense:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 6</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Initiative:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 9</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Armor:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (3)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Note:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Despite technically being part of Task Force VALKYRIE, Carlin Sanders is in charge of collecting information, not a field agent. As such, her sta