"value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T15:18:03-07:00","id":1087944,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's just my screen size, but I think we need to cut the size of a lot of the stuff like the example hunters and the Status explanations<br /> <br /> Also, can someone explain the origin/inspiration for the &quot;Magisters of the Economie&quot; name for me?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 05-04-2017, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T04:27:26-07:00","id":1088194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe it's just my screen size, but I think we need to cut the size of a lot of the stuff like the example hunters and the Status explanations </div> </div> </div>I feel like that's only the case for #Ammit, and I already tried. Couldn't; there is too much essetial stuff that cannot be cut;<br /> <br /> Anyway, currently I am working on the story hooks. Wondering how I should write them. Should I stick to just a quick summary like the format in Nightstalkers and Spirit-Slayers? Or a more elaborate one with Summary/Setup/Tiers like in Mortal Remains?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T05:51:33-07:00","id":1088226,"title":"","content":"Considering how different your interactions with a Noble can be depending on your Tier and specific Conspiracy, I'd suggest Mortal Remains method.<br /> <br /> More story hook setups to come as I think of them","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T05:52:38-07:00","id":1089089,"title":"","content":"Okay, guys, if any of you is familiar with Dreamcatchers (or any other fan-made Hunter supplement), could he provide a list of the new Compact and Conspiracies offered by it and a summary of what they are? That would help to make eventual additional stereotypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T07:38:37-07:00","id":1089143,"title":"","content":"Click the link in my sig.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T13:52:05-07:00","id":1089358,"title":"","content":"Thank you.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, here are the current story hooks we added to the book:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prison Break</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Summary:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A group of Nobles has assaulted a base of operations for a group of Hunters and freed several prisoners, including both humans and suspected supernatural beings. The player\u2019s cell seek to track down the escapees and (depending on their goals), assist, recapture, or destroy them, Of course, they\u2019ll also probably want to figure out what could have motivated the Hopeful into acting like this...</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Setup:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The prisoners the Nobles freed were innocent (or at least as innocent as a supernatural creature can be), and may even include friends of them they have been trying to help deal with their dark urges. Will the hunters place the priority on the mission and fight the Nobles to decide the fate of the monsters themselves? Or sympathize with them and let the Nobles handle things, at the risk of endangering the community or attracting themselves the ire of their superiors?</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tier One:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The characters know one of the captives personally, and the Nobles\u2019 assault may very well occur while the Hunters are planning their own breakout attempt. The attempts of the Hunters to bring the freed supernaturals under control are likely to be complicated by the reaction of their freed ally; are they grateful to the Nobles who freed them, concerned about the freed monsters, or even supportive of the methods used to hold the monsters in the first place? The Hunters who took the humans and monsters prisoner in the first place are a local cell themselves, and the damages they sustained in the Nobles\u2019 assault will likely drive them to desperate measures in an attempt to recapture their prisoners and regain control. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Tier Two:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The characters are experienced enough and know the area well enough to notice when supernatural beings start disappearing. Once the Nobles\u2019 breakout goes down, the cell is likely to encounter at least one supernatural among the captives that is new to them, and the Nobles, captives, and captors are likely a convergence of the supernatural on a scale that the characters are unused to. The base is well-equipped, a tempting target to compact members who want to enhance the power of their compact (or at least their place in it), and the characters will have to deal with the base\u2019s original owners and members of their own compact who want a cut of the spoils.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Tier Three:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The characters are sent by their superiors to investigate the sudden spike in supernatural activity. As they take down one escaped (and enraged) threat after another, they run into both the Nobles and reinforcements for the group that imprisoned the monsters in the first place, with each side trying to recruit them in their war against the other (unless the characters themselves are the reinforcements). The base itself is major base of operations for the group running it, and its resources and equipment may be as much the Nobles\u2019 and characters\u2019 target as the captives themselves. The captives themselves come from far and wide; the breakout was the first, but it won\u2019t be the last if the Nobles are not stopped. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Safe Haven</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Summary: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">An infestation of supernatural creatures has already caused several fatalities. At first it seems a contact of the cell is among them when they seemingly drop off the earth. But further investigation reveals that the contact was gathering supplies to some purpose. When the PCs spy a young person they don\u2019t know fighting the monsters and promising to take people to a place called Alhambra, \u201cwhere they can be safe,\u201d the cell wonders if their contact is still alive, and if they can still be found. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Setup:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alhambra is a city in the Dark World where the Queen of Tears reigns. It is a sunless, hidebound medieval-style city where lamps keep away a darkness that destroys what it envelops and spawns monsters. The people who live here eke out a miserable existence subsisting on rainwater, seaweed, and fish, all of which taste of tears and even their ghosts remain rather admit that a better existence could be held elsewhere. Some come for safety, others to serve the last living Queen of an otherwise-lost Kingdom, but few if any have ever left. Any mundane who enters Alhambra should be considered lost to the world.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tier One:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The characters in a local cell consider the area their home. They\u2019ll have to handle the double-duty of dealing with the monsters while maintaining the hope of the local community before the Noble can lead more of them astray. The job will be complicated by the fact that they may need the Noble\u2019s help to handle the incursion - what happens when they demand the right to spread the news of Alhambra to others? It\u2019s too late to save their contact, but can the characters save other people from making the same mistake?</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tier Two:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The cell has come to handle monsters, but they stay to deal with the Noble. Once they learn that their contact has been taken away, the characters may decide to take their revenge on the Noble. Depending on the compact, they may try to interrogate the Noble to learn about Alhambra, attempt to force the Noble to retrieve their contact, or put the Noble down before they can spirit anyone away. The ability of the Noble to reach such an area at all is likely to be of interest, with the characters seeking to prevent, document, or even replicate the ability for themselves. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Tier Three:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The contact was ordered to take the offer. The task was to get into this \u201cAlhambra,\u201d do reconnaissance, and get out. But they never returned, and the cell is tasked by their superiors with the contact\u2019s extraction. They can handle the supernatural monsters, but will that cause the Noble to stop making the offer? How can they make themselves enticing enough to be offered safety in Alhambra without coming off as too dangerous? And if they do get into Alhambra, how do they get their contact out? What if their contact doesn\u2019t want to leave?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 05-07-2017, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T14:03:29-07:00","id":1089368,"title":"","content":"I like your version of the Tears story better than my basic one. It leaves the question of why Alhambra is actively trying to recruit now. Is Alhambra still safe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T15:08:25-07:00","id":1089414,"title":"","content":"Alhambra does have this weird idea that one day they'll conquer the world to share the perfection of their city with everyone. There's a lot of double think involved, even the highest levels of Alhambra believe their own propaganda but they also have hard evidence that one small city cannot conquer an entire plant. The logistics are impossible. While Alhambra has magic, their front line soldiers are in the same ballpark as a first world soldier.<br /> <br /> However the return of Princesses has caused meant that the part of their psyche that wants to conquer is tempoarally ahead of the part that knows it's impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T16:08:39-07:00","id":1089444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1089414#post1089414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alhambra does have this weird idea that one day they'll conquer the world to share the perfection of their city with everyone. There's a lot of double think involved, even the highest levels of Alhambra believe their own propaganda but they also have hard evidence that one small city cannot conquer an entire plant. The logistics are impossible. While Alhambra has magic, their front line soldiers are in the same ballpark as a first world soldier.<br /> <br /> However the return of Princesses has caused meant that the part of their psyche that wants to conquer is tempoarally ahead of the part that knows it's impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Mmmm... that reminds me of the speculations about Future Crystal Tokyo from Sailor Moon. Surprisingly, a lot of people find hard to believe letting a bunch of magical teenagers with zero political experience in charge of the entire planet would be a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T16:21:55-07:00","id":1089450,"title":"","content":"Yeaaaah, here's a fun thing: not all Princesses are teenagers. They do have adults in their ranks, including ones with political experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T23:43:12-07:00","id":1089610,"title":"","content":"And the teenagers might remember political experience from their past life, or have applicable magic powers like super intelligence or magic oration. It's not all magic lasers. Though arguably the most useful thing is that the Light is a very good judge of charachter, while a Princess' life and experience can push her down dark paths Nobles are predisposed to good, as represented by the fact that you cannot Blossom without the Virtuous merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-08-2017, 05:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T07:21:42-07:00","id":1089760,"title":"","content":"Yeah, again, that's part of what I like in Princess the Hopeful. It didn't go too far in the deconstruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T07:29:11-07:00","id":1089767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1089760#post1089760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, again, that's part of what I like in Princess the Hopeful. It didn't go too far in the deconstruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually, the core books are quite sympathetic to their splat. Hunters of course have different opinions about the supernatural ones, which may not be unjustified.<br /> From a cynical point of view, Hunters would argue that the road to Hell is paved with good intentions, and the only way Alhambra could realistically rule the world would involve a massive cataclysm (WW3 anyone?) or long scale brainwashing. And that without counting what happened the last time they were in charge.<br /> Once again, I\u00b4m not justifying either side, just comparing their point of views.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 05-08-2017, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T08:05:08-07:00","id":1089787,"title":"","content":"I'm well-aware of this, I actually adressed this in the supplement if you go check the lore sections. I am just saying that in the case of Princess, the argument &quot;they are inexperienced teenagers&quot; doesn't hold much water. Granted, hunters still have plenty other reasons to not agree with Nobles, but not this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T08:20:50-07:00","id":1089798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1089767#post1089767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Usually, the core books are quite sympathetic to their splat. Hunters of course have different opinions which may not be unjustified.<br /> From a cynical point of view, Hunters would argue that the road to Hell is paved with good intentions, and the only way Alhambra could realistically rule the world would involve a massive cataclysm (WW3 anyone?) or long scale brainwashing. And that without counting what happened the last time they were in charge.<br /> Once again, I\u00b4m not justifying either side, just comparing their point of views.</div> </div> </div> </div>You realize Alhambra is presented as a villainous force in the Princess corebook too, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T15:19:26-07:00","id":1089993,"title":"","content":"Right...my phone is proving difficult again so I'm going to just have to give my best description of the Compact and Conspiracy Icons for the supplement and get feedback that way. - . -'<br /> <br /> <br /> #Ammit: As detailed and accurate a depiction of Ammit in the Egyptian hieroglyphic style facing the right, and blending seemlessly from it's left is the # sign. The # isn't colored black though, instead it's almost as if it's a window to more hieroglyphics but only within the space of the # itself. <br /> <br /> <br /> Character Risk Analysis: Fairly straight forward, a metallic plate (hinting at precious metal) with the cursive abbreviations C.R.A. engraved onto it. The inside edges of the plate are also engraved in a Victorian esc frame design. <br /> <br /> <br /> The Star of Bethlehem: A loving/joke reference to the Onyx Path's own logo. Logo picture of a hill and a winding road slowly getting smaller as it goes into the background and larger as it reaches the foreground. The key differences would be that rather than the Onyx Path moon above the road it would instead be a distant eight pointed star, and near the start of the road there would be the depiction of a parent/older sibling walking down the road towards the star with their child/younger sibling. (To avoid copyright problems all together, just remove road entirely and have the parent/older sibling and child/younger sibling standing on a low hill looking up at the centered eight pointed star.)<br /> <br /> <br /> The Cold Guard: Simple but crude depiction of a human handprint, except there's a faint trail from above the handprint like it was smeared down to it's current position, hinting that it's either a bloody handprint or the surface is very cold and slightly covered in frost.<br /> <br /> <br /> Crown Jewels: A ring of eight jewels, each distinctly different colorations and slightly different designs but interconnected by runes and script as closely taken from known Princess the Hopefull supplements representing the different Courts, even the Twilight Courts, and their unified connection to fight back the Darkness. In the center of the ring is the depiction of a medieval longsword, representing the Sworn and their faithful duty to the Crown.<br /> <br /> <br /> Magisters of the Economie: Eligant and romanticized depiction of a female Orb Weaver Spider, representing the bargain between the Magisters and the Wardens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 05-08-2017, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T03:16:08-07:00","id":1090663,"title":"","content":"Sounds cool so far, but I'll wait to see.<br /> <br /> On an unrelated note, hesitating between two ideas for the third Princess Story Hook. I am thinking either one focused on the Princesses of Storm, or a Cult led by a Princess of Mirrors...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T05:41:56-07:00","id":1090687,"title":"","content":"I like the Princess of Mirrors one. Storms are relatively easy to make stories about, but you need a bit more creativity with Mirrors","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T16:47:07-07:00","id":1090923,"title":"","content":"Okay, here's my try at it. It's just a draft, so feel free to suggest improvements:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lightbringer Cult</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Summary:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A new cult is spreading in town around a self-proclaimed goddess. They don\u2019t seem particularly dangerous so far, in that they don\u2019t practice any form of human sacrifice or unholy rites, but they still resort to a particularly impressive form of brainwashing that makes them obsessed with their leader and rely entirely on her for everything. Moreover, said leader and her inner circle definitely do have supernatural powers. It isn\u2019t long before the PCs get involved to figure out what is going.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Setup:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The cult leader is a Noble, one from the Court of Mirrors to be specific; She is genuinely trying to protect the people around her, but her ego has gotten the better of her, and she has used her power to enhance her charisma to such a level people are forming a cult around her; her inner circle are Sworn, who she granted part of her powers. She has no nefarious intentions, but as she grows more and more self-imbued, she might abuse her worshipper, forming her own harem and urging them to give up their life to serve her. How will the PCs handle her? Will they try to bring her to reason, or take her down before she becomes dangerous?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, currently working on the Sekhmet Roar tactic. Tell me, which dice pools do you think would work best for spreading meme and psychological profiling?</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 05-10-2017, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T19:13:51-07:00","id":1090962,"title":"","content":"Memes should have expression involved. And maybe Intelligence as part of profiling. Stumped past that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T16:50:41-07:00","id":1091331,"title":"","content":"Okay. I am thinking Intelligence + Computer for profiling and Manipulation + Expression for meme spreading. How does that sound?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T16:57:57-07:00","id":1091335,"title":"","content":"I like the latter one, but I leave something as complex as profiling to the capable hands of more experienced designers","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T16:59:56-07:00","id":1091337,"title":"","content":"What kind of profiling are we talking about?<br /> <br /> Depending on how you do it, it could be Science, Academics, Investigation or Computers","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T17:28:36-07:00","id":1091347,"title":"","content":"Well, that's kinda the issue. But seeing how it's #Ammit's signature tactic, and they are an hacktivist group, I guess Computer would make sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T18:51:44-07:00","id":1091375,"title":"","content":"Would making it Attribute + skill + skill make it too powerful?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T19:17:09-07:00","id":1091382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1091375#post1091375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would making it Attribute + skill + skill make it too powerful?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe just give two skills, and let the player choose? Make it Attribute + Skill <b>or</b> Skill?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T10:25:34-07:00","id":1091999,"title":"","content":"okay, we now have 3 Story Hooks for Nobles, I'd say that'll do. Now does anyone have story hooks ideas about the Darkness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T10:46:02-07:00","id":1092006,"title":"","content":"darkened politician?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 05-13-2017, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T14:35:13-07:00","id":1092102,"title":"","content":"I like the idea^^ Will see what I can do with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T20:03:46-07:00","id":1092201,"title":"","content":"A Darkness Cult that's masquerading as an Envangelist Christian church pushing a particularly toxic form of the prosperity gospel?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T03:12:58-07:00","id":1092287,"title":"","content":"Thinking about both these ideas right now^^' but in the meantime, I had an idea of my own. Hope you like it:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Redeem the castle</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Summary:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Following a recent team-up with a group of Nobles, the players have set up their new safe house into a Nest; using their magic, the Hopeful have made the Corruption temporarily dormant, leaving the place relatively safe. According to them, however, the Nest will eventually awaken again, reverting the place to its nightmarish state\u2026 unless it is taken care of in the meantime. The players have a month (this time is flexible depending on the Storyteller) to put the place to good use and accomplish good actions with it; if they do enough, they should be able to eradicate the corruption and make the safe house their once and for al.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Setup:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Princesses were genuine; the players really can purify the Nest if they do enough good with it. This would include things such as helping and saving civilians, arranging peaceful solutions with supernatural creatures who can be reasoned with, offering shelter to the poor, or even showing genuine friendship and camaraderie to each other. Even healthy romance can help. Conversely, things like torture, brutal murder, rape and unhealthy experiment might reinforce the corruption if they aren\u2019t careful. As such, this story hook is primarily a test of the hunters\u2019 morality, since it depends on them being at least somewhat good despite all the horrible thing they fight everyday. Of course, that\u2019s not to say the dormant corruption is all they have to worry about; Infiltrators and Lurkers probably are outside the Safe house, and ready to anything to recover their home before it\u2019s lost to them...<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, by the way, I got a new idea for a sample Infiltrator (Mnemosyne to be specific), but I need to ask for that: do Mnemosyne live longer than regular humans?</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 05-14-2017, 06:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T15:46:44-07:00","id":1092996,"title":"","content":"Still waiting for answers...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T02:17:50-07:00","id":1093159,"title":"","content":"I don't think it says one way or the other. So, no? But they aren't actually human anymore either...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T06:20:41-07:00","id":1093205,"title":"","content":"I'd say that they live as long as serves the plot, honestly. If your game needs an ancient Mnemosyne that's been tormenting a city for over a century, go for it. If you need the stress the Darkness puts on the body to kill them, sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T06:37:14-07:00","id":1093210,"title":"","content":"Thank you. That'll help for one of the sample characters.<br /> <br /> And by the way, here's another fiction for the book. Hope you enjoy it:<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cWhat the hell are you talking about?\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Nathan reloaded his shotgun while talking. Camille was sitting in a corner, attending to her own wounds. She could barely look him in the face. The monster had left some nasty scars on her leg, but she seemed like she would still be able to walk as long as the injury didn\u2019t get infected. Unfortunately, the same could not be said about Nathan\u2019s right eye; the creature\u2019s claw had managed to reach the hunter\u2019s face, digging through his orbit. He would survive, but unless they could find some sort of magic cure, he would never see from this eye ever again.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cI am saying I am sorry,\u201d she repeated, still avoiding his face. \u201cIt\u2019s my fault you got dragged into this.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cCut that crap. I would probably dead if not for you.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cBut I could have left it at that!\u201d she protested. \u201cI could have just walked away instead of getting you involved, and you\u2026\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cI would have probably gone fight these things anyway,\u201d he cut her. \u201cExcept even less prepared and not knowing what I was about to face. Pretty sure I am better off that way.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The girl lowered her head.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cI just never wanted these creatures to attack your family. Or to hurt you. Or\u2026\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cCamille.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Approaching her, Nathan carefully raised her face to maker her look at him in the eye.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cIt\u2019s alright. I know your empathy thing is hitting again, but trust me: I regret nothing.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>He then stood up and cocked his shotgun.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cNow get your shit together and make some magic so we can at least get out of this alive.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The girl hesitated for a few seconds, then, with a little smile, nodded. Standing up, she grabbed her wristband and made a small gesture. In a flash of light, she found herself in a blue-and-silver armor with a strange wand in her hand. Satisfied, Nathan focused, and his shotgun transformed as well, turning into some strange, elongated weapon.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cThat\u2019s more like it,\u201d he said. \u201cNow, let us show that thing what we can really do...\u201d</i></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T12:41:04-07:00","id":1093376,"title":"","content":"Calagines and Umbrae are supposed to be super flexible within the thematic confines of the Darkness, so there's really no reason you can't have an immortal antagonist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T12:57:31-07:00","id":1093760,"title":"","content":"Thank you, King Raven.<br /> <br /> Currently, I am working on an idea based on the Pongamia Coven from the Princess book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T08:16:42-07:00","id":1095139,"title":"","content":"Okay need a small piece of advice here. For the Pongamia Coven character mentionned above, I would like to make her linked to a specific town. But I am not that familiar with how cities are in the World of Darkness, soooo... which american city would you say fits the best as a town controlled from behind the scene by a cult of darkness-worshipping sorcerers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T08:21:26-07:00","id":1095141,"title":"","content":"I'd say a small town far from others. Having a whole city controlled by people as obviously evil as Darkened as opposed to any of the other supernatural powers of the world strains belief","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T11:03:55-07:00","id":1095175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1095141#post1095141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say a small town far from others. Having a whole city controlled by people as obviously evil as Darkened as opposed to any of the other supernatural powers of the world strains belief</div> </div> </div> </div>Chicago? I joke (but only barely).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T11:10:51-07:00","id":1095179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1095139#post1095139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay need a small piece of advice here. For the Pongamia Coven character mentionned above, I would like to make her linked to a specific town. But I am not that familiar with how cities are in the World of Darkness, soooo... which american city would you say fits the best as a town controlled from behind the scene by a cult of darkness-worshipping sorcerers?</div> </div> </div> </div>What general plot threads are you thinking of? A large town still needs some industry to justify its local economy. Maybe a river town? Especially if the are upstream from other people (which also adds plot options - Darkened poisoning the river, or the Cell gets a lead when bodies start mysteriously washing up downstream).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T11:17:36-07:00","id":1095180,"title":"","content":"so, does anyone mind to detail where I should place the different Compacts and Conspiracies of this supplement in my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/518231-hunters-around-the-globe\">Hunters Around the Globe</a> thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T11:37:10-07:00","id":1095186,"title":"","content":"#Ammit seems pretty Egyptian. Magisters strike me a vaguely imperialistic British (but any aggressively capitalistic region would fit). Star of Bethlehem seems pretty Protestant (as oppossed to Catholic or Orthodox), so anywhere with a strong presence in that regard. The Cold Guard could be anywhere. Crown Jewels are global.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T13:19:27-07:00","id":1095217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1095141#post1095141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say a small town far from others. Having a whole city controlled by people as obviously evil as Darkened as opposed to any of the other supernatural powers of the world strains belief</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless it's Detroit, which is nearly in ruins. (Speaking of which, Super_Dave's &quot;<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17vKlzHddpi-5PVLHy8yuonVH3rqbrawiNLDz35gBlGc/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a>&quot; is a Princess take on Detroit, getting on towards completion.)<br /> <br /> But yes, the Pongamia Covens (or the Vocation counterpart the Upas Covens) aren't really big enough to control a major city. I envision them as an extended family out in the boondocks, or an Old Money aristocratic clan that has a county or two in their coils - prosperous and somewhat influential, but not serious power brokers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T13:23:19-07:00","id":1095219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What general plot threads are you thinking of? A large town still needs some industry to justify its local economy. Maybe a river town? Especially if the are upstream from other people (which also adds plot options - Darkened poisoning the river, or the Cell gets a lead when bodies start mysteriously washing up downstream). </div> </div> </div>I guess you aren't familiar with the Pongamia Coven?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> so, does anyone mind to detail where I should place the different Compacts and Conspiracies of this supplement in my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/518231-hunters-around-the-globe\">Hunters Around the Globe</a> thread? </div> </div> </div>Agree with most of Vent0 says. And I'd suggest the Crown Jewels to have started in France (would be a nice little reference to my home country^^).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But yes, the Pongamia Covens (or the Vocation counterpart the Upas Covens) aren't really big enough to control a major city. I envision them as an extended family out in the boondocks, or an Old Money aristocratic clan that has a county or two in their coils - prosperous and somewhat influential, but not serious power brokers. </div> </div> </div>Well, I imagined it more like them manipulating the population from behind to their own interest so they could practice their rituals in peace.<br /> <br /> But wait... they have a different name in the Vocation version? Crap! I guess i'll have to find another idea, since that would give priority to one version over the other...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 05-21-2017, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T14:24:04-07:00","id":1095240,"title":"","content":"Okay after discussing with another of the writers, we more or less agreed that the Magister of Economie and the Crown Jewels both have their headquarters in France, and have been in opposition for a long time as a result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T01:21:45-07:00","id":1095403,"title":"","content":"And what about the Character Risk Analysis? the US?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T02:28:22-07:00","id":1095414,"title":"","content":"I would say US, yes. No offense to anyone american here, but I feel the USA are the country with the most firms and corrupt rich people who would need the services of such an organization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T04:13:58-07:00","id":1095434,"title":"","content":"aaaaaaand added them to thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","da