ic bring?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably block certain Social Merits (Staff, Retainer, Resources, etc.) like Status can (but, obviously, temporary and limited in scope) or maybe drop a Condition on the target representing people hating them. Like harder Social Maneuvering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T19:03:52-07:00","id":1095711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1095680#post1095680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably block certain Social Merits (Staff, Retainer, Resources, etc.) like Status can (but, obviously, temporary and limited in scope) or maybe drop a Condition on the target representing people hating them. Like harder Social Maneuvering.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe interfere with their cult's activities, in the case of Mummies and Leviathans (and possibly a few Magi or Vamps), by putting them in a more negative public light?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T03:03:31-07:00","id":1097473,"title":"","content":"Okay, here's what I could do with is so far. Your opinion, guys?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sekhmet\u2019s Roar</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (All participants): Computer 2, Intelligence 2, (primary actor) Expression 2, Manipulation 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Requires:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Dice pool:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Manipulation + Expression</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Secondary Dice pools:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Intelligence + Computer</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Description:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Only recently developped with the rise of the Internet, this Tactic takes full advantage of the web in order to destroy the public image of monsters who rely on support from communities to protect themselves. In order to accomplish this, at least two members must do some psychological profiling on a targeted group, while the others then start seeding memes, reports, and \u201cfake news\u201d designed to trigger said group\u2019s rage-button.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You can apply the success either as a social penalty to the targeted group or monsters, or temporarily remove a number of dots equal to the success in one of the target\u2019s social merit the Cell is aware of. You have to decide which effect you wish to apply before using the Tactic.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Organizations:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> This is #Ammit\u2019s signature Tactic, and their typical approach when dealing with Apophites. Network Zero also makes frequent use of it.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T04:03:22-07:00","id":1097739,"title":"","content":"Okay, guys, need your opinion on another Tactic. Which Compact/Conspiracy do you think is most likely to use this:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Divide to Reign</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (all participant) Resolve 2, (secondary actors) Stamina 2, Athletic 3, (primary actor) Wits 3</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Requires:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b> 3; </b>each participant above 3 grants a +1 bonus to the primary actor\u2019s dice pool</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Dice pool:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Wits + Subterfuge</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Secondary Dice pools:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Stamina + Athletic</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Description:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hunters who survived enough confrontations with intelligent Spawns capable of controlling Lurkers have come to realize their control over their repulsive servants tend to wear out after a while away from them. This Tactic was invented to take advantage of this weakness. Using part of their members as willing baits, the Cell tries its best to lure the creatures as far away as possible from their masters, then resort to traps and ambush to make sure he won\u2019t be able to approach them until the effect of his power ceases.This is risky, as a Spawn powerful enough to posses such an ability rarely is harmless, but when used well, this can break an organized force of Spawns into small groups of mindless monsters much easier to dispose of.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Tactic is meant to be used against Spawns with the Monster Lord Dread Power, and works in two phases; during the first one, the hunters split up, with the secondary actors doing their best to attract the Lurkers\u2019 attention and bring them out of range of their master\u2019s power. This part is particularly risky, as they take the risk of having the monsters catch up with them; any secondary actor who fail his roll ends up having to fight the targeted Lurkers. Fortunately, a larger number of hunters can lessen this problem: the number of Lurkers he has to fight is divided by the number of secondary actors taking part in this Tactic.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For the second phase, the primary actor confronts the Lurkers\u2019 master if he shows up, and does everything he can to prevent him from getting to his minions, hopefully with help from any secondary actor who could make it back. Each success on the primary actor means the Spawn is hold back for one hour; if he\u2019s hold back long enough for Monster Lord to wear off, he loses his control over his Lurkers.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Tactic is equally effective against any creature using some form of mind control or compelling effect to keep a hold over its minions, as long as you can keep them away the needed time, such as vampire thralls, or people under the effect of a mad scientist\u2019s mind control device. If the mind manipulating power\u2019s effect is based on range rather than duration, replace the hours gained for each success by yards.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T08:58:34-07:00","id":1097791,"title":"","content":"Also, new Darkness Story hook. Enjoy.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Enemy at the City Hall</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Summary:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> An Infiltrator has successfully got into a position of power. He is now using his newfound influence to help the Darkness spread, distracting the authorities away from Nests and Dark Cults while turning them against Nobles and Hunters alike. Now it\u2019s up to the players to take the twice corrupt politician down, by all means necessary.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Set up:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> A good start for this one is to define what position the Infiltrator was able to acquire. Becoming mayor seems like the most logical option (hence the Story hook\u2019s name), but he could also have become a police chief, a high-rank member of a church, a senator, or any other position where he would have influence. Consider as well if the Infiltrator has any ulterior motives. Does he hope to accomplish something beyond corrupting the entire city?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Tier One: </b>The area is relatively small, but it\u2019s still home to the characters. To successfully depose the Infiltrator (or to handle the aftermath if they try to simply assassinate them), the characters will have to gain the trust of their local community. And when they succeed, they\u2019ll have to work to make sure the replacement has their best interests, or at least the best interests of the community, at heart.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Tier Two:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Infiltrator wasn\u2019t born in a vacuum. The characters discover that the Infiltrator is but one of a small group of Darkness-infested humans, forming an up-and-coming power base. The characters must find a way to smother this group before it grows in power, and find out how the group came to be in the first place.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Tier Three:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Infiltrator isn\u2019t intentionally covering for other monsters, but the environment they\u2019ve created has made it much easier for said monsters to operate. Still, even other monsters are uneasy with having an Infiltrator at the helm. The area gains an undercurrent of intrigue as multiple supernatural groups prepare to wrest control from the Darkness and take it for themselves. It\u2019s up to the Hunters to cut through the morass and return control of the area to human hands.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T15:35:30-07:00","id":1097888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1097739#post1097739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, guys, need your opinion on another Tactic. Which Compact/Conspiracy do you think is most likely to use this:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Divide to Reign</span></span></b></div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean &quot;Divide and Conquer&quot;?<br /> <br /> Because that's the common English translation of the Latin phrase &quot;Divide et Impera,&quot; which I think may have been what the name there refers to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T18:33:38-07:00","id":1097927,"title":"","content":"Actually, yes, the one I put is the french translation^^' sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T20:45:30-07:00","id":1097961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1097927#post1097927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, yes, the one I put is the french translation^^' sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>C'est bon. Ecrire en anglais est difficile. C'est un langue plut\u00f4t \u00e9pineux.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T17:26:10-07:00","id":1099692,"title":"","content":"Thanks^^ And Good french here.<br /> <br /> Anyway, at this point, I guess all that's really missing is two Darkness sample characters. And I admit I am out of inspiration. If any of you has a cool idea, I am open to suggestion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T18:40:09-07:00","id":1099710,"title":"","content":"Define Darkness characters. Darkened, Darkspawn, Mnemosyne? Mastermind, manipulators, bruisers? Low powered or high?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T15:37:45-07:00","id":1099934,"title":"","content":"Well, we already have a Cataphractoi, so I guess ideal would be one Mnemosyne and one Darkspawn, maybe? And I would say all fairly high powered, or at least powerful enough to play a decent roll in a campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T17:56:56-07:00","id":1099969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1099934#post1099934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, we already have a Cataphractoi, so I guess ideal would be one Mnemosyne and one Darkspawn, maybe? And I would say all fairly high powered, or at least powerful enough to play a decent roll in a campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alright. I got some vague ideas on a Darkened/Mnemosyne social manipulator/mastermind. I guess it would most thematic for the Darkspawn to be the bruiser.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T04:51:13-07:00","id":1100075,"title":"","content":"Agreed. Waiting for your ideas then^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T04:07:30-07:00","id":1100765,"title":"","content":"Alright, I'm going to list out the core concepts, then work on the details later. If someone stats them out or comes up with more in the meantime, great.<br /> <br /> Subject #1: A woman who turned to the Darkness in desperation to get things done. She basically saw the world around her going to shit, and decided to fight fire with fire (or darkness with Darkness, in this case). By the end of it, her motives ended up being &quot;if you can't destroy the darkness, might as well join it&quot; - becoming a Mnemosyne. Modus Operadus would be about manipulating institutions, usually socially (she can still emulate human responses, like a well adapted sociopath). While possessing personal power in the form of Calignes, mostly it is institutional or numbers are where her threat lies.<br /> <br /> Given more time and space, I'd stat her during her Darkened days, right before the Umbrae scare (she knew enough to know what would happen if she bottomed out on Integrity with any Umbrae on her), and again as if she didn't get rid of it before bottoming out.<br /> <br /> Subject #2: A thug, turned Slasher, turned outright Monster. A darkspawn loaded up with whatever nasty powers necessary to turn him/it into a beast. Might throw in some minion control, just to deal with groups, optionally.<br /> <br /> Notes were/are in Princess form - I'll need to convert the Umbrae and Calignes to generic Dread Powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T05:12:39-07:00","id":1100781,"title":"","content":"Good so far. Funny you mentioned the idea of a darkened slasher, I used a character like that in one of my campaigns, once^^<br /> <br /> And I have already converted a few of the Umbrae and Caligines into dread Powers if that can help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T04:01:20-07:00","id":1106472,"title":"","content":"Soooo still waiting for these suggestions that were mentioned sooner?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T05:06:56-07:00","id":1106490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1106472#post1106472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soooo still waiting for these suggestions that were mentioned sooner?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, side-tracked. I'll post them this weekend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T08:41:41-07:00","id":1106580,"title":"","content":"It's alright, I understand^^ I'll wait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T16:50:56-07:00","id":1107804,"title":"","content":"Does anyone want/need a Philly write-up for this one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T17:07:15-07:00","id":1107812,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, I am not familiar with that term, what's a Philly Write-up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T17:08:48-07:00","id":1107815,"title":"","content":"In the Hunter sourcebooks, they all have a short section on the Philadelphia area. Since we did one for Dream Catchers, I figured I'd offer to do one for this book as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T03:02:54-07:00","id":1107955,"title":"","content":"Oh. Then sure, yes^^ I wasn't aware of this, but any plus like this is a welcome addition. I'd love to see you do this for this book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T16:56:30-07:00","id":1109031,"title":"","content":"And now for some quick monsters. Note that they are done in the Brief Nightmares style of Horrors (from the core Chronicles of Darkness book). <hr /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lurker Infector</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201c</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Hrrrnh. (Followed with insane cackling/coughing.)\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">These wretched husks seem pitiful compared to some other threats of the night, but can quickly explode into a serious problem is left unchecked. Like a zombie horde in movies, one of them can infect others to create more of their kind - which can then spread to others, and so on, like a virus. Cells are advised to cull these quickly and burn down whatever Nest they came from, lest they wake up to a coughing, cackling tide outside their door.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Description:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> A wreck of a humanoid, hunched over and hopping in a broken gait.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Storyteller Hint:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Spawn aren\u2019t much of a threat to a Cell, or even a decently combat capable hunter, but they represent the risk that relaxing from the Vigil can bring.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Profile</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Disposable Darkspawn hordelings. You can throw them at a Cell to keep them on their toes, content in the knowledge that if they just leave it alone, or even let one escape, you can add complications later.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Best At:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5 (Attacking the vulnerable, escaping from combat)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Worst At:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chance (Everything else)</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Other Pools:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 2</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Aspiration:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Create more like itself, Cause Pain and Grief</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Willpower/Scene:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Initiative:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">7</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Defense:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Speed:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">7</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Size:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Health:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">7</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Banes:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Jade</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dread Powers:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Contagion (Reduce Health until it reaches zero), Natural Weapons \u2022, Wall Climb</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Story Ideas:</span></span></b><ul><li>Another Cell screwed up. Rather than purify or burn a Nest down, they just collapsed the entrances to it and called it a night. Everything was fine for months until sanitation workers breached a rotting wall that bordered the Nest and some were killed by the things lurking inside. Now packs of the creatures are roaming the sewer system, and there are even rumors of them abducting pets that near the grates. Now a few children and homeless people have gone missing.</li> <li>A Null Mysteriis Cell yours is on decent terms with have learned about a type of Lurker that can spread to others by touch. Since they aren\u2019t really skilled at this sort of thing, and are recovering from a prior incident, they are offering your group a bounty to capture one of these things alive for study.</li> </ul><hr /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shadow Ripper</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201c</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Hiss!\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The are few things a Cell likes seeing less than monster appear out of nowhere right when it looks like the hard part is done. Sadly, these Lurkers seem to exist to embody that disappointment, waiting until a person\u2019s guard is down before plunging a dark blade into their unsuspecting flesh.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Description:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> A wiry humanoid figure shrouded in shadow, wielding a blade made of darkness.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Storyteller Hint:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> These Lurkers might assault a Cell as they breach a hardened Nest, or be used as assassins by more powerful Infiltrators.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Best At:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5 (Attacking from hiding, sneaking)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Worst At:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chance (Social Interaction, Complex mental tasks)</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Other Pools:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 2</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Aspiration:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Stab the unsuspecting, defend the Nest</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Willpower/Scene:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Initiative:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">7</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Defense:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Speed:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">10</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Size:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Health:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">7</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Banes:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Jade</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dread Powers:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Surprise Entrance, Shadowblade \u2022\u2022\u2022, Shadow Walk \u2022\u2022</span> <hr /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dark Tyrant</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201c</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Kill! Kill them all!\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dread generals of the Darkness, these imposing figures lord over their lesser kin and direct them against forces of the hated Light. Few Cells have encountered one of these monstrosities and survived - at least without Noble help. Though rare, a Dark Tyrant appearing in the area is usually enough to get Cells to band together, and even ally (if only momentarily) with supernaturals to take it down.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Description:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> An imposing armored giant wielding a weapon made of writhing darkness.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Storyteller Hint:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> These are for when you need a \u201cBoss Monster\u201d to end a Chapter, or even a short Chronicle. Their abilities let them command other monsters, debilitate Cells, deal catastrophic damage to single targets, or even slay whole groups of supporters with ease.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Best At:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">10 (Attacking with minions, Leading a horde)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Worst At:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2 (Empathy, Abstaining from violence)</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Other Pools:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 5</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Aspiration:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Crush agents of the Light, Sow fear and death, Create more Nests</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Willpower/Scene:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 6</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Initiative:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">7</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Defense:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Speed:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">15</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Size:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">6</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Health:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">12</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Banes:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Jade</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dread Powers:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Monster Lord \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Shadowblade \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Reap, Madness and Terror, Influence (Corruption) \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Lightstalker \u2022, Armor of Darkness \u2022\u2022\u2022</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-28-2017, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T18:42:45-07:00","id":1109529,"title":"","content":"So given how Philadelphia is, I'm gonna safely presume that there's plenty of Stormwracked in the region?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T19:22:27-07:00","id":1109547,"title":"","content":"No idea, I don't know how Philadelphia is in the other books. But yeah, I figured that would make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T23:04:13-07:00","id":1109637,"title":"","content":"Okay, general idea is that Philadelphia has been a rough city yes, but it's also a city full of it's own intrinsic hope that can seemingly never be dampened. To princesses, it's hard to gain a true hold in the city because the hunters are already the local symbols of hope in the supernatural scene. Unfortunately, the nature of the Philadelphia vigil has created a sizable population of stormwracked cells, enough that they're actually spreading out along the East Coast from Philly. The princesses are trying to make inroads, but in a bit of an inverse, to the hunters the stormwracked are their problem in their city, and they don't trust princesses to handle it. Here's the initial writeup I've got.<br /> <br /> <b>The Hope of Philadelphia</b><br /> <i>I love Philadelphia. I was shocked at what a great city this is. For me, it is the cat's pajamas. I love everything about it. I love where I live. I love the people. I have been met with such kindness and affection here.</i><ul><li><i>George Dzundza</i></li> </ul><br /> The other Hunter books have discussed at length about what many already know: Philadelphia is a messed-up city. The reality is that people don\u2019t look closely at Philadelphia, at the <i>people</i> of Philadelphia. It is a city of problems, like all cities. It\u2019s also a city of beauty, if people would care to find it.<br /> <br /> <b>Modern Nights</b><br /> Now, as far as Philadelphia goes, the princesses are at a crossroads the hunters control with an iron fist. Even as the diplomats of the Queens try to make inroads as peacefully as possible, the hunters continually stonewall them. The fact is that the hunters consider the stormwracked their own problem, but the reality is that the stormwracked may be more deeply embedded into the hunter establishment than many would like to admit, or even imagine.<br /> <br /> <b>Aegis Kai Doru: Scouring:</b> Two cells of the conspiracy are seeking out princesses specifically to steal the strange relics they use. They\u2019re also trying to capture a princess, seeking more information about this \u201cAlhambra\u201d city that keeps coming up. The AKD had a cell in Alhambra for several decades, and the cell reported constantly that a group of princesses kept trying to claim it as, \u201cThe earthly home of the true queen.\u201d What do they see in Philadelphia?<br /> <br /> <b>Ascending Ones: Guarded:</b> It\u2019s one thing when normal civilians try to end the drug trade. Supernatural creatures trying to end it, whether by burning the stock or campaigning for legalization? No, that would destroy the primary source the Ascending Ones use for their money in the Vigil. They\u2019ve seen what the Abe is doing, and they\u2019ve decided to use the Abbey in Philadelphia as their proxy, helping them stoke the tempers of hunters while quietly silencing possible peacemakers on both sides.<br /> <br /> <b>Ashwood Abbey: Excited:</b> Secretly, the Abe <i>longs</i> for a war to start with the princesses. Longing to let loose on a monster that actually looks <i>good</i> for a change, the Abe are quietly doing their best to make the situation more complicated. Whether it involves quietly supplying stormwracked cults or getting between hunters and princesses over a possible common ground, the hope for the Abe is that the other hunters will eventually tire of the princesses\u2019 \u201cempty promises\u201d.<br /> <br /> <b>Cheiron Group: Anxious:</b> Cheiron has heard the rumors of a war, but knows a war would only hurt business as the monsters go to ground while the bullets are flying. Still, the creatures of the Darkness <i>and</i> princesses are rare and valuable finds for Cheiron\u2019s cells. Cheiron is readying for a war that might happen, knowing that if it does they can capture a few transformed princesses in the early confusion to hopefully extract the implants they\u2019re looking for before they transform back into your average schmuck.<br /> <br /> <b>Long Night: Conflicted:</b> Of any group in Philadelphia, the Long Night is seeking to try and find a common ground with princesses. Only the princesses they\u2019ve spoken to have brought troubling news. It seems that they see several local churches involved in the Vigil as corrupted; churches that have claimed to have seen one of God\u2019s holy angels. If these churches are somehow corrupted, the Long Night will only be handicapping themselves by taking them out of the picture.<br /> <br /> <b>Lucifuge: Diplomatic:</b> Where others have at best informal relationships with princesses, the Lucifuge are fully opening their arms. Princesses are actively trying to stamp out evil, and so the Lucifuge see them as a new ally in their mission. Unfortunately, the Abe and an unknown party much bigger in the game are trying to sabotage a possibly peace, even alliance. The Seventh Generation want to put an end to the cults, and so are working with the princesses in exchange for their aid in finding a rumored \u201clost relative\u201d in West Philadelphia reportedly corrupting a high school.<br /> <br /> <b>Malleus Maleficarum: Divided:</b> While the Longinians are seeking out vampires and the Ambrosians are seeking witches and wizards for their knowledge, the Sisterhood of St. Wisdom and Brotherhood of St. Athanasious are finally going for each other\u2019s throats. The Sisterhood believe that the Athanasians are letting their dogmatic views on the world to ignore the reality that the princesses are trying to help. The Athanasians counter with evidence the Sisterhood itself has gathered about princesses literally stealing hope, making golems with body parts, or even killing families for being \u201cdarkened\u201d. If fairies were the start of the rope fraying, princesses might be a sword to slide it apart.<br /> <br /> <b>Network 0: Zealous:</b> The princesses are probably the only supernatural beings who aren\u2019t trying to kill NetZo cells. To the Secret Frequency, the princesses might be the first break in the mask of secrecy that covers the world. Unfortunately the leaders of the princesses aren\u2019t quite ready, and have caused the corruption of several files that were about to hit the web. This has led a few cells to draw up plans to accompany a princess on a live-stream, no more waiting for the editing to get things just right.<br /> <br /> <b>Null Mysteriis:</b> <b>Hopeful:</b> A group of princesses have continually made contact with ORAS over the years, also believing that scientific inquiry is the key to understanding the world around them. ORAS\u2019 Philadelphia branch are reaching out in hopes to finally get some real empirical data on the princesses in the strictest confidence, but the swirling rumors of a coming war have the Misties rushing to keep a potential future from being destroyed.<br /> <br /> <b>Task Force: VALKYRIE: Investigating:</b> Liberty Cell has gotten intelligence that the princesses are slow burns of a problem, so they\u2019re waiting for a while to strike a killing blow. For now they\u2019re gathering evidence. Princesses are tracked back to their mundane lives, files compiled on who they are, who they love, and even their favorite types of animal. The general profile is that princesses care, and TFV knows that if you have to strike a monster in the heart, you\u2019d better land home on the first blow.<br /> <br /> <b>Union: Doubtful:</b> In the eyes of the Union, Philadelphia\u2019s problems are theirs to solve. So if these stormwracked cults are that big of a problem, they\u2019ll handle it their way, thank you. To the older members of the Union, the princesses are a bigger danger than the stormwracked. They see the princesses are children, literally. It\u2019s one thing for a family to introduce a son or daughter to the vigil over time, it\u2019s another for a kid to suddenly get powers and think they\u2019re a crusader for good. They won\u2019t start a war with the princesses, but they won\u2019t be rushing to help if it throws down either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T04:14:04-07:00","id":1109688,"title":"","content":"A good basis, but just would like to know, have you gone check the section in the current draft describing how each Compact and Conspiracy interact with Princesses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T16:40:56-07:00","id":1109961,"title":"","content":"I did, but this is based off the situation in Philadelphia itself. Which, going by the books, is a little more intense than the &quot;general&quot; Vigil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T17:38:41-07:00","id":1109977,"title":"","content":"Oh okay, just making sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T19:04:25-07:00","id":1109999,"title":"","content":"Here's an idea:.<br /> <br /> Make the &quot;angels&quot; visiting the Long Night have multiple explanations, obviously. One is &quot;something else&quot; maybe actually angels of God or something stranger. Option 2 is a Twilight Princess, likely a Mirrors, with a religous bent, who actually wants to protect these churches and is enlisting angelic Dreamlanders to help. Option 3 are Avatars of the Queens, which is probably cue for the Nobility to decide false alarms but will really not make the Long Night happy.<br /> <br /> Option 4 ties into the setting's Big Bad Evil Girl; the angels are Dethroned familiars who managed to escape a seal placed on their mistress.<br /> <br /> The mistress still exists regardless of the explanation-she is a relatively old Shrieker who used to be a nun trainee, leading her to have a theme of Warped Holiness. Her reincarnation cycle was halted by religous hunters, preventing her from manifesting again to menace Philly-but she has enough mental influence to unconsciously evoke Philly's Spawn, even human Infiltrators, towards actions that might free her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T19:22:34-07:00","id":1110007,"title":"","content":"I like it. Though for Philadelphia, I was gonna go for &quot;Queen of Storms&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T22:54:30-07:00","id":1110064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1110007#post1110007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it. Though for Philadelphia, I was gonna go for &quot;Queen of Storms&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, better her than Mirrors, actually. Stormites are crafty when they have the opportunity to be. But I think we do need a Dethroned somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T22:59:39-07:00","id":1110066,"title":"","content":"Welcome to North Philly.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> Having said that, someone give me a good idea of what exactly a dethroned can do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 07-01-2017, 02:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T00:13:30-07:00","id":1110085,"title":"","content":"First, a Dethroned has a personal territory in the Dark World that reflects how she fell. Most of them can connect that territory to Tainted areas (&quot;Nests&quot;), which warps them further towards her personal themes. A fair number can pull people who are in those Nests into the Dark World within her territory.<br /> <br /> Second, a Dethroned can take over other Dark creatures, making them bit players in her story. A lot of them can create Darkspawn to serve them as minions.<br /> <br /> Third, Dethroned can develop a bunch of other powers, like growing to immense sizes (Size 10 at <i>minimum</i>), drawing power when people near her reach breaking points or check Sensitivity, or inflicting the Tainted Condition, either personally or through a subverted minion.<br /> <br /> One thing they <i>can't</i> do is escape the Dark World, so the main way they affect the normal world is through minions - new types of lurkers, infiltrators behaving strangely, nests becoming warped, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T10:10:10-07:00","id":1110240,"title":"","content":"So if a princess lost her hope through gang warfare and constant drug crime, would her part of the Dark World look like a worn-down ghetto covered in ruined cars, bullet holes, and drug paraphernalia everywhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T11:07:07-07:00","id":1110264,"title":"","content":"I honestly don't know. Most likely King Raven can provide an answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T11:41:59-07:00","id":1110283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1110240#post1110240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if a princess lost her hope through gang warfare and constant drug crime, would her part of the Dark World look like a worn-down ghetto covered in ruined cars, bullet holes, and drug paraphernalia everywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Post-Apocalyptiaville?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T14:12:55-07:00","id":1110350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1110240#post1110240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if a princess lost her hope through gang warfare and constant drug crime, would her part of the Dark World look like a worn-down ghetto covered in ruined cars, bullet holes, and drug paraphernalia everywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a general aesthetic, sure. But Dethroned fall through actions, not situations, so what the former Noble did in response to gang warfare and the trade in illegal drugs would color what you found in her Fortress. For instance, if the Dethroned decided the only way to stop gang warfare in her home was to murder all the gangsters, the Fortress would emphasize the urban warfare aspects: bullet holes, burned-out buildings, graffiti tags, Darkspawn fighting each other when their mistress isn't around. If she despaired and fell by self-destruction, the Fortress would show less violence and more of the results of addiction - lots of drugs and drug paraphernalia, Darkspawn acting like junkies and pushers, buildings decaying due to poor maintenance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T14:46:39-07:00","id":1110374,"title":"","content":"A Dethroned's fortress doesn't have to look like the physical world. A gang warfare themed fortress could look like you're inside grafitti; and it could be more symbolic rather than a literal world of drugs and gangs. They're based on Madoka's Witches if you want some examples.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1110085#post1110085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing they <i>can't</i> do is escape the Dark World, so the main way they affect the normal world is through minions - new types of lurkers, infiltrators behaving strangely, nests becoming warped, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can in the Dream version, but it's still something they rarely do. (I mean, why block of that option if the Stroyteller wants it?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-01-2017, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T12:57:50-07:00","id":1111382,"title":"","content":"Okay, if I understand Nests properly, here's what I think are some powerful ones for the section.<br /> <br /> <b>Known Nests</b><br /> <br /> <b>Osage Ave:</b> If spirits were the suspected start of the destruction of Osage Avenue, the area is now the largest nest in Philadelphia. Even after new row homes were built on the ruins, something dark still lurks within the very street itself. Families move in happy, hopeful, ready to begin a new day. They typically leave broken, practically destroyed by whatever they did to each other in those houses. 6221 itself is dangerous, with dark rumors that the current owner is a man bearing an uncanny resemblance to one of the members of MOVE that died in the bombing. Who or whatever he might be, Osage Ave is one location the city\u2019s hunters would rather leave alone.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairmount Park:</b> After the Fairmount Reclamation/Slaughter, the lingering stain of what had happened that night between hunters and werewolves created a lair deep inside the park. Tended to by several \u201cmissing persons\u201d turned lurkers, the nest is nestled in the trees flanking I-76. Why it has gone unnoticed for so long is a mystery, but with the \u201cnobles\u201d trying to make peace a possibility by alerting the hunters to such problems, the feeling is that maybe something has been colluding to make the nest as invisible as possible.<br /> <br /> <b>Gosnell\u2019s Clinic:</b> What was on the surface an option for young women to control their lives instead became a literal house of horrors. Gosnell\u2019s actions in luring these young desperate women in only to practically mutilate them turned the former \u201cclinic\u201d into a terrible nest that seems to spawn lurkers whole. Hunters are trying to clear out the place, but the neighborhood is in the middle of the war between the Summer Court and several hunter cells.<br /> <br /> <b>Heidnik\u2019s House:</b> The site of a sick serial killer who liked to torture his victims, Heidnik\u2019s House is the home to a nest that currently is actually being fought by a cell of the Long Night. Unfortunately for them, the house is a popular site for \u201cmurder tours\u201d, and the bile fascination the house has over such visitors has led the cell to fear that the site is actively trying to spread the dark sickness inside farther than just Philadelphia.<br /> <br /> <b>Graham\u2019s House: </b>Less well known but just as dangerous is Graham\u2019s House, where a more prolific serial killer plied his trade. Few even in the local area know about Graham though, as black serial killers are relatively unheard of in the United States. The house is allegedly haunted by the ghosts of his victims, but there are also rumors of the nearby residents acting strangely whenever the anniversary of Graham\u2019s arrest nears.<br /> <br /> <b>Lex Street:</b> In 2000, ten drug addicts were gunned down in one of the worst drug crimes the city had seen. Though not quite as \u201cmassive\u201d as the other nests, the fact is that Lex Street flies under the radar, slowly growing in power as hunters ignore it and the princesses struggle to find a foothold.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>Also, does anyone remember if any of the other books looked at the Philly mob war in the 1990s? If that's when princesses started to appear in numbers again, we can use that.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit 2: </b>Here's a character for Center City.<br /> <br /> <b>Center City</b><br /> <br /> As the neutral ground of Philadelphia, Center City is home to where the hunters and princesses try to come together to work out just how they can work together.<br /> <br /> <b>Arlan Tamm; City Councilman</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cI understand that you\u2019re looking to bring a new ballot measure on next election. Let\u2019s talk about this privately so we can keep the press from skewing things wildly out of control against either of us.</i>\u201d<br /> <br /> Arlan Tamm grew up in the district he now represents on the council. Going off to college back in 1969, Tamm returned to try and set up a better future for his city to keep his children out of the trouble he got into as a boy. Unfortunately his hopes for a better future collided with a particularly dangerous cult of the Darkness that saw children as the best way to foster the spread of their \u201cgod\u201d. Tamm didn\u2019t understand what it was they worshipped, but when he realized the truth he spearheaded the initiatives that killed one small problem from Philadelphia\u2019s streets. The amazing part to many hunters was that he did it without a shotgun or a coverup.<br /> <br /> Since then Arlan has tried to be the man on the inside for Philly\u2019s hunters. He\u2019s met with the Union on the Walnut Street theater problem, tried to act as a voice of reason for the constant war over Fairmount Park. He\u2019s attended one Abbey social event at least to try and see who they were, though afterword he can only politely but firmly decline. He\u2019d tell the Abe what he thinks of them, but then he\u2019d lose a lot of charity money for a lot of good causes. Like Ben Franklin, Tamm knows that politics is, \u201cThe art of the possible\u201d.<br /> <br /> When the princesses made their first appearances, Tamm was skeptical. \u201cToo good to be true\u201d was the phrase his cellmates heard the most often, until a princess of Diamonds came to him to discuss the problem of the stormwracked flowing out of Philadelphia. When brought to observe just how pervasive the problem was, Tamm agreed that something needed to be done. He focused on trying to root out what let the darkness gain power. He tried to get as many abandoned homes torn down as possible, to keep the schools from sliding any further into budgetary neglect from the city and state. He continues to fight, and has earned the respect of the hunters who know what Tamm is really going up against. Younger or more arrogant hunters mock Arlan Tamm for sitting behind his desk and fighting with a pen; these hunters don\u2019t know about the night Tamm had to fight off a vampire in his office with nothing more than his chair and a coat hanger.<br /> <br /> The Barrett Commission has approached Tamm, seeking him out to be their man in Philadelphia. Tamm has declined their offers as well, as he sees the Commission too nationally focused to understand the problems of his city, his people. Which is why Tamm has agreed to help the princesses.<br /> It would be small at first, city beautification and massive infrastructure efforts. Having the sheriff\u2019s office work with the DA to make sure that the people being incarcerated deserved to be in jail and prison in the first place. That was when a cell of the stormwracked he\u2019s been fighting made it their mission to try and stop <i>him</i> as well. Thankfully Tamm had done enough favors for the Philadelphia vigil that a cell from the top of the food chain was able to stop the cult from killing him.<br /> <br /> Tamm is convinced that the princesses are onto something with these cults, but for each organization he has had to use a different spin. They\u2019re idolaters for the Long Night and Malleus, while for the Union they\u2019re willing to destroy whole neighborhoods to drive out a problem that can be solved by rallying the community. Twists on words become proof to cell after cell, and while it\u2019s effective Tamm is slowly starting to worry that he\u2019s building a house of cards soaked in gasoline. Because how easy would it be for one of these cults to turn the narrative around, to suck in the cells by offering them the solution to burn it all down? Tamm is especially concerned about the cells of Network Zero in Philadelphia. The lack of concern the cults have for collateral damage combined with Network Zero\u2019s desire to put the truth to the masses makes a terrible thought to hold in the mind.<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> Tamm is what most people imagine when the words \u201cmiddle-aged politician\u201d are said. He\u2019s losing his hair, and what\u2019s left is rapidly going gray to the point where he\u2019s started dying the rest the same to look statelier. Despite his age, he still makes it a point to maintain some level of fitness; even if he works in City Hall, he must go home at night, and he doesn\u2019t plan on making it easy for any monster coming after him. His eyes still gleam with the same spark that launched him into politics in the first place, and even years of dealing with the realities of government haven\u2019t stopped him from fighting for his causes.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> Tamm isn\u2019t going to let his usual hunter prejudices blind him to a threat, especially one that\u2019s spreading <i>from</i> Philadelphia rather than coming into it. The princesses are still relative unknowns to him, but he\u2019s learning fast that the hunters for the first time might have allies instead of more enemies. He meets weekly with the \u201cambassador\u201d from something known as the court of Diamonds, though that\u2019s just about all he knows for now. Still, he\u2019s aided other hunters in getting information that has saved their lives, giving him just enough leeway to convince Joey Carcione that maybe the princesses aren\u2019t yet another problem for Philadelphia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 07-04-2017, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T14:25:48-07:00","id":1111411,"title":"","content":"Really, an evil abortion clinic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T14:30:22-07:00","id":1111413,"title":"","content":"If I understand the Darkness right, it isn't that the place is &quot;evil&quot;. It matters that there's suffering, pain, <i>hurt.</i><br /> <br /> It isn't about abortion in this case. It's about what happened in this so-called &quot;clinic&quot;. This should help get a better picture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J7YmrsY4KSY\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J7YmrsY4KSY\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J7YmrsY4KSY\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J7YmrsY4KSY </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T16:47:40-07:00","id":1111460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1111413#post1111413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I understand the Darkness right, it isn't that the place is &amp;quot;evil&amp;quot;. It matters that there's suffering, pain, <i>hurt.</i><br /> <br /> It isn't about abortion in this case. It's about what happened in this so-called &amp;quot;clinic&amp;quot;. This should help get a better picture.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J7YmrsY4KSY\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J7YmrsY4KSY</a></div> </div> </div> </div>No, the Darkness literally is evil. Not all of its servants are pure evil (yet), but it's unambiguously evil So this is an evil abortion clinic","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T05:46:18-07:00","id":1111626,"title":"","content":"The Darkness is a literal incarnation of evil; but you don't have to be an an immoral villain to create a nest. Something minor, like medical neglect (particularly if it happened over an extended period and involved wilful blindness rather than an innocent mistake) could create a minor Nest. However a talented priest could destroy a minor Taint like that single handedly with an exorcism, and it might spontaneously collapse because Taint tries to infect the souls of any human inside; and the human souls fight back.<br /> <br /> Now if the doctor was acting out of sadism; that could create a truly monstrous nest. Though it might be hard to convince many paitents to step into somewhere where you can feel the evil all around you.<br /> <br /> As a rule of thumb though, Nests tends to either be extremely potent or well hidden since all but the most potent Nests are easy to destroy. However an exceptional potent Nest would either require a highly risky strategy like astral travel into the Nest's dreams or clearing out what could be dozens of monsters; locking the place down, and then taking the time to cleanse the taint. Or just burning the entire place to the ground.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd recommend hitting the Princess books Flyboy; since it has all the mechanics for creating &amp; destroying Taint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T17:39:38-07:00","id":1111905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1111460#post1111460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the Darkness literally is evil. Not all of its servants are pure evil (yet), but it's unambiguously evil So this is an evil abortion clinic</div> </div> </div> </div>Kermit Gosnell's trial is in the public record. Compare what he and his employees routinely did to the list of actions that cause Taint, and it's clear that his clinic, in a Princess setting, has to be a potent Nest, even if you don't count abortion as murder. (Every horror story you hear about &quot;back-alley abortionists&quot; before Roe v. Wade? Gosnell topped them all.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T18:44:49-07:00","id":1111929,"title":"","content":"Well, people have been busy while I was away...<br /> <br /> Thank you Flyboy, this is pretty solid overall. I approve of this getting included in the book so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T19:54:31-07:00","id":1111954,"title":"","content":"God, it's me, Sam. Please don't let this thread devolve into an argument about abortions","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T04:04:04-07:00","id":1112036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1111905#post1111905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kermit Gosnell's trial is in the public record. Compare what he and his employees routinely did to the list of actions that cause Taint, and it's clear that his clinic, in a Princess setting, has to be a potent Nest</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming you say the real life events happened the same way in the WoD. Even if you assume that the new Taint didn't unfreeze any Darkspawn, the wrong Umbrae could crash Gosnell's career or attract attention fast. Obviously it would be athematic to say that in the WoD the events were less horrific than real life; but a Stormwracked bombing the place with staff and paitents inside could be a compromise between avoiding questions like &quot;how come nobody noticed overt supernatural evil?&quot; and thematics.<br /> <br /> Mind you, saying that real events happened in a roughly similar way in the WoD is pretty standard.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T05:53:53-07:00","id":1112067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> God, it's me, Sam. Please don't let this thread devolve into an argument about abortions </div> </div> </div>Not yet, and I would greatly appreciate if it didn't. I think we all agree these kinds of debates are best avoided here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T09:05:22-07:00","id":1112136,"title":"","content":"Quite.<br /> <br /> Having read up on<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kermit_Gosnell\" target=\"_blank\"> Gosnell </a>(TRIGGER WARNING FOR CHILD DEATH), I can say that <i>he</i> generating a Nest is not exactly a condemnation of abortion so much as a condemnation of infanticide for purely banal reasons, but if (if) we're throwing it in, we definitely need a sidebar saying &quot;This is taking no side in the abortion debate, this is a very (hopefully) unique case where the doctor was unambiguously in the wrong, killing <i>successful </i>births purely out of bloody-mindedness.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T09:45:06-07:00","id":1112161,"title":"","content":"Personally I find sidebars like that to be patronising to the audience. I like to assume the reader is able to see something as obvious as the fact a portrayal of medical malpractice is not a criticism of medicine itself.<br /> <br /> (Obviously it's vital to have all the important info is in the write-up itself, most people won't have heard of Gosnell)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T10:00:04-07:00","id":1112169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1112161#post1112161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I find sidebars like that to be patronising to the audience. I like to assume the reader is able to see something as obvious as the fact a portrayal of medical malpractice is not a criticism of medicine itself.<br /> <br /> (Obviously it's vital to have all the important info is in the write-up itself, most people won't have heard of Gosnell)</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright. It's treading near flame war territory, but we're all adults here, I think<br /> <br /> Also, wow that Gosnell story is brutal. Yep, that's a drug ring right there along with murder of infants. Pretty sure that's a frigging minor Sloth Wound (in the original sense of not stopping to think of the moral implications of your actions) even if it's not a Nest<br /> <br /> Edit: wait, isn't Philly itself a Wound? I could swear one of Leliel's contributors mentioned that in his first Let's Read. Can there be Wounds within Wounds?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 07-06-2017, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T11:27:13-07:00","id":1112240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1112169#post1112169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: wait, isn't Philly itself a Wound?</div> </div> </div> </div> I doubt a Wound would reach the size of an entire city, but parts of it: Sure.<br /> <br /> My advice is to casually pretend Wounds don't exist in Princess. Too much thematic overlap with Tainted Places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T11:29:42-07:00","id":1112242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1112240#post1112240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I doubt a Wound would reach the size of an entire city, but parts of it: Sure.<br /> <br /> My advice is to casually pretend Wounds don't exist in Princess. Too much thematic overlap with Tainted Places.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. 3-way fight between Wound spirits, Darkspawn, and Inferno demons over the same spiritual cesspit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T12:45:31-07:00","id":1112282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1112242#post1112242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heh. 3-way fight between Wound spirits, Darkspawn, and Inferno demons over the same spiritual cesspit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought Wound Spirits worked with Inferno demons of the same sin? Don't the Maeljin boss around both of them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T13:25:33-07:00","id":1112306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1112240#post1112240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My advice is to casually pretend Wounds don't exist in Princess. Too much thematic overlap with Tainted Places.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I put a Caligo in the Vocation edition that summons spirits out of Tainted areas, because I wanted the witchcraft-themed Dark cult to call up evil spirits. Thematic overlap = potential crossover.<br /> <br /> I would say that, if you're doing a Princess game that gets heavily into the spirit world, you absolutely should have Wounds on the Shadow side of the worst Tainted areas. If the spiritual ecology isn't a big thing in your game, though, there's no reason to bring up Wounds just because Werewolf says they'd be there. Same reason you don't talk about the Hedge if you don't have fae characters, or the Underworld if you're not dealing with ghosts, or Infrastructure if the God-Machine doesn't interest the players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T21:09:19-07:00","id":1112488,"title":"","content":"Anyway, I'm thinking more ideas. See, the Italian Mob launched into a civil war between the old school Cosa Nostra and the &quot;Young Turks&quot; who were more GTA-style criminals. The princesses started showing up in-numbers around the 1990s right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T05:23:12-07:00","id":1112611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1112306#post1112306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I put a Caligo in the Vocation edition that summons spirits out of Tainted areas, because I wanted the witchcraft-themed Dark cult to call up evil spirits. Thematic overlap = potential crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the mortal rules in the GMC corebook covers that nicely. (When I wrote the Coven I imagined them to be (in Mage terms) Fate/Death. Less authentic European folklore, more curse spewing wicked witch.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T07:22:37-07:00","id":1112665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1112488#post1112488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I'm thinking more ideas. See, the Italian Mob launched into a civil war between the old school Cosa Nostra and the &quot;Young Turks&quot; who were more GTA-style criminals. The princesses started showing up in-numbers around the 1990s right?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was the hope from the Apollo Landings that freed most of the Noble souls from the Dreamlands, I think. That said, I don't see a reason why Nobility wouldn't have become more active in that time. Lots of stuff was happening, plenty of reasons for a Princess to get riled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T07:39:18-07:00","id":1112670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1112665#post1112665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was the hope from the Apollo Landings that freed most of the Noble souls from the Dreamlands, I think. That said, I don't see a reason why Nobility wouldn't have become more active in that time. Lots of stuff was happening, plenty of reasons for a Princess to get riled.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the Moon Landing broke the Dreamlands trap, wasn't there still a delay before Blossomings picked up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T08:04:17-07:00","id":1112681,"title":"","content":"At least 13-18 years. A reincarnating Princess soul enters a foetus via the same mechanism that causes any human foetus to acquire a souls. Then they need to grow up before Blossoming.<br /> <br /> It also wasn't an overnight change. Some souls take longer to reach Earth than others; it's entirely possible that the rate of Blossomings is still increasing now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T09:37:05-07:00","id":1112739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1112488#post1112488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I'm thinking more ideas. See, the Italian Mob launched into a civil war between the old school Cosa Nostra and the &quot;Young Turks&quot; who were more GTA-style criminals. The princesses started showing up in-numbers around the 1990s right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Princesses start to appear in numbers when IRL magical girls become a Thing, which, yes, is the early 1990s - the Sailor Moon manga came out from 1991 to 1997.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1112611#post1112611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I wrote the Coven I imagined them to be (in Mage terms) Fate/Death. Less authentic European folklore, more curse spewing wicked witch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Authentic European folklore's more fun, IMO. Also, Pongamia's benefits don't actually do &quot;curse spewing wicked witch&quot;; they're more half-dead cannibal occultists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T14:34:28-07:00","id":1112923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1112739#post1112739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Authentic European folklore's more fun, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but I'd done it already in Dream Catchers with the Lord Stewards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1112739#post1112739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, Pongamia's benefits don't actually do &quot;curse spewing wicked witch&quot;; they're more half-dead cannibal occultists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. But I wasn't going to write an entire unique set of mechanics just for one sample antagonist. It would feel really weird to give that much disproprtoinate attention to a single example antagonist IMO.<br /> <br /> Plus there are Caligines to throw curses; it's not like they're limited to just their initiation bonuses. I'd would have suggested Second Sight, but Thamaturges are both seriously underpowered (except for their abilities to work with spirits, that's powerful) and don't have much for curses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-07-2017, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T17:57:59-07:00","id":1113013,"title":"","content":"Okay then, general rundown I'm imagining is that the mob war occupied the attention of the city's hunters, and so the region's princesses blossomed in relative anonymity. While the princesses don't care about the mob war too much, the hunters are more focused on the fact that during the war for control of the mob, several princesses were sighted &quot;feeding&quot; off the families suffering because of it. This can also lead into the small Alhambran operation to find out more about the &quot;rebels&quot; in the provinces. Could anyone write up an Alhambran princess who's studying hunters in Philly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T18:08:55-07:00","id":1113018,"title":"","content":"Why would the princesses ignore the mob war?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T18:29:25-07:00","id":1113030,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine because<br /> <br /> A: The Young Turks weren't exactly &quot;picky&quot; in their murders.<br /> <br /> B: Many of the princesses had just blossomed, so I'm gonna guess as young teens a mob war wasn't first priority.<br /> <br /> C: The infighting between the Italians was only one area of concern. You also had the Breed angling to control the turf of other outlaw MCs, black and Latin gangs on the violent rise, drugs everywhere and a shaky urban economy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T19:22:04-07:00","id":1113054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1113030#post1113030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd imagine because<br /> <br /> A: The Young Turks weren't exactly &amp;quot;picky&amp;quot; in their murders.<br /> <br /> B: Many of the princesses had just blossomed, so I'm gonna guess as young teens a mob war wasn't first priority.<br /> <br /> C: The infighting between the Italians was only one area of concern. You also had the Breed angling to control the turf of other outlaw MCs, black and Latin gangs on the violent rise, drugs everywhere and a shaky urban economy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd imagine a lot of blossoming happened to people who refused to stand by and let it all happen though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T20:31:43-07:00","id":1113078,"title":"","content":"Which is why the hunters became the symbols of the city's hopes and dreams. They were busy actually dealing with the fallout of the war and the supernatural incidents happening in the background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T21:58:31-07:00","id":1113106,"title":"","content":"So... I'm wondering, if an Oroboros is friends with a Princess, like as a Maiden, and that Princess dies, can they figure out who they are when they're reincarnated? Even better, can they maybe affect who they're reincarnated as? What if, like, this Oroboros' Princess/Maiden/wife died and they like, had a kid, who would be a Pilot Light, and made the Princess reincarnate as thier daughter so they could have their wife... oh...<br /> <br /> ...That went somewhere weird fast...<br /> <br /> ......Actually, come to think of it, this IS World of Darkness, so... DAUGHTER-WIFE-REINCARNATION PLOT, GO!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T05:40:04-07:00","id":1113198,"title":"","content":"Nice try Racoon^^ But there's one slight flaw in your reasonning. I don't know the exact mechanics of Nobles' reincarnation, but I am pretty sure a Princess' reincarnation can only be born once the previous incarnation died. It's not like a spirit possessing a different person, it's the Princess being reborn in a different life. And I am 100% sure the mother and the daughter need to be both alive at the same time at some point, otherwise the mother might have trouble giving birth. So, yeah, not possible^^<br /> <br /> Anyway back on topic, so far I like the direction it's taking for Philadelphia. We will need to figure out where to put this part in the supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T05:48:25-07:00","id":1113200,"title":"","content":"... I never said the Princess was the mother of herself, only that the Oroboros would have a child. The Oroboros could be a female pregnant by a male Princess or a male who gets a female pregnant for this purpose. I don't understand the confusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T07:31:17-07:00","id":1113238,"title":"","content":"This is an interesting topic, but I'd like to point out that there is a general Princess: the Hopeful thread for discussions like this. This thread is about creating a Hunter fan supplement for Princesses","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T08:45:26-07:00","id":1113264,"title":"","content":"The Philly appendix always goes at the very end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T10:17:46-07:00","id":1113283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1113030#post1113030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">B: Many of the princesses had just blossomed, so I'm gonna guess as young teens a mob war wasn't first priority.</div> </div> </div> </div> Unless there's something worse to attract attention than a mob war would grab the attention of Seekers and Champions.<br /> <br /> Princesses aren't your average teenagers; to qualify for a Blossoming you have to be exceptionally moral and generally proactive doing good. A mob war would definately get their attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T10:49:22-07:00","id":1113289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1113283#post1113283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Unless there's something worse to attract attention than a mob war would grab the attention of Seekers and Champions.<br /> <br /> Princesses aren't your average teenagers; to qualify for a Blossoming you have to be exceptionally moral and generally proactive doing good. A mob war would definately get their attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think Graces could be involved too with their emphasis on building and preserving communities like those being torn apart by the mob wars.<br /> <br /> Princesses don't tend to ignore mundane problems both because they are too proactive and because their main supernatural enemies are born from mundane problems","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T11:47:17-07:00","id":1113306,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that they have friends and families in those communities that are likely to be affected; and often seek mortal supporters and allies. The Democratic Princess running for office is going to team up with mortals, not the Republican Princess running against her, or the Champion who's busy fighting monsters and dosn't mind who gets in so long as they increase the police budget.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T15:41:44-07:00","id":1113424,"title":"","content":"Meanwhile, here's something local that I believe would be a good intersection between Hunters and Princesses. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mural_Arts_Program\" target=\"_blank\">The Mural Arts Program</a> has been a vital point of local pride, and Philadelphia's murals are famous the world over. The Union and first-tier cells like it because it draws out a community spirit and sense of pride in what the city is, while the princesses like it because each new mural is another strike against the Darkness in some small way and acts as a beacon of light to the local community.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>Also, got someone who did pieces for the fairy-focused fanbook on the job for pieces for this project.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 07-10-2017, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T18:02:47-07:00","id":1114835,"title":"","content":"Got two characters, consider very in-progress.<br /> <br /> <b>Heather Ingram, Tears Spy</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cYou have another option, one that doesn\u2019t involve bowing to corrupt churches or shadowy governments.</i>\u201d<br /> <br /> Heather Ingram became a princess shortly after the mob war ended, though the effects of it still washed over her life. Even before her transformation she chose to always defend her little siblings from the abuses of their father. Even driving him out with her newfound powers didn\u2019t make things easier, as their poverty from his leaving with his income and savings forced their mother to work even harder for her children. Ingram had to help raise her siblings during the day, and protect them from monsters at night. She was easy prey for Tears, and realizing there was a place they could always be safe she swore fealty almost the second she found out the option was available.<br /> <br /> Her queen issued a new task; gain intelligence on the \u201ccapital\u201d of the rebels. Each night Ingram sets out through the city, following hunters in their vigil to find out just what, exactly, they are. She\u2019s nearly been killed several times, and has justified the murders she\u2019s committed by reminding herself that she was defending herself during her duties to her queen.<br /> <br /> So far, Ingram has found that the hunters are, above all else, <i>not</i> a unified force. Acting out of a desire to protect that they know and care about, she has managed to convince several cells in the city that service to Alhambra is the best way to save their loved ones and to spread the word about the true ruler of mankind waiting to take back the planet from the monsters. This has also earned her the attention of Philadelphia\u2019s hunter rumor mill, and at least three of the city\u2019s conspiracies are already on the lookout for her.<br /> <br /> More worrying is the stormite presence in the city. Their presence is nearly overwhelming compared to other regions on Earth (WIP)<br /> <br /> <b>The Princess of the Diamond</b><br /> <br /> Philadelphia is a sports town, even though the teams never quite make it as far as the fans want them to in a season. It isn\u2019t unusual for hunters to organize around their favorite teams, using game nights as an excuse to step out of the house or reasons to get together to plan their actions in crowded, noisy settings. Spiritualists report that the power of the fans coalesces into a force of hope, joy, sorrow, and anger.<br /> <br /> Which is why no one was surprised a few years ago when reports started cropping up in the grapevine of someone going at the monsters with a bat. It\u2019s a simple tool, one easily available and untraceable, but the reports never changed. Always a woman, practically a young girl, going against monsters with a baseball bat. Then the stories got weirder; she was dressed in gaudy clothes, almost a parody of a baseball uniform. Her bat gave off light, and could throw balls of fire at her enemies. Contacts in the witch community knew nothing of any of their own doing any night vigilante work.<br /> <br /> The reality is that it\u2019s a princess. Theresa Fontaine blossomed three years ago, realizing that she had a light inside her that needed to be used for good. A lifelong Phils fan, it was obvious how she wanted to style her new \u201cpersona\u201d, as she calls it. Grabbing up as much sports gear as she could, that night \u201cThe Princess of the Diamond\u201d took her fight to the streets. She stopped a mugging in progress in Packer Park after a home game one night, and took on the threats of South Philadelphia ever since.<br /> <br /> Of course, South Philadelphia is Union turf, and already has \u201cprotectors\u201d for the Sports Complex. The territorially-minded Union has bigger problems to worry about of course, but the Princess of the Diamond is an example of how the Union in Philly views princesses; as unnecessary troublemakers who are making more trouble than they solve. Several videos have already sprouted up of a \u201ccostumed superhero\u201d that could be passed off as one of those assholes who thinks that a gimmick and costume makes a \u201csuperhero\u201d, but now that magic is involved the Union is getting antsy. The battle over the Walnut Street Theater, the war with the werewolves over Fairmount Park, and the risk of conflict with fairies in West Philadelphia is pulling the Union in every direction, and they don\u2019t need a kid with a bat and dreams of glory throwing things out of the delicate balance that\u2019s been constructed.<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> Theresa is a black-haired teenager presently enrolled in her diocese high school, popular enough to not be bullied and willing to stand up for those that are. She\u2019s reasonably fit for her age, though her parents just chalk it up to gym class rather than living a double-life as a vigilante. When on the street she prefers clothes that are stylish, but not flashy. Ever since she realized what she is, practicality is her biggest concern.<br /> <br /> (Description of Transformed clothing)<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> For Theresa, the fact is that she\u2019s a hero, a <i>princess</i>, and that means something to her. She\u2019s even close to letting her closest friends in on the new life she\u2019s living and making them sworn to the cause. Unfortunately she doesn\u2019t understand that he powers don\u2019t extend to making her friends as seemingly invincible as she is. Knocking a few muggers around and fighting the odd vampire isn\u2019t the full measure of what the world has waiting for her, but Theresa is so high up on cloud nine that she thinks all it will take to fight the deeper dangers of the world will only take some training.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T03:19:11-07:00","id":1116772,"title":"","content":"Good progress I see. Do continue, Flyboy. I like where this is going.<br /> <br /> As for me, made a few more fictions:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cIt was a nightmare, I\u2019m telling you. Just three days ago, the park was normal. Then the next day, all of sudden, it started being infected with monsters. Hideous beasts who kidnapped people, vanished out of thin air only to appear somewhere else, ambushing our cellmates. We lost many people before we finally managed to make it to the main building. But once we arrived\u2026 there, we saw the cause of all this mess. A group of veiled witches in purple dress were assembled here, doing some crazy ritual. Oh, nothing explicitly horrible- they weren\u2019t sacrificing children or anything\u2026 but I could just feel something happening while they sang their unholy incantations. They were draining the park of something, and whatever they left missing was causing the monsters to come. We attacked, but they just raised some strange shield to protect themselves from the bullets. One of them spoke in a weird language I didn\u2019t know, and they suddenly all turned into shadows before disappearing. It took us years to purge the park from the monsters, and even today it still hasn\u2019t fully recovered from the damages.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>And this, my friends, is why I don\u2019t trust the Empaths.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cLisa landed in the isolated street and pulled out her trinket. A flash of light bathed the area as she reverted back to her mundane form. She had just spent the day successfully damaging the city\u2019s drug traffic. Happy with herself, she walked back to her home.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>However, as she arrived, she quickly realized something wasn\u2019t right. Her parents seemed concerned, worried. They asked her to join them in the living room. But she didn\u2019t realize how bad the situation was until she saw the men in black suits waiting here, saying they needed to ask her a few questions about something.\u201c</i></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T02:45:07-07:00","id":1118115,"title":"","content":"So who's up for discussing the theme and mood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T18:26:28-07:00","id":1118333,"title":"","content":"I would appreciate more response here. Fine, I will open. Here is what has been suggested so far. Feel free to give opinions, impressions, and constructive criticisms.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Suggested) Theme One: A Thousand Fractious Points of Light</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">People who join the Vigil almost always have a reason for doing so. Some honestly want to make a better world. Others seek redemption, profit, or pleasure. But a cause is very easy to lose sight of. They fall into the background, becoming the justification for whatever a person feels they need (or want) to do, no matter how monstrous. People can come to feel small in the shadow of a cause; the more certain about it they are, the more certain they become that they themselves will never bring it about. They grind their lives down until there is nothing left in their life but service to a cause because it\u2019s all they have left. When such people speak of their cause, it\u2019s nothing but lip service.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Nobles are different. They carry hope in their hearts and their hearts on their sleeves. They are beings of magic charged by their Queens to build a better world, and they are willing to fight their fears and stare down their nightmares to do it. To some, Nobles exemplify light in shadows as well as any Hunter, perhaps even better. Nobles may break, but their causes do not.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To Hunters, this can be an inspiration and a threat. As the Nobles fight for their causes it forces others to re-examine their Vigils, to ask if their own causes are worth fighting for. And most do, renewing their faith in the cause; some because they draw strength from the example the Nobles set, others because they will never cede the rightness of their cause, much less to supernatural beings. When Hunters and Nobles collide, it\u2019s not just lives at stake, it\u2019s worldviews. If Hunters and Nobles can come together despite their differences, perhaps their shared efforts can truly make a better world. If they can\u2019t, the clash of perspectives can lead to wounds deeper than a knife or gun could ever leave.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Suggested) Theme Two: The Duality of Light</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The theme of </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hunter: the Vigil</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> is Light in Shadows. This refers to the lights of action and knowledge, of single points seeking their way or multiple lights coming together to form great fires, of the Hunter\u2019s knowledge that their Vigil will burn them out in time. But perhaps there is an additional meaning in play. Even though the Hunters see themselves as the light against the shadows, they must keep their Vigil in the shadows. They know if they come into the open they expose themselves to the retribution of monsters and the ostracization of mundane humanity, and so they keep to their secrecy. As time goes on, many find themselves sacrificing their humanity to keep their sanity and their Hunt going a little longer.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This situation is complicated with the entrance of Nobles. Like Hunters, the lives of Nobles has both human and supernatural aspects. Unlike most Hunters, a Noble tends to see both aspects of their lives as important. Many Nobles see their fight against human evils and human suffering as vital a mission as their war against the Darkness, and will fight on both fronts even to the point of exhaustion.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thus groups who seek to cooperate or contend with a Noble often find themselves dragged back into the public sphere, either by the Noble themselves or by their own attempts to find opportunity. The conjunction and </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">disjunction between what a Hunter does in private and what they do in public becomes as drawn into sharp relief as it is for the Noble, and mundane matters take on a new importance they often didn\u2019t before. Can a Hunter keep the candle burning at both ends, or will find themselves burnt out all the faster?</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Suggested Moods: Fragile Hope and Ready Distrust</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hunters have heard it before. Nobles are by no means the first supernatural beings who have claimed to work for the betterment of the world; some have even spoken of the betterment of mankind. Sometimes alliances form, but all too often it ends in betrayal when the differences can no longer be overlooked or the monsters\u2019 instincts and desires can no longer be ignored. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To Hunters, Nobles are no different. They may claim a higher calling, but how can a Hunter trust someone who couples a power they can barely understand with a morality they can\u2019t afford to match? Especially one who can hide their human self so deeply and who claims a mandate from otherworldly beings? It becomes so easy for a Hunter to construe a Noble\u2019s worldview and actions as monstrous, or at least detached from proper humanity. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Nobles who work with Hunters find themselves grappling with similar questions. They see what mundane humans will resort to doing to fend off the supernatural. They flinch from Hunters who see other supernatural beings as monsters to be slain, unworthy of respect or recognition. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It becomes so easy for a Noble to construe a Hunter\u2019s worldview and actions as monstrous, or at least detached from proper humanity.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Nobles and Hunters who work together combine their hopes for a better world, a world where lives can come together and respect each other\u2019s differences, even those they don\u2019t understand. They must defend that hope not just from external dangers but the threat of internal distrust and exploitation. Can Hunters find common ground with these strange supernatural beings? Or will this source of hope be reduced to ashes as too often occurs for those who carry the Vigil?</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T06:41:56-07:00","id":1118514,"title":"","content":"What about &quot;Ends and Means&quot;? At the basic level, Hunters prefer to eliminate a problem where the princesses go for what seems like a reform-minded approach. If the book is focused on hunters, it can talk about how hunters are so jaded by the Vigil, even at the start, that to them princesses are just naive fools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T18:38:48-07:00","id":1118780,"title":"","content":"Are you suggesting this as a theme or a mood? Otherwise, yes, it sounds like a good idea.<br /> <br /> Also, by the way, right now most of the mechanics and lore is complete, so we are starting to add fictions. If anyone wishes to contribute, go nuts. Post them here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T17:19:39-07:00","id":1119689,"title":"","content":"Still nothing? Okay, well if that can get guidelines, we would currently need opening fictions for the Crown Jewels, the Star of Bethleem and #Ammit. The ones for Character Risk Analysis, the Cold Guard and the Magisters have already been covered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T05:30:03-07:00","id":1119846,"title":"","content":"I agree with flyboy on this one. There's some parts (unless it's changed since I last looked) where it talks about Hunters disagreeing with Princesses because they were too closed minded about the Darkspawn; and it felt just thematically weird for Hunters to be the open minded and Princesses to be the closed minded ones. (With the exception of Storms of course).<br /> <br /> While I'm talking about weirdness, I still feel the Cold Guard's philosophy of agreeing with Princesses but disliking the Princess' use of magic (&quot;only by caring for each other naturally can humans being peace to the world&quot;) doesn't make thematic sense for Princess; because in Princess magic is thematically an excuse to let young idealistic activists play on the same level as moguls and politicians. What Princesses believe in and use magic for is what matters; not the simple fact that they have magic... But I've said this before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T06:07:37-07:00","id":1119853,"title":"","content":"Sooooo basically here, the problem is theme vs realism. Realistically, it makes sense for an anti-magic faction like the Cold Guard to develop. Thematically, the fact Princess are a metaphor for social power causes issues. Is there a way to balance that? Anyone has a suggestion?<br /> <br /> As for the whole Hunter being the open-minded ones... yeaaaah, I agree with King Raven here, having the Princesses portrayed as close-minded, especially when they typically try to cure Darkened whenever it's possible, feels... just out of character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T08:21:39-07:00","id":1119879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1119853#post1119853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sooooo basically here, the problem is theme vs realism. Realistically, it makes sense for an anti-magic faction like the Cold Guard to develop. Thematically, the fact Princess are a metaphor for social power causes issues. Is there a way to balance that? Anyone has a suggestion?<br /> <br /> As for the whole Hunter being the open-minded ones... yeaaaah, I agree with King Raven here, having the Princesses portrayed as close-minded, especially when they typically try to cure Darkened whenever it's possible, feels... just out of character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure what to do with the Cold Guard. You can only stretch &quot;magic == evil&quot; so far.<br /> <br /> As for Hunters view of Princesses, I can see them more seen as Naive - both between thinking good intentions and personal power can change the whole world, and the simplistic view of Good vs Evil.<br /> <br /> And yes, there is probably some hypocrisy going around, depending on the group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T09:27:36-07:00","id":1119915,"title":"","content":"My thought for the Cold Guard was to make them full on foils to idealism. They don't think the world can be improved, they don't think the Darkness can be pushed back. But within that confine they're still heroic types to try to defend humanity. Rather than clense nests they seal them up with the Darkness inside. Rather than cure Darkened they teach them an Endowment that removes most of the Drawbacks and help them build up Resolve to avoid sinking further.<br /> <br /> That is practically a ground up-rewrite though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T10:28:46-07:00","id":1119940,"title":"","content":"Just going to chime in with my two cents. <br /> <br /> None of the suggestions have been bad, but I do feel there's an underlying trend that's been developing: this is a Hunter the Vigil supplement about the Princess fan game, not a supplement for Princess the Hopeful about how to incorporate Hunter into the gameline.<br /> <br /> Hunter has always been about the raw human side of the Chronicles of Darkness. It's the natural progression after that first mortal chronicle where the player characters eyes are opened and can thus never be closed again. The supplements may be incomplete due to the human's lack of context for the monster's actions, but often it's a more purer perspective because it shows the ugly side of all of the gamelines when all pretty philosophy and ideology has no meaning to the Hunters. Vampires are blood drinking immortals who hide in plain sight and enslave others to sate their appetite, Mages are dangerous individuals who by dint of their phenomenal powers eventually lose touch with humanity and endanger everyone around them, and no matter how seemingly beneficent nothing good will ever come from making a deal with a Demon. <br /> <br /> At first this perspective was embraced full heartedly, and it really shows in the early writing &amp; Compacts and Conspiracies. Each Hunter organization challenges some facet of the Princess gameline's philosophy and each one is human enough to potentially become monstrous themselves (some delightfully more so than others, which also keeps with Hunter's theme.) But slowly over time it seems the discussions have become more about keeping to Princess' themes above all else. In the spirit of Hunter the Vigil I would suggest compromise is the best course of action. The Princess' in the supplement don't need to perfectly reflect the source material, and neither does the Darkness for that matter. So long as it focuse on two groups of thought that both want to genuinely help make the world a better place (albeit sometimes just for themselves, and within both camps might I add) but can't fully bring themselves to trust the other group and thus will always been in conflict then you'll be golden. <br /> <br /> Or, perhaps that's just my own belief. I'll let you all be the judge of that. <br /> <br /> <br /> P.S.<br /> <br /> We've been over this before The Kings Raven, the Cold Guard is a foil to the Hopeful because they represent that idealistic hope and magical powers aren't the only ways to make the world a better place. They are cold and often cruel pragmatism put in action, and that's what makes them interesting when compared to the Hopeful. Having their philosophy be &quot;the world can't be fixed&quot; turns that philosophy into defeatism, and besides being profoundly boring it doesn't fit with a Conspiracy that's main purpose is to remove the source of the Darkness itself: the Sorcerer Queens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 07-24-2017, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T11:45:23-07:00","id":1119974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1119940#post1119940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just going to chime in with my two cents.<br /> <br /> None of the suggestions have been bad, but I do feel there's an underlying trend that's been developing: this is a Hunter the Vigil supplement about the Princess fan game, not a supplement for Princess the Hopeful about how to incorporate Hunter into the gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's not about keeping to Princess' themes above Hunter's themes. It's about keeping to the themes of both games.<br /> <br /> Hunter is a game where moral compromises are a primary path to victory; exemplified in it's signature mechanic The Code. Princess where moral convictions are a source of strength; exemplified by the fact it's Integrity analogue is Belief (but taking it too far leads to the Court of Mirrors).<br /> <br /> Having Hunters oppose Princesses because they take a more idealistic line on how to treat Darkspawn goes against the themes of both games by putting them both on the wrong side of the argument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1119940#post1119940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've been over this before The Kings Raven, the Cold Guard is a foil to the Hopeful because they represent that idealistic hope and magical powers aren't the only ways to make the world a better place. They are cold and often cruel pragmatism put in action, and that's what makes them interesting when compared to the Hopeful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they represent cruel pragmatism? Because I see a lot in their write up about opposing magic simply because it's magic. I see some parts of Princess' like idealism &quot;The Cold Guard believes that only by caring for each other naturally can humans being peace to the world.&quot; but I don't see much cold and cruel pragmatism there.<br /> <br /> And if I'm honest The Magisters of the Ecconomy would be a better place to put cold and cruel pragmatism. Because in order for a pragmatist vs idealistic foil to Princesses to work; the pragmatists have to actually have some way of improving the world. The Magisters can do it easily. &quot;Yes it feels bad when a small all-american town dies after we move it's factories to Mexico, but the cheaper goods raise living standards for everyone and on balance it does more good than harm&quot;. (actual argument common to real life Magister types).<br /> <br /> You could rewrite the Cold Guard to include lots of socio-ecconomic influence and to actually emphasise cruel pragmatism; the underneath the glossy PR the Magisters are already there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T11:57:35-07:00","id":1119978,"title":"","content":"Wait a minute, wasn't it you who we-wrote that part of the Cold Guards write up? Because they were more like the former originally. If not, whoever changed the doc made the focus of the Guard more on enduring hardships that opposing the Darkness by destroying it's source. Either way, the Cold Guard embody pragmatism because they &quot;see past the short term fix&quot; that is kill the monster and instead target what they believe to be the source of the problem so there won't be any more monsters (arguably foolishly, but from the mortal perspective where there are Nobles there are Nests.)<br /> <br /> The Magisters on the other hand question Princess' ideology that only the virtuous can make a difference in the world. The Magisters flout that logic by being despicable, self interested scumbags who provide jobs for millions and provide more for the general community that a single Princess can do within a year's time. <br /> <br /> The difference is that the Cold Guard believes they're doing the right thing, it's just the necessary evil in order to free the world from the Sorcerer Queen's endless war for humanity's heart and mind. The Magisters are shamelessly doing it for themselves, because f$&amp;k those little bastards. They probably haven't done an honest day's work in their life, how come they get magical powers from on high? They could put those powers waaaay to better use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 07-24-2017, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T12:00:45-07:00","id":1119981,"title":"","content":"Don't worry, Duskage, I still try to keep the Hunter perspective. That said, I want the book to seem like it could believably fit in the same setting, which is why I try to make sure Nobles and the Darkness are not <i>too</i> different from how they are described in the main book. For example, before that there was a discussion on how it seems weird when you know everything about Princess that Hunters could make a Princess go Dethroned by accident; I think that can pass because we don't know the whole story, and the Hunters themselve don't know everything about <i>how</i> Princesses dethrone, so it's alright to keep it. On the other hand, if I went to give Princesses and Darkspawns ability they couldn't possibly have nor be mistaken for having, that would be problematic.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, King Raven has difficulty seeing the book with a Hunter perspective (something he admits himself), but given he is better-versed in Princess, he can't be blamed for that^^<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Cold Guard and the Magisters... yeah, pretty much. I think they are both distinct interesting foils to the Nobles; the Cold Guard are cold, pragmatic, close-minded but well-intentioned extremists. The Magisters, meanwhile, are trying to BE Nobles and envious of their powers, but end up as a grotesque, twisted parody of the thing (And I love them for it, in a love to hate kind of way), because they lack what truly make Nobles: the very virtue they reject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 07-24-2017, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T12:06:02-07:00","id":1119984,"title":"","content":"That's why I'm here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T12:25:19-07:00","id":1119997,"title":"","content":"Because you're better-versed into Hunters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T12:30:47-07:00","id":1120002,"title":"","content":"Kings, you field that one?<br /> <br /> Also, Null Mysteriis character for West Philly.<br /> <br /> <b>West Philadelphia</b><br /> <br /> Aside from the current stirrings of war with the fairies, most of West Philadelphia is relatively calm compared to the rest of the city east of the Schuylkill. Unfortunately, this peace may not last very long.<br /> <br /> <b>Dr. Douglas Palmer, Null Mysteriis Zoologist</b><br /> <br /> \u201c<i>Everyone forgets that the animal kingdom is just as vulnerable as the rest of us.</i>\u201d<br /> <br /> Dr. Palmer has been working at the Philadelphia Zoo for ten years now, occasionally leaving to make an expedition or conference with his close friend, Dr. Malcom Yee. Palmer didn\u2019t learn about the stranger things in the shadows until three years ago however, when the zoo was in danger of losing Tony, their Southern White Rhinoceros. Tony was supposedly sick, but none of the vets could figure out what the problem was. Determined to uncover the cause, Palmer camped out that night with Yee, hoping his friend could help him figure out just was wrong with Tony. That was when the <i>thing</i> slithered over the walls of the enclosure.<br /> <br /> Malcom guided Palmer to ORAS, and from there Palmer has taken it upon himself to both guard the zoo from the predations of monsters trying to use the zoo\u2019s animals as resources and to study what he might come across. He found that for years, the zoo had been a veritable candy store for the unknown in Philadelphia. Gorilla blood, lion fur, lizard scales, resources for paranormal \u201crecipes\u201d capable of doing anything from imbuing a man with the sprinting speed of a cheetah to venom of a cottonmouth. The zoo had been lucky though, the animals were too precious to outright kill. Still, Palmer took up his protection of the zoo, and has been consulted by ORAS on several cryptozoological finds since Yee\u2019s disappearance.<br /> <br /> Worrying incidents have Palmer on edge now. Someone has been trying to break into the zoo, he finds the evidence each morning when he has his daily talks with the morning staff. Scratch marks, locks jimmied, and gouges in the landscaping outside several exhibits. The animals are all healthy however, none are showing any odd or adverse symptoms that could indicate a paranormal incident in the making. Still, Palmer is worried, and has considered the possibility that someone is through with the zoo being under hunter control.<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> Palmer is just over 40, but his work has kept him healthy enough; sometimes you need to wrestle the animal down when it gets riled for it\u2019s own good. His hair is lightly salted, and a gleaming enthusiasm for the animals always keeps his eyes lit brightly.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> Palmer\u2019s role in the Vigil is one few hunters remember to care about. Of course, this worries him greatly, since he wonders just how long it\u2019s been since someone realized that creatures of the darkness were stalking his zoo and the animals under his charge. He doesn\u2019t know who or what is trying to get at the animals, but he\u2019s also curious as to what\u2019s stopping them. They\u2019re clearly able to enter the zoo, but why aren\u2019t the animals being harmed yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T12:32:42-07:00","id":1120005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120002#post1120002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kings, you field that one?</div> </div> </div> </div> No comment on who's better <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1119981#post1119981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Admittedly, King Raven has difficulty seeing the book with a Hunter perspective (something he admits himself), but given he is better-versed in Princess, he can't be blamed for that^^</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I was just talking about The Crown Jewels - which being an organisation made up exclusively by splats that originate in Princesses is hard for me to see through a hunter lens.<br /> <br /> Apart from that I've got no issue. I've written tons of hunter material myself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1119978#post1119978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait a minute, wasn't it you who we-wrote that part of the Cold Guards write up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Which part? The bit I quoted:<br /> <br /> &quot;The Cold Guard believes that only by caring for each other naturally can humans being peace to the world.&quot;<br /> <br /> That definitely wasn't me. I might have made some suggestions to the cold guard on the doc, I can't remember if I did or not, but if I did I know I would have massively restrained myself because there wasn't a consensus for making them about enduring rather than defeating Darkness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1119978#post1119978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either way, the Cold Guard embody pragmatism because they &quot;see past the short term fix&quot; that is kill the monster and instead target what they believe to be the source of the problem so there won't be any more monsters (arguably foolishly, but from the mortal perspective where there are Nobles there are Nests.)</div> </div> </div> </div> That's not pragmatism by any definition of the world. Long term vs short term is a <b>completely</b> different debate to idealism vs pragmatism.<br /> <br /> What's more you can't make a long term foil to short term Princesses because Princesses are not short term thinkers. You can make a pragmatic foil to idealists because Princesses are idealists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1119978#post1119978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and provide more for the general community that a single Princess can do within a year's time.</div> </div> </div> </div> Are you exaggerating for emphasis or do you really think that's true?<br /> <br /> Because it's not. Sure some Princesses who do nothing more than patrol the night punching monsters. There are other Princesses who're CEOs and business women who's skill at running a company is literally superhuman; and they do it while maintaining impeccable ethics. There's even an entire Z-Splat based around economic work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1119978#post1119978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference is that the Cold Guard believes they're doing the right thing, it's just the necessary evil in order to free the world from the Sorcerer Queen's endless war for humanity's heart and mind. The Magisters are shamelessly doing it for themselves, because f$&amp;k those little bastards.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is that the Magisters selfishness and cold pragmatic approach to doing good is a foil to Princesses. The Cold Guard's &quot;seeing past the short term fix&quot; are not a foil to Princesses.<br /> <br /> That's the issue with the Cold Guard.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T12:58:47-07:00","id":1120026,"title":"","content":"@The Kings Raven,<br /> <br /> I'm quite certain pragmatism is the right word for the Cold Guard, but I have been using the improper application of it within my argument. Allow me to rephrase: the quickest and most efficient way to end the threat of the Darkness is to eliminate it's source. The most efficient way to resist the enchantments of the Queens and their deluded brainwashed servants is to want for nothing and embrace the suffering and compromise the Nobility so whole heartedly reject. <br /> <br /> Now in regards to the Noble CEOs...even I see the futility of arguing with one of the creators of the gameline, so I'll just say that when I wrote that originally I imagined any Princess who dared to try and make a difference in the corporate world quickly burned out to nothingness or went super Dethroned thanks to the absolutely necessary dehumanization that comes from corporate capitalism. It appears I was wrong so I retract that statement in regards to the Magisters. <br /> <br /> <br /> @Darinas,<br /> <br /> Thank you for your concern. Like I said the ideas floating around are good, I just might be a little hyper sensitive *drumsnare* to keeping Hunter's themes important in the supplement. I'm very glad my fear is misplaced. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 07-24-2017, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T13:22:49-07:00","id":1120042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120026#post1120026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm quite certain pragmatism is the right word for the Cold Guard, but I have been using the improper application of it within my argument. Allow me to rephrase: the quickest and most efficient way to end the threat of the Darkness is to eliminate it's source. The most efficient way to resist the enchantments of the Queens and their deluded brainwashed servants is to want for nothing and embrace the suffering and compromise the Nobility so whole heartedly reject.</div> </div> </div> </div> But that does not make the Cold Guard a foil to Princesses. There are plenty of Princesses who believe in quickly and efficently fighting the Darkness at it's source by walking into Nests and burning it down. Both Swords and Storms have this approach, with Storms just taking it to extremes.<br /> <br /> I'd also suggest that if you wanted a group who hunts Princesses they should have a motive that's not factually wrong. I never liked it when Hunters were fighting for reasons that are wrong; it makes them feel incompetent. I much prefer it when Hunters point out legitimate flaws in the monsters* and use that as their motive. If they ignore an individual who defies the steryotype and hunt him anyway that's fine too.<br /> <br /> * Or hunt out of self interest. That's good too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120026#post1120026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now in regards to the Noble CEOs...even I see the futility of arguing with one of the creators of the gameline, so I'll just say that when I wrote that originally I imagined any Princess who dared to try and make a difference in the corporate world quickly burned out to nothingness or went super Dethroned thanks to the absolutely necessary dehumanization that comes from corporate capitalism. It appears I was wrong so I retract that statement in regards to the Magisters.</div> </div> </div> </div> Corporate capitalism, for all it's flaws, is less harmful to the soul than watching your friends and comrades cut down in battle beside you in battle. And being superhumanly intelligent and skilled is a good way find a balance between ethics and capitalism.<br /> <br /> It's a trope in magical girl shows for the world to become a better place once magical girls start running it; Sailor Moon did it (twice). So in Princess we made sure to actually justify the trope by ensuring that Princess' had abilities that would actually be useful to running a nation and that there were splats that actually had philosophies and ideas on what they'd do if they got elected president.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-24-2017, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T13:55:51-07:00","id":1120059,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, the Cold Guard's basic premise is that magic and the supernatural are <i>inherently</i> evil; the better and more innocent magic looks, the worse it really is, and the more it needs to be wiped out lest it deceive the unwary. They're foils to Princesses because they cast doubt on the whole Hopeful mythos, and the assumption that the Light is beneficial - especially since they know a lot about that mythos. (And, you know, it's actually true in P:tH that Dark creatures are drawn to the Light-touched. The Cold Guard's view would be hard to refute in-setting. We know that Nests feed on human evil because P:tH's rules say so, but the Nobles can't be sure.) It has nothing to do with idealism vs. pragmatism or short-term vs. long-term thinking.<br /> <br /> I don't know of any other hunter group that takes that view exactly, and makes a point of hunting supernaturals who are trying to help humans.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I think the Cold Guard's Endowment is over-powerful for what it costs - Endowments are priced as Merits, IIRC? I'd split Ice Dam into three: a Merit that gives Supernatural Tolerance equal to the dots bought, a Merit that adds to abjuration and exorcism dice pools, and a Merit that forces a Clash of Wills to activate supernatural powers. The second and third would have the first as a prerequisite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T14:48:35-07:00","id":1120086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120059#post1120059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it, the Cold Guard's basic premise is that magic and the supernatural are <i>inherently</i> evil; the better and more innocent magic looks, the worse it really is, and the more it needs to be wiped out lest it deceive the unwary. They're foils to Princesses because they cast doubt on the whole Hopeful mythos, and the assumption that the Light is beneficial - especially since they know a lot about that mythos. (And, you know, it's actually true in P:tH that Dark creatures are drawn to the Light-touched. The Cold Guard's view would be hard to refute in-setting. We know that Nests feed on human evil because P:tH's rules say so, but the Nobles can't be sure.) It has nothing to do with idealism vs. pragmatism or short-term vs. long-term thinking.<br /> <br /> I don't know of any other hunter group that takes that view exactly, and makes a point of hunting supernaturals who are trying to help humans.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I think the Cold Guard's Endowment is over-powerful for what it costs - Endowments are priced as Merits, IIRC? I'd split Ice Dam into three: a Merit that gives Supernatural Tolerance equal to the dots bought, a Merit that adds to abjuration and exorcism dice pools, and a Merit that forces a Clash of Wills to activate supernatural powers. The second and third would have the first as a prerequisite.</div> </div> </div> </div>This ^<br /> <br /> Masterfully put Michael Brazier. That was a far more concise point that I could have made given my own personal biases. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And as a last note about the Cold Guard's philosophy: Are they really wrong when the ST has the final say over setting material? The CofD's strong suit is that nothing is entirely certain from one Chronicle to the next. Having concrete facts in CofD kinda defeats the purpose, and why having Hunter organizations that question that so damn fascinating. Hunter should force the Princess players to ask &quot;What if I'm wrong?&quot; or &quot;What if I've been lied to by this otherworldly force?&quot; Just like how the Hunter players should ask questions like &quot;What if I'm really just killing people who are just trying to help others?&quot; or &quot;What if there was something that could be done to save these people rather than just killing them?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T15:34:48-07:00","id":1120104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120059#post1120059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They're foils to Princesses because they cast doubt on the whole Hopeful mythos, and the assumption that the Light is beneficial - especially since they know a lot about that mythos.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's the thing, I don't think they cast doubt upon the Hopeful mythos. Imagine a hypothetical debate between a Cold Guard and a Princess.<br /> <br /> Cold Guard: Magic is evil.<br /> Princess: No it's not.<br /> Cold Guard, pulling out a gun: Yes it is.<br /> <br /> That's not an argument that would make either the Princess or (more importantly) the player think twice about magic. What's worse, it leads to a flat empty conflict with no underlying substance. When the biggest magic haters in Hunter Cannon (the Malleus Maleficarum) fight Mage hunters there's tons of deeper philosophical debates that can underlay the conflict. Hubris vs humility before god. Awakened curiosity/obsession vs faith. Ect.<br /> <br /> That's what the Cold Guard need. Something that they can actually argue about to a Princess, preferably where both sides have a point. Better yet, something where a Cold Guard and a Princess can both see a suffering mortal and have a real argument about how to help them. That something should be the core of the Cold Guard. Not their hatred for magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120059#post1120059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We know that Nests feed on human evil because P:tH's rules say so, but the Nobles can't be sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Objection! The Charm Weight of Memory provides objective proof that acts of human evil cause nests. A Princess &quot;has a vision of the most emotionally intense event the object was involved in within the Longevity period&quot; and may learn &quot;did the event cause the growth of a Tainted or Blessed area&quot;. (That's from your version)<br /> <br /> So Princesses have proof that human evil causes Tainted Places.<br /> <br /> (Besides, the best Hunter organisations are ones that have arguments that can make a player playing their prey's splat think, not just a charachter).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120086#post1120086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as a last note about the Cold Guard's philosophy: Are they really wrong when the ST has the final say over setting material? The CofD's strong suit is that nothing is entirely certain from one Chronicle to the next. Having concrete facts in CofD kinda defeats the purpose, and why having Hunter organizations that question that so damn fascinating. Hunter should force the Princess players to ask &quot;What if I'm wrong?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This philosophy can be taken too far. &quot;Kindred burn in sunlight&quot; is an objective fact in the CofD.<br /> <br /> The problem with applying this to the cold guard is that either way you end up with a flat conflict. Wheather or not the Cold Guard are right, wrong, or the Storyteller leaves it ambigious an encounter between the Cold Guard and a Princess will still fall back to flat arguments like &quot;magic is evil&quot;, &quot;no it's not&quot;. Compare to the Malleus Maleficarum; where regardless of if the Exarchs are real; regardless of wheather god is real, the MM Hunter and the Mage can still have an argument about solving mysteries vs faith.<br /> <br /> I'd also point out that in most games where one player is playing a Princess and another is playing a Cold Guard the Storyteller will use the rules for Tainted Places as written in the Princess books. That's the way every Crossover game I've ever played worked; the gameline that first introduced a phenomina sets it's rules. So if the player's read the rulebook, and the Princess charachter has a Charm that reveals how Tainted Places form; what exactly can the Cold Guard's player say to make the Princess' player feel doubt on the Hopeful mythos?<br /> <br /> I contend that there is nothing the Cold Guard could say to make the Princess' player feel doubt, and that the Cold Guard need to be reworked until there is something they could say; and that something forms the core to their write-up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-24-2017, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T16:01:02-07:00","id":1120116,"title":"","content":"...Ok, I'm not going into the whole &quot;Games rules state X so therefore all creative liberty is null and void in favor of game rule X&quot; mess right now (although I must point out that there ARE vampires who can go out during the day. In fact they're introduced in Night Stalkers, the Hunter the Vigil supplement for VtR.) Instead, I'd like to point out that the whole Cold Guard argument you just made is a flawed argument.<br /> <br /> Literally ALL hunters organizations can be summed up by the whole: &quot;Magic is evil/no it's not&quot; argument. No exceptions. Especially so in the cases of the far reaching Conspiracies. To go with the obvious low hanging fruit, the Mallius Maleficarun LITERALLY F$&amp;KING TORTURES witches into confessing their crimes before god before either &quot;reforming&quot; them (whatever that means) or putting a bullet in their head (good old burning a fell out of favor sadly.) It falls to individual Hunters and their own moral compass to go against the default beliefs of the group in order to ask the really hard questions. The same can be said for all Conspiracies and Compacts, including the Cold Guard. Choosing not to is a personal decision on behalf of the storyteller, just like choosing not to in regards to the Shadow Congregation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 07-24-2017, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T16:41:53-07:00","id":1120132,"title":"","content":"What was the purpose and point where the Cold Guard turned from a &quot;Using the enemy's weapon against it&quot; Grey Warden inspired org, to &quot;we hate magic. Pure Humanity FTW&quot; group?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-24-2017, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T16:55:23-07:00","id":1120141,"title":"","content":"You know, that is an excellent question Vent0. Because the Grey Warden approach was my original write up for the Cold Guard. I though it was The Kings Raven who revised the Conspiracy since it fit more into the endure pain rather than magically fix pain themes that better fit the context of Princess, but it's clear now it wasn't them who changed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T17:03:07-07:00","id":1120145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120141#post1120141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, that is an excellent question Vent0. Because the Grey Warden approach was my original write up for the Cold Guard. I though it was The Kings Raven who revised the Conspiracy since it fit more into the endure pain rather than magically fix pain themes that better fit the context of Princess, but it's clear now it wasn't them who changed it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Make the Guard Grey Again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T17:13:34-07:00","id":1120152,"title":"","content":"Honestly, my whole goal with the Cold Guard was to create a faction that sees some of the more sinister stuff Princess hints at (I.E. All Nobles can become Dethroned simply by circumstances beyond their control, manipulate people with magic for their &quot;betterment&quot;, serves otherworldly entities that seek utopia without acknowledging that one utopia is another's dystopia, all Nobles are ruthless killing machines against creatures that seem to only show up or are strictly drawn too places where the Nobles themselves are.) Whether they are Grey Warden esc soldiers who take the Darkness into themselves in order to fight a war they believe has been going on for centuries that fuels the power base of an other worldly aristocracy, or Bleak Cabal esc missionaries who try to rid humanity of it's growing dependance on magical intervention and free the world from the shackles of Sorcerer Queens, I'm game for whichever so long as they're proactive and deeply flawed individuals. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 07-24-2017, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T17:19:03-07:00","id":1120156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120152#post1120152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, my whole goal with the Cold Guard was to create a faction that sees some of the more sinister stuff Princess hints at (I.E. All Nobles can become Dethroned simply by circumstances beyond their control, manipulate people with magic for their &quot;betterment&quot;, serves otherworldly entities that seek utopia without acknowledging that one utopia is another's dystopia, all Nobles are ruthless killing machines against creatures that seem to only show up or are strictly drawn too places where the Nobles themselves are.) Whether they are Grey Warden esc soldiers who take the Darkness into themselves in order to fight a war they believe has been going on for centuries that fuels the power base of an other worldly aristocracy, or Bleak Cabal esc missionaries who try to rid humanity of it's growing dependance on magical intervention and free the world from the shackles of Sorcerer Queens, I'm game for whichever so long as they're proactive and deeply flawed individuals. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Would there be room philosophically for both factions in the organization? One group thinks they need to fight the Darkness with darkness (and, restrained by <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/HeroicWillpower\" target=\"_blank\">Heroic Willpower</a>, they have a point, to a degree), while the other sees what the Nobles are selling as Too Good To Be True, and pick up whatever weapon they can to strike before the Queens have control? Both sides, of course, acknowledging that they are expecting themselves from whatever better tomorrow they are fighting for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T17:39:29-07:00","id":1120163,"title":"","content":"Vent0, you are definitely on to something with this. <br /> <br /> They could sort of be like the Mysterium from MtAw in that the Cold Guard was once actually two separate Compacts that joined forces to better resist what they saw as a sinister takeover of humanity by an otherworldly force. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T17:45:15-07:00","id":1120165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120104#post1120104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's the thing, I don't think they cast doubt upon the Hopeful mythos. Imagine a hypothetical debate between a Cold Guard and a Princess.<br /> <br /> Cold Guard: Magic is evil.<br /> Princess: No it's not.<br /> Cold Guard, pulling out a gun: Yes it is.<br /> <br /> That's not an argument that would make either the Princess or (more importantly) the player think twice about magic. What's worse, it leads to a flat empty conflict with no underlying substance. When the biggest magic haters in Hunter Cannon (the Malleus Maleficarum) fight Mage hunters there's tons of deeper philosophical debates that can underlay the conflict. Hubris vs humility before god. Awakened curiosity/obsession vs faith. Ect.</div> </div> </div> </div>How often does the Shadow Congregation <i>argue</i> with its targets? Not at all, would be my bet. You aren't going to see deep philosophical debates between a killer and his victim, or on the field of battle.<br /> <br /> It isn't exactly difficult for a Storyteller to present the Cold Guard's doctrine in a way that allows Princesses to learn it and respond. You need only introduce a third character, whom both the Cold Guard and the Hopeful want to persuade, and who won't be favorably impressed by violence. Which is also how you'd handle any other case of fanatical hunters vs. monsters, if you wanted to show that both sides have a point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120104#post1120104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Objection! The Charm Weight of Memory provides objective proof that acts of human evil cause nests. A Princess &quot;has a vision of the most emotionally intense event the object was involved in within the Longevity period&quot; and may learn &quot;did the event cause the growth of a Tainted or Blessed area&quot;. (That's from your version)</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by the document, I expect the Cold Guard would say that, while the form a Nest's corruption takes is set by human evil, its efficiacy is due to the cumulative use of magic over time. According to them, magic made the Dark World, and using it strengthens that world; human evil just opens the way to Darkness. Using a Charm doesn't refute this argument, supposing the Cold Guard would believe information from a Charm - the debate is over the ultimate origin of Taint, not how it infected a specific Nest.<br /> <br /> In some ways the Cold Guard is dualistic: they regard evil as a thing in itself, with its own reality, separable from the good, and they blame the Hopeful for separating them and thus creating the monsters that they fight, along with the force that empowers them. Princess (the game) has a different view: it defines evil as a corruption of good, parasitic on it, not separable from it, and vanishing entirely when the corruption is cleaned away. So a debate between the Cold Guard and the Nobles plunges into metaphysical arguments on the nature of evil and the possibility of moral perfection. Those are some <i>very</i> deep waters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T00:03:02-07:00","id":1120250,"title":"","content":"Both wrong really what's evel is abstract an insane person doesn't know what he's doing so the only good is what's keeps the human world going refrom I've been told is what keeps the human world stable but if there's life outside of humanity then they might deserve equal treatment unless there like serial killer's or something but I'm 16 so what do i know","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T01:05:32-07:00","id":1120261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120165#post1120165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How often does the Shadow Congregation <i>argue</i> with its targets? Not at all, would be my bet.</div> </div> </div> </div> Having their targets confess and repent is an officially sanctioned goal of the Shadow Congregation. So as often as they can, if perhaps with hot coals involved.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120165#post1120165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't exactly difficult for a Storyteller to present the Cold Guard's doctrine in a way that allows Princesses to learn it and respond. You need only introduce a third character, whom both the Cold Guard and the Hopeful want to persuade, and who won't be favorably impressed by violence. Which is also how you'd handle any other case of fanatical hunters vs. monsters, if you wanted to show that both sides have a point.</div> </div> </div> </div> That works too; and it shows why it's important for the Cold Guard to have a docterine that can make players pause and think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120165#post1120165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In some ways the Cold Guard is dualistic: they regard evil as a thing in itself, with its own reality, separable from the good, and they blame the Hopeful for separating them and thus creating the monsters that they fight, along with the force that empowers them. Princess (the game) has a different view: it defines evil as a corruption of good, parasitic on it, not separable from it, and vanishing entirely when the corruption is cleaned away. So a debate between the Cold Guard and the Nobles plunges into metaphysical arguments on the nature of evil and the possibility of moral perfection. Those are some <i>very</i> deep waters.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this would do everything I'm asking for, it would the Cold Guard foils to Princesses, it would allow characters to get into a debate that makes players think, it would give real philosophical and emotional weight to the conflict; if it was <i>actually in the text.</i><br /> <br /> This is your interpretation of the Cold Guard, but what the Cold Guard's write up actually talks about is their belief that magic is evil. Their Endowment is specifically an anti-magic effect. If the write up instead talked about the above view of of good and evil as the source of conflict between the Cold Guard and Princesses with magic being, at most, a reason why they prioritise Princesses above mortals who think and act like Princesses, I'd be happy.<br /> <br /> It would also help if their Endowment was replaced with something that let them proactively help people in ways that fit their philosophy so as to provide evidence a charachter or player could point to that their ideas work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-25-2017, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T01:51:53-07:00","id":1120269,"title":"","content":"I have an idea so for the cold guards endowment maybe it's an attack that only works on beings with integrity or equivalent of 5 or less and princesses that would work but it would have to be stong so every dot has 2 dice of damage but gey im sure you can come up with a better idea mines not that good and it's pretty plane","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T10:00:53-07:00","id":1120390,"title":"","content":"Alright, at this point in time it's very apperant that the core idea for the Cold Guard is sound but it really needs to be expressed more clearly in the write up. So, with your permission <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11745_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11745\" data-vbnamecard=\"11745\">Darinas</a> I will personally re-write the Cold Guard's write up after work tonight since I finally have access to an actual computer. <br /> <br /> If green lit for the re-write I can't guarentee that everyone will like it, but I try with all my creative might to bring their core concept back into focus: Hunting the Hopeful because they believe the Queens have transformed them into monsters that allow them to both enslave humanity and propigate the Darkness, creating an endless cycle of dependance for the Queen's chosen.<br /> <br /> P.S. This also counts for their Endowment. While I agree that it should be changed, I believe they should return to their original Edowment: Penumbrae. It adds more customization to the Cold Guard and gives credence that either the Darkness and the Light were one and the same at some point in time, or that at least Human will and dedication can keep the Darkness at bay for a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 07-25-2017, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T11:03:59-07:00","id":1120416,"title":"","content":"... Fine, but I won't approve it until I see the result. And <i>please</i> let this be the last time we change their Endowment. We already changed its name and effect around four times by now, and I would really like us to chose a name and stick to it, so we can finally move to parts that actually need to be developped, like the Philadelphia Appendix, the fictions, or the new Endowments for already existing Conspiracies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T11:19:34-07:00","id":1120423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120416#post1120416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Fine, but I won't approve it until I see the result. And <i>please</i> let this be the last time we change their Endowment. We already changed its name and effect around four times by now, and I would really like us to chose a name and stick to it, so we can finally move to parts that actually need to be developped, like the Philadelphia Appendix, the fictions, or the new Endowments for already existing Conspiracies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought we had additions to the existing Endowments already?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T11:22:54-07:00","id":1120425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I thought we had additions to the existing Endowments already? </div> </div> </div>We do. I just feel we could do a few more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T11:59:32-07:00","id":1120440,"title":"","content":"Eh, don't go too overboard. Sometimes less really is more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T12:52:50-07:00","id":1120451,"title":"","content":"True, but right now, we have around 1 or 2 per Conspiracy. I can't help but feel a few more would be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T13:03:23-07:00","id":1120455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120390#post1120390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If green lit for the re-write I can't guarentee that everyone will like it, but I try with all my creative might to bring their core concept back into focus: Hunting the Hopeful because they believe the Queens have transformed them into monsters that allow them to both enslave humanity and propigate the Darkness, creating an endless cycle of dependance for the Queen's chosen.</div> </div> </div> </div> Obviously it's not written yet. But I don't see much difference between this and hunting Princesses because they think magic is inherently bad. Both are a disagreement over facts: Either magic is inherently bad or it's not. Either the Queens created Princesses as part of a sinister plot or they did not.<br /> <br /> A philosophical difference like MB's interpretation of the Cold Guard objecting to the seperation of good and evil makes a better core concept. Something like the Queens having created Princesses as part of a plot can be added on top by talking about the Guard's views on the nature of good and evil first; and then using the Queens creating Princesses as an example of seperating good and evil later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T14:47:33-07:00","id":1120500,"title":"","content":"Design Process Notes: Still at work, so basically thoughts &amp; outlines.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Cold Guard serves the purpose of being the Conspiracy that hunts the Princesses. This is a core part of their being, and the trick has been to give a reasonable background and structure to why they fight. Surprisingly, this has been easier than I though for me personally because there are seriously fucked up undertones to Princess the Hopeful, with how they technically &quot;feed&quot; off of the hope of others, how fucked up Belief as a Integrity system actually is when it punishes the players for &quot;giving up on their beliefs&quot; in a very disproportionate manner, and of course with how fucking comfortable this game is with all of it's focus of dreams and hope with turning the player characters into monster butchering machines. The potential is there for some really interesting exploration regarding just what being a Noble entails, buuuut that's also where I've gotten the most pushback. Especially when most of that disturbing subtext is just dismissed with &quot;What they're doing is good&quot; and &quot;It's Anime, deal with it&quot; mentalities. <br /> <br /> So screw it, let's start from scratch. What's a core concept that the Conspracy can embody that justified their hunt and examines Princess the Hopeful in a meaningful way. How about examining their convictions? The line from Captain America: Civil War comes to mind: not a perfect quote but the core concept is there. <br /> <br /> CA: &quot;What did Stark tell you about me?&quot;<br /> SM: &quot;He said that you think what your doing is right, and that you won't stop. And that makes you dangerous.&quot;<br /> CA: &quot;Well, he's not wrong...&quot;<br /> <br /> Changing the core of the Cold Guards motives from &quot;Princesses are evil&quot; to Princesses are too dangerous to be left alone&quot; might be a step in the right direction without changing their core as Noble Hunters.<br /> <br /> Your throughts and opinions?<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. Digital Aid<br /> <br /> Here's one of the sources that helped me come to this decision. It's a video from a series called Trope Talks, specifically focusing on the Trope of the Paragon. Since Princesses must be Paragons due to that aforementioned fucked up Belief system the material in the vid can easily translate to Princess on several levels. <br /> Here's the link to the vid: <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?list=PLDb22nlVXGgcljcdyDk80bBDXGyeZjZ5e&amp;v=zm_Pi6OpNKU\" target=\"_blank\">https://m.youtube.com/watch?list=PLD...&amp;v=zm_Pi6OpNKU</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 07-25-2017, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T16:35:14-07:00","id":1120536,"title":"","content":"So, the Cold Guard opposes extremists who are convinced they are in the right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T18:57:14-07:00","id":1120578,"title":"","content":"So basically the Cold Guard are Cape Busters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T20:32:34-07:00","id":1120615,"title":"","content":"Design Process Notes: Done with work but have to head home so more thoughts. <br /> <br /> <br /> To sum up the new core premise of the Cold Guard: Yes. They oppose extremists who use their supernatural powers and otherworldly magic to amass followers and forcibly control belief. The reason for this will become apparent with this next focus for the new write up: The Cold Guard's history and the extent of their reach.<br /> <br /> Before the one thing I had trouble seeing in regards to my own contributions to the doc, the Cold Guard and Magisters respectively, is how the Cold Guard IS a Conspiracy compared to the Crown Jewels and the Magisters of the Economy...ok quick quick tangent. Is it still possible to change their name to something like The Magisters of Dreams or something? The Economy just doesn't roll off the tongue that well...right, back on topic. For this new write up I'd like to spend a but more time going into their background and how they became a full fledged Conspiracy compared to just a Compact. And for that, I'd like to purpose that the Cold Guard came to be during the height of the Terror after the French Revolution. It was a time where belief in liberty, freedom, and equality for all strata of society could be achieved before the reality set in and the revolution's lack of foresight led to the entire dream collapsing in on itself and into a hungry monster. Never has there been such a clear metaphor for a Noble becoming Dethroned than what happened to the ideals of the French Revolution after the dust settled and it became clear that dreams alone weren't enough to make a stable system of government. It's during this terrifying era that a group of revolutionaries watched their leader, the one who rallied them to the cause and gave them such hope, turn into a literal monster and rampaged before he was put down with sword and gunfire. After his death the eyes of his compatriots slowly began to clear and they realized just how powerful an influence he had over them. Supernaturally so, and from there they began a journey of discovery that led to the revelations of the Nobility who stoked the fires of both the revolution and aristocracy and how, while not directly their fault, their ability to effortlessly sway the hearts and minds of others made the situation worse for everyone in the end. Thus did they swear an oath to do what is necessary to prevent these Enchanters from ensnaring the beliefs of society as heavily as they had done to their own nation. Thus did the seeds of a Conspiracy get sown.<br /> <br /> Yes, I realized while writing this that the whole escape from Dreamland didn't happen until the Apolo 11 moon landing. But I'm pretty sure that it was said that there were basic Princesses throughout history, just not nearly as many as after the whole escape.<br /> <br /> Yes, this does fundamentally change some of the other themes of the Cold Guard. But it's still an interesting theme to explore in my opinion, and it doesn't change the fact that they still Hunt the Nobles. Only that they don't always hunt them to the death now. Everybody wins.<br /> <br /> Please feel free to leave thoughts &amp; comments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 07-25-2017, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T22:49:26-07:00","id":1120662,"title":"","content":"Okay, got a rough idea for the mob war.<br /> <br /> <b>The Philly Mob War</b><br /> <br /> A decade before the princesses returned to Earth, Philadelphia\u2019s criminal underworld experienced a massive upheaval. For years, the local family of <i>La Cosa Nostra</i> had been relatively quiet. Angelo Bruno, \u201cThe Gentle Don\u201d, preferred the business-like approach to crime that involved quiet rackets with minimal violence to make money. This didn\u2019t sit well with his underlings however, and on March 21<sup>st</sup>, 1980, the Gentle Don was murdered in front of his own home on 10<sup>th</sup> and Snyder. The murderer was brought to answer to the Commission, and suffice to say never made any trouble again.<br /> <br /> Bruno\u2019s assassination paved the way for younger mobsters to try and take the city themselves, but they made themselves too big a target for the Feds to ignore. A short mob war was fought, and despite angling by others the New York families organized John Stanfa to take over Philadelphia. This didn\u2019t sit well with many of Philly\u2019s native mobsters, and these \u201cYoung Turks\u201d began their own war to seize control of Philadelphia, especially the drug trade. For over a decade Philadelphia would experience a mob war right out of the worst Depression Era. Street hoods with chips on their shoulders squared off against the experienced men who made their bones for decades. The fighting dragged in other crime outfits, from outlaw bikers to black gangs who wanted a cut of what the Mafia could offer. Despite the lucrative hopes, the volatility of the family pushed many criminals away, and even into the arms of the up-and-coming Slavic mobsters streaming out from the Iron Curtain.<br /> <br /> By all rights, the newly blossoming princesses would have become part of the mob war if not for the fact that the various hunter organizations were already making their plays. TFV made sure that the FBI had a close finger on the pulse of the problem, as the Malleus listened in on some dark and desperate confessions. The embryotic Union took to the streets, as the Ascending Ones cut off drugs to anyone getting too violent towards civilians (and out of their control). The new princesses, most of them teenagers, were still trying to figure out what, exactly, they were. The idea of facing down armed and dangerous groups in such an environment was a little too much even for such proactive individuals, especially when the stories started to spread about hunters calling <i>them</i> dangerous witches.<br /> <br /> Realizing that they needed to safeguard their lives, the oldest and most experienced princesses in Philadelphia steered their younger charges away from the mob war, focusing them on anything else. Urban decay, street gangs, decaying schools, anything to keep them safe from the mob war, and the hunters who claimed it as their problem. Two princesses who decided to buck the warning were later reported missing by their families, and have never been found.<br /> <br /> The aftermath is still felt through the city, as the Philly Mob is weakened and left adrift by the bad blood felt by other criminals thanks to the Young Turks actions. Despite being reasonably active for such a weakened family, the Philadelphia Mafia is seen by many to be on the decline, and some have posited that what was once their territory will be up for grabs by the New York families very soon.<br /> <br /> <b>Story Hooks</b><br /> <br /> An older princess who lived through the war sees the lack of attention on the Philly Mob as a chance to right the wrongs she never had a chance to. The police are spreading rumors that a woman is attacking gambling rackets, money laundering fronts, and threatening the lives of several soldiers of the mob. Unfortunately, the mob has also become semi-reliable for getting weapons and information for several hunter groups, to the point of being nearly indispensable. Either the princess stops, or someone needs to fill a sizable power vacuum.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T00:21:49-07:00","id":1120683,"title":"","content":"Design Process Notes: Urrrghh...so...tired...<br /> <br /> <br /> Well I'm quite sure I'm not getting to the write up tonight after all. In my defense, I dare anyone to walk 30 min home with the last leg being up a particularly steep hill and then see just how much into writing you are. That being said, I did want to talk about one last point I'd like to hone...*hehe*...when I do get some time to write without feeling exhausted. Particularly something that's also been a point of pushback from the community: the fact that the Cold Guard does hunt the Hopeful. <br /> <br /> Because there's no denying it is a brutal aspect of their character. The Hopeful are often young, genuinely trying to help, and have put themselves in danger for others many times. What would drive a person to look at someone like that and see a monster? Especially when it could really be just a child underneath the magic and illusions. Well, the fact that they can and do gives the Conspiracy Teeth. And every Compact and Conspiracy needs Teeth in Hunter the Vigil because the game emphasizes both the potential for great heroism and great atrocity. Without Teeth, they're not really Hunters with a capital H are they. They're just regular mortals. With too much Teeth they become unsympathetic. And to the credit of some of the pushback, the way they are written now does lean a little to much on the Teeth aspect. I don't think this was done intentionally though, and from many of the supporters of the original concept we see instances where the balance works out just right. To give some examples of my thought process for why the Cold Guard hunts the Hopeful, here is a list I made while on a 10 today: <br /> <br /> ~ Q: Why do Hunters hunt Princesses? <br /> ~ A: Because despite their intentions, all Princesses are walking time bombs that will naturally cause many casualties when they do finally go off. <br /> ~ A: Because the face of the Dethroned is the true face of the Nobility. For all their ideology they are still nothing more than hungry monsters. <br /> ~ A: Because Princesses foster dependency in those they help, forcing them to rely upon the Nobles to solve all their worldly problems. <br /> ~ A: Because Princesses straight up manipulate people, and because they believe they're right that makes them extremely dangerous. <br /> <br /> That last point has stuck with me the entire day, and has informed a lot of the design process I've been formulating. Because of all the answers given that one is the most human and relatable reason for why a person would look at a Princess and see a monster. Everything else is an added incentive while this could very well be what make a mortal a Hunter. And that angle is what I'd like to explore with this iteration of the Cold Guard. So, if this is why they hunt Princesses then the next logical step is: What are they willing to do to stop them?<br /> <br /> Yes, this has been gone over before in the doc. That's entirely to the community's credit though. It's what gives me confidence in the heart of this project.<br /> <br /> Yes, writing is not my strong suit. But progress is being made. I'll get a write up for it out, it just might take a couple of days.<br /> <br /> Thoughts and opinions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":"Polish 07-26-2017, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T02:46:31-07:00","id":1120712,"title":"","content":"I feel like I should correct some factual inacuracies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120683#post1120683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Princesses straight up manipulate people</div> </div> </div> </div>The leadership splat of Princesses, Graces, have an automatic Belief Compromise for manipulating people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120683#post1120683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Princesses foster dependency in those they help</div> </div> </div> </div> Hearts and Diamonds go out of this way to avoid this by investing in mortals. Other courts might foster dependency by accident; but intentionally encouraging mortals to depend on you is considered Mirrors behaviour by the Radiant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120500#post1120500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">with how they technically &quot;feed&quot; off of the hope of others</div> </div> </div> </div> They do not feed on hope. Princesses recharge by generating new Wisps internally when feeling positive emotions.<br /> <br /> Only the Court of Tears feeds from Hope, and that's why they're considered to be bad guys by other Princesses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120500#post1120500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> how fucked up Belief as a Integrity system actually is when it punishes the players for &quot;giving up on their beliefs&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> While giving up on your beliefs does trigger a breaking point roll; there is a positive dice modifier when a Princess abandoned a belief because she realised it wasn't a good idea. I designed the Court of Mirrors as a metaphor to highlight that:<br /> <br /> 1) Clinging too hard to impractical Beliefs is a flaw Nobles are prone too.<br /> 2) Nobles know they have this flaw and work to overcome it.<br /> <br /> There is nothing fucked up about saying that strong belief can be a source of strength. Which is what the Princess' core book actually says. And there is nothing in the Princess text that says Nobles should dogmatically hold onto their Beliefs; quite the opposite. By villifing the Court of Mirrors the book says that if you draw strength from Beliefs you should make sure your Beliefs are sensible ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120500#post1120500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and of course with how fucking comfortable this game is with all of it's focus of dreams and hope with turning the player characters into monster butchering machines.</div> </div> </div> </div> Given that a theme is child soldiers; that Sensitivity explicitly says that a Princess will never become immune to the pain of seeing friends and comrades fall in battle; that Shadows are inspired by PTSD. I don't think you can call the text too comfortable with anything.<br /> <br /> That said, while the truth will never be made cannon, a likely possibility is that the Light has no mind. It's simply a natural force like gravity that's drawn to some people and turns them into Princesses. So nobody's morally culpable for making Princesses fight, and nobody is preventing her from stopping (Princesses encourage each other not to push themselves too far).<br /> <br /> (It's also possible for a Princess to have a long and successful career without ever fighting monsters. Champions are one X splat; there's four others)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120500#post1120500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The potential is there for some really interesting exploration regarding just what being a Noble entails, buuuut that's also where I've gotten the most pushback.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think that the reason you're getting pushback is that you are not exploring what being a Noble entails; but exploring a misuderstanding of what being a Noble entails; criticisng Princesses for things that the Princess book takes the time to explicitly address without taking that addressing into account.<br /> <br /> Since you brought up Captain America: Civil War; I'd point out that in that film Tony Stark and Steve Rogers would <i>both</i> be Princesses.<br /> <br /> Tony is a Prince of Hearts, and Hearts believe that Princesses must be held accountable to the communities they serve. Steve is a Prince of Swords believe that Princesses should be independent heroes who're free to follow their conscience.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Here's one of the sources that helped me come to this decision. It's a video from a series called Trope Talks, specifically focusing on the Trope of the Paragon. Since Princesses must be Paragons due to that aforementioned fucked up Belief system the material in the vid can easily translate to Princess on several levels.<br /> Here's the link to the vid: <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?list=PLDb22nlVXGgcljcdyDk80bBDXGyeZjZ5e&amp;v=zm_Pi6OpNKU\" target=\"_blank\">https://m.youtube.com/watch?list=PLD...&amp;v=zm_Pi6OpNKU</a> </div> </div> </div> It's a good video, and I think the most important thing to take from it is that Paragons are a really diverse archetype - because that's definately true for Princesses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120683#post1120683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">~ Q: Why do Hunters hunt Princesses?</div> </div> </div> </div> It is a a tough question. While it's easy to say why do Hunters hunt this specific Princess; asking why Hunters hunt Princesses in general is a very hard question.<br /> <br /> Because for most reasons you can think of, either they're factually wrong (e.g. all Princesses are walking time bombs) which means the Conspiracy will not have the power to make a Princess player stop and think. Or they apply to some Princesses but are directly contradicted by other Princesses. If you say that Princesses are too emotional to be trusted with so much power; the Court of Diamonds believes in logic and reason. If you say that Princesses are too stubborn and always doing what they think is right the Court of Clubs believes in understanding and compromise. etc<br /> <br /> Groups like Charachter Risk Analysis bypasses the problem because they don't oppose all Princesses; they oppose individual Princesses when their goals conflict. The Magisters of the Ecconomy work because even though their criticisms of the Nobility don't work for all Princesses, the fact that they are also in it for personal gain means that it dosn't need to work for all Princesses.<br /> <br /> But if you want a criticism of all Princesses that's accurate enough to make a Princess' player think twice. Then you need to criticise something fundamental like idealism or doing good. And you've already said you want to avoid the Cold Guard feeling futile.<br /> <br /> <br /> The only thing I can think of that is general enough to apply to most Princesses; and that would avoid futility, would be to challenge the definition of good and evil that's implied by the Princess core book. That evil is something which must be fought and overcome. Come up with another definition of good and evil; and another way of doing good that fits the new definition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120500#post1120500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your throughts and opinions?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;you think what your doing is right, and that you won't stop. And that makes you dangerous&quot; Describes only a small minority of Princesses. I'm all for exploring what being a Noble entails; but that has to start with an understanding of what being a Noble entails.<br /> <br /> There's just too many factual inaccuracies in what you're saying about Princesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-26-2017, 06:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T03:03:42-07:00","id":1120717,"title":"","content":"Yeah what he said raven knows it sence he made it so let him do it he's an word of god for princess and he worked on hunter homebrews and even worked on 2 fan supplements","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T05:17:25-07:00","id":1120754,"title":"","content":"So, to summarize potential CG motivations:<br /> -We don't like magic in general (because it is evil? It gives an unnatural/unfair advantage?)<br /> -We don't like extremists who are convinced they are right (because they are dangerous, even unintentionally? Because it is unrealistic and thus dangerous?)<br /> -We think simplistic notions of Good and Evil, specifically destroying Evil will lead to good, is misguided and dangerous (think the Miranda incident in Serenity)<br /> <br /> Those right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T06:05:28-07:00","id":1120763,"title":"","content":"Wow, there have been a lot of dialogues while I was sleeping, it seems. Let me see...<br /> <br /> For Flyboy, great job, keep up the good work. Feel free to add this to the doc whenever you feel like it.<br /> <br /> As for the other two...<br /> <br /> I admit I am starting to get uncomfortable with all the rewritings for the Cold Guard. With the direction it's taking, it sounds like they will have nothing to do with their original concept. Maybe we are going a bit too far with the rewriting?<br /> <br /> As for the reason for Hunters to hunt Princesses, yes, that has already been covered. I agree with most of Raven's counter-argument regarding Princesses being creepy; again, they do not feed off hope, they feed by <i>creating</i> more hope. That said, there are plenty of ways for Princesses to be creepy from the Hunters' perspective (and I insist on the word perspective):<br /> <br /> * Paranoia: thanks to Dual Identity, a Princess can be anyone, anywhere, and it's incredibly hard ot figure out who she is. This would naturally make Hunters wary of them, especially Task Force Valkyrie, who see them as vigilantes;<br /> * The Twilight Princesses. You gotta remember that until the Apollo Landing, most Princesses were Twilight-affiliated, so hunters would have years of experiences meeting nothing but psycho vigilantes who kill monsters with no care for collateral damages, creepy necromancer-like veiled women who do weird rituals causing monsters to appear wherever they show up, and capricious egomaniacs who make everybody worship them because they believe themselves the &quot;Chosen ones&quot;. Yeaaaaaah, I can see why they would be wary of Princesses because of that.<br /> * Magic; yeah, I know, that one is weird, but it's been established magic is inherently scary to mortals in the World of Darkness, so I think it's worth mentioning;<br /> * The Dethroned, which give the (incorrrect) feeling they are just time bombs waiting to happen.<br /> * The Queens, which are essentially alien, immortal beings from another realm trying to influence the world; not so different from the God-Machine or the True Fae if you don't know the details about their motivations.<br /> * And of course, the clashing morality issue, which we already adressed in the themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T07:17:19-07:00","id":1120787,"title":"","content":"I don't like logging in. I really don't like logging in. But I'm going to do it anyways for this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120712#post1120712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because for most reasons you can think of, either they're factually wrong (e.g. all Princesses are walking time bombs) which means the Conspiracy will not have the power to make a Princess player stop and think. Or they apply to some Princesses but are directly contradicted by other Princesses. If you say that Princesses are too emotional to be trusted with so much power; the Court of Diamonds believes in logic and reason. If you say that Princesses are too stubborn and always doing what they think is right the Court of Clubs believes in understanding and compromise. etc<br /> <br /> There's just too many factual inaccuracies in what you're saying about Princesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds to me less like someone who sees a Hunter Supplement and more like someone who sees a Princess Supplement. The idea of this supplement (I thought) was to make the Hunter player stop and think. To me, Hunters are precisely the kind of people who could take a factual inaccuracy and except it because of their dogma, their prior experiences, or hatred for &quot;monsters&quot;.They feel they have to assume the exception is the rule, because the exceptions are when people die.<br /> <br /> To me, the Cold Guard doesn't need a 100% accurate reason to hunt Nobles. What they have is a personal grudge and a rationale that makes them feel that they know better than the ones who they blame for the catastrophe of the Kingdoms' Fall. The question shouldn't be &quot;How does a Princess react to seeing a member of the Cold Guard opposing them?&quot; but rather &quot;How does a member of the Cold Guard react to a Noble defying their expectations.<br /> <br /> Feel free to engage in further discussion via comments on the document. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8064-mp122984","name":"mp122984","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T07:27:01-07:00","id":1120788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120763#post1120763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit I am starting to get uncomfortable with all the rewritings for the Cold Guard. With the direction it's taking, it sounds like they will have nothing to do with their original concept. Maybe we are going a bit too far with the rewriting?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing wrong with changing an initiail concept into something different. It happens all the time in writing. Terry Pratchett said that Captain Carrot was going to be the main character in his Watch series all the way up till halfway through the drafting process, where he shifted the focus to Commander Vimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T08:05:43-07:00","id":1120803,"title":"","content":"I know, I know, but I feel like we are really taking excessive time rewriting this ONE Conspiracy.<br /> <br /> Also, to counter the argument that the Cold Guard needs to have an accurate argument to hunt Nobles: Les Myst\u00e8res think Spirits are benevolent beings who should be allowed in the physical world and werewolves are bullies endangering the world by destroying bridges with the Spirit World. The Keepers of the Sources believe Werewolves and Mages are damaging the Earth by drawing mana and essence from it. The Knights of Saint Adrian think the God-Machine's Angels are classic benevolent angels and Unchained Demons are the usual malevolent inhabitants of hell. Everyone who read the Werewolf, Mage or Demon books knows these arguments are bullcrap, and there's no doubt that if a Mage/Werewolf/Demon was confronted with these arguments, he would laught it off as complete nonsense rather than think about it.<br /> <br /> My point is, Compacts and Conspiracies whose motivations are based on complete inaccurate beliefs regarding what they are hunting already exist in plenty, the Cold Guard will hardly not fit in. Hunters having completely wrong ideas of what is actually going on is part of the game.<br /> <br /> Which is why I don't really have problem with the Cold Guard believing the Hopeful's magic makes the Darkness stronger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T09:47:39-07:00","id":1120870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mp122984</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120787#post1120787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds to me less like someone who sees a Hunter Supplement and more like someone who sees a Princess Supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div> I feel the exact opposite. Having hunters who can only be plaid as zealots out to kill Princesses for reasons that are wrong makes this feel more like a Princess supplement full of NPCs for players to fight, rather than a Hunter supplement full of player characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mp122984</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120787#post1120787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of this supplement (I thought) was to make the Hunter player stop and think.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think you can seperate out making hunter players stop and think from making Princesses stop and think. Either the juxtaposition of the Cold Guard and Radiant raises philosphical questions that make players on every side stop and think, or it doesn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mp122984</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120787#post1120787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but rather &quot;How does a member of the Cold Guard react to a Noble defying their expectations.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem here is that the Cold Guard's expectations for a Noble are unfalsifiable. In order for a Noble to defy their expectations they'd have to somehow prove that magic doesn't create Darkness; and that's impossible to do within the rules of the game (and the WoD's theme of no clear answers).<br /> <br /> Now if you do what I've been suggesting; and focus the Cold Guard around comprehensive philosophy that extends beyond disliking magic; and give them an Endowment that lets them fight evil in a method that fits their philosophy. Then it becomes possible for a Princess to defy their expectations by demonstrating that the Noble strategy and world-view leads to better outcomes than the Cold Guard strategy and worldview.<br /> <br /> As an added bonus it becomes possible for a skilled Cold Guard player to also defy the nobles expectations; if the player is skilled enough they might be able to make their strategy produce better outcomes than the Princess. At which point the Cold Guard player gets to do a little victory dance give the Princess' player some good natured ribbing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120803#post1120803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Which is why I don't really have problem with the Cold Guard believing the Hopeful's magic makes the Darkness stronger.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's nothing wrong with the Cold Guard being wrong and believing that Hopeful magic makes the Darkness stronger. If it's presented in an interesting way that gives Cold Guard players hooks to create a charachter who has good reasons to believe what they do.<br /> <br /> Take one of your examples. Les Myst\u00e8res. Anyone who's read Werewolf knows that Spirits are selfish and bad news. And yet, through their Endowment Les Myst\u00e8res prove that spirit and flesh can co-exist. Sure it's dangerous, but if they're skilled and careful they prove that humans and spirits can work togeather for mutual benefit. That gives a Les Myst\u00e8res player plenty of material to create a three dimensional charachter who good reasons to believe in Les Myst\u00e8res' ideology and can argue it's case against Werewolves.<br /> <br /> And that's what the Cold Guard need. Not a view on Princess magic that's correct; but a view on Princess magic that's part of a broader worldview, and backed up with enough evidence, that a Cold Guard could plausible believe it without being closed minded and ignoring the evidence from every Radiant Princess they meet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T09:51:59-07:00","id":1120871,"title":"","content":"Raven king right again","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T09:59:11-07:00","id":1120873,"title":"","content":"I'm done. I'm just done. I've tried to be as creative as I can to add options of play for this Hunter supplement, I've examined and re-examined the nuances of just what Princess the Hopeful tells it's audience compared to what the primary mechanics and gameplay enforce, but I am not wasting another second of my time if it's just going to be either biasly or mindlessly dismissed with what amounts to &quot;because I don't like it&quot; arguments. So for those who did support both the original idea and update progress, I thank you. But I just can't stand it any more, and I have very little free time these days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T10:09:30-07:00","id":1120876,"title":"","content":"Well, great, what do we do now?<br /> <br /> See now why I was saying we were spending too much time and thinking on rewriting the Cold Guard?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T10:16:31-07:00","id":1120880,"title":"","content":"Please don't let this kill the project. There's so much cool ideas still around. I promise I'll get back to editing.<br /> <br /> EDIT (heh): Dusksage, having a civil discussion with you and trying to refute your points is not the same as dismissing your viewpoint.<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: That said, if you feel this is not how you want to spend your free time, a precious commodity in this day and age, I can't stop you from leaving and neither can anyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 07-26-2017, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T10:18:03-07:00","id":1120881,"title":"","content":"Eeep <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> but if you don't let it discourage you it won't kill the project.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-26-2017, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T10:32:25-07:00","id":1120889,"title":"","content":"I do hope Duskage might come back. But don't worry, I won't let the project die. Not when we accomplished so much already. I mean, seriously, when I first posted this idea, I expected nobody to be interested in it. And yet, we currently have more than 110 pages, full rules to play both Princesses AND the Darkness in Hunters, and not less than 6 new Compacts and Conspiracies. I am honestly amazed by what we already accomplished in so little time. And I want to finish it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T11:23:26-07:00","id":1120917,"title":"","content":"Okay, I was willing to sit this one out, but when I get back to my barracks I'm throwing down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T11:27:10-07:00","id":1120920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120917#post1120917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I was willing to sit this one out, but when I get back to my barracks I'm throwing down.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would be best if we didn't do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T11:32:48-07:00","id":1120922,"title":"","content":"Ideas, boss, throwing down ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T11:42:52-07:00","id":1120928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120922#post1120922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ideas, boss, throwing down ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh...phew. Sorry for jumping to conclusions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T11:45:45-07:00","id":1120930,"title":"","content":"In your defence, I made the same mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T12:33:04-07:00","id":1120959,"title":"","content":"*Cracks knuckles* Okay, let's hit this bitch head on. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9PaphOzOBBc\" target=\"_blank\">Music, maestro.</a><br /> <br /> So, let me start with the compacts.<br /> <br /> <b>#Ammit</b><br /> <br /> I honestly need clarification, are they still <i>under</i> Storms control, or have they bucked and struck out on their own? Otherwise, their role as a hacktivist group trying to root out corruption by rooting out the actual roots is interesting, and I do appreciate that they focus on the Darkness and not princesses. Let's face it, you can't have a book about Hunters focused on princesses without looking at the Darkness as well. Also, like the fact that they're also easily enraged. Internet anger is a dangerous force.<br /> <br /> <b>Character Risk Analysis</b><br /> <br /> Frankly my favorite group, because they're willing to look at the damages a princess can do without realizing it. One things Sailor Moon Abridged did was mention that there's still a world around being affected by this shit, Because like it says in the TFV write-up, you sometimes <i>have</i> to let a bad guy stay to keep a worse guy in check. So personally, I say keep them as-is.<br /> <br /> <b>Star of Bethlehem</b><br /> <br /> Frankly, feels weak. I don't know if it's the fact that I can't see such a group of concerned parents being able to organize at a compact level with such a frankly narrow goal (Which to me reads as &quot;Always save the princess&quot;) or if the logistics of keep that many families in contact is a little bit of a stretch. I mean the baseline concept of treating princesses as children, I'm liking it, but maybe we could add some more detail and specifics?<br /> <br /> <b>Overall</b><br /> <br /> #Ammit and Star of Bethlehem feel weak, and could definitely use more details about what they do. For #Ammit, a little more history? What they did as a stormite cult, what exactly was the tipping point, a base to build off.<br /> <br /> Star, I'm honestly worried it might be too weak. If these parents are so concerned about their children, how do they organize? How did their kids let slip about the queens so easily? Why aren't they part of another compact or conspiracy? Give us a history here, not just a blanket statement.<br /> <br /> And now, conspiracies.<br /> <br /> <b>Cold Guard</b><br /> <br /> I actually PM'ed Dusk about this. Basically, if the princesses are supernatural royalty, the Cold Guard as a foil are humanist egalitarians to the extreme, the ultimate expression of &quot;Humanity, Fuck Yeah&quot;. They look at the failures of the other &quot;supernatural kingdoms&quot; like princesses, witches, and mummies, and then point to all that humans have accomplished. They don't want a kingdom, that idea failed and failed hard. They want to keep what's here, now, still working even with the flaws.<br /> <br /> <b>Crown Jewels</b><br /> <br /> If I'm reading this right, the crown jewels are the willing servants of the princesses. To which I must frankly say, &quot;Hell the fuck no&quot;. I could handle Division Six because, hey, the Seers are good at pulling the wool over people's eyes and they're probably as afraid of Division Six as other witches are. Les Mysteries are based off of dozens of spiritual beliefs and faiths, so again, there's a basis for thinking they're on the right side. This? Ehhhhhhhhhh. Play up the manipulation angle a little more, make it clear they're controlling the nobles so well that &quot;Puppet on a string&quot; is too dignified. We're talking about getting tyke-bombs to do the bidding of &quot;valets&quot; after all. If they're angling to be the power behind the throne, make it clear that the nobles aren't going to have a say in the matter if the Jewels get their way.<br /> <br /> <b>Magisters of the Economie</b><br /> <br /> Basically the same idea I suggested for the Crown Jewels, only with more kidnapping and human trafficking. So really, why the human trafficking angle at all?<br /> <br /> <b>Overall</b><br /> <br /> Basically, there's probably a reason each sourcebook only has one conspiracy a pop. So here's my suggestion; merger. They all hold the old ways of the Kingdom in contempt, they all view princesses on a range from &quot;naive children&quot; to &quot;idiotic relics&quot;, and (again, if I read things right), none of them care to see the Kingdom return and wipe away everything that's happened since the fall.<br /> <br /> Also, guess what guys, rewrites happen. Kings and I went through a lot of work on Dream Catchers to make it reasonably in-line with my opinions on Hunters as Kings kept me in-line on how the rules worked for Changeling. Sometimes you just have to go back and work on something to make it good. Don't be afraid to reach into the guts and tweak a few knobs and gears.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T12:59:13-07:00","id":1120978,"title":"","content":"I for one am ok with at least trying out the idea of combining the conspiracies. But I want to hear their creators talk about their ideas first.<br /> <br /> EDIT: you also make good points about the Star of Bethlehem. It's taking a concept that works for an individual character who stays at Tier 1 or joins a group to help their kid and tries to turn that concept into a full Compact.<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: That said, I disagree about playing up the manipulation angle for the Crown Jewels. Radiant Nobles are probably the most connected and united out of all supernaturals and if one of the smarter Graces caught on to what the Jewels were doing, it would be up on the in-universe Princess forums and confirmed by other Nobles faster than you can say &quot;there goes your Endowment&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 07-26-2017, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T13:12:16-07:00","id":1120984,"title":"","content":"Also, #Ammit is a -former- Stormwracked cult. They got sick of being the torch-wielding mob and went and became social manipulators who take great care in picking out worthy targets both human and supernatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T13:14:42-07:00","id":1120986,"title":"","content":"Well, let's see what I can answer to each....<br /> <br /> <b>#Ammit</b><br /> <br /> They were still Stormwracked in the original idea, but yeah, in the current version, I would say this has been discarded... somewhat. From what I understand, they STILL consider they serve the Queen of Storms in their own way and still believe in her ideal to eradicate the Darkness (just using a different method), but they no longer use Tempesta Sworn abilities, nor do they use the terrorist methods of the Stormwracked... most of the time at least. I am not sure how the Queen of Storms feel about them, though, nor do I know if Stormwracked, Princesses of Storms and Goalenu would approve of what they do. I think King Raven would answer to this particular question better than I would.<br /> <br /> <b>Character Risk Analysis</b><br /> <br /> Not much to say about them, you seem to like their group anyway.<br /> <br /> <b>The Star of Bethleem</b><br /> <br /> Well, I do think they lack a subfaction, so yeah, I guess adding a few things to them would be cool. Personally I like them as the guys who call out the Queens for essentially turning Princesses into a Child Soldiers (however justified this point of view is). Not sure what we should add, but regarding your doubt on parents being ready to do that... you'd be surprised what parents are ready to do in real life to protect their children.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Cold Guard</b><br /> <br /> Soooo, basically they are the Equalists from Legend of Korra ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Crown Jewels</b><br /> <br /> I'll have to strongly disagree with you on that one. For starter, I really wanted a Sworn-based Conspiracy from the moment I started working on this project, as I felt this was a perfect way to make connections between the two and give additional world-building; I feel like there was a lot of potential to it. Second, Sworns in general, at least the way I understand the concept aren't really valet as much as they are <i>knights</i>, which is much more valuable. Third, they provide a Conspiracy who actually is pro-Nobles, which makes for a nice contrast to the Cold Guard and the Magisters (ESPECIALLY the Magisters, who have a somewhat similar origin gone in a different direction). And last but not least, I don't get the feeling they are &quot;servants&quot; when I read their entry; more that they have since become their own entity and try to keep helping the Nobles... while still making secrets behind their back and being afraid they would find out. That makes them rather unique not only in this supplement, but in Hunter in general. I am NOT removing them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Magisters of the Economie</b><br /> <br /> ... No, really not at all. If anything, the Magisters are the OPPOSITE of the Crown Jewels; former allies/servants who went rogue out of envy and try to replace the Nobles, only to become a grotesque parody of them. I mean, they are not manipulating Nobles, they are using them as power sources. And the human trafic thing is meant to emphasize their contrast with Nobles and twisted sense of morality. Really, if your idea of rewriting the Crown Jewels is to make them more like the Magisters, then it's a big NO, because that would be completely missing the point of both factions.<br /> <br /> <b>Overall</b><br /> <br /> I'm not entirely opposed to rewrite, but in this case, I don't see the point of combining any of the three conspiracies; they have all very distinct identities, stories, powers and motivations, we couldn't combine them without losing something. The Cold Guard doesn't fit with any of the two, while the Magisters and Crown Jewels are basically the opposite of each other. That just doesn't work.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sorry if I am a bit brutal, I just wanted to express how adamant I am about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 07-26-2017, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T13:57:38-07:00","id":1121011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120959#post1120959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>#Ammit</b></div> </div> </div> </div> Are they under Storms control? I think I can answer that one.<br /> <br /> If they're not physically attacking Darkspawn they're waaaay off the Storms reservation. They might consider themselves loyal to the Queen (I like the idea that they do, just because venerating hatred is an interesting twist on internet mobs), but at this point it's unlikely any actual Stormwracked would see them as fellow courtiers.<br /> <br /> If I was to change one thing about #Ammit it would be the other groups steryotypes of them. Emphasise a bit more that in many respects they're, well a mob, so they're unpredictable and you never know what will set them off and put you on their list.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120959#post1120959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Cold Guard</b></div> </div> </div> </div> As I keep saying these ideas could work if they were put into a broader context. If opposition to magic/supernatural wasn't the core of their philosophy, but a natural extension of it.<br /> <br /> If their opposition to any sort of kingdom was expressed as an opposition to any sort of radical change; French Revolution, communism, the Princess running for office, then you could make it work. You'd still hit the ocasional Princess who's a as much of a conservative as they are but on the whole most Princesses are pushing for large changes.<br /> <br /> (My faovourite of the broader contexts suggested so far was MB's interpretation; the one with not seperating good and evil)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1120959#post1120959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Crown Jewels</b></div> </div> </div> </div> On this we're going to disagree. I loath it when a Hunter group is secretly controlled by the supernatural, but if it's handled carefully I'm ok with a group that's openly and knowingly serving the supernatural. After all The Malleus Maleficarum would be more than happy to follow any order an angel gave (provided they're convinced it's a messenger from the Abrahamic god or His Son and not one of the <i>many</i> imposters).<br /> <br /> I'm not sure an entire international organisation of Sworn makes much sense. Given the investment it takes to create a Sworn Princesses usually pick people close to their hearts; so why would they be working far away rather than at their Lady's side? I'm willing to overlook that as a Hunter thing; but personally I'd have made them a Compact. Remember that scene in spiderman films where the citizens of New York rally to Spiderman's side. (<a href=\"https://youtu.be/dRuKh5TN-x0?t=1m25s\" target=\"_blank\">Like this one</a>.) That's how I would have done the Crown Jewels. Those citizens as protagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-26-2017, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T14:15:00-07:00","id":1121016,"title":"","content":"We can't make the Crown Jewels a Compact, for mechanics reasons: Compacts cannot have supernatural Endowments. Only Conspiracies have access to that; even when they gave the Compacts their own Endowments in Compacts &amp; Conspiracies, it was mostly mundane things. That said, I do understand your point, especially since with the exception of Stormwracked, Sworns typically need Princesses to operate anyway. But I don't think it's that hard to solve; nothing in the Crown Jewels imply they work away from Nobles, just that they have formed a larger Conspiracy behind their back; even even then, they did so with nothing but good intentions. You could have it that Crown Jewels typically stick to their respective Nobles, but every now and then keep contacts and operate together. Maybe we should add a rule in their Endowment that each of them automatically has a Noble NPC which they must keep contact with in order to retain their powers? That could be interesting, especially if we add an angle of having to keep a friendship with them while still not telling them everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T14:24:29-07:00","id":1121020,"title":"","content":"It does feel a bit weird that they'd do it behind the Nobles back though; or that any such network wouldn't welcome Nobles as full members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-26-2017, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T14:45:32-07:00","id":1121029,"title":"","content":"True, but in my defense the behind the Noble's back angle wasn't from me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T15:06:36-07:00","id":1121040,"title":"","content":"I may as well chip in on the conspiracies.<br /> <br /> The <b>Magisters</b> strike me as essentially the same as the Cheiron Group, Last Dynasty International in Mummy, or the alchemists in Promethean: mortals who steal power from a class of supernatural beings. They're only different from Cheiron because they specialize, and thanks to how the powers they steal work, they have to be more vile.<br /> <br /> The <b>Crown Jewels</b> don't feel like a group of hunters at all, but like a Camaraderie that's developed in a peculiar direction. I'd honestly rather see them in a pure Princess supplement with the focus of Damnation City or The Pack - talking about the Hopeful's support structures, how to build one for your campaign, and how to do a mortal-centric game in the Princess setting. The Magisters would fit in such a supplement too, as an example of a support group gone <i>really</i> bad.<br /> <br /> The <b>Cold Guard</b>, IMO, don't need reworking at all, just expansion. They're the only one of the three that isn't limited to the Hopeful (there's <i>lots</i> of supernaturals in CofD who look back fondly to a legendary era when they ruled the world), they have a take on the Vigil that doesn't turn up anywhere in official Hunter material, and they can provoke interesting moral dilemmas in a Hunter game even if you never throw a magical girl into play. What's not to like about all that?<br /> <br /> If this were my project I'd spin the Magisters and Crown Jewels off into a separate thing, and concentrate on the Cold Guard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T15:41:36-07:00","id":1121054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If this were my project I'd spin the Magisters and Crown Jewels off into a separate thing, and concentrate on the Cold Guard. </div> </div> </div>Yeaaaaah... let's not get too ambitious. We'll finish this supplement before we start working on other fan-made Princess supplements. It'll already be an accomplishment if we finish this.<br /> <br /> Besides, I strongly disagree on many points:<br /> <br /> * the Magisters are closer to the Promethean Conspiracy from Witchfinders, though I feel they have an identity of their own, So I don't think they are remotely out of place in this supplement, especially since, you know, they are about hunting Princesses. Also, yeah, they ARE different from the Group Cheiron. The Group Cheiron is a MegaCorp \u00e0 la Umbrella with power all over the world, most of their hunters are expandable field agents who gets monster body parts in their body as part of their sick experiment, and they try to use the supernaturals to industrial means, so they can make better products; meanwhile the Magisters are a group of rich people, their hunters are the privilegied boss, and they try to get supernatural powers through personal means, so they can themselves get poweful. It's a very different approach.<br /> <br /> * The Cold Guard are NOT the only one to not focus on Princesses; the Magisters are mentioned to hunt supernaturals as part of trying to act like Princesses, and the Crown Jewels fight the Darkness too.<br /> <br /> * I already explained why the Crown Jewels were important to me. Why exactly do you feel they don't feel like hunters at all? As far as I am concerned, Hunter pretty much covers all humans who become aware of the supernaturals and decide to do something against them. The Crown Jewels fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T15:53:26-07:00","id":1121063,"title":"","content":"Feedback. I'd Quote, but the replies have since gotten a bit lengthy.<br /> <br /> <b>#Ammit</b>: They don't use the same violent tactics, but they are still the Internet Hate Machine in the service of Storm's creed (Destroy the Darkness)<br /> <br /> <b>CRA</b>: Amoral PR people. They offer a fine addition to the grey ranks of the Vigil.<br /> <br /> <b>Star of Bethlehem</b>: Honestly? They could probably be wrapped up into either the Talbot Group or Habibti Ma.<br /> <br /> <b>Cold Guard</b>: They really need their philosophy ironed out, followed by their Endowment. Or even the other way around. As it currently stands, many sides have merit that they need to be clarified, it is just - which take?<br /> <br /> <b>Crown Jewels</b>: I see them as basically a Mercenary Group. Princesses might need them if they require more Sworn than they can support, or specialized skills. The Jewels get Wisps and Bequests, and other material support. It could even be their (Hunter-like) secret on how they operate without needing Princesses (and without being Stormwracked).<br /> <br /> <b>Magisters</b>: Cheiron focuses on monster parts and medicine. Magisters are the dirty bastard, general capitalist who is more socio-political. Maybe their Endowment could use a bit of tinkering (and their name seems clunky).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-26-2017, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T15:58:30-07:00","id":1121065,"title":"","content":"Fair enough regarding the Star of Bethlehem, but I still don't think they should be removed.<br /> <br /> And not necessarly a bad idea regarding the Crown Jewels.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T16:04:18-07:00","id":1121068,"title":"","content":"So, the <b>Cold Guard</b>.<br /> <br /> Philosophically, I like them with the concept that Good and Evil aren't so clearly defined, and clash with the Nobles in that regard. Not sure how to elaborate on that, though.<br /> <br /> I like the feel of their original take/Endowment of using the powers of the Darkness toward good/better ends (martyring themselves the whole time). It suggests that Darkness can be used for selfless ends, just like the Magisters demonstrate the Light being used for selfish ends. (And if that flaunts Princess's own setting? Well, Hunter <i>is</i> known for playing a bit loose with the other Gamelines' rules.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-26-2017, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T17:01:33-07:00","id":1121095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121054#post1121054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* the Magisters are closer to the Promethean Conspiracy from Witchfinders, though I feel they have an identity of their own, So I don't think they are remotely out of place in this supplement, especially since, you know, they are about hunting Princesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. It's just that, if it weren't so big already, I could drop the Magisters into Princess itself as an antagonist group, and they'd feel just as appropriate as they do here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121054#post1121054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* I already explained why the Crown Jewels were important to me. Why exactly do you feel they don't feel like hunters at all? As far as I am concerned, Hunter pretty much covers all humans who become aware of the supernaturals and decide to do something against them. The Crown Jewels fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Crown Jewels' thing is being Sworn (a Princess minor template) who are at one remove from individual Nobles. It's like writing up groups of free ghouls, or wolf-blooded, or Proximi as hunter conspiracies in a Hunter: the Vigil book. I mean, yes, those are things you could do, but it's more natural to explain ghouls as hunters in a Requiem book, wolf-blooded as hunters in a Forsaken book, and Proximi as hunters in a Mage book.<br /> <br /> It's not like a &quot;thieves of supernatural power&quot; concept, which could fit equally well as antagonists in a supernatural corebook or as hunters in a Vigil supplement. Allies, even uneasy ones, to a specific supernatural type are tied much more strongly to their sponsors than any of the official Hunter: the Vigil conspiracies are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T17:25:25-07:00","id":1121101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fair enough. It's just that, if it weren't so big already, I could drop the Magisters into Princess itself as an antagonist group, and they'd feel just as appropriate as they do here. </div> </div> </div>Very true. But to be fair, you could say the same of, say, the Cainite Heresy for Vampires. Or the Faithful of Schulpae for Mummies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Crown Jewels' thing is being Sworn (a Princess minor template) who are at one remove from individual Nobles. It's like writing up groups of free ghouls, or wolf-blooded, or Proximi as hunter conspiracies in a Hunter: the Vigil book. I mean, yes, those are things you could do, but it's more natural to explain ghouls as hunters in a Requiem book, wolf-blooded as hunters in a Forsaken book, and Proximi as hunters in a Mage book. </div> </div> </div>The Promethean Brotherhood was mostly founded by Sleepwalkers. And Spirit Slayer provides a merit to play as a Wolf-Blooded. I don't think it's that big of a deal. And again, makes for nice world-building.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T18:38:33-07:00","id":1121132,"title":"","content":"So here's an idea for a fiction piece.<br /> <br /> <b>Task Force: VALKYRIE<br /> File: 319-G3-EJ2<br /> Operation Code Name: GALE</b><br /> <br /> <b>Summary:</b> In coordination with in-place DoD assets, task force domestic agents have for the past several months been tracking a threat that is believed to be emerging after a period of either enforced hibernation or coordinated rising (Related file; MARIANAS) in operations against national interests. Information to be expanded in the following report.<br /> <br /> Initial contact with new confirmed class of P/S-ENE, calling themselves &quot;princesses&quot;, &quot;nobles&quot;, and various like titles, have begun cropping up heavily in the San Francisco area since roughly 1982, and have continued to grow in number as time has gone on. Individuals are proactive in activities according to several reports from MRU 10-8 and from Agilaz Group on what was once thought to be an upswing in P/S-ENE activity related to what was presumed to be VOLVA incidents. Further inquiry required several interviews and suborning of local resources to discern the reality of the situation.<br /> <br /> Aforementioned P/S-ENEs given temporary designation of &quot;Brynhildr&quot;; rough psychological profiling in the field suggests individuals are primarily concerned with what would be considered &quot;traditional&quot; ideals on morality, good and evil, right and wrong. Have been noted as unwilling to resort to extreme measures when faced with adversity, though have also been noted as being skilled in influencing others to do what P/S-ENE desires. Situation compounded by apparent ages of targets; oldest to date encountered claimed to be 19 years old. Claims from subject ENEs suspect and require confirmation from command.<br /> <br /> Individuals believed to be responsible for hindering task force operations in San Francisco, Glasgow, Milan, and Tokyo. Commonality is their belief that task force personnel and enthralled to a &quot;darkness&quot; and must be willing to work &quot;in the light&quot; to &quot;restore the kingdom&quot;. Believed to be barely disguised attempts to coerce task force personnel and seconded personnel to become traitorous and turn allegiances. Claims of a &quot;kingdom&quot; taken to imply massive socio-political upheaval and revelation of highly classified incidents.<br /> <br /> Further information has revealed rough factional differences between subjects, though details are being determined in the field. Recommend personnel do all possible to secure one subject over the age of 18 alive for questioning.<br /> <br /> *Stamp: PRIORITY CODE: RAGNAROK*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T18:49:16-07:00","id":1121141,"title":"","content":"Pretty good! Feel free to add it on the doc, either in the Quote and Fiction section or in the part of the book where you think it'll best fit. And thanks for finally doing more fictions!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T22:21:37-07:00","id":1121196,"title":"","content":"The thing is hunter's hunter not be simplely people who understands the supernatural or else every mortel game would be a hunter game so jewels need to go plus there not grey anuff they seem to much like good guy for hunter so remove cwrone jewel","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T22:23:39-07:00","id":1121197,"title":"","content":"But that's just me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T22:39:22-07:00","id":1121199,"title":"","content":"Haven't read the entire document but skimmed it, but I'm willing to give a hand. I'd need to revisit Princess a whole lot though.<br /> <br /> Doesn't seem we have Endowments up for the new Conspiracies.<br /> (Wait, I see them)<br /> <br /> We still adding more stuff?<br /> <br /> I'm not going to lie, the first thing I thought of to make a conspiracy to hunt magical girls would be to see what kinds of other anime genres would be useful to pick for combatants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 07-27-2017, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T03:18:18-07:00","id":1121243,"title":"","content":"Perfect idea almark what about mechs no really I'd play that to death but there's already mech conspiracy for monarch","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T03:26:34-07:00","id":1121244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121199#post1121199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not going to lie, the first thing I thought of to make a conspiracy to hunt magical girls would be to see what kinds of other anime genres would be useful to pick for combatants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have any recommendation? I suppose the hardest part is justifiable motivations that fit the setting. As I understand, many of the anti-MG opponents are either &quot;evil&quot; (in nature, or manipulated) or have reasons stemming from the nature of that series' MG.<br /> <br /> I'd say we could use another Compact or two, but I'm not sure based around what...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T04:00:12-07:00","id":1121249,"title":"","content":"I just want to say that, all in all, I personally like most of the groups in the doc. Sure, some of them may need to be expanded a little, and some of the Endowments may need a some kick (I've always felt the Cold Guard's were a bit crowded, even though I liked the rest of the groups writeup), but I haven't found some &quot;deal breaker&quot;. For example, one of the things Hunter Conspiracies tends to do is &quot;mass producing&quot; a certain type of Supernatural Merits (which is their Endowment). I see nothing wrong with certain Hunter orgs working with monsters to achieve that goal and fight worse monsters- like how the Crown Jewels work with Nobles in order to fight the Darkness. Notice that I've said &quot;with&quot; and not &quot;for&quot;- because that may be an important factor for the group (not that there aren't groups who work &quot;for&quot; monsters. The Knights of St George work for the Faceless Angels, and I actually find it as cool).<br /> <br /> The only revision I could suggest for the group is to embrace the &quot;mass producing&quot; aspect of Endowment and instead of the hunters personally present their oath to a noble, they present it to some high ranked member of the conspiracy, which in turn was has pledged to another member, which has pledged to another member, etc, etc, until getting to one of a few actual Nobles which support the conspiracy. That serves a number of goals- first, it reinforce the theme of &quot;serving nobility&quot; which the conspiracy has, by creating a some sort of feudal system with the &quot;king&quot; being the Nobles on the top. Second, ti gives much more freedom for the conspiracy, as they pledge their loyalty to the organization itself instead to one of the Nobles. Third, it may allow you to reduce the number of Nobles needed to support the conspiracy, and making it more realistic. Finally, it may put the hunters at odds with Nobles which are not a part of the conspiracy, as the act may not be liked by certain Nobles which would find it as unnatural (and probably a corruption of the Darkness), a way for them to lose their power, or both. Hunters doing things which the monster they hunt can't understand is also a part of Hunter, after all, and the monsters really don't like it when it happens.<br /> <br /> Still, it is just a suggestion- so feel free to ignore it! Remember that not every hunter group is for everyone. It is true for canon, and especially true for homebrew. The most important thing is that you would understand what you group is, and make sure it fulfill its potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 07-27-2017, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T05:28:05-07:00","id":1121266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thing is hunter's hunter not be simplely people who understands the supernatural or else every mortel game would be a hunter game so jewels need to go plus there not grey anuff they seem to much like good guy for hunter so remove cwrone jewel </div> </div> </div>One: While I know it's rare, you <i>can</i> play a mortal game with no supernatural elements involved.<br /> <br /> Two: ... Yes, they are, actually. Regular mortal games typically involves humans who get confronted with the supernatural for the first time or are starting to understand it. Hunter, meanwhile, deals with humans who after becoming aware of the supernatural decide to take arms and do something about it, typically by hunting supernatural creatures (hence their name). That's pretty much the ONLY thing all hunter groups have in common, and even that is questionable (the Hunt Club hunts humans). I dare you find anything else connecting them all. And the Crown Jewels qualify for both aspect: they are in on the supernatural, they try to do something about it, and they fight malevolent supernatural creatures.<br /> <br /> And three: The Talbot Group. Yuri's Group, the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood. These are three hunter groups I can think of who are waaaaaay less grey and more straight good guys than the Crown Jewels (who at least have the &quot;work behind the Nobles' back&quot; angle and the fact they do some questionable experiments with the Darkness). So yeah, the &quot;not enough grey stuff&quot; argument doesn't hold much water.<br /> <br /> Conclusion: I stand by my point, the Crown Jewels aren't going anywhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We still adding more stuff? </div> </div> </div>We might, yes. The doc is overall complete, safe for the Philadelphia appendix, but we are still trying to add more. Mainly I take any fiction you guys can think of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not going to lie, the first thing I thought of to make a conspiracy to hunt magical girls would be to see what kinds of other anime genres would be useful to pick for combatants. </div> </div> </div>Not necessarly a bad idea. What are you thinking about?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Perfect idea almark what about mechs no really I'd play that to death but there's already mech conspiracy for monarch </div> </div> </div>... wouldn't that be a bit hard to swallow for the Masquerade? Then again, that never was an issue for Genius...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For example, one of the things Hunter Conspiracies tends to do is &quot;mass producing&quot; a certain type of Supernatural Merits (which is their Endowment). I see nothing wrong with certain Hunter orgs working with monsters to achieve that goal and fight worse monsters- like how the Crown Jewels work with Nobles in order to fight the Darkness. Notice that I've said &quot;with&quot; and not &quot;for&quot;- because that may be an important factor for the group (not that there aren't groups who work &quot;for&quot; monsters. The Knights of St George work for the Faceless Angels, and I actually find it as cool). </div> </div> </div>Thanks^^ finally someone who sees my point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only revision I could suggest for the group is to embrace the &quot;mass producing&quot; aspect of Endowment and instead of the hunters personally present their oath to a noble, they present it to some high ranked member of the conspiracy, which in turn was has pledged to another member, which has pledged to another member, etc, etc, until getting to one of a few actual Nobles which support the conspiracy. That serves a number of goals- first, it reinforce the theme of &quot;serving nobility&quot; which the conspiracy has, by creating a some sort of feudal system with the &quot;king&quot; being the Nobles on the top. Second, ti gives much more freedom for the conspiracy, as they pledge their loyalty to the organization itself instead to one of the Nobles. Third, it may allow you to reduce the number of Nobles needed to support the conspiracy, and making it more realistic. Finally, it may put the hunters at odds with Nobles which are not a part of the conspiracy, as the act may not be liked by certain Nobles which would find it as unnatural (and probably a corruption of the Darkness), a way for them to lose their power, or both. Hunters doing things which the monster they hunt can't understand is also a part of Hunter, after all, and the monsters really don't like it when it happens. </div> </div> </div>I guess that could work, maybe...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 07-27-2017, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T06:37:46-07:00","id":1121281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121244#post1121244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have any recommendation? I suppose the hardest part is justifiable motivations that fit the setting. As I understand, many of the anti-MG opponents are either &quot;evil&quot; (in nature, or manipulated) or have reasons stemming from the nature of that series' MG.<br /> <br /> I'd say we could use another Compact or two, but I'm not sure based around what...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the two most important genres I thought about were...<br /> <br /> One attached to the mons genre. Friendship is a theme in princess and in the mods genre it's stresses to the point of being a relevant power enhancer. <br /> <br /> Mecha. Solely because I always seen its them as an opposition or cimpliemtn of mafical girls, being a heavily not favored genre and relying on machinery instead of tech. The main problem with mecha is that it is loud...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ameraaaaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121243#post1121243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perfect idea almark what about mechs no really I'd play that to death but there's already mech conspiracy for monarch</div> </div> </div> </div>Monarchs mecha conspiracy was designed for justifying one man armies figjtin g up against actual armies. The conspiracy as I envisioned it would have been overpowered to a degree that just doesn't happen unintentionally. .and it isn't fully completed either. We can use that theme again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So my current suggestion is maybe a conspiracy bases on the idea of.... converting both darkness and light into a fuel source, something tangibly useful that is decidedly dangerous, to power something maybe? A harvest of some sort. Take an incredibly utilitarian approach to everything and show they do have good containment protocols.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 07-27-2017, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T07:37:16-07:00","id":1121302,"title":"","content":"Good idea man guess converted energy is an isea","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T07:45:14-07:00","id":1121305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ameraaaaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121302#post1121302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good idea man guess converted energy is an isea</div> </div> </div> </div>Currently thinking maybe a good plan would be something powered armor based, maybe fall them Knights of Something","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T08:59:51-07:00","id":1121331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121305#post1121305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Currently thinking maybe a good plan would be something powered armor based, maybe fall them Knights of Something</div> </div> </div> </div>So, how would they combine Darkness and Light?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T09:19:21-07:00","id":1121339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121331#post1121331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, how would they combine Darkness and Light?</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess some sort of device that converts supernatural energy into something they could use like an extraction device or maybe through rituals if you want a more magic feel. Creatures of darkness or light just produce it more than anything else.<br /> <br /> It's a really tough idea to be honest with loads of holes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 07-27-2017, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T09:24:15-07:00","id":1121340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121063#post1121063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Cold Guard</b>: They really need their philosophy ironed out, followed by their Endowment. Or even the other way around. As it currently stands, many sides have merit that they need to be clarified, it is just - which take?</div> </div> </div> </div> A good summisation. What take do people like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121063#post1121063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Crown Jewels</b>: I see them as basically a Mercenary Group.</div> </div> </div> </div> If you don't pay attention to the &quot;economics&quot; of it (or make most members mortals rather than Sworn) a mercenary group would be more interesting than Sworn-as-an-organised-group. And putting a bit more emotional distance between the members and the Nobles they work with would help justify why there is a separate organisation that's not full of Nobles.<br /> <br /> Perhaps go with the more archaic name &quot;Free Company&quot;; as it's more medieval and tied into real world nobility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121068#post1121068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Philosophically, I like them with the concept that Good and Evil aren't so clearly defined, and clash with the Nobles in that regard. Not sure how to elaborate on that, though.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd say the obvious choice with the philosophy that evil is a part of every person that must be managed, not some external force (<i>Outer </i>Darkness<i>) </i>that can be purged. E.G. If you have violent urges, channel them into a sport like boxing, but don't deny or remove them or you'll make things worse.<br /> <br /> Then give them Darkness themed powers that let them manage the Darkness rather than destroy it outright. Examples would be powers to transform a Nest into a prison for any Dark Creature that enters it. Or to make a nest into a sponge, so that any time someone does evil in a wide area that Nest grows instead of a new one forming.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ameraaaaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121243#post1121243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perfect idea almark what about mechs no really I'd play that to death but there's already mech conspiracy for monarch</div> </div> </div> </div>However mech shows are very magical girl like in most respects. They focus on friendships, coming of age, etc. Also, as others have said Mechs are really loud.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121249#post1121249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only revision I could suggest for the group is to embrace the &quot;mass producing&quot; aspect of Endowment</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if you're willing to break entirely with the Princess setting; I took special attention to ensure there's no loophole that would allow mass produced Sworn as part of a general policy that there should be no magical silver bullets as an alternative to Nobles working hard for a better world. Even Alhambra is limited in the number of Sworn they can produce and they have a Queen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-27-2017, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T09:50:37-07:00","id":1121351,"title":"","content":"Quick step in, Cold Guard are being roughly turned into a force of egalitarian humanists opposed to princesses on princple, more details to follow. Now here's Cosmo with the weather.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T10:08:43-07:00","id":1121362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121132#post1121132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So here's an idea for a fiction piece.<br /> <br /> <b>Task Force: VALKYRIE<br /> File: 319-G3-EJ2<br /> Operation Code Name: GALE</b></div> </div> </div> </div>One small detail - when is this memo supposed to be written? The line &quot;oldest to date encountered claimed to be 19 years old&quot; suggests the early 1990s, when Hopeful over 20 are extremely rare, but it'd be good to be explicit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121249#post1121249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only revision I could suggest for the group is to embrace the &quot;mass producing&quot; aspect of Endowment and instead of the hunters personally present their oath to a noble, they present it to some high ranked member of the conspiracy, which in turn was has pledged to another member, which has pledged to another member, etc, etc, until getting to one of a few actual Nobles which support the conspiracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should mention that, in the Vocation edition, it's possible to build an organization that can create Sworn without any Hopeful members at all, by exploiting the rules for Nations. A Nation can teach its members a ritual that has the same effect as a Bequest; and the power to make someone Sworn is a Charm that can be Bequeathed. So you can define the Crown Jewels as a Nation that has an Accept Fealty variant as one of their Endowments, and they don't need even one Princess to support them!<br /> <br /> ... apparently this is one of my disagreements with Kings Raven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T10:13:31-07:00","id":1121364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121340#post1121340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only if you're willing to break entirely with the Princess setting; I took special attention to ensure there's no loophole that would allow mass produced Sworn as part of a general policy that there should be no magical silver bullets as an alternative to Nobles working hard for a better world. Even Alhambra is limited in the number of Sworn they can produce and they have a Queen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, who is to say that the Crown Jewels secretly <i> don't </i>? No one &quot;really&quot; knows what Mirrors is up to, and I think it was established that there could be/arise more Queens?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T10:16:05-07:00","id":1121367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121362#post1121362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One small detail - when is this memo supposed to be written? The line &amp;quot;oldest to date encountered claimed to be 19 years old&amp;quot; suggests the early 1990s, when Hopeful over 20 are extremely rare, but it'd be good to be explicit.<br /> <br /> <br /> I should mention that, in the Vocation edition, it's possible to build an organization that can create Sworn without any Hopeful members at all, by exploiting the rules for Nations. A Nation can teach its members a ritual that has the same effect as a Bequest; and the power to make someone Sworn is a Charm that can be Bequeathed. So you can define the Crown Jewels as a Nation that has an Accept Fealty variant as one of their Endowments, and they don't need even one Princess to support them!<br /> <br /> ... apparently this is one of my disagreements with Kings Raven.</div> </div> </div> </div>So at this point, there is a method in at least one version, and Hunter is known to play fast-and-loose with the setting constraints. I'd say it is good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T10:39:28-07:00","id":1121382,"title":"","content":"Alright, I'm back. And apologies are in order since I did over-react yesterday when I childishly rage quit. In my defense though, I did accidentally slice my ring finger open yesterday at work and needed to get stitches so I wasn't in the best frame of mind to begin with. I am sorry for reacting so poorly, it was more from the pain and stress than from anything actually said. <br /> <br /> That being said I am happy with the ideas that have been floating around regarding the Cold Guard. Flyboy254's got the right idea, and personally I can't wait to see what they come up with in the full write up. <br /> <br /> For now, I think I'm going to take it easy and just look specifically at their Endowment and try to work out something that will better fit and be more mechanically sound than their previous power. The first idea that comes to mind is a Carthian Law type Endowment where by fostering and manipulating the passions of the masses in a given area they can effectively cut off the Princess' power source, as well as that of other monsters who draw power from the Astral Realm like Beasts, Heroes, Goetia, and some Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T11:00:59-07:00","id":1121396,"title":"","content":"Honestly, physical injury is a good defence. Hope you recover swiftly!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121351#post1121351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick step in, Cold Guard are being roughly turned into a force of egalitarian humanists opposed to princesses on princple, more details to follow. Now here's Cosmo with the weather.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this decided? I admit I preferred the one about not seperating good and evil. But radical egalitarianism is a philosophy that could make them interesting foils for Princesses.<br /> <br /> If you're going this route I'd recommend cutting the Darkness from their powers and backstory, and making them more likely to oppose Princesses by competing with them rather than by trying to kill them. Otherwise they'd be a walking strawman who illustrates why egalitarianism is bad and a noble class is good; and I'm all in favour of egalitarianism. (At least, in the real world where noble classes are chosen by birth and not by the physical manifestation of virtue itself). Something like Carthian Law could work.<br /> <br /> I'd also recommending brushing up on the Court of Hearts section in the corebook. As hearts are simultaneously the Court most in favour of and the court most opposed a noble class. Their philosophy is nuanced. Also brush up on the Court of Mirrors who're flat out Princess suprematists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121364#post1121364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, who is to say that the Crown Jewels secretly <i> don't </i>? No one &quot;really&quot; knows what Mirrors is up to, and I think it was established that there could be/arise more Queens?</div> </div> </div> </div>Becoming a Queen is basically a victory condition in Princess (at least it is in Dream), so if they have a Queen who's able to act outside the Dreamlands you have to ask why they haven't won already. For Tears, Storms, and Mirrors have an obvious reason: Their Queens are all screwed up and morally dubious.<br /> <br /> But I'm not sure a screwed up and morally dubious Queen is what Darinas wants from them though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121362#post1121362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... apparently this is one of my disagreements with Kings Raven.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is. In Dream the Charm to Create Sworn specifically cannot be used by Sworn to prevent the following exploit. <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Create Bequest</li> <li>Create Sworn 1</li> <li>Give Sworn 1 Bequest</li> <li>Sworn 1 creates Sworn 2</li> <li>Give Sworn 2 Bequest</li> <li>Repeat until the entire world is Sworn. It's hard for anyone to do evil because of Sensitivity, and everyone is immune to becoming Darkened.</li> </ol><br /> In principal I could see an organisation being able to create Sworn on it's own working. But it would have to have some kind of limiter to avoid infinite Sworn. E.G. only a finite number of people<br /> <br /> That said; I still think mercenary sworn who contract with Princesses in exchange for Bequests or members being promoted to Sworn is the most interesting interpretation I've heard so far. And the one that best explains why they're a cohesive independent group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-27-2017, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T11:13:52-07:00","id":1121410,"title":"","content":"Sheesh, saying the truth, I have not seen it coming! I admit that I don't really know Princess that well (hence why I didn't get involved in this thread), but I assumed that hunters making Sworn without Nobles to support them wasn't something supported by &quot;canon&quot;, which is why I have suggested it- you know, to make the Hopeful outside of the conspiracy to say &quot;wait- <i>what??</i>&quot; when they meet with them, among other reasons. I had no idea I was getting into an Edition War :P <br /> <br /> About the Cold Guard, I do like that the Darkness is a part of their backstory. My personal preference would be that if it is toned down, at least it would still be a valid possibility to have it that way. Again, at the moment I do not plan on taking an active part of this thread, so those are still just suggestions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T11:15:53-07:00","id":1121414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alright, I'm back. And apologies are in order since I did over-react yesterday when I childishly rage quit. In my defense though, I did accidentally slice my ring finger open yesterday at work and needed to get stitches so I wasn't in the best frame of mind to begin with. </div> </div> </div>Welcome back! And don't worry about it^^ Also sorry to hear for your finger.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I'm not sure a screwed up and morally dubious Queen is what Darinas wants from them though. </div> </div> </div>Indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T12:10:36-07:00","id":1121445,"title":"","content":"Okay, so here's a better (but still rough) outline for the Cold Guard, or, as I feel would be a better pair of names...<br /> <br /> <b>The Peasant's Guard/La Garde de Paysans: The Egalitarians</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Ask yourself this; Why should the people trust a kingdom that fell?</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Basic background is that the Guard formed in revolutionary France, a force of peasants and artisans who took up arms after the storming of the Bastille. Seizing the momentum, they marched on the local noble palace, intent of making the local duke and duchess see for themselves the starvation and pain the people were going through. Only the castle was better defended than they thought, and after fighting through the ghosts and &quot;loyal&quot; staff in the place, they found themselves face to face with a princess of Tears. Suffice to say, she didn't last.<br /> <br /> Since then, the Guard has spent the better part of the first-half of the 20th century flowing from revolution to revolution in the name of the people. Their heyday was during Europe's Age of Revolution, with a lull between the age of revolution and the beginnings of anarchism, communism, and nationalism. Their numbers waxed and waned with the years, but something went terribly wrong in the Russian Revolution, and the Guard was nearly gutted by their paranormal enemies. Still, their numbers came back during the Civil Rights era, which also increased the Guard's numbers in America again after the disastrous anarchist era.<br /> <br /> It was at this time that the Guard found...something. It was some kind of &quot;anti-magic&quot;, a force capable of nullifying paranormal abilities (though not innate paranormal durability), dragging their foes down (roughly) to the level of the common man.<br /> <br /> Their focus on princesses came from their very origins, and the realization that there were paranormal &quot;royals&quot; abusing their abilities to become the absolute authorities over those who are unfortunate enough to be under their rule. This has also led to their encountering creatures that captured &quot;royals&quot; called the Darkness. Of course, the Egalitarians have also encountered other creatures in their time, and most often stand opposed to vampires and witches for their abuse of the people. Still, their numbers fell again roughly during the 1970s, until a massive amount of encounters were reported around the globe.<br /> <br /> Since the 1980s, the Guard fears that their old enemies are reasserting their goal of ruling all mankind. The Guard opposes the idea of what the princesses want to accomplish, seeing their &quot;kingdom&quot; as a relic of a bygone era, swept away when they failed to carry out the duties of a government. If the Kingdom collapsed, it should stay dead and let what other men have accomplished rule instead.<br /> <br /> (Again, VERY ROUGH, but that's what I've gotten for the general gist.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T12:22:26-07:00","id":1121455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121396#post1121396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is. In Dream the Charm to Create Sworn specifically cannot be used by Sworn to prevent the following exploit.<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Create Bequest</li> <li>Create Sworn 1</li> <li>Give Sworn 1 Bequest</li> <li>Sworn 1 creates Sworn 2</li> <li>Give Sworn 2 Bequest</li> <li>Repeat until the entire world is Sworn. It's hard for anyone to do evil because of Sensitivity, and everyone is immune to becoming Darkened.</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>Accept Fealty has a special limit that it won't work unless you have 3 dots in the right Invocation. So you've skipped a step in the list: &quot;2.5 Sworn 1 spends six Experiences to qualify for Bequest.&quot; Which isn't a trivial commitment. You can't get the whole world this way, just the people who are serious about following a Queen; and it'll take a long time to build up your numbers.<br /> <br /> Besides, without some such exploit as this, the Queen of Tears' cadres of Sworn couldn't exist, and Alhambra couldn't maintain itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T13:01:26-07:00","id":1121474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121455#post1121455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Accept Fealty has a special limit that it won't work unless you have 3 dots in the right Invocation. So you've skipped a step in the list: &quot;2.5 Sworn 1 spends six Experiences to qualify for Bequest.&quot; Which isn't a trivial commitment. You can't get the whole world this way, just the people who are serious about following a Queen; and it'll take a long time to build up your numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div> That doesn't matter. You're still looking at exponential growth so you can still get the whole world, it just takes a bit longer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121455#post1121455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, without some such exploit as this, the Queen of Tears' cadres of Sworn couldn't exist, and Alhambra couldn't maintain itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nonsense. You don't need an exploit to justify Tears' cadre of Sworn. Just say that the Queen of Tears handles the bulk of it personally.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T14:23:43-07:00","id":1121538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121445#post1121445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so here's a better (but still rough) outline for the Cold Guard, or, as I feel would be a better pair of names...<br /> <br /> <b>The Peasant's Guard/La Garde de Paysans: The Egalitarians</b><br /> <br /> <i>&amp;quot;Ask yourself this; Why should the people trust a kingdom that fell?</i>&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Basic background is that the Guard formed in revolutionary France, a force of peasants and artisans who took up arms after the storming of the Bastille. Seizing the momentum, they marched on the local noble palace, intent of making the local duke and duchess see for themselves the starvation and pain the people were going through. Only the castle was better defended than they thought, and after fighting through the ghosts and &amp;quot;loyal&amp;quot; staff in the place, they found themselves face to face with a princess of Tears. Suffice to say, she didn't last.<br /> <br /> Since then, the Guard has spent the better part of the first-half of the 20th century flowing from revolution to revolution in the name of the people. Their heyday was during Europe's Age of Revolution, with a lull between the age of revolution and the beginnings of anarchism, communism, and nationalism. Their numbers waxed and waned with the years, but something went terribly wrong in the Russian Revolution, and the Guard was nearly gutted by their paranormal enemies. Still, their numbers came back during the Civil Rights era, which also increased the Guard's numbers in America again after the disastrous anarchist era.<br /> <br /> It was at this time that the Guard found...something. It was some kind of &amp;quot;anti-magic&amp;quot;, a force capable of nullifying paranormal abilities (though not innate paranormal durability), dragging their foes down (roughly) to the level of the common man.<br /> <br /> Their focus on princesses came from their very origins, and the realization that there were paranormal &amp;quot;royals&amp;quot; abusing their abilities to become the absolute authorities over those who are unfortunate enough to be under their rule. This has also led to their encountering creatures that captured &amp;quot;royals&amp;quot; called the Darkness. Of course, the Egalitarians have also encountered other creatures in their time, and most often stand opposed to vampires and witches for their abuse of the people. Still, their numbers fell again roughly during the 1970s, until a massive amount of encounters were reported around the globe.<br /> <br /> Since the 1980s, the Guard fears that their old enemies are reasserting their goal of ruling all mankind. The Guard opposes the idea of what the princesses want to accomplish, seeing their &amp;quot;kingdom&amp;quot; as a relic of a bygone era, swept away when they failed to carry out the duties of a government. If the Kingdom collapsed, it should stay dead and let what other men have accomplished rule instead.<br /> <br /> (Again, VERY ROUGH, but that's what I've gotten for the general gist.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This ^ <br /> <br /> This so hard. Excellently done Flyboy254. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T14:35:44-07:00","id":1121546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121474#post1121474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That doesn't matter. You're still looking at exponential growth so you can still get the whole world, it just takes a bit longer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this is ignoring that Sworn can die and Bequests can be destroyed. Additionally, not everyone can be made Sworn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T14:38:01-07:00","id":1121550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121538#post1121538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This ^ <br /> <br /> This so hard. Excellently done Flyboy254. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Regarding the Guard and Anti-magic, isn't it stated that the Darkness consumes everything, even itself?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T14:51:58-07:00","id":1121558,"title":"","content":"Hence why I didn't mention that it came from the Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T15:05:13-07:00","id":1121566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121546#post1121546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this is ignoring that Sworn can die and Bequests can be destroyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even in the WoD the death rate isn't nearly high enough to outpace an expoential growth curve.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121546#post1121546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, not everyone can be made Sworn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that a rule in Vocation? In Dream anyone can provided they give informed consent.<br /> <br /> Regardless; even making 10% of the population Sworn is too much of an exploit in the rules; especially when there's no actual disadvantage to introducing limits to how fast Sworn can be made.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar483_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"483\" data-vbnamecard=\"483\">Flyboy254</a><br /> <br /> A little something you might like Flyboy<br /> <br /> But can a Princess not believe in \u00e9galit\u00e9 and support the R\u00e9publique will her charisma and magic? To this the Garde say non! A Princess can be noble in deed as well as name, she can be just, she can be virtuous, but there cannot be equality when one woman is placed above her peers by the Light. Every action a Princess takes to support the R\u00e9publique will only demonstrate that she is magical and a commoner is not; and the guard have no wish to trade a noble ruling class for a Noble ruling class. Even if a Princess would promise to depart the moment the last tyrant falls, how can the third estate hope to hold a R\u00e9publique that it did not build and shape with it's own hands?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-27-2017, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T15:27:32-07:00","id":1121576,"title":"","content":"VIVA LA REVALUCION!<br /> <br /> ...I don't do other languages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T15:28:50-07:00","id":1121577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121576#post1121576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I don't do other languages.</div> </div> </div> </div> Clearly. That's Spanish <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (I know this because I said it to the French woman who sits next to me in the office on the anniversary of the French Revolution)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T15:36:50-07:00","id":1121586,"title":"","content":"Well anyway, if anyone knows their European history, I'd be glad to see it so I can make a better write up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T15:43:51-07:00","id":1121591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121558#post1121558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hence why I didn't mention that it came from the Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eh? I meant it might offer a justifiable source. Using the Dark to consume supernatural power, even other Darkness-based powers. Unless you mean keep-it-vague so you can have multiple potential sources for their Anti-Magic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T15:44:41-07:00","id":1121593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121591#post1121591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you mean keep-it-vague so you can have multiple potential sources for their Anti-Magic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Multiple and unknown sources in the Chronicles of Darkness? No, surely you jest. *Grin*<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T15:47:21-07:00","id":1121597,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar483_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"483\" data-vbnamecard=\"483\">Flyboy254</a> Actually, as much as I like the flavor of the Peasant's Guard, do you think it might work better as a Compact, unburdened by needing to justify a clearly supernatural (and potentially hypocritical) Endowment?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T15:52:52-07:00","id":1121599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121566#post1121566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even in the WoD the death rate isn't nearly high enough to outpace an expoential growth curve.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't Darkspawn drawn to the Light, though? And Sworn being generally more risk-adverse? And the Vocation version needing the spending of additional XP (that not all Sworn might live to acquire)?<br /> <br /> I think those might be factors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121566#post1121566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that a rule in Vocation? In Dream anyone can provided they give informed consent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't know, but the downsides of Sensativity and being a target of the Darkness are nothing to sneeze at. This provides another break on the exponential growth scheme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121566#post1121566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless; even making 10% of the population Sworn is too much of an exploit in the rules; especially when there's no actual disadvantage to introducing limits to how fast Sworn can be made.</div> </div> </div> </div>They still need to acquire and dedicate the XP, then get someone else to agree. Before they get targeted and eliminated.<br /> <br /> Other supernatural creatures have potential exponential growth models, and they are held in check.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T16:29:04-07:00","id":1121610,"title":"","content":"The boss has made it clear that the Guard are a conspiracy, and a conspiracy they will stay unless I'm told otherwise. Plus, how often do we actually see <i>anti-magic </i>in CofD? We have the Supernal, Glamour, Innvocations, etc, but why can't we have something that <i>nullifies</i> instead of fighting on an even keel?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T16:33:54-07:00","id":1121613,"title":"","content":"I think having the Guard's Endowment be a kind of field is a good idea. The ideas going through my head right now is to diversify it a bit to allow for some effects beyond just nullification. The Nullifying ability will be what they're most known for, but the ability to galvanize themselves and their allies, or even conjure an entity comprised of passion &amp; rebellion might fun avenues to explore. Something like how the Marick Institute's endowments is several different merits that can be used together to great effect. <br /> <br /> That and the idea that their power stems from the collective passions and rebellion of humanity is a nice and potent parallel to the Nobles own abilities and power source.<br /> <br /> Examples<br /> <br /> ~ The People's Voice (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> &gt; Effect: Works functionally similar to current Endowment. Each dot makes it more difficult for supernatural creatures to draw upon otherworldly power. Doesn't work that well against natural abilities. <br /> <br /> ~ The People's Strenght (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> &gt; Effect: For each dot it helps other members of the Cell with rolls, especially when working together for a common cause. Think storming the Bastile and that's the image of this power in action. <br /> <br /> ~ The People's Will (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> &gt; Effect: Conjures a Tulpa created as the representation of liberty and equality. A astral entity that can match the Nobility and the most potent forces of the Darkness but at the cost of being difficult to control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 07-27-2017, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T17:07:25-07:00","id":1121625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121576#post1121576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VIVA LA REVALUCION!<br /> <br /> ...I don't do other languages.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Long live the revaluation&quot;? Mobs in the streets chanting demands for the end of inflation and a return to hard money?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T17:22:26-07:00","id":1121628,"title":"","content":"Well, I guess we finally have a background that works for the Cold Guard^^ Well done Flyboy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T17:24:00-07:00","id":1121629,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://orig14.deviantart.net/f88b/f/2016/185/a/7/image_by_herooftheemblem-da8sg7y.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> You're welcome. Now, let's get to some details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T22:36:58-07:00","id":1121720,"title":"","content":"Alright, little more detail on the Guard.<br /> <br /> <b>The Peasant\u2019s Guard: <i>The Egalitarians</i></b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cThe little guy isn\u2019t so little anymore, is he?\u201d</i><br /> <br /> The Guard is one of the few, perhaps even only of, conspiracies that can trace their direct roots from the present all the way back to their founding. That\u2019s impressive enough, but the second is that they\u2019ve managed to stay in place as long as they have despite being one of the youngest conspiracies in existence as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b><br /> <br /> The Peasant\u2019s Guard was a small force of revolutionaries in Northern France during the French Revolution. Angered that their grain was being squandered on Versailles and the noble palaces, the small force of farmers and artisans had heard of the unrest in Paris and across France. Gathering together, they realized that the target of their anger was obvious; the local duchess was nothing more than a pampered pet of her husband, growing healthier on good food as the children starved and the elderly withered away.<br /> <br /> When news finally arrived of the assault on the Bastille and the uprising Parisians, the Peasant\u2019s Guard realized their time had arrived. Seizing what few weapons they had and forming their band, they marched on the noble\u2019s palace and stormed the gates. The few guards fell quickly, unwilling to fire on their countrymen in such desperate times. Only entering the castle itself was another matter. The second the great doors were breached, the group was set on by all manner of household items. Wardrobes, coat racks, even the tea set and china were attacking them. Of course, once the initial shock wore off, they quickly set on the demonic objects with a purpose. Not only was their noblewoman a careless wench, she was a witch.<br /> <br /> Fighting up to her own personal chambers, they found her weeping over her vanity with her handmaidens trying to look threatening as they held daggers in their hands. They were easily dispatched, but the duchess proved to be a fight. Her magics somehow summoned up the ghosts of all those lost to famine and disease in the area, setting them upon family and friends in a nightmarish mockery of the fighting outside the walls of the palace. It wasn\u2019t enough though, the Guard struggled through to finally kill the woman. With her dying breath she cursed them, \u201cRebels, you\u2019re nothing but rebels.\u201d<br /> <br /> The men and women who killed her stood proudly, and decided to embrace the title she gave them. They also knew that where you found one dead rat, ten more were in the grain store. They spread through the revolution, scouring France for more beings like the one they found. They found them not just in the palaces though. They found them in the ghettos trying to burn down buildings that housed dozens of families, in convents trying to steer the faithful away from the love of God, even trying to build cults around their own personalities to make themselves the new queens of France.<br /> <br /> Eventually, revolutionary fervor spread across Europe, and in this new age the Peasant\u2019s Guard spread. The flame of the Vigil had been fully lit, a bonfire spreading through the disenfranchised and hungry of Europe. They cared not for vampires playing petty power games or warlocks trying to work bizarre magics unless they were actively worsening the lives of the nation like the \u201cnobles\u201d were. Yet in France, the Reign of Terror drew their focus back. What was supposed to be the beginning of an enlightened new nation soon turned into petty political scheming and bickering, ending in death and mayhem. Still, revolution does not die easily, and the Peasant\u2019s Guard persisted. They stood watch as France rebuilt, taking care to eliminate the diabolical nobles where they were found.<br /> <br /> So it went, for decades at a time, the Guard withering as the revolutions died down but not truly disappearing. There\u2019s always someone hungry, someone hurting, someone looking to find a reason. The Guard didn\u2019t stop hunting, they just became cleverer. Mobs of pitchforks and torches gave way to groups working to fight the status quo. Anarchist cells were suborned, new recruits to the cause. Freethinkers were interviewed, their ideas discussed in \u201chypothetical\u201d contexts for ideas and plans. The Guard spread through Europe again, patrolling the poorhouses in London and the factories in Berlin. More nobles were found, and killed. The casualties were high, but there were signs of progress at least. Members maintained what contact they could for the era, mailing coded letters by the fastest means possible and even paying off gypsies to act as couriers across the borders. Three groups of the nobles were securely identified; the Weeping, who claimed that everything they did was for a greater purpose. The Wrathful, who believed that the only way to save the world was to burn everything down to ash. The Selfish, who claimed that theirs was the only way, and that all others should pay heed and bow in supplication.<br /> <br /> Of course, you don\u2019t stay in the Vigil that long without learning about the other creatures of the world. For the Egalitarians, they found out that there were darker creatures involved in their war. Creatures that were men, or more accurately once men. Black, infected things that made their lairs in the dark and despoiled places of the earth. The Guard learned to fight these creatures out of necessity, but realized that such places acted as a honey trap for the nobles. When the nobles stopped coming, the Guard would destroy their trap and move on.<br /> Then the Russian Revolution happened, and everything went haywire.<br /> <br /> At first, the Guard took part on the side of the Bolsheviks, trudging through the Russian aristocracy to find the nobles hiding within. Then the Bolsheviks were pushed aside as the communists took control. Suddenly the brotherhood of communist principles was morphed into something unrecognizable, a police-state where only a select few held the power as the people were forced into subservience. Disgusted with what they created, the Guard could do nothing as the secret police rooted them out. It wasn\u2019t until later that the Egalitarians found that their enemies had used sections of the Soviet state against them, hoping to use the new power to promote their own vision (Unaware that the Soviets were already forming their own hunters to replace the fractured power of the tsar\u2019s court).<br /> <br /> Forced underground again, the Guard did little through World War II and the early years of the Cold War. Their state was bad enough that other conspiracies circled their hideouts and safehouses, hoping to snatch up the useful members and have the rest arrested or eliminated. Then the Civil Rights movement picked up in America, and the Guard found fertile grounds.<br /> Vampires hated the movement for \u201criling up\u201d once subservient feeding grounds. Werewolves raged at a passive flock stepping up to a higher station. Mages cursed the idea that those without magic would try to better their lives without their permission from on high. Worse, the \u201croyals\u201d appeared again. They tried to keep the movement in check, using all manner of foul and emotionally manipulating magics to steer the works of the great names of the movement into disrepute. The Guard took to this challenge head on, facing down these threats with sheer determination. Unfortunately, America\u2019s gun laws proved hard to face for the primarily European Guard, and casualties mounted.<br /> <br /> By the 1970s, the assassination of the great names of the Civil Rights era had taken their toll. The movement stalled, and the Guard was scattered around the world trying to reunite and return to their roots. Unfortunately, other conspiracies were enforcing the status quo as often as the monsters. American men in black, Catholic inquisitors, ancient orders wielding strange magics, all of them saw the Guard as much an enemy as the monsters. It was a never-ending source of confusion for the Guard, as they knew that secrecy of what was truly happening in the world was more valuable to their actions than revealing everything and causing a panic.<br /> <br /> That was when they discovered\u2026well, they discovered <i>something</i>. While fighting a group of the royals the Guard managed to dispel the magics the royals used. Their abilities floundered, their manipulations worthless. There was still a fight of course, but by the end the cell that found the \u201cgift\u201d gave them a leg up. They started spreading what they found across the Guard, and the group was saved from slow, lingering extinction. That was when more royals started to appear. Younger, yes. More na\u00efve about the world, even unwilling to face the fact that reality wasn\u2019t kind. Still, they were new royals. The Guard knew how to face royals now.<br /> <br /> Capturing one, she spilled everything when she figured out what had formed the group. She went on at length about the Kingdom, about its glories and the hopes and dreams it would save. About queens waiting to be returned to earth and the beautiful life they would bring with them. The local police found her body about a week later.<br /> The Guard realized that it was just one oppressor trading in the old ways for a kindly face. Where were these \u201cgood\u201d royals when the people were starving? Where did they hide when great men, men who changed the world without powers or magics, were cut down by assassins? What did they do when children grasped for help and found only scorn for the conditions of their birth. Their kingdom fell through the failures of the leaders, and their people suffered for it. Their time has passed like all old orders.<br /> <br /> The path has been paved for men and women <i>without</i> a fluke of birth to decide the path for the future. It doesn\u2019t matter that the princesses are younger now, because the world has changed in ways to give the Guard new blood as well. Angry young men and women are as upset with the new nobility of corporate shills and government patsies. Marchers and protestors are the new fertile ground from which the Guard will grow again.<br /> <br /> As it was in their early days; Liberty, Equality, Fraternity<br /> <br /> *A young man wears a ballcap, sunglasses, and a bandanna over his face, with a backpack on and a Molotov in one hand and a cell phone in the other. Hanging from a chain on his jeans are several transformation charms from various princesses.*<br /> <br /> <b>Stereotypes</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Union:</b> They have the right idea, but they get lost in protecting their little neighborhoods. There\u2019s a whole world out there, ready to be changed, and they just settle into their little ruts pretending to be the ones changing the world.<br /> <br /> <b>Task Force: VALKYRIE:</b> The governments aren\u2019t the greatest evils, we\u2019ve learned to accept that. What we won\u2019t is when their own pet monster hunters try to order us around. They hate the royals too though, let them do the heavy lifting then finish what\u2019s left.<br /> <br /> <b>The Cheiron Group:</b> The corporate rulers can be just as terrible and lordly as yesterday\u2019s nobility. We can\u2019t take them on yet, not until we stop the royals, but keep an eye on them just in case. And watch over anyone protesting their offices.<br /> <br /> <b>Ascending Ones:</b> You poison communities, you destroy all that people work for with your crime, and you <i>dare</i> to say we fight the same war? When did dragging mankind down count as protecting him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T00:26:00-07:00","id":1121739,"title":"","content":"Perfect wow amazing fantastic you should do this more often","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T00:50:05-07:00","id":1121748,"title":"","content":"I couldn't agree more. That was absolutely brilliant. The only thing I could possibly think to suggest is to change the word gypsie to Romani, or at least vagabond if you want to avoid cultural associations all together. Other than that, it truly is a work of art. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 07-28-2017, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T02:16:00-07:00","id":1121757,"title":"","content":"Okay, even I gotta admit, that's a way better backstory than the one we were using so far. Especially since it fits with the theme of Twilight Princesses giving Nobles a bad reputation. Gotta ask though, is the whole Beauty and the Beast furniture attacking something Princesses can really do? I read most of the Dream version and I don't remember seeing anything of the sort in the Charms.<br /> <br /> On a note, I am still not going to remove either the Magister or the Crown Jewels, but if we can flesh them out in a similar way, I am all for it.<br /> <br /> I also note that, with this new origin, all three Princess-related Conspiracies now have french roots in their origins. Maybe we should try doing something with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 07-28-2017, 05:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T02:31:02-07:00","id":1121758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121757#post1121757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also note that, with this new origin, all three Princess-related Conspiracies now have french roots in their origins. Maybe we should try doing something with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't see anything in the CJ or Magisters that requires them to be French like the new Guard are.<br /> <br /> Searching for &quot;Crown Jewels&quot; points to England, and &quot;Magister&quot; is a Latin word.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-28-2017, 05:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T02:37:28-07:00","id":1121759,"title":"","content":"The Magister of the &quot;Economie&quot;. Which is a french word, and the one who came up with them envisioned them as french. And we established sooner in the thread that the Crown Jewels had their headquarters in France.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T02:51:46-07:00","id":1121762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121759#post1121759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Magister of the &quot;Economie&quot;. Which is a french word, and the one who came up with them envisioned them as french. And we established sooner in the thread that the Crown Jewels had their headquarters in France.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were originally named Magisters, Unlimited, right? It was changed to Economie. And we could just as easily move the CJ's headquarters. Switzerland?<br /> <br /> For the Magisters, what about one if the French colonies? Or even Quebec (Canada)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-28-2017, 05:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T04:15:31-07:00","id":1121776,"title":"","content":"You really don't want the three Conspiracies to all be in the same Country, do you? Personally I see potential in it. Plus it doesn't really matter, they're all global by the moment of the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T04:33:44-07:00","id":1121783,"title":"","content":"My two cents is that France wasn't the only country having a revolution at that time. Looking it up, I found there was a whole &quot;Age of Revolution&quot; going on from 1774 to 1848 across Europe and the Americas. Perhaps the United Irishmen could be another source for them?<br /> <br /> That said, nothing against keeping them all French","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T05:15:17-07:00","id":1121789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121776#post1121776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You really don't want the three Conspiracies to all be in the same Country, do you? Personally I see potential in it. Plus it doesn't really matter, they're all global by the moment of the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually don't really care. You just pointed out that they are and I'm just trying to come up with alternatives or support for spreading them out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T06:14:56-07:00","id":1121799,"title":"","content":"My two cents/francs/pounds/dinero/lira/yen here, I don't think they should all come from France either. Surely we can be more creative than that? C'mon let's come up with some good stuff here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T06:49:31-07:00","id":1121809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121799#post1121799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My two cents/francs/pounds/dinero/lira/yen here, I don't think they should all come from France either. Surely we can be more creative than that? C'mon let's come up with some good stuff here.</div> </div> </div> </div>After throwing it out as a suggestion, I think the parallels between colonialism and the &quot;we can do better than you&quot; mentality of the Magisters is fitting for them originating in a colony (they also may have already been there, and the modern naming occurred after being colonized).<br /> <br /> The Crown Jewels, by nature, seem to have been multiple groups globally coming together. They could easily have multiple HQs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T07:18:39-07:00","id":1121826,"title":"","content":"Okay, let's see if I can't do some work on the Crown Jewels and Magisters then. *Cracks knuckles*<br /> <br /> Crown Jewels: Someone mentioned mercenary sworn, and I think we can expand on that. Maybe a princess of swords was able to amass a small compact of sworn, capable of standing as a strong defense capable of marching on nests and clearing them out. Only something went wrong one day, and the princess was cut down and left the sworn leaderless. Knowing that it was too late to abandon the fight. these sworn instead decided that there had to be other princesses in need of their services. Arming up and sending out feelers, they found other leaderless sworn scattered about the globe. Taking them in, this force realized that they were like the olden mercenary companies like the Swiss; they were good, and their services were in demand. Of course, this took resources and funding. So the highest princesses have been convinced to keep them on retainer, but allowing them their autonomy unless a truly grave threat exists. They are the Freie Gesellschaft, the Free Company.<br /> <br /> Magisters of the Economie: The fact is that princesses are trying to change a world that doesn't change without a reason. As was said by William Daniels, &quot;Economy, always economy.&quot; And there was money in what the princesses were offering. Only the problem was that it's hard to monetize hope. So the willy economists struck on an idea; deal with the princesses. Making deals with Alhambrans to harvest hope from specific areas. Selling arms to stormite cultists. Payments from the Radiant to keep the authorities off their backs. They soon became known as Maestri dell'economia, the Masters of the Economy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T08:35:25-07:00","id":1121870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121757#post1121757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, even I gotta admit, that's a way better backstory than the one we were using so far. Especially since it fits with the theme of Twilight Princesses giving Nobles a bad reputation. Gotta ask though, is the whole Beauty and the Beast furniture attacking something Princesses can really do? I read most of the Dream version and I don't remember seeing anything of the sort in the Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tool Whispering is close enough that I'd allow it as an upgrade that particular Noble came up with (or something a PC Princess could develop, if this were a P:tH supplement.)<br /> <br /> Alternately, she could have used ghostly retainers who had the Telekinesis Numen. That's actually more likely, since she called up ghosts in her last battle, and necromancy is one of Tears' specialties. (And in the original tale, the Beast's servants were changed into ghosts, not furniture.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121826#post1121826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magisters of the Economie: The fact is that princesses are trying to change a world that doesn't change without a reason. As was said by William Daniels, &quot;Economy, always economy.&quot; And there was money in what the princesses were offering. Only the problem was that it's hard to monetize hope. So the willy economists struck on an idea; deal with the princesses. Making deals with Alhambrans to harvest hope from specific areas. Selling arms to stormite cultists. Payments from the Radiant to keep the authorities off their backs. They soon became known as Maestri dell'economia, the Masters of the Economy.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO this one's a miss. The Magisters' thing is stealing powers from Nobles and justifying it as &quot;we can use them better, so we deserve them&quot;. Whatever they might pretend, they're not merchants, but kidnappers that sell people for magic baubles. Making them actual merchants diminishes them. Also, it moves them closer to the Crown Jewels' role of hunters who work with the Hopeful, instead of the venal antagonists they are at present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1133,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","user":"Michael Brazier","date":". 07-28-2017, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T09:46:52-07:00","id":1121914,"title":"","content":"Now hold on, the Magister's thing is stealing power from the Nobility because f$&amp;k those little shots right? But their core theme is that they are the Conspiracy that's like the archtypical ambitions Viscier. Having them sell their services to the Hopeful in order to lure them into a false sense of security is a perfectly good strategy, especially when by nature there are more than pleanty of reasons for a Princess to suddenly disappear. Plus it does play upon the nativity &amp; overconfidence of some of the Hopeful in a deliciously sinister way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 07-28-2017, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T09:54:09-07:00","id":1121917,"title":"","content":"So, kidnappers first, merchants second?<br /> <br /> They primarily sell Princesses back to the Wardens in exchange for power. Ostensibly, because they can use it better. But nothing says they can't extract some green from their targets beforehand, right? There is a reason the Viziers are in a position to betray, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T09:58:59-07:00","id":1121924,"title":"","content":"I don't know, the merchant angle feels like something capable of giving them greater depth as a group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T10:12:32-07:00","id":1121931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121924#post1121924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, the merchant angle feels like something capable of giving them greater depth as a group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they still can be merchants. Or venture capitalists. Everyone needs a day job. But their distinguishing bit is that they command the powers of the Light. By trading Nobles to Wardens. It's supply and demand, really.<br /> <br /> Do we have a quote for the Crown Jewels/Free Company, yet? Because with the mercenary focus, this quote now fits perfectly:<br /> &quot;Look, I ain't in this for your revolution. I'm not in it for you Princess. I expect to be well paid. I'm in it for the money.&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT: We do, I see. Does the above fit better?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-28-2017, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T10:18:27-07:00","id":1121938,"title":"","content":"I was imagining more, &quot;We're the best at what we do. That's why we charge up-front.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T10:50:32-07:00","id":1121960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121938#post1121938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was imagining more, &amp;quot;We're the best at what we do. That's why we charge up-front.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Also a good quote, to be honest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T12:02:15-07:00","id":1121987,"title":"","content":"Another idea for the Free Company. They're mercs, they're willing to work for anyone who can keep the money coming. Vampires, Twilight Queens, other conspiracies, even demons and mad scientists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T12:16:30-07:00","id":1121993,"title":"","content":"Well, you guys have been busy again, I see.<br /> <br /> I have a few things I'd like to say regarding all of this. For starter, while I admit the new origin for the Guard is good, I am less enthousiastic about the Peasant's Guard name. Yeah, I know, it makes sense give their new origin, but Cold Guard just felt like a catchier name. Also, I don't care how much of revolutionary they are, there is no way you can name a Conspiracy after peasants and expect people to take them seriously.<br /> <br /> Regarding Flyboy's suggestions for the Crown Jewels and the Magisters, I am afraid I am not a fan. In the Magisters' case, I feel we completely lose the original theme, which I loved for the whole Noble-wannabe (a fitting reference to the real life occurrence of rich middle-class who tried to be aristocrats, and was a big part in the cause of the French Revolution); moreover, I liked the fact their source of power was connected to the Warden, since it gave these more of a role outside the Dreamlands and produced some world-building. All these are lost in favor of making them glorified merchants. As for the Crown Jewels... I don't know, the mercenary angle feels a bit at odd with their base concept to me. Not sure how to explain it. Also, if they are mercenary who work FOR supernaturals, then yeah, not really hunters anymore. At least the original version had them hunt the Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T12:31:54-07:00","id":1122000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121993#post1121993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you guys have been busy again, I see.<br /> <br /> I have a few things I'd like to say regarding all of this. For starter, while I admit the new origin for the Guard is good, I am less enthousiastic about the Peasant's Guard name. Yeah, I know, it makes sense give their new origin, but Cold Guard just felt like a catchier name. Also, I don't care how much of revolutionary they are, there is no way you can name a Conspiracy after peasants and expect people to take them seriously.<br /> <br /> Regarding Flyboy's suggestions for the Crown Jewels and the Magisters, I am afraid I am not a fan. In the Magisters' case, I feel we completely lose the original theme, which I loved for the whole Noble-wannabe (a fitting reference to the real life occurrence of rich middle-class who tried to be aristocrats, and was a big part in the cause of the French Revolution); moreover, I liked the fact their source of power was connected to the Warden, since it gave these more of a role outside the Dreamlands and produced some world-building. All these are lost in favor of making them glorified merchants. As for the Crown Jewels... I don't know, the mercenary angle feels a bit at odd with their base concept to me. Not sure how to explain it. Also, if they are mercenary who work FOR supernaturals, then yeah, not really hunters anymore. At least the original version had them hunt the Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>The People's Guard, then?<br /> <br /> The CJs are mercenaries to Princesses - they still are based on Hope-powered Sworn, so they can't get too mercenary. They'd need to be a little choosey. But they can still be self governed, and not bound to Nobles. Ronin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T12:45:51-07:00","id":1122012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The People's Guard, then? </div> </div> </div>Less ridiculous, yes. But still not quite as catchy as &quot;Cold Guard&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T13:07:35-07:00","id":1122027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1122012#post1122012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Less ridiculous, yes. But still not quite as catchy as &amp;quot;Cold Guard&amp;quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, I was hoping the old Umbrae-wielding warriors could be salvaged, so there would be a group that could do raids in/on the Dark World an survive (maybe).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T13:08:21-07:00","id":1122028,"title":"","content":"I'm going to do a section by section read through.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121720#post1121720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Her magics somehow summoned up the ghosts of all those lost to famine and disease in the area, setting them upon family and friends in a nightmarish mockery of the fighting outside the walls of the palace. It wasn\u2019t enough though, the Guard struggled through to finally kill the woman. With her dying breath she cursed them, \u201cRebels, you\u2019re nothing but rebels.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd suggest a small tweak here. Rather than fighting a Princess on day one - since Hunters need strategy and preparation to take on a supernatural - they instead fight the dutchess' Sworn servants (who could still have control over ghosts). Sworn of Tears would be more vulnerable to a peasant zerg rush. And knowing the Dutchess is out there with power beyond anything they faced could serve as motivation to for the group to improve themslves and learn more about their enemy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121720#post1121720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">even trying to build cults around their own personalities to make themselves the new queens of France.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm guessing this is referring to Mirrors and not Tears?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121720#post1121720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They cared not for vampires playing petty power games or warlocks trying to work bizarre magics unless they were actively worsening the lives of the nation like the \u201cnobles\u201d were.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that Vampires and Mages should be high priority targets. As they'd be far more involved in the mortal politics the status quo against revolution than the Princesses of the era. Since Tears keep to isolated fringes where they can hide their wisp harvests, Storms don't care about politics, and Mirrors often have a... warped perception of current affairs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121720#post1121720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Guard spread through Europe again, patrolling the poorhouses in London</div> </div> </div> </div> You asked for European history. I'd suggest using Luddism (origonal worker's rights Luddism, not anti-science) and Chartism here. Both of those were more a Northern English thing, but there's more to England than London despite what urban fantasy might think <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I've even seen a little of it.<br /> <br /> Also, there was an Irish revolution about a decade after the French.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121720#post1121720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, you don\u2019t stay in the Vigil that long without learning about the other creatures of the world. For the Egalitarians, they found out that there were darker creatures involved in their war. Creatures that were men, or more accurately once men. Black, infected things that made their lairs in the dark and despoiled places of the earth.</div> </div> </div> </div> You should probably call out Infiltrators here. Since they love to build up cults and worm their way into positions of power, and then intentionally abuse them in the most evil ways they can think of here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121720#post1121720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves raged at a passive flock stepping up to a higher station.</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe use Beasts here, &quot;Beasts tried to teach chained men their place&quot;. My guess is that Vampires would mostly be anti-civil rights because no rights means easy meals. Mages and Beasts would be fighting on both sides. Werewolves would mostly consider it none of their buisness or in some cases pro civil rights because racism pollutes the Hisil.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121720#post1121720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Mages cursed the idea that those without magic would try to better their lives without their permission from on high. Worse, the \u201croyals\u201d appeared again. They tried to keep the movement in check, using all manner of foul and emotionally manipulating magics to steer the works of the great names of the movement into disrepute.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd suggest blaming this one on Storms rather than Tears. Tears don't care enough about mortal politics to get involved. But Storms would care about the fact that racism creates Nests. And their destructive campaign against the Darkness would bring the civil rights movement into disrepute by association.<br /> <br /> You from the Guard's POV it could be another case of nobles playing their games without thinking of the commoners who get crushed underfoot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121720#post1121720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> By the 1970s, the assassination of the great names of the Civil Rights era had taken their toll. The movement stalled, and the Guard was scattered around the world trying to reunite and return to their roots. Unfortunately, other conspiracies were enforcing the status quo as often as the monsters. American men in black, Catholic inquisitors, ancient orders wielding strange magics, all of them saw the Guard as much an enemy as the monsters. It was a never-ending source of confusion for the Guard, as they knew that secrecy of what was truly happening in the world was more valuable to their actions than revealing everything and causing a panic.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think this should be a source of &quot;confusion&quot;, seperating church and state was a big part of the French Revolution, so even if the guard didn't fight the church directly they'd still have a full understanding on the church's place in relation to themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121720#post1121720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was when they discovered\u2026well, they discovered <i>something</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div> Once their Endowment is written I'd suggest coming back to this and having more detail.<br /> <br /> I'd also suggest moving the Endowment closer to their origins because having an Endowment would go along way to explain why they lasted as a cohesive group for so long; and because it means you can play them in the French Revolution. Why wouldn't you want to support that? There could be plenty of spoils in a Tears duchess' manor to get them started.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121720#post1121720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As it was in their early days; Liberty, Equality, Fraternity</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd suggest using the French spellings.<br /> <br /> Some final random thoughts:<ul><li>Do we go &quot;all in&quot; and mention Trump or Brexit? Both had significant elements of a backlash by the working class against the elite. E.G. #DrainTheSwamp</li> <li>Ever notice how Twitter is just full of people using Harry Potter to explain politics these days? Nobody ever mentions that the wizards are privilged class in the books. #MuggleRights</li> </ul><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121757#post1121757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotta ask though, is the whole Beauty and the Beast furniture attacking something Princesses can really do? I read most of the Dream version and I don't remember seeing anything of the sort in the Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div> Phantom and Thinking could do illusionary furnature but apart from that the answer is no. Princesses are not nearly as good at magic that works independently of themselves as Mages are.<br /> <br /> MB is right that Wands could do it. There's no power for it written up but it fits their themes.<br /> <br /> MB's also right that telekenetic ghosts would be better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121757#post1121757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Crown Jewels, but if we can flesh them out in a similar way, I am all for it.</div> </div> </div> </div> I could have a try at making the mercenary interpretation of the Crown Jewels if you're interested.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121757#post1121757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe we should try doing something with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Swiss works great for the Magisters of the Ecconomy, all those banks. The Crown Jewels could perhaps be Italian, Portugese, Spanish, or Greek. All those areas have high unemployement (particularly among the young) without them facing life threatening danger or crime making it a likely place for people to latch onto figures of hope.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121870#post1121870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO this one's a miss. The Magisters' thing is stealing powers from Nobles and justifying it as &quot;we can use them better, so we deserve them&quot;. Whatever they might pretend, they're not merchants, but kidnappers that sell people for magic baubles. Making them actual merchants diminishes them. Also, it moves them closer to the Crown Jewels' role of hunters who work with the Hopeful, instead of the venal antagonists they are at present.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121914#post1121914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now hold on, the Magister's thing is stealing power from the Nobility because f$&amp;k those little shots right? But their core theme is that they are the Conspiracy that's like the archtypical ambitions Viscier. Having them sell their services to the Hopeful in order to lure them into a false sense of security is a perfectly good strategy</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with this. In a face to face meeting the advantage is with the Princess. There's a fair chance she's got a Charm that alerts her if the Magister is being decietful; or six plus dots in Empathy which is practically the same thing.<br /> <br /> On the other hand when the Magister sits in the top floor of the corporate tower pulling strings and making a few calls while the Princess sits in the boardroom of her 30 employee charity the Magister has the advantage.<br /> <br /> If a Magister is selling to Nobles than chances are the guy the Noble actually sees face to face is a uniformed UPS driver. Can't detect dishonesty if it's just an honest guy doing his job making a delivery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1121987#post1121987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another idea for the Free Company. They're mercs, they're willing to work for anyone who can keep the money coming. Vampires, Twilight Queens, other conspiracies, even demons and mad scientists.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd keep them Princess specific. They're working for things only Princesses can reliably supply; becoming Sworn or Bequests. AKA magic without decades of study, working for a dubious Conspiracy or inbuilt immorality (the only other group who can match the Nobles at creating minor templates are Vampires).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1122027#post1122027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, I was hoping the old Umbrae-wielding warriors could be salvaged, so there would be a group that could do raids in/on the Dark World an survive (maybe).</div> </div> </div> </div>No reason why it can't. The People's Guard are radical egalitarians. That's a very different motive to a unique philosophy of good or evil.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-28-2017, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T13:35:20-07:00","id":1122040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I could have a try at making the mercenary interpretation of the Crown Jewels if you're interested. </div> </div> </div>Be my guest.<br /> <br /> Also, good to see people mostly agree with me regarding the Magisters.<br /> <br /> Right now I am unconvinced by the mercenary interpretation of the Crown Jewels (though I admit the idea of Ronin Sworns does sound cool). But I'll wait to see how it turns out if fleshed out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T14:20:37-07:00","id":1122049,"title":"","content":"Well, if there's room for one more Compact then I could expand upon option #2 for what I would have done with the Cold Guard.<br /> <br /> Imagine this: Militant Budhist excorsists who hunt the Nobility becaus they numb people to the suffering intrinsic to existence. They use the Tainted locations along with Loci and Haunts and other supernatural places to test themselves as they seek enlightenment and an escape from the cycle of suffering. The hightest ranking members would be budhistatva-like beings who have reached an inner calm that makes them immune to Tainted locations entirely, and even allow them to astral project themselves into the Dark World. <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T14:52:31-07:00","id":1122068,"title":"","content":"Do any of us know enough about Buddhism to make that reasonably well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T15:05:03-07:00","id":1122075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1122049#post1122049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if there's room for one more Compact then I could expand upon option #2 for what I would have done with the Cold Guard.<br /> <br /> Imagine this: Militant Budhist excorsists who hunt the Nobility becaus they numb people to the suffering intrinsic to existence. They use the Tainted locations along with Loci and Haunts and other supernatural places to test themselves as they seek enlightenment and an escape from the cycle of suffering. The hightest ranking members would be budhistatva-like beings who have reached an inner calm that makes them immune to Tainted locations entirely, and even allow them to astral project themselves into the Dark World. <br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Might need more to be a full group. It would make a great plot or one-off, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T16:09:43-07:00","id":1122112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1122068#post1122068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do any of us know enough about Buddhism to make that reasonably well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not me. Buddhist ideas do contradict Princess in some ways, in that Princesses seek to improve the world and enlightenment is to escape the world. But I also know that Buddhist monks do typical priestly charitable work. So I doubt the Dalhi Lama would object to doing good. I certianly don't know enough theology to write a convincing Buddhist extremist group.<br /> <br /> I do have a half written not-Buddhist group from ages back. That is they're safron robed martial artist monks, but their theology is actually a syncretism of Buddhist and standard Noble ideas. Their monastery is built on one of the largest nests in existence and the entire monastery using Bequests to keep the Nest sealed*. They're basically a big excuse to play magical martial artists wondering the earth and fighting monsters.<br /> <br /> * This doesn't make any sense; because even the largest nest would have been destroyed after been rendered powerless for centuries while monks live virtuous lives atop it. One of the reasons I didn't finish it, though now I think about it a Dethroned would work here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T23:37:51-07:00","id":1122246,"title":"","content":"Okay, general ideas for the Guard's endowment source. Pick your favorite.<br /> <br /> <b>Sidebar: What <i>is</i> The People\u2019s Will?</b><br /> <br /> No one in the Guard is exactly a mystic or occultist on the level they would need to figure out what exactly their endowment is. All they know is that it\u2019s something special, and something they could use to change the world for the better. So, as the storyteller, you have options.<br /> <br /> <b>1: It\u2019s the Darkness</b><br /> <br /> The Darkness is a force, and it\u2019s somehow sentient. Everything else pretty much flies right out the window when it comes to actually understanding this stuff. What everyone knows for sure is that the Darkness can stop magic in action just by being present, making it misfire horribly and taking away a tool that many creatures rely on out of necessity.<br /> <br /> <b>2: It\u2019s a Lost Relic</b><br /> <br /> Some relics are imbued with magic, why wouldn\u2019t there be some that are a bane to magic? The Guard found a relic in the palace, a tool that the royal was hoping to bring to her queen in an attempt to possibly use it to save Alhambra. The location is a secret, but what is for sure is that its power is felt across the whole of the Guard.<br /> <br /> <b>3: It\u2019s Gestalt Energy</b><br /> <br /> Some fringe theories postulate that all of mankind has a collective psychic consciousness, capable of creating and destroying when a large-enough group of people agree on something as being \u201creal\u201d, or when an emotional drive is unified among a group of people. There\u2019s nothing quite \u201cmagical\u201d about the People\u2019s Will, but it certainly is an unknown by the rest of the world. That doesn\u2019t matter to the Egalitarians, what does is that it works against the royals.<br /> <br /> <b>4: It\u2019s Related to Witches</b><br /> <br /> Everyone knows that the most powerful magic users are witches, or at least they\u2019re the most numerous and dangerous. Maybe they were working on something to stop an enemy group of witches, and things went haywire. Their creation turned on them, and unable to stop it the group was unable to tell their fellows about it. The royal found it, but didn\u2019t know how to activate it. Of course, that implies that the Guard were able to find a way to make it work.<br /> <br /> <b>5: Fucked if We Know</b><br /> <br /> Let\u2019s face facts; the in this world things are just messed up. Whatever the People\u2019s Will is, it isn\u2019t something that just appeared one day because someone wanted it to. More likely, it was something that someone didn\u2019t want to see the light of day ever again. Of course, in the middle of revolution nothing stands in your way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T09:41:15-07:00","id":1122373,"title":"","content":"I approve of giving various possible sources for their power personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T10:59:32-07:00","id":1122396,"title":"","content":"And I will incorporate intentional vagueness into the write up for the powers themselves, like how those with dots in the People's Will often carry around a token that helps them focus on the gift (Magical artifact or related to Witches), or how the most powerful of the People's Voice manifestations often hauntingly resemble the Dethroned (connected to the Darkness.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T12:17:04-07:00","id":1122419,"title":"","content":"First art piece up! To start us off, a princess of Hearts and a TFV suit have a small disagreement on what's the biggest problem in their area as the shiki watches in annoyance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://sta.sh/01kb2cvzq4u3\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://st.deviantart.net/minish/main/logo/card_black_large.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://sta.sh/01kb2cvzq4u3\" target=\"_blank\"> DeviantArt: 404 </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://sta.sh/01kb2cvzq4u3\" target=\"_blank\"> http://sta.sh/01kb2cvzq4u3 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> DeviantArt is the world's largest online social community for artists and art enthusiasts, allowing people to connect through the creation and sharing of art. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T17:54:02-07:00","id":1122863,"title":"","content":"I like it enough personally^^ the Facepalming Shikigami is priceless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T20:06:12-07:00","id":1122883,"title":"","content":"Okay, some more ideas for the Guard.<br /> <br /> <b>Groups</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Channel</b> are the means the Guard keeps contact with their various cells. Couriers, messengers, and network administrators, the rise of cell phones and email has only made them more valuable as the keepers of the names and lists of fellow Egalitarians.<br /> <br /> <b>The Action</b> are the ground troops of the Guard, organizing the marches and strikes on their enemies. The most numerous, they\u2019re often kept in check by not being able to move without the proper intelligence on where and what the threat is.<br /> <br /> <b>The Patrol</b> watch for signs of the royals and other supernatural beings trying to gain control over the people; people acting oddly, non-sensical police crackdowns, and new trends in the local politicians\u2019 actions.<br /> <br /> <b>Status</b><br /> <br /> In the Guard, the ability to fight for the people against the paranormal and supernatural is an easy way to earn status, but even more vital is changing things for the <i>better</i>. Marching to change laws and social norms, dragging people kicking and screaming into the modern age, that wins points in the Guard\u2019s eyes.<br /> <br /> <b>Status 1:</b> You\u2019re new, you\u2019re angry, and you\u2019re ready to march. Not only do you have the ability to throw in for Vox Populi, you also gain a dot of Allies in the People\u2019s Guard.<br /> <br /> <b>Status 3:</b> You\u2019re a little longer in the tooth, but you haven\u2019t lost your passion. You\u2019re more an organizer now, planning marches and meeting with possible allies to accomplish the same goals. This means you have an ear to the streets, with three dots of Contacts in The Street, The Press, and The Poor.<br /> <br /> <b>Status 5:</b> History is a cycle, and you\u2019re experienced enough to help with the latest round. This has earned you not just allies, but friends. You gain tree dots in the Support Network merit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T04:03:15-07:00","id":1122960,"title":"","content":"Wait, so you don't want to keep <i>anything</i> from the Old Guard write-up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T04:49:17-07:00","id":1122967,"title":"","content":"He's just making suggestions","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T04:59:11-07:00","id":1122971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1122967#post1122967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's just making suggestions</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides, what actually fits from the old write-up?<br /> <br /> I still think what is there could be salvaged for a Conspiracy, but it would need a nice take on their philosophy to make sense. Something with Good and Evil being balanced or the same or both necessary.<br /> <br /> Actually, LostLight has a nice concept with their most recent Hunter group, the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1121751-penyihir-mayat-strains-of-cursed-blood-south-east-asia?p=1122670\">Penyihir Mayat</a>.<br /> <br /> I also vaguely recall a thread with something about Judaism and owning all your qualities (because God gave them to you for a reason, or something). I'll try to dig them up and edit this with the links/quotes later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-31-2017, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T05:09:15-07:00","id":1122974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1122971#post1122971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Besides, what actually fits from the old write-up?<br /> <br /> I still think what is there could be salvaged for a Conspiracy, but it would need a nice take on their philosophy to make sense. Something with Good and Evil being balanced or the same or both necessary.<br /> <br /> Actually, LostLight has a nice concept with their most recent Hunter group (the latest Promethean-based Cursed Blood one). I also vaguely recall a thread with something about Judaism and owning all your qualities (because God gave them to you for a reason, or something). I'll try to dig them up and edit this with the links/quotes later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I remember someone saying that in reference to Beast. I think the example was of a person who feels the urge to steal and is good at conning people should work for a charity, convincing people to donate","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T07:01:21-07:00","id":1123004,"title":"","content":"How much of this new stuff and fictions are in the google doc. I've been lazy on editing for a while and I want to get working on the new stuff, editing for clarity and style and so on","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T07:02:16-07:00","id":1123005,"title":"","content":"First result for a google seaarch <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> site:forum.theonyxpath.com beast primordial jewdism </div> </div> </div> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1104161-why-do-you-think-beast-is-good-bad/page2\">found it</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm not religious enough to really comment on the theological side ( <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> might be), but it just doesn't feel like it fits Beast. The idea is that negative urges should be turned into good actions. But few of the actions Beasts do to feed qualify as good actions by typical modern standards, and Jewish religious standards are even stricter.<br /> <br /> From a Princess perspective, Taint is formed when people hurt others. So wheather a Princess encourages people to redirect the urge to hurt others into a positive outlet - like running a butcher's shop - or try to purge those urges. She's still fighting against the Darkness.<br /> <br /> A hunter group based around a philosophy of good and evil would have to go further than quoting Rabbis to actually disagree with Princesses. They'd have to say that you cannot get rid of the negative urges or turn them to positive ends, but simply have to manage the damage they do and endure it. Though I'm sure there's a great group in that concept; and a nifty Endowment based around managing Darkness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1122419#post1122419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First art piece up! To start us off, a princess of Hearts and a TFV suit have a small disagreement on what's the biggest problem in their area as the shiki watches in annoyance.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://sta.sh/01kb2cvzq4u3\" target=\"_blank\">http://sta.sh/01kb2cvzq4u3</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Is it just me or does the Princess look more masculine than the magister? I think it's the thickness of her limbs and the sharp angles on the face?<br /> <br /> Darinas is right about the facepalming cat. That's neat.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T07:21:35-07:00","id":1123010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1123005#post1123005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it just me or does the Princess look more masculine than the magister? I think it's the thickness of her limbs and the sharp angles on the face?<br /> <br /> Darinas is right about the facepalming cat. That's neat. <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>The cat is lovely. Anyway, that's supposed to be an MiB from Task Force: Valkyrie, not a Magister","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 07-31-2017, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T09:55:02-07:00","id":1123052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How much of this new stuff and fictions are in the google doc. I've been lazy on editing for a while and I want to get working on the new stuff, editing for clarity and style and so on </div> </div> </div>The new stuff about the Peasant's Guard has been added, but the old Guard entry hasn't been removed yet, partially because I am still not sold over the Peasant/People Guard name yet and partially because MP has a different idea regarding that. Most fictions have already been added to the doc, but not all of them have been placed, and new fictions are welcome additions, since I feel we could use more of them. If you wish to add more, be my guest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it just me or does the Princess look more masculine than the magister? I think it's the thickness of her limbs and the sharp angles on the face? </div> </div> </div>I admit I kinda have the same feeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T11:42:55-07:00","id":1123093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1123005#post1123005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not religious enough to really comment on the theological side ( <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> might be), but it just doesn't feel like it fits Beast. The idea is that negative urges should be turned into good actions. But few of the actions Beasts do to feed qualify as good actions by typical modern standards, and Jewish religious standards are even stricter.</div> </div> </div> </div>well, I am no rabbi, but Judaism does have a very complicated relationships with &quot;good and evil&quot;. The reason is that in Judaism, there is no &quot;devil&quot; (I mean, yeah, there are evil angels, with Samael being their leader, but the point is that they aren't &quot;fallen angels&quot;, as angels can't fall. Demons, are another thing entirely, but they are also not the source of evil as much as being created by evil, like in Inferno. Lilith is such an example- as humans can fall, but angels can't). The basic principle in how Judaism sees the struggle between good and evil is that both good and evil are done by God. Good is anything which is just, or anything which is currently bad but is meant to bring fourth justice. Evil is anything else (that is, &quot;evil for its own sake&quot;). When something bad happen to a person, it is not because of the devil- it is because of God. It may be a punishment, it may be be a test, it may even be a reward- but both good and evil exist are part of God's plan. Turning against that plan means working against justice, and as such it means doing evil. Each person has what is known as &quot;Yetzer HaRaa&quot; (&quot;the evil desire&quot;), which is your little devil which whispers in your ear, a way for Satan to tempt you- but even that is part of God's plan, as he has created the Devil in the first place, so he could tempt you, so you could gain a reward for resisting that temptation, or learn something from the fall. In sort, the general view is that &quot;everything is according the plan&quot;, even if we don't understand it.<br /> <br /> Now, because of that, there are two ways the &quot;Jewish Beast&quot; may act because of that- the first is that she sees her Horror as the Yetzer HaRaa manifested, which tempts her to sin and so she must fight it as much as she can. The second is that the Beast believes that she is an &quot;evil angel&quot;, made by god to fight teach mankind and bring fourth justice. After all, a seemingly evil act which is meant to bring fourth good is actually a good act. The Beast does good by teaching mankind, for their harsh lessons create a better future. It is not that the Beast itself is a good person- in the contrary- but her actions are &quot;good&quot;. Eventually, the Beast should be punished for her crimes, like that the Devil is meant to be punished at the end of times, but that is what she was made to do, and it is her role in the world- and denying that role is the true evil.<br /> <br /> In sort, Judaism is not much about the &quot;balance&quot; between good and evil as much it is about &quot;everything has a role, and evil is turning against that role&quot;. Evil is not something god does- it is something humans does for themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T12:02:18-07:00","id":1123097,"title":"","content":"I know this is off topic but I have to ask:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1123093#post1123093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After all, a seemingly evil act which is meant to bring fourth good is actually a good act.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you mean &quot;meant&quot; as in the actor's intent? Or did you meant meant as in &quot;part of God's plan&quot;? I'm guessing the second, because the first one would allow for all kinds of puppy kicking evil if you could justify it to yourself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1123093#post1123093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second is that the Beast believes that she is an &quot;evil angel&quot;, made by god to fight teach mankind and bring fourth justice.</div> </div> </div> </div> Equally intersting is what a Rabbi would think of a Beast. I could totally imagine a Beast thinking they're an evil angel, maybe even having an angel shaped Horror. But they don't strike me as competent enough at teaching lessons to actually be angels. (Even if you ignore the fact we know their cannonical origins are the Tenemos, not the Empyrian, they don't have any supernatural advantage at choosing students who need a lesson or at teaching them)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1123093#post1123093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eventually, the Beast should be punished for her crimes, like that the Devil is meant to be punished at the end of times, but that is what she was made to do, and it is her role in the world- and denying that role is the true evil.</div> </div> </div> </div> So a Jewish Beast is supposed to be slain by a Hero and trying to subvert this narrative is the true evil.<br /> <br /> That's a pretty nasty gotcha for any Beast who wants to justify themselves by Judaism, and it could get interesting in the best way if that came up in charachter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-31-2017, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T12:29:50-07:00","id":1123113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1123097#post1123097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this is off topic but I have to ask:<br /> <br /> Did you mean &quot;meant&quot; as in the actor's intent? Or did you meant meant as in &quot;part of God's plan&quot;? I'm guessing the second, because the first one would allow for all kinds of puppy kicking evil if you could justify it to yourself.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>yes, the second. People shouldn't kick puppies :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T12:52:50-07:00","id":1123128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1123093#post1123093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> well, I am no rabbi, but Judaism does have a very complicated relationships with &quot;good and evil&quot;. The reason is that in Judaism, there is no &quot;devil&quot; (I mean, yeah, there are evil angels, with Samael being their leader, but the point is that they aren't &quot;fallen angels&quot;, as angels can't fall. Demons, are another thing entirely, but they are also not the source of evil as much as being created by evil, like in Inferno. Lilith is such an example- as humans can fall, but angels can't). The basic principle in how Judaism sees the struggle between good and evil is that both good and evil are done by God. Good is anything which is just, or anything which is currently bad but is meant to bring fourth justice. Evil is anything else (that is, &quot;evil for its own sake&quot;). When something bad happen to a person, it is not because of the devil- it is because of God. It may be a punishment, it may be be a test, it may even be a reward- but both good and evil exist are part of God's plan. Turning against that plan means working against justice, and as such it means doing evil. Each person has what is known as &quot;Yetzer HaRaa&quot; (&quot;the evil desire&quot;), which is your little devil which whispers in your ear, a way for Satan to tempt you- but even that is part of God's plan, as he has created the Devil in the first place, so he could tempt you, so you could gain a reward for resisting that temptation, or learn something from the fall. In sort, the general view is that &quot;everything is according the plan&quot;, even if we don't understand it.<br /> <br /> Now, because of that, there are two ways the &quot;Jewish Beast&quot; may act because of that- the first is that she sees her Horror as the Yetzer HaRaa manifested, which tempts her to sin and so she must fight it as much as she can. The second is that the Beast believes that she is an &quot;evil angel&quot;, made by god to fight teach mankind and bring fourth justice. After all, a seemingly evil act which is meant to bring fourth good is actually a good act. The Beast does good by teaching mankind, for their harsh lessons create a better future. It is not that the Beast itself is a good person- in the contrary- but her actions are &quot;good&quot;. Eventually, the Beast should be punished for her crimes, like that the Devil is meant to be punished at the end of times, but that is what she was made to do, and it is her role in the world- and denying that role is the true evil.<br /> <br /> In sort, Judaism is not much about the &quot;balance&quot; between good and evil as much it is about &quot;everything has a role, and evil is turning against that role&quot;. Evil is not something god does- it is something humans does for themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, would a Cold Guard that saw the Darkness as being part of God's plan (or equivalent philosophical grounds) be a valid concept, in their opposition of Nobles?<br /> <br /> IE. Princesses are Evil for trying to Destroy the Darkness, and the group uses the Darkness for good ends?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T13:00:16-07:00","id":1123132,"title":"","content":"Going by what LostLight said, they'd have to believe that not only was the Darkness part of God's Plan. But that the Plan specifically says that Princesses are not supposed to fight the Darkness. It seems like a weird thing to think. God created the Darkness, God created Princesses, but God doesn't want Princesses to fight the Darkness.<br /> <br /> I have to say I'm not keen on using the Darkness for good ends though as a foil to Princesses. For one thing the Court of Tears already does it (for a given value of good, there's a reason it's Twilight Court not Dark Court). More generally it feels less like providing a contrasting view to Princess and more like interpreting Princess in an overly narrow way. There's nothing that stops a Princess believing that Darkness would be part of God's Plan and capable of doing god by filling it's role, it's not the standard viewpoint, but there's no incompatibilities with the Princess text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-31-2017, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T13:24:11-07:00","id":1123146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1123132#post1123132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going by what LostLight said, they'd have to believe that not only was the Darkness part of God's Plan. But that the Plan specifically says that Princesses are not supposed to fight the Darkness. It seems like a weird thing to think. God created the Darkness, God created Princesses, but God doesn't want Princesses to fight the Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that would be a valid explanation by canonical Judaism- sure, the Darkness was a part of God's plan, but evil exists to test good and bring creates good. God wants people to fight against evil- especially their own inner evil- in order to become better people. A better explanation would be that Princesses are doing &quot;evil&quot; by offering mankind the &quot;easy way out&quot;, so they can'tr deal it by their own, and stopping them from getting their reward and fulfilling their fate. Princesses hope to make a better world- the Cold Guard know how to make one, and it means allowing people to solve their problems by themselves, without tricks. Such a thing is doomed to fail, as it is not a part of God's plan, and as such it is evil.<br /> <br /> Again, it is only according to &quot;canonical&quot; Judaism. Nobody said anything about an heretical one.<br /> <br /> How- and just a small note. Did you knew that in mystical Judaism, there is a concept which says that the divinity takes the form of &quot;terrifying ice&quot; when seen in the material, and that Heaven is a dome of frost- as ice is the closest for perfection that exist in the world? Just something to think about, if you talk about the &quot;Cold Guard&quot; is Jewish context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T13:29:20-07:00","id":1123149,"title":"","content":"Plus, isn't the Dark World supposed to be very cold?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T13:31:07-07:00","id":1123151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1123149#post1123149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, isn't the Dark World supposed to be very cold?</div> </div> </div> </div>my point exactly","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T13:47:16-07:00","id":1123159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1123146#post1123146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure that would be a valid explanation by canonical Judaism- sure, the Darkness was a part of God's plan, but evil exists to test good and bring creates good. God wants people to fight against evil- especially their own inner evil- in order to become better people. A better explanation would be that Princesses are doing &quot;evil&quot; by offering mankind the &quot;easy way out&quot;, so they can'tr deal it by their own, and stopping them from getting their reward and fulfilling their fate. Princesses hope to make a better world- the Cold Guard know how to make one, and it means allowing people to solve their problems by themselves, without tricks. Such a thing is doomed to fail, as it is not a part of God's plan, and as such it is evil.</div> </div> </div> </div> That sounds almost identical to the current Cold Guard.<br /> <br /> My issue with it and the current Guard is that it's not contrasting philosophy of evil, it's merely a disagreement on techniques - do you use magic or not - but in both cases the end goal is that the Darkness is defeated. It's really hard to explore the relationship beyond a simple fight scene. The Cold Guard would say the Princess is going against God's Plan. The Princess would say she's doing exactly what she's supposed to under God's Plan. And where do you take it from there?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1123146#post1123146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How- and just a small note. Did you knew that in mystical Judaism, there is a concept which says that the divinity takes the form of &quot;terrifying ice&quot; when seen in the material, and that Heaven is a dome of frost- as ice is the closest for perfection that exist in the world? Just something to think about, if you talk about the &quot;Cold Guard&quot; is Jewish context.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically Ice falls under Princesses (Diamonds). The Darkness has Cold instead.<br /> <br /> So Dark Magic can drain heat out of water or moisture in the air to create ice, but it's Princesses who can wave their hands and create a ice palace in the middle of a desert Frozen style. (hmmm, I should clarify that point in the text).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-31-2017, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T14:02:29-07:00","id":1123169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1123159#post1123159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That sounds almost identical to the current Cold Guard.<br /> <br /> My issue with it and the current Guard is that it's not contrasting philosophy of evil, it's merely a disagreement on techniques - do you use magic or not - but in both cases the end goal is that the Darkness is defeated. It's really hard to explore the relationship beyond a simple fight scene. The Cold Guard would say the Princess is going against God's Plan. The Princess would say she's doing exactly what she's supposed to under God's Plan. And where do you take it from there?</div> </div> </div> </div>like I've said- that's for canonical judaism. Heretics do whatever the hell they want<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Technically Ice falls under Princesses (Diamonds). The Darkness has Cold instead.<br /> <br /> So Dark Magic can drain heat out of water or moisture in the air to create ice, but it's Princesses who can wave their hands and create a ice palace in the middle of a desert Frozen style. (hmmm, I should clarify that point in the text). </div> </div> </div>the &quot;ice&quot; metaphor I talked about is exactly just this- a metaphor. We can't start getting to picky about a semi heretical group which translates the texts in the way which is the best to justify their goal because Princess (the enemy!) say they are wrong. Who listens to those glittery bastards in sailor moon suits anyway?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","da