=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1123970#post1123970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fSUTGbFf2BrzTKFYGXFj6MsgOEkko-NkhzXgedGY4-E/edit?usp=sharing&quot;]Here's</a> the Mercenary Free Company version of the Crown Jewels[/URL]</div> </div> </div> </div>Funky brilliant! Only change is I think becoming Sworn should be the 5th dot status benefit<br /> <br /> Also, since this seems to be a group in which people might join after becoming Sworn, what's the alternate benefit to becoming a Sworn?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 08-02-2017, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T12:50:36-07:00","id":1123980,"title":"","content":"Meh. Still mixed feelings. I really don't think they should be a Compact, and again, I liked the old name better. I'll say though, it's well-written and coherent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T13:02:27-07:00","id":1123985,"title":"","content":"Another case where I liked the old name better, but I think this one needs to have company in the name. They're definately not large enough or centralised enough to be a Conspiracy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1123975#post1123975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funky brilliant!</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1123975#post1123975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Only change is I think becoming Sworn should be the 5th dot status benefit</div> </div> </div> </div> The way I understand Status, putting it as the 5th dot would mean there's about 3-10 people at any one time who qualify for the benefit. They'd be c-level executives. I wanted it more reachable for players. (Incidently I'm not fully satisfied with the 5 dot Status. But I definately want it to be a mundane merit that says something about their operating style).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1123975#post1123975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, since this seems to be a group in which people might join after becoming Sworn, what's the alternate benefit go becoming a Sworn?</div> </div> </div> </div>The text says they get Bequests, Wisps, and leads on new oppotunities. Of those Bequests are the obvious choice for a mechanical benefit. I'll add it in.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T14:28:40-07:00","id":1124007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1123985#post1123985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> The way I understand Status, putting it as the 5th dot would mean there's about 3-10 people at any one time who qualify for the benefit. They'd be c-level executives. I wanted it more reachable for players. (Incidently I'm not fully satisfied with the 5 dot Status. But I definately want it to be a mundane merit that says something about their operating style).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but think of it this way. Who but those who can be vouched as the best they have without supernatural powers are going to have the references and credentials to convince a Noble to Swear (is that the word for the process of becoming Sworn?) them without knowing them personally?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T14:35:54-07:00","id":1124009,"title":"","content":"Good write up, not terribly badass name for a merc group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T14:46:35-07:00","id":1124012,"title":"","content":"I think there's a misunderstanding here. It doesn't require much in the way of trust for a Noble to create a Sworn. Creating a Sworn doesn't automatically mean you're going to be working togeather or sharing eachother's secrets. It's quite common for a Princess to create a Sworn for another Princess who doesn't know the nessacary Charm.<br /> <br /> Some Princesses think it's tacky to create a sworn without a committed Princess-Sworn partnership on the table, but that's cultural rather than magical and far from universal.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T14:48:51-07:00","id":1124013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1124012#post1124012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's a misunderstanding here. It doesn't require much in the way of trust for a Noble to create a Sworn. Creating a Sworn doesn't automatically mean you're going to be working togeather or sharing eachother's secrets. It's quite common for a Princess to create a Sworn for another Princess who doesn't know the nessacary Charm.<br /> <br /> Some Princesses think it's tacky to create a sworn without a committed Princess-Sworn partnership on the table, but that's cultural rather than magical and far from universal.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> *shrugs* ok. Don't regret bringing the topic up, but I'll concede to your expertise","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T14:49:43-07:00","id":1124016,"title":"","content":"Totally minor, but one aspect of at least the intro bothers me. Sorry if I brought this up before; feel free to use the same arguments. Anyway, how is it that Hunters seem to know so much more about Princesses than say, Werewolves. Stuff like &quot;they can use magic around people&quot; and even &quot;There's a mental block around connecting their two identities&quot; makes sense. But how do they know their magic is instinctual while other witches' magic is not? They're not the only ones with instinctual magic or psychic powers (e.g. humans with supernatural merits and certain microtemplates). How have they tied it to their emotions? How have certain groups figured out their transformation's link to their trinket?<br /> <br /> I'm obviously excluding our Noble-focused groups here for some of this knowledge, but I feel like the introduction has the Hunters knowing too much. And that's not very Hunter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T15:07:06-07:00","id":1124024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1124009#post1124009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good write up, not terribly badass name for a merc group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks Flyboy. Feel free to suggest an alternative name, prefrably with the word Company or Free Company in it.<br /> <br /> (Sorry I missed your post earlier)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T15:23:41-07:00","id":1124030,"title":"","content":"Well, since their most effective cover today would be a PMC/security contractor, (Meaningful Name) Security Solutions, Inc, but just calling them &quot;The Free Company&quot; works honestly, because they aren't beholden to any one princess or court after all. What we need now is a good nickname that sounds derogatory that can be turned around and used by the Free Company themselves because it sounded good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T16:26:18-07:00","id":1124071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1124016#post1124016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the introduction has the Hunters knowing too much. And that's not very Hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. We need to make the Hunters more &quot;Witches? Not-witches? Quasi-witches?&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T16:35:48-07:00","id":1124075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1124071#post1124071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. We need to make the Hunters more &quot;Witches? Not-witches? Quasi-witches?&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are we saying except for the Princess-focused groups or -including- the Princess-focused groups? 'Cause it's not like Aegis Kai Doru knows too much about Mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T16:42:27-07:00","id":1124080,"title":"","content":"Well, as previously stated, Princesses probably talk (at length) about their own powers and philosophy more than the other &quot;monsters&quot;, so some information should be available. Whether Hunter trust it, or have access to it is another matter.<br /> <br /> The Ignorant probably go &quot;Witches?&quot;. The Skeptical probably go &quot;Sure, 'Noble', right&quot;. The Informed have probably talked with Princesses before, and know as much as they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-02-2017, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T17:24:59-07:00","id":1124089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, as previously stated, Princesses probably talk (at length) about their own powers and philosophy more than the other &quot;monsters&quot;, so some information should be available. Whether Hunter trust it, or have access to it is another matter. </div> </div> </div>Thank you, Vent. Glad to see at least one person was listening last time I answered that concern.<br /> <br /> Again, for starter, that book wouldn't have a point to exist if hunters were just like &quot;witches?&quot;, because then they would treat Princesses no different than mages and you might as well just read Witchfinders.<br /> <br /> Second, I actually did take the effort to explain how hunters know all these informations; they figured Princesses were using their powers instinctively while seeing them in action (true, psychic do too, but there are enough differences between the two that they wouldn't confuse them), they deduce the link to their emotions because they saw Princesses would get weaker when faced with emotional trauma and stronger when they helped people (I do think they would pay attention to anything that might show them how to weaken an enemy), and assuming they caught at least one or two Princesses transforming, I would assume they would see them pull out the Phylacteries before transforming and be smart enough to put two and two together. I REALLY don't think it's that impossible they would figure out all of this.<br /> <br /> Third, as Vent just explained, Princesses are more inclined to share informations about themselves than, say, Vampires (who are obsessed with hiding their existence for their own safety), Mages (who know most of the stuff they work on would drive humans insane), or Werewolves (who prefers minding their own business and hate having humans interfering).<br /> <br /> Finally, I would like to point out Hunters still lack a lot of informations: they aren't sure what Princesses are, don't trust them, have various theories on their origin and nature... I feel like there still are plenty of dark areas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T17:44:18-07:00","id":1124095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1124089#post1124089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you, Vent. Glad to see at least one person was listening last time I answered that concern.<br /> <br /> Again, for starter, that book wouldn't have a point to exist if hunters were just like &quot;witches?&quot;, because then they would treat Princesses no different than mages and you might as well just read Witchfinders.<br /> <br /> Second, I actually did take the effort to explain how hunters know all these informations; they figured Princesses were using their powers instinctively while seeing them in action (true, psychic do too, but there are enough differences between the two that they wouldn't confuse them), they deduce the link to their emotions because they saw Princesses would get weaker when faced with emotional trauma and stronger when they helped people (I do think they would pay attention to anything that might show them how to weaken an enemy), and assuming they caught at least one or two Princesses transforming, I would assume they would see them pull out the Phylacteries before transforming and be smart enough to put two and two together. I REALLY don't think it's that impossible they would figure out all of this.<br /> <br /> Third, as Vent just explained, Princesses are more inclined to share informations about themselves than, say, Vampires (who are obsessed with hiding their existence for their own safety), Mages (who know most of the stuff they work on would drive humans insane), or Werewolves (who prefers minding their own business and hate having humans interfering).<br /> <br /> Finally, I would like to point out Hunters still lack a lot of informations: they aren't sure what Princesses are, don't trust them, have various theories on their origin and nature... I feel like there still are plenty of dark areas.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While all of the above is true, we <i>could</i> highlight how that information may not be communicated. If Cell A found out about Phylacteries, who says they communicated it so Cell B knows? Hunter do tend to keep things close to their vests. And spread general misinformation for Reasons. Example A: The Cheiron Field Manual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T18:14:14-07:00","id":1124106,"title":"","content":"I like that. Nice middle ground","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T05:34:52-07:00","id":1124710,"title":"","content":"That could work I guess, but how would we communicate that exactly?<br /> <br /> Also, I hate to repeat myself, but since King Raven started adding it to the doc, I have to say it again: I am REALLY not sold on the whole Free Company thing. Aside from me not liking the very military-like name, I still don't think they should be a Compact. Compacts aren't supposed to have access to a supernatural Endowment (and don't try to bring up the Promethean Brotherhood's case, the book explicitly states they are on the verge of becoming a Conspiracy; only reason they aren't one is because their &quot;Endowment&quot; is still very unreliable). Moreover, I would rather have a third more likable Conspiracy focused on fighting the Darkness rather than only the two Princess-hunting conspiracies we currently have. The Magisters are complete assholes, and the Guard, while more understandable, are still extremists who I find hard to sympathize with. I feel we need a third foil.<br /> <br /> Not to mention, we aready had 3 Compacts, I don't think a fourth one is needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 08-04-2017, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T06:36:30-07:00","id":1124734,"title":"","content":"This is getting silly. A design convention should never be treated as a hard rule. What will actually go wrong if you give a compact access to a supernatural endowment? I do it all the time with hunter groups like Ride to Damascus and they're well recieved. If you want to exclude the Promethean Brotherhood on a silly technicality because their Endowment is risky I point out that the Azusa Miko get a potent supernatural power at Status 1 and another at Status 5, and the Loyalists of Thule have a sidebar in Compacts and Conspiracies saying they have access to all sorts of magic, like rituals from Witch Finders.<br /> <br /> The simple fact is that a Conspiracy of Sworn who work alongside nobles is a contradiction in terms. A Conspiracy cannot function if most of the members are more loyal to the Princess they work with than to the Conspiracy and it's mission; which most Sworn will be since most are chosen from people with a deep personal intimacy with the Princess. You can have a Conspiracy that fights the Darkness and is a foil to the light, you can have a group of sworn, but they can't be the same group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-04-2017, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T07:17:04-07:00","id":1124753,"title":"","content":"a wild suggestion-<br /> <br /> what if instead of starting to fall into a political argument about what should be the &quot;right&quot; version of Princess Hunters, we'll keep both versions in the doc as possible alternative? This is an homebrew work, and clearly Darinas has a different view for how the Cold/People/Peasant Guard and the Crown Jewels should be. It is not fair to stop a possible player from using one version, if they prefer the other. We could just make an &quot;alternatives&quot; section in the doc and be done with it, you know, let the potential players and STs to make the choice by themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T07:40:56-07:00","id":1124768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is getting silly. A design convention should never be treated as a hard rule. What will actually go wrong if you give a compact access to a supernatural endowment? I do it all the time with hunter groups like Ride to Damascus and they're well recieved. If you want to exclude the Promethean Brotherhood on a silly technicality because their Endowment is risky I point out that the Azusa Miko get a potent supernatural power at Status 1 and another at Status 5, and the Loyalists of Thule have a sidebar in Compacts and Conspiracies saying they have access to all sorts of magic, like rituals from Witch Finders.<br /> <br /> The simple fact is that a Conspiracy of Sworn who work alongside nobles is a contradiction in terms. A Conspiracy cannot function if most of the members are more loyal to the Princess they work with than to the Conspiracy and it's mission; which most Sworn will be since most are chosen from people with a deep personal intimacy with the Princess. You can have a Conspiracy that fights the Darkness and is a foil to the light, you can have a group of sworn, but they can't be the same group. </div> </div> </div>Even if your points are valid, my other arguments still stand: we already have three Compacts, we don't need to reduce the number of Conspiracies to get a fourth one. And if you remove the Crown Jewels from the equation, then the only two Conspiracies left are a Corporate assholes who kidnap Princesses for more powers and bigoted revolutionary-wannabe who hunt Nobles because they refuse to accept not all of them are like the Queen of Tears (not saying the People's Guard are bad as a concept, I just find it difficult, or even impossible in my personal tastes, to have any sympathy for them). I feel we need a third Conspiracy who would be more white and grey than black and grey-- something the Crown Jewels used to provide.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> what if instead of starting to fall into a political argument about what should be the &quot;right&quot; version of Princess Hunters, we'll keep both versions in the doc as possible alternative? This is an homebrew work, and clearly Darinas has a different view for how the Cold/People/Peasant Guard and the Crown Jewels should be. It is not fair to stop a possible player from using one version, if they prefer the other. We could just make an &quot;alternatives&quot; section in the doc and be done with it, you know, let the potential players and STs to make the choice by themselves. </div> </div> </div>Meh. That's a temporary solution at best.<br /> <br /> I wasn't a fan of the People's Guard replacing the Cold Guard, mainly for name reasons, but I agreed to the change because it seemed like I was a minority and most people here like the new version better, and really just scratching an idea everyone approves of for the name would have been idiotic on my part. But as I have made it abondantly clear, I don't want the Crown Jewels removed from the equation <i>at all</i>, and while I am midly less bothered about making them a merc group (even though I REALLY don't like that Free Company name again), I have made my arguments why I think downgrading them into a Compact causes more problems than it resolves.<br /> <br /> On a note, how do Crown Jewels no longer fit as a name anyway? I mean, for the Cold Guard, I get it, their theme was entirely changed and it no longer made any sense for them to have that name, but the name &quot;Crown Jewels&quot; doesn't suggest they are a Conspiracy, and they still have connection to the Princesses, so why even change the name?<br /> <br /> Look, King Raven, if you really think they work better as a Compact, and most people here agree with you, then fine, I might be willing to let it slide. But then, I want a new Conspiracy to fill the slot they no longer have. 4 Compacts for 2 Conspiracies feels just unbalanced to me, especially when both Conspiracies are on the darkest shade of grey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 08-04-2017, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T08:38:16-07:00","id":1124794,"title":"","content":"So me and Darinas talked it out in the chat and came to an agreement <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Part of that is that we're discussing what could be a new morally white/grey Conspiracy. Thus far I have one suggestion, and Darinas asked me to present it here (as well as solicit more ideas).<br /> <br /> The idea is a Conspiracy of working class types who fight Darkspawn for minimum wages. Imagine an illegal Mexican immigrant scrubbing up bloodstains that form a Nest's foci. The contrast with the nobility is that while they both do the same job, because of an accident of birth* Nobles get fame, and magical perks, while if they're lucky the Conspiracy get enough to feed their family south of the border.<br /> <br /> I was thinking that they might be a religious group. That would justify how they have the command and control structure needed for a Conspiracy without the high status members being bad guys who rip off their workers. They'd be a secret society with members in cleaning companies, but the bosses of those companies would not be members.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Princesses earn their powers through exceptional merit in their first life. But they only need to be above average in their subsequent lives to regain their powers.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-04-2017, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T10:11:05-07:00","id":1124823,"title":"","content":"Suggestion seems more Compact worthy than the Crown Jewels (or Free Company), honestly.<br /> <br /> I still don't know why we can't bend the rules and have the CJ/FC maintain Sworn status without being loyal to Princesses. Their cause is still just, they just don't want to cave into a Noble's command structure. Their loyalty lies with the Conspiracy, and not whatever Princess happens to elevate them.<br /> <br /> We can always keep how they are able to do this a mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T10:46:10-07:00","id":1124833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1124823#post1124823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suggestion seems more Compact worthy than the Crown Jewels (or Free Company), honestly.<br /> <br /> I still don't know why we can't bend the rules and have the CJ/FC maintain Sworn status without being loyal to Princesses. Their cause is still just, they just don't want to cave into a Noble's command structure. Their loyalty lies with the Conspiracy, and not whatever Princess happens to elevate them.<br /> <br /> We can always keep how they are able to do this a mystery.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought we were having a lot of them be Sworn to dead Nobles anyway?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T11:00:55-07:00","id":1124837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1124823#post1124823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suggestion seems more Compact worthy than the Crown Jewels (or Free Company), honestly.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's a fair point now I think about it. But can it be fixed?<br /> <br /> For example, what if they used their employment as maids and cleaners to collect blackmail material on politicians and other figures of authority who's actions create Taint and perform other similar actions to try and improve the world. Would that make them more Conspiracy like?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1124823#post1124823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still don't know why we can't bend the rules and have the CJ/FC maintain Sworn status without being loyal to Princesses. Their cause is still just, they just don't want to cave into a Noble's command structure. Their loyalty lies with the Conspiracy, and not whatever Princess happens to elevate them.<br /> <br /> We can always keep how they are able to do this a mystery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Sworn don't work like that. Becoming Sworn doesn't implant any sort of magical loyalty. Sworn are loyal because Princesses choose people they have strong bond with. Thus, you have to explain why someone would work behind her beloved big sister's back as part of a Conspiracy. And you have to explain why it's a common occurrence because a Conspiracy of Sworn would have lots of little sisters in it, it just isn't believable to say that none of them reveal the big secret and once some of them do Nobles will share the information.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1124833#post1124833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought we were having a lot of them be Sworn to dead Nobles anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of them are. I kept the exact proportions vague, because vagueness creates flexibility for the players.<br /> <br /> However even a Sworn who was left alive after her big sister died would have strong feelings and loyalty to the memory of her sister. It would be weird if they responded to a loved one's death by trying to manipulate people like her. They'd know and respect why Nobles do what they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-04-2017, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T11:44:00-07:00","id":1124856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1124794#post1124794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea is a Conspiracy of working class types who fight Darkspawn for minimum wages. Imagine an illegal Mexican immigrant scrubbing up bloodstains that form a Nest's foci. The contrast with the nobility is that while they both do the same job, because of an accident of birth* Nobles get fame, and magical perks, while if they're lucky the Conspiracy get enough to feed their family south of the border.<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>So we're doing away with the merc angle then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T11:49:51-07:00","id":1124858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1124768#post1124768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, King Raven, if you really think they work better as a Compact, and most people here agree with you, then fine, I might be willing to let it slide. But then, I want a new Conspiracy to fill the slot they no longer have. 4 Compacts for 2 Conspiracies feels just unbalanced to me, especially when both Conspiracies are on the darkest shade of grey.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you by any chance familiar with the French animated TV show <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miraculous_Ladybug\" target=\"_blank\">Miraculous</a>? It's an inspiration for a Merit in Princess (Vocation version) that allows a mundane human to fuse with a Shikigami temporarily, and learn Charms and use them while fused ... and it occurs to me that its basic conceit could work as a Conspiracy Endowment just as well. And a Conspiracy based on encouraging possession by helpful Dreamlanders would be a lot whiter than the Magisters or the Guard ... while still being shady enough that outsiders would have good reason to suspect it. IOW a riff on Miraculous, CofD style, might well be what you're after here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T11:53:55-07:00","id":1124860,"title":"","content":"<br /> The TV show is news to me but Dream has it's own way of fusing with Dreamlanders; the Harmonious Merge Manifestation. I could see an Endowment based on Miraculous working. Can you give us the low down on how everything else would work - their organisation, ideals, and how they're a foil to Princesses?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1124856#post1124856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we're doing away with the merc angle then?</div> </div> </div> </div>That suggestion is for a seperate group to the Sworn group.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T14:04:00-07:00","id":1124934,"title":"","content":"... actually that's not a bad idea. Kinda like a Dreamlander version of Les Myst\u00e8res?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T10:41:32-07:00","id":1125275,"title":"","content":"Okay, finished pic is paid for and ready for use!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://sta.sh/0133qg5wzzar\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://images-wixmp-ed30a86b8c4ca887773594c2.wixmp.com/f/8fabbc7c-436b-4716-94c9-1a42d5d879d2/dbixsp9-bd3359ca-3148-4a15-ac11-6f4a4422d380.png/v1/fill/w_600,h_650,q_80,strp/commission_hunters_and_hearts_by_erinptah_dbixsp9-fullview.jpg?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..M-k_ztpGq5vqmNsg8N8SHSBoLrK830PpHPVreTYf9xE\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://sta.sh/0133qg5wzzar\" target=\"_blank\"> Commission - Hunters and Hearts by ErinPtah on DeviantArt </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://sta.sh/0133qg5wzzar\" target=\"_blank\"> http://sta.sh/0133qg5wzzar </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Commission - Hunters and Hearts &mdash; artwork by ErinPtah on DeviantArt. Published: 2017-08-06 &middot; Likes: 16 &middot; Views: 976 &middot; Comments: 4 &middot; Tags: commission, meninblack </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T14:37:27-07:00","id":1125353,"title":"","content":"Good^^ no we just need to chose where to put it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T13:19:42-07:00","id":1125673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1124934#post1124934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... actually that's not a bad idea. Kinda like a Dreamlander version of Les Myst\u00e8res?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda-sorta - but with transformation trinkets that are actually Dreamlanders instead of summoning rites.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1124860#post1124860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The TV show is news to me but Dream has it's own way of fusing with Dreamlanders; the Harmonious Merge Manifestation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more like Claiming than what I was talking about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1124860#post1124860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see an Endowment based on Miraculous working. Can you give us the low down on how everything else would work - their organisation, ideals, and how they're a foil to Princesses?</div> </div> </div> </div>... I honestly haven't a clue. The one thing I'm sure of is that the Conspiracy should be small - roughly on par with the Merrick Institute, which is a few hundred people at best.<br /> <br /> Two possibilities I've thought of:<ul><li>An unconventional psychiatrist treats a number of people with the Tainted or Darkened Conditions, and (for unrelated reasons) is also experimenting with meditation techniques and discovers a way to reach the Dreamlands. The Dreamlanders he meets give him clues to what's going on with his patients, after which he starts up a program of matching mortals with Dreamlanders to fight the Darkness.</li> <li>A mysterious woman has been opening <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TheLittleShopThatWasntThereYesterday\" target=\"_blank\">Little Shops that Weren't There Yesterday</a> and selling intelligent magical jewelry to people who are about to encounter supernatural danger. Her surviving customers have been contacting each other and trying to track her down, and fight monsters along the way. (The woman's description varies but always mentions silver-gray eyes.)</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T13:35:57-07:00","id":1125678,"title":"","content":"On a note, since we are mentioning Harmonious Merge, I would like to ask King Raven: Do the rules for Claim regarding the merging of the attributes and skills apply? The book doesn't say...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T00:11:23-07:00","id":1125808,"title":"","content":"Yes and no. You get mental attributes and skills; but Dreamlanders / astral entities can't affect the physical world like Spirits can. (Unless that changed in 2E, but I don't think it did)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T04:55:06-07:00","id":1125846,"title":"","content":"No, it didn't change (for Dreamlanders at least, didn't check for Astral Entities), which is why I was confused on that part. So if I get your explanation correct, people merged with Dreamlanders using this manifestation won't change physically nor gain actual physical enhancemens, but they will get super-intelligence ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T06:02:51-07:00","id":1125871,"title":"","content":"Precisely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T10:14:19-07:00","id":1126345,"title":"","content":"What if we take this Dreamlander based endowment idea and combine it with the other anime genre idea?<br /> <br /> Instead of merging peacefully with Dreamlanders to get powers they capture and weaponize Shikigami they merge with as a darker take on the mon genre.<br /> <br /> They can seek to &quot;liberate&quot; the Shikigami from under the Nobles and elevate them to their true potential. A process that happens to involve kidnapping, torture and possibly darkness based rituals but it's for the Shikigami's best interest, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T10:45:16-07:00","id":1126364,"title":"","content":"... You didn't read the part about us wanting a more white and grey conspiracy, did you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T05:03:41-07:00","id":1126658,"title":"","content":"Also just realize something: How the heck didn't we think about making a japanese Compact of Conspiracy? I mean, this is a magical girl-related book, that should be a given.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T06:16:42-07:00","id":1127082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1126364#post1126364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... You didn't read the part about us wanting a more white and grey conspiracy, did you?</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll be pleased to know that I've been hard at work with mp on one: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1t7U_sglV9RXTBc3oU3J-bJFSRVbEAobbFEwyxPrD838/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...yxPrD838/edit#</a><br /> <br /> They make a nice contrasting pair with the People's Guard. The People's Guard are radicals who want to tear down the system (and it looks like their Endowment works best if they whip up a crowd). The Collective are pragmatists who want to manipulate the system and specalise in stealth and suberfuge.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T08:42:43-07:00","id":1127147,"title":"","content":"... Mixed feelings. There is potential here, but the source of their Endowment still is a bit unclear, and the motivation behind them and how they were founded still is a bit TOO close to the People's Guard for me. I mean seriously, they are basically just like the People's Guard, but not extremist in that area. They need more of an identity of their own.<br /> <br /> Sorry if that sounds harsh, King Raven. I appreciate the efforts you put into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T09:09:58-07:00","id":1127158,"title":"","content":"A new group should be lighter, right? So recasting it as the run-away remnant of Tyler Durden-esque cult won't fit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T09:41:39-07:00","id":1127175,"title":"","content":".... I have no idea who Tyler Durden is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T09:56:50-07:00","id":1127180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1127175#post1127175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.... I have no idea who Tyler Durden is.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I have no idea how to respond to that.<br /> <br /> Yes I do: Watch Fight Club.<br /> <br /> It will enrich your media and gaming experience.<br /> <br /> (You could do a Google Search, but spoilers)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T10:50:07-07:00","id":1127196,"title":"","content":"Oooooh, right, <i>him</i>. Actually I did watch Fight Club, it's just one of these movies which I remember in itself yet I can never remember the characters' names.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T11:15:15-07:00","id":1127212,"title":"","content":"Ironically mp started with Fight Club as an inspiration. I haven't watched fight club. But yeah, this is supposed to be a lighter group so cults of any stripe wouldn't fit.<br /> <br /> Anyway, any suggestions Darinas, or anyone else? One idea I had at the start was to play up the religious angle - not a cult, but a religious movement - but I'd want to run it past mp. He wanted it more secular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T13:24:25-07:00","id":1127278,"title":"","content":"Well, let me see....<br /> <br /> Playing up the religious angle could work, but I also feel like the Endowment needs to be developped. Ideally, I would like it to have ties to Nobles and the Dreamlands; this supplement is meant to be about how Hunters interact with these after all. Maybe do something with the whole merging with Dreamlanders thing, for example? Or have them find vestiges of the Kingdom and discover ancient documents explaining how to channel the Light through benedictions-like powers for mortals? Also, maybe having their founder be a Beacon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T14:06:45-07:00","id":1127316,"title":"","content":"Other random ideas:<br /> Can they also originate much longer ago? They might have been destroyed or near destroyed numerous times, only to pop back up. Their job isn't exactly limited to modern times.<br /> Maybe they are the result of a curse? Or at least the organization is. I'm not sure what Princess themed force would curse a whole people as a clean-up service, but maybe a powerful and particularly egocentric Princess of Mirrors did it.<br /> I'm still not seeing much supernatural about a cleaning crew, or why they have the organizational hierarchy for a Conspiracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T14:49:50-07:00","id":1127342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1127278#post1127278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ideally, I would like it to have ties to Nobles and the Dreamlands</div> </div> </div> </div>Tying their endowment to Nobles would defeat the point I think; the entire point is that they're the servants not the nobles. Dreamlanders would just be hard to make work I think, since their powers thematically tie to what they are rather than what they wish they are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1127316#post1127316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still not seeing much supernatural about a cleaning crew, or why they have the organizational hierarchy for a Conspiracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't think of them as a cleaning crew that happens to be a Conspiracy.<br /> <br /> Rather think of them as a secret Conspiracy that intentionally recruits cleaners, maids, minimum wage security guards, etc, because it knows nobody pays attention to them; making them excellent spies and agents. (And for philosophical reasons)<br /> <br /> The higher ups aren't struggling working class types; but secretive mastermind types who direct the Conspiracy to their own ends. It's just that their ends are protecting the little guy, even if they have to orchestrate a political assassination or blackmail a CEO to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-10-2017, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T16:24:35-07:00","id":1127393,"title":"","content":"I am not suggesting making them Sworn or having the Nobles give them their powers, I am suggesting tying their origin to things from Princess lore. Regardless of the point, their Endowment has to come from <i>somewhere</i>, and we aready made the multiple options origin for the People's Guard so just doing the same would feel 1) Redundant and 2) Like we lack imagination. I thought having them channel the Light in a way different than Noble could be a cool idea. And again, making them the servants might be too close to the People's Guard. I'd rather them be something unique.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rather think of them as a secret Conspiracy that intentionally recruits cleaners, maids, minimum wage security guards, etc, because it knows nobody pays attention to them; making them excellent spies and agents. </div> </div> </div>I kinda like the spy idea. Maybe play up that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T06:38:43-07:00","id":1127596,"title":"","content":"Pretty much everything from princess lore is fairly fantastical and often ties the user to standards of behaviour, which clashes with the concept of their power being subtle and based on enhancing various traits they already have. (E.G. people rarely pay attention to the cleaning lady, and their endowment boosts this until they can sneak into highly secure facilities).<br /> <br /> For the origin of their power I could see something theological working, something along the lines of Benediction. Especially if we play up the religious angle to make them more distinct from the Guard. Alternatively a psychic origin based on focusing the resolve they needed to survive the hard knock life could work.<br /> <br /> As for playing up the spy angle. What did you have in mind? It feels pretty played up to me already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-11-2017, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T04:23:44-07:00","id":1128386,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Here's what I have so far for my Cold Guard salvage efforts. I'm still working on the fluff and refining the mechanics. Feedback is appreciated. <hr /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Cold Guard</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Background</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They depended on Nobles, but were &quot;betrayed&quot; (possibly they were merely left unprotected when the Princesses defending them fell). *They survived as best they could, fighting back as fiercely, when they noticed that the Darkness often fought against itself. And wasn't exactly picky about who it conferred power to.* [&lt;- This part is optional] They reached the grim decision to use the Darkness against itself, making a vow not to let it turn them from their purpose. Through group effort, codified ritual, rigorous training, and grim determination, they've managed to utilize the powers of the Dark without being corrupted from their goals (up to a point).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>The Enemy</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They oppose the monsters of the Darkness on base principle, turning its powers against itself. The oppose other monsters both for their threat to humanity, and for their tendency to create Nests incidentally through their depredations. They oppose Princesses due to prior experience and philosophy - throughout history, the &quot;Nobles&quot; have either tried to kill them on sight, been self-absorbed tyrants, or committed hypocrisy by furthering the Darkness. The newer ones have argued for forsaking one's sins, rather than drawing strength from utilizing them, all while they try to make humanity dependent upon themselves once more.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Hunters</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[The Cold Guard only takes those who've done something to gain Shadows or have proven the necessary resolve and willingness to fight the Darkness with itself. They offer purpose, if not redemption.] [Hunters are encouraged to form bonds, if not too close ones, with their fellows. They need all the emotional and moral support they can get.]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Philosophy</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fight fire with fire. Keep to your purpose, despite the costs. Don't hide from your inner darkness - use it.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Endowment: Cold Resolve (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>:</b> Status (Cold Guard) 1+</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Guardsman has faced their sins and taken part of the Darkness into their own heart. Only through chilly resolve and determination, do they hold its corruption at bay. They can acquire a number of Penumbrae or Darkness-based Dread Powers equal to their dots in this Endowment plus their Resolve without affecting their Integrity or being treated as a creature of Darkness.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The corruption of the Darkness can't be held at bay forever, nor invoked lightly. Each Penumbrae or Dread Power acquired gives the Hunter a </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>permanent</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> dot of Shadows. Each use often gives the Guardsman a temporary point of Shadows, which fade at a rate of one per day (or once per Scene, if the Guardsman fulfills their Virtue that Scene). If their Shadows (permanent and temporary) exceeds their dots in this merit and Resolve, they either take 1 Lethal damage or suffer a Breaking Point each day, and each additional time they gain a dot of Shadows.</span><br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Penumbrae</span></b></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Channel Spite</b></span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Resolve + Athletics - Defense</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Instant</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 1 Willpower + gain 1 Temporary Shadow</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Guardsman taps into their hunger for violence and revenge, directing a bolt of shadow at the monster. Treat this as a ranged attack with a Damage Rating equal to the number of damaged Health boxes the Guardsman has.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Devouring Dark</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Composure + Occult</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Instant</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 1 Willpower + gain 1 Temporary Shadow</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Darkness consumes everything, even itself. The Hunter turns this hungry darkness upon a supernatural source, draining it of power. This triggers a Clash of Wills against the supernatural effect with the Hunter using the dice pool above - if they win, the supernatural effect is instantly cancelled.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Veil of Corruption</b></span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Stamina + Subterfuge - number of targets</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Extended, 10 minutes per roll</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 1 Willpower + gain 1 Temporary Shadow</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Guardsman chants a litany of hatred, wrapping themselves and others in a shroud of Darkness. This veil will disguise the recipients as creatures of evil and Darkness, protecting them from the Curses of Nests, passive aggression from the less intelligent Lurkers, and even slight protection from the deadly effects of the Dark World. The effect lasts for a number of Scenes or Hours equal to the target number the Hunter sets when beginning the ritual.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The targets count as Creatures of Darkness for supernatural effects, and acquire their Bane of Jade as well, for the duration of the effect.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Cloak of Shadows</b></span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Resolve + Occult</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Instant</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 1 Willpower + gain 1 Temporary Shadow</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: By accepting the Darkness in their heart, the Hunter can hide in it from hostile supernatural powers. For the rest of the Scene, they may treat their Shadows as a Supernatural Tolerance trait for the purposes of resisting effects.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Hunter counts as a creature of Darkness for supernatural effects, and acquire their Bane of Jade as well, for the duration of the effect. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Bleak Oubliette</b></span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Manipulation + Persuasion</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Extended, 1 roll per hour</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 1 Willpower per roll + gain 1 Temporary Shadow per use</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Through ritual invocation of a Nest\u2019s sins while maintaining their own detachment, the Hunter constructs a honeyed prison out of the tainted place. After achieving a number of successes equal to the Nest\u2019s Corruption plus its Size, the entire place is affected - it begins attracting all creatures of Darkness within a number of miles equal to its Size, and once they arrive, they must succeed at a Resolve + Composure - Corruption roll to leave its confines. The effect lasts for a number of days equal to the Nest\u2019s Hold track, though if a blood sacrifice (Lethal damage equal to the Hold track) is used, it lasts for 1 year per Hold box instead. [Or tie it directly to clearing the Hold Track instead?]</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Note</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Attempts to purify the Nest directly inhibit this power\u2019s functioning. Each Hold box that is checked off lowers the remaining duration by 1 interval.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Feast of Sins</b></span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Wits + Socialize - Resolve (optional)</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Instant or Scene</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 1 Willpower</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: By engaging in ceremonial confession and judgement, the Hunter is able to transfer Shadows from themselves and others. Temporary Shadows can be exchanged between willing targets, up to the number of successes rolled. If used offensively, this power is resisted by Resolve, and instead allows the Hunter to temporarily remove up to successes dots of Shadows (minimum 1) from creatures of Darkness, gaining them as temporary Shadows. The dots of Shadows return to the creature of Darkness at a rate of one per Scene (regardless of whether the Hunter has shed them or not).</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: A Scene-long ritual version also exists, that lets the Guardsman permanently move dots of Shadows from willing targets, but the recipient gains those dots as permanent Shadows as well.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ebon Fury</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Reflexive</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 1 Willpower + gain 1 Temporary Shadow</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: By drowning themselves in their own hatred and anger, the Hunter is able to bolster themselves with the Darkness. For each dot of Shadows they possess, they can add a plus one bonus to any physical attribute. This can even exceed human limits, by an amount equal to their dots in Cold Resolve (so, up to 6 at one dot, and up to 10 at five dots). They can maintain this state for a number of turns equal to their Composure.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Vile Curse</b></span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Presence + Intimidation vs Resolve + Potency</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Instant and Contested</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 1 Willpower + gain 1 Temporary Shadow</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: By spewing a litany of invective and malice, the Guardsman cripples their target with an infection born of the Darkness inside them. For each dot of Shadows they possess, they can inflict one curse (as per a Nest) upon a target, which fades at the end of the Scene.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: If they destroy the Foci of a Nest prior to using this ability (taking 1 Instant action), the power affects everyone in the same area as the Size of the Nest. In this case, each potential target that rolls less successes than the Hunter is affected.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: By willingly sacrificing a portion of themselves, the Guardsman can even turn the curses of the Darkness upon its own minions. The Hunter may take 1 Lethal damage and make a Breaking Point roll (as if acting on their Vice), and in exchange the curse will even affect creatures of Darkness.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Feed on Madness</b></span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Intelligence + Empathy - Shadows</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Roll</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Reflexive</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: gain 1 Temporary Shadow</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: As the Darkness grows stronger at the decay of sanity, so too can the Hunter syphon energy from madness. Whenever a Breaking Point (or equivalent, at the Storyteller's option) is inflicted, the Hunter gains either 1 point of Willpower (as if satisfying their Vice), or downgrades 1 box of Lethal damage to Bashing. If Integrity (or equivalent) was lost this way, they may instead regain 1 point of Willpower (without limitation per Scene), or completely heal 1 box of Lethal damage.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-13-2017, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T05:09:28-07:00","id":1128389,"title":"","content":"Love it. Two questions <br /> <br /> 1) given the flavor, I would like to see Ebon Fury given some sort of mental drawback. Perhaps a Condition along the lines of &quot;Berserker&quot;?<br /> <br /> 2) how does Feed on Madness use a dice pool? Does it only activate if you succeed on that roll?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T05:09:47-07:00","id":1128390,"title":"","content":"I admit I actually kinda like this version of the Endowment. By far one of the most concrete Endowment we have so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 08-13-2017, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T06:31:58-07:00","id":1128417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1128389#post1128389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Love it. Two questions<br /> <br /> 1) given the flavor, I would like to see Ebon Fury given some sort of mental drawback. Perhaps a Condition along the lines of &quot;Berserker&quot;?<br /> <br /> 2) how does Feed on Madness use a dice pool? Does it only activate if you succeed on that roll?</div> </div> </div> </div><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Yeah, Berzerker might fit. Maybe if you try and sustain it after the Composure in Turns duration? It's powerful, but <i>very</i> short. And every activation edges you closer to the limit.</li> <li>So, the reason it is Reflexive, is that you can use it every time there is a Breaking Point you are on the Scene for (yes, including your own, for what it is worth). You roll Intelligence + Empathy - your Shadows. If the Breaking Point roll was a success, you get Vice Willpower or downgrade damage. If the Breaking Point failed, you get actual healing or 1 Willpower (no Vice-based limitation). Of course, using it gives you Temporary Shadows, so further rolls get harder and harder. And eventually you exceed your limit, leading to Lethal damage or Breaking Points from that (which, as written, you can also try to farm for healing... except you are increasing your Shadows each time, to likely fatal levels if you try it).</li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T10:04:18-07:00","id":1128499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1128386#post1128386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Endowment: Cold Resolve (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>:</b> Status (Cold Guard) 1+</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Guardsman has faced their sins and taken part of the Darkness into their own heart. Only through chilly resolve and determination, do they hold its corruption at bay. They can acquire a number of Penumbrae or Darkness-based Dread Powers equal to their dots in this Endowment plus their Resolve without affecting their Integrity or being treated as a creature of Darkness.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The corruption of the Darkness can't be held at bay forever, nor invoked lightly. Each Penumbrae or Dread Power acquired gives the Hunter a </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>permanent</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> dot of Shadows. Each use often gives the Guardsman a temporary point of Shadows, which fade at a rate of one per day (or once per Scene, if the Guardsman fulfills their Virtue that Scene). If their Shadows (permanent and temporary) exceeds their dots in this merit and Resolve, they either take 1 Lethal damage or suffer a Breaking Point each day, and each additional time they gain a dot of Shadows.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>This is a cool idea, and the powers are nicely thematic too. But that drawback ... if I read that correctly, once Shadows &gt; Resolve + Endowment dots, it never goes back down below the limit. The hunter gains one temporary Shadows dot each day for being over the limit, then loses that dot from the natural fading, leaving him where he was - and he takes damage or an Integrity hit as well. Only fulfilling Virtue gets him partly out of the hole. Is that intentional?<br /> <br /> If so, abilities like Channel Spite and Ebon Fury are a mug's game. You have a strict limit on the number of times you can use Penumbrae before you lock yourself into the damage-or-breaking-point loop, so each use had better give a major advantage. A scene-long buff or debuff may be worth what you're paying; a single ranged attack, or a few turns of boosted strength, aren't. A Penumbra should be designed on the assumption that it'll see use maybe twice in a session.<br /> <br /> An alternative, if that's not what you had in mind, is that going over the limit just imposes the Darkened Condition, with all that that implies. It's a lot harder to get out of being Darkened, but the Condition doesn't kill you by inches as this drawback would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T10:33:55-07:00","id":1128505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1128499#post1128499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a cool idea, and the powers are nicely thematic too. But that drawback ... if I read that correctly, once Shadows &gt; Resolve + Endowment dots, it never goes back down below the limit. The hunter gains one temporary Shadows dot each day for being over the limit, then loses that dot from the natural fading, leaving him where he was - and he takes damage or an Integrity hit as well. Only fulfilling Virtue gets him partly out of the hole. Is that intentional?<br /> <br /> If so, abilities like Channel Spite and Ebon Fury are a mug's game. You have a strict limit on the number of times you can use Penumbrae before you lock yourself into the damage-or-breaking-point loop, so each use had better give a major advantage. A scene-long buff or debuff may be worth what you're paying; a single ranged attack, or a few turns of boosted strength, aren't. A Penumbra should be designed on the assumption that it'll see use maybe twice in a session.<br /> <br /> An alternative, if that's not what you had in mind, is that going over the limit just imposes the Darkened Condition, with all that that implies. It's a lot harder to get out of being Darkened, but the Condition doesn't kill you by inches as this drawback would.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the idea is... let me use some examples.<br /> <br /> Ian McInitiate, Cold Resolve 1, Resolve 2 - Has Channel Spite.<br /> Their &quot;Shadows&quot; track looks like [X][ ][ ] normally. Using it once gives them a dot of Temporary Shadows [X][\u2022][ ]. They use it again [X][\u2022][\u2022]. They really are in trouble and use it <i>again</i> [X][\u2022][\u2022] \u2022 , which puts their Shadows over the Safe limit. They can either take 1 Lethal damage or a Breaking Point. After a day, one Temporary Shadow falls off, leaving them with [X][\u2022][\u2022], which is within the safe threshold (as long as they don't use their powers again). Eventually they will drop back down to their 1 Permanent Shadows (from having Channel Spite). Fulfilling/embodying their Virtue will make the Temporary Shadows fall off faster. If they picked up Ebon Fury and Vile Curse, they would look like [X][X][X], meaning they don't have <i>any</i> safety for actually using their powers (the moron) until they increase either Cold Resolve or their Resolve.<br /> <br /> This puts the maximum safe threshold at 10 (Cold Resolve 5, Resolve 5). Each hunter has the choice of more powers, or more ability to use their powers. Going over is Bad, but not immediately fatal/corrupting. If they can suffer through the Lethal poisoning of their own corruption long enough for their Shadows to fall within the safe Zone, they can survive and start to heal the damage. Or they can be virtuous and lower it quicker. <i>Or</i> just spiral into Lurker/Darkspawn-hood and get taken out by their fellows or a Princess. Whichever, you know?<br /> <br /> <br /> Still, I get your point about the variable costs. But with the Virtue clause, is only inflicting Temporary Shadows one per Scene (per power) costly enough?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-13-2017, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T11:56:02-07:00","id":1128531,"title":"","content":"Two things<br /> <br /> 1) If you go over your rating in Shadows, do you also gain the Darkened Template temporarily?<br /> <br /> 2) Going on a trip out west but want to keep editing printouts. If I did this, which parts still need the most editing, as I obviously don't want to print the whole thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T12:44:38-07:00","id":1128549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1128505#post1128505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the idea is... let me use some examples.<br /> <br /> Ian McInitiate, Cold Resolve 1, Resolve 2 - Has Channel Spite.<br /> Their &quot;Shadows&quot; track looks like [X][ ][ ] normally. Using it once gives them a dot of Temporary Shadows [X][\u2022][ ]. They use it again [X][\u2022][\u2022]. They really are in trouble and use it <i>again</i> [X][\u2022][\u2022] \u2022 , which puts their Shadows over the Safe limit. They can either take 1 Lethal damage or a Breaking Point. After a day, one Temporary Shadow falls off, leaving them with [X][\u2022][\u2022], which is within the safe threshold (as long as they don't use their powers again). Eventually they will drop back down to their 1 Permanent Shadows (from having Channel Spite). Fulfilling/embodying their Virtue will make the Temporary Shadows fall off faster. If they picked up Ebon Fury and Vile Curse, they would look like [X][X][X], meaning they don't have <i>any</i> safety for actually using their powers (the moron) until they increase either Cold Resolve or their Resolve.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. So the intent is, each time a Guardsman gains a Shadows dot past his limit, <i>and</i> each day a Guardsman spends with Shadows over his limit, he either takes damage or hits a breaking point. You should probably write it that way round, to avoid others misreading it as I did.<br /> <br /> OK, since overusing Penumbrae doesn't lock you into permanently wasting away and going insane, there's no issue with Channel Spite anymore. I'd just add one refinement. If you kill yourself with damage from Penumbrae, your corpse rises as a Darkspawn. If you drop to Integrity 0 from a Penumbra's breaking point, though, you don't die, but turn into a Mnemosyne. The Cold Guard tests its members regularly with jade to spot Guardsmen that have become Infiltrators ... but since several Penumbrae impose the Darkened Condition temporarily, jade isn't a perfectly reliable test. (Paranoia is a lovely source of drama, in mild doses. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T14:45:11-07:00","id":1128581,"title":"","content":"I made a start on a reworking of the cold guard myself, but it didn't get far before I started working on the Church of the Valley (the new name for the Sanitation Workers Collective). Feel free to make use of anything you find <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1i602NhlNOi4MZj3fzVoEAtf9i3LjsgfoLNZUQvYZ6Fg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. I do like the design of Cold Resolve<br /> <br /> Speaking of the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1t7U_sglV9RXTBc3oU3J-bJFSRVbEAobbFEwyxPrD838/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Church of the Valley</a>, Darinas have you had a chance to look at the updates we made to make them more distinct from the People's Guard?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T15:48:23-07:00","id":1128599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1128549#post1128549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah. So the intent is, each time a Guardsman gains a Shadows dot past his limit, <i>and</i> each day a Guardsman spends with Shadows over his limit, he either takes damage or hits a breaking point. You should probably write it that way round, to avoid others misreading it as I did.<br /> <br /> OK, since overusing Penumbrae doesn't lock you into permanently wasting away and going insane, there's no issue with Channel Spite anymore. I'd just add one refinement. If you kill yourself with damage from Penumbrae, your corpse rises as a Darkspawn. If you drop to Integrity 0 from a Penumbra's breaking point, though, you don't die, but turn into a Mnemosyne. The Cold Guard tests its members regularly with jade to spot Guardsmen that have become Infiltrators ... but since several Penumbrae impose the Darkened Condition temporarily, jade isn't a perfectly reliable test. (Paranoia is a lovely source of drama, in mild doses. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, how's this version?<br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Endowment: Cold Resolve (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Status (Cold Guard) 1+</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Guardsman has faced their sins and taken part of the Darkness into their own heart. Only through chilly resolve and determination, do they hold its corruption at bay. They can acquire Penumbrae or Darkness-based Dread Powers, with each one giving them a permanent dot of Shadows. The Hunter can have Shadows equal to their dots in this Endowment plus their Resolve without affecting their Integrity or being treated as a creature of Darkness.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The corruption of the Darkness can't be held at bay forever, nor invoked lightly. Each use of a Dread Power, and most Penumbrae, gives the Guardsman a temporary point of Shadows. These Temporary Shadows fade at a rate of one per day (or once per Scene, if the Guardsman fulfills their Virtue that Scene). Whenever their Shadows are over their safe limit, the Guardsman is treated as a creature of Darkness, and must take 1 Lethal damage or suffer a Breaking Point. This happens for each new Shadow acquired, as well as once per day spent over their safe limit.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T07:46:38-07:00","id":1128813,"title":"","content":"We still have references to the old magic-hating Cold Guard in the &quot;Stereotypes&quot; section under the official organizations. May I have permission to think up replacements or additions for The People's Guard for that Section?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T13:00:41-07:00","id":1128932,"title":"","content":"Be my guest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T15:12:27-07:00","id":1128974,"title":"","content":"Cool, Will post them as suggestions when I get back home on the 26th. Feel free to make some before I get back","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T16:22:54-07:00","id":1129008,"title":"","content":"Anyone have any input on some of Penumbrae mechanics? Bleak Oubliette is a little clunky, I think, and I'm kind torn about some of the powers using your current Shadows while others just don't care.<br /> <br /> Are there any gaps or ideas that should be filled? Or should I work on fluff next?<br /> <br /> Should total Shadows be capped at twice the safe limit and/or the Lethal damage made Resistant? Because otherwise it can get arbitrarily high, and Shadow are used for certain calculations and effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-14-2017, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T01:40:40-07:00","id":1129146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1129008#post1129008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bleak Oubliette is a little clunky</div> </div> </div> </div> It seems fine to me, and it's my favourite power of the lot. Maybe put a limit on how often monsters can try to escape, e.g. they can only try when whey can see some prey outside the Nest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1129008#post1129008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think, and I'm kind torn about some of the powers using your current Shadows while others just don't care.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd say try and use Shadows in everything.<ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Channel Spite: You could use Shadows as the Damage rating.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Devouring Dark: Replace occult with Shadows? </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Veil of Corruption: Actually this one is in an awkward spot, since it has a lot of overlap with Cloak of Shadows. If you count as a Creature of the Darkness you automatically are fully protected from Nests. Maybe make Veil of Corruption a power that purely focuses on ivisiblity from Dark Creatures, with them taking a Shadows penalty to perception rolls to spot you. </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bleak Oubliette: You could use Shadows in place of Hold boxes. </span></li> </ul><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1129008#post1129008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any gaps or ideas that should be filled? Or should I work on fluff next?</div> </div> </div> </div> A power to mind control Lurkers would work IMO.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1129008#post1129008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should total Shadows be capped at twice the safe limit and/or the Lethal damage made Resistant? Because otherwise it can get arbitrarily high, and Shadow are used for certain calculations and effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd suggest making it so that if you're above the safe limit you, in addition to the current effects, count as an Infected/Darkened; and have a note that while the Cold Guard often have the resolve to resist the Darkness until their Shadows fall under the safe limit again, even they struggle to resist the Darkness forever.<br /> <br /> Then leave it to players to roleplay it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T18:10:12-07:00","id":1130630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1129146#post1129146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It seems fine to me, and it's my favourite power of the lot. Maybe put a limit on how often monsters can try to escape, e.g. they can only try when whey can see some prey outside the Nest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll try specify that. Like once per day, or given motivating circumstances.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1129146#post1129146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say try and use Shadows in everything.<ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Channel Spite: You could use Shadows as the Damage rating.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Devouring Dark: Replace occult with Shadows? </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Veil of Corruption: Actually this one is in an awkward spot, since it has a lot of overlap with Cloak of Shadows. If you count as a Creature of the Darkness you automatically are fully protected from Nests. Maybe make Veil of Corruption a power that purely focuses on ivisiblity from Dark Creatures, with them taking a Shadows penalty to perception rolls to spot you. </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bleak Oubliette: You could use Shadows in place of Hold boxes. </span></li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Issue with Channel Spite is that the damage could get crazy high, fast.<br /> For Devouring Dark, I could. I was thinking of that. Though Shadows can get pretty high, making it almost unfair.<br /> Hmm. Good point on Veil of Corruption. So make it a more stealth and Dark World excursion power?<br /> For Bleak Oubliette, I wanted to base all (or most) of the effects based on the Nest itself, since it is basically turning the Nest's powers against itself. I could make it Shadows, and still keep the &quot;filling Hold boxes reduces the duration&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1129146#post1129146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A power to mind control Lurkers would work IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other than the Monster Lord Dread Power?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1129146#post1129146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd suggest making it so that if you're above the safe limit you, in addition to the current effects, count as an Infected/Darkened; and have a note that while the Cold Guard often have the resolve to resist the Darkness until their Shadows fall under the safe limit again, even they struggle to resist the Darkness forever.<br /> <br /> Then leave it to players to roleplay it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, when they exceed their safe limit, they now start counting as creatures of Darkness (technically Darkened).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T19:31:41-07:00","id":1130653,"title":"","content":"Okay guys, I prefer to be frank with you, I think the new Compacts and Conspiracies have now become kind of a mess. There are too many retooling in too many different directions: some want to keep the Cold Guard, others want the Peasant Guard, some want tor reimaging the Cold Guard as a different group. Then we have that third lighter Conspiracy nobody seems to have a clear idea for, and the former Crown Jewels who have been converted into a compact... #Ammit, Character Risk Analysis and the Magisters are still mostly stable, but everything else is getting messy.<br /> <br /> So I think we need to organize ourselves on that. See what's everybody's opinion on which direction we should go for each group, and agree on a common direction so we can finally have clear plans rather than go in every possible direction.<br /> <br /> Please list your opinions clearly below for each compacts, and once that's done we'll try finding an agreement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T03:34:11-07:00","id":1130759,"title":"","content":"#Ammit: Good concept. Small overlap with Network Zero, but their goals and methods are different. They really just need a little more material to give a grasp on how they operate, and they are fine.<br /> <br /> Character Risk Assessment: Same (except the N0 overlap). They provide a nice, non-physical approach to the Vigil.<br /> <br /> Star of Bethlehem: Honestly, I think they could be rolled into the Talbot Group and Habibti Ma, if the former weren't also Splat-focused on different targets.<br /> <br /> Crown Jewels: I think they should still be a Conspiracy, their Endowment being Bequests separate from need Princesses. The arguments that they would need to be loyal to Nobles to exist isn't as convincing in a Hunter book. They can still be an organization that employs former Sworn to their own independent, monster hunting ends - without being a fawning Princess Sworn-recruitment agency.<br /> <br /> Magisters of the Economie: Still don't like the name. Other than that, the concept is great. Rich bastards with power. Using Dreamlands brainwashing. Taking the powers of the Light for their own ends. Wonderful.<br /> <br /> Cold Guard/People's Guard: I like the former flavor (obviously). For the People's Guard, they are good, but other than their origin, I could easily see them as a non-specific target Hunter organization. I'm not sure if they would fit better as a Conspiracy (if so, I think they should have older roots that were rediscovered or revived during the French Revolution - democracy and plebian uprisings weren't invented just then), or just a determined Compact (especially with their Endowment being a hazy &quot;teamwork is magic&quot;).<br /> <br /> ???: Not sure about the &quot;Cleaners&quot; as they seem to be under revision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T04:34:32-07:00","id":1130767,"title":"","content":"Obviously my views are going to be biased because I worked on some of these groups, but nevertheless my opinions:<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Crown Jewels / Free Company</b></u><br /> <br /> The issue I have with the Crown Jewels is that they go against a core principal of Hunter: the Vigil: Hunters defeat supernatural opponents by using numbers, tactics, and exploiting their weaknesses. As written the Crown Jewels are the exact opposite. By trying to manipulate and manage Princesses, and compete for the loyalty of sworn they're going against Princesses on their strengths, not their weaknesses.<br /> <br /> The closest analogue would be the Bear Lodge who compete with Werewolves against their strength of hunting; but note that the Bear Lodge do exploit Werewolves' weaknesses with silver weapons, the Crown Jewels don't have an equivalent, and the Bear Lodge canonically have taken major losses. As a decentralised Compact they can afford those losses, but Princesses are much better at sharing information than Werewolves. If the Crown Jewels had a similar attrition rate to the Bear Lodge their secret would be exposed to the Noble community and it's game over.<br /> <br /> The Free Company is an attempt to take the core concept of a hunter group of Sworn who work with and support Princesses, but avoid the above flaws. For example, rather than competing with Princesses for the Sworn's loyalty; I made it a win-win situation if a Princess recruits a member to be her retainer.<br /> <br /> My vote is to use the Free Company.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>The Star of Bethlehem</b></u><br /> <br /> The positives: They're a believable group with plausible motivations. And they seem like the sort of group that would naturally exist.<br /> <br /> The negatives: Their motives are incorrect as the Queens don't encourage children to fight monsters, they're just genere savvy and know it's pointless to try and stop them (unless the ST twists the Princess setting to make the Star of Bethlehem right). Their goal of opposing the Queens is also mostly impossible, since they can't reach the Dreamlands, and the Queens are demigods surrounded by entire armies of magic wielders.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if they'll appeal to players given the above.<br /> <br /> My thought: I wouldn't object to dropping them. I would object to making them an Endowed Conspiracy with a real chance of fighting Queens \u2013 it would remove the \u201cordinary parent in an unordinary situation\u201d vibe that makes the group good in the first place.<br /> <br /> Giving them a more achievable goal could work, but I'm not sure what goal could be: Relatable, achievable, and conflicts with Princesses.<br /> <br /> My vote: Abstain, but I'd vote against turning them into a Conspiracy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>The Cold Guard</b></u><br /> <br /> My views are simple. Any group who outright tries to hunt and kill Princesses needs to have a philosophical reason for doing so, and that reason needs to be solid enough that players can make a convincing argument in character. The Cold Guard don't do this, the replacement groups do.<br /> <br /> My vote: Replace them.<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Cold Guard (Vent0's version)</b></u><br /> <br /> It's still early days so it's hard to say too much. I like the Endowment. I like the philosophical opposition to nobles based on overcoming your sins / managing your sins and drawing strength from them; and I'd like to see their methods of fighting the Darkness thematically embody that philosophy. Bleak Oubliette is a good start (I did say it was my favourite <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).<br /> <br /> I'm less keen on the bit about opposing nobles because nobles want to make people dependent upon them. It's not exactly wrong, but I think it's less interesting than \u201c overcoming your sins / drawing strength from them\u201d.<br /> <br /> My vote: It's really too early to say. But it shows promise.<br /> <br /> <u><b>The People's Guard</b></u><br /> <br /> I very much like that it ties into real world history and a real world philosophical idea that actually would object to Nobles on principal.<br /> <br /> Given that they're willing to kill over that principal, and their origins in the bloodthirsty French Revolution, I suspect they'll come off as fanatics and morally tainted, but at the same time that's not a bad thing. There's plenty of morally dubious Hunters, and it's kinda neat to see fanatics who aren't religiously motivated. I've never heard of an urban fantasy group who object to the way magic creates a privileged class before.<br /> <br /> However like Vent0's Cold Guard it's early in development so it's hard to say much.<br /> <br /> My vote: It's really too early to say. But it shows promise.<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Church of the Valley</b></u><br /> <br /> (The new name for the Sanitation Workers Collective. <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1t7U_sglV9RXTBc3oU3J-bJFSRVbEAobbFEwyxPrD838/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Link is here</a>)<br /> <br /> Thus far I think they're the only group we have who fit the morally white/grey Conspiracy niche. The People's Guard are grey/grey at best because of their fanaticism, and Vent0's Cold Guard are powered by the physical embodiment of evil and can be corrupted by it so grey/grey at best; their philosophy of accepting and drawing strength from their own sins also strikes me as anti-heroic (I recommend embracing that, who doesn't like a good anti-hero?).<br /> <br /> And I think this group has a lot going for it. They have a philosophical objection to Princesses and a modus operandi that can result in the two groups working together or working against each other depending on the situation. There's a nice \u201cprotect the world that looks down on you vibe\u201d to it. They explore parts of Hunter that rarely get explored \u2013 which is to say they put a lot of focus on actually acting like a conspiracy, infiltrating the corridors of power and manipulating them. But at the same time you can still run them in the classic hunter style of finding monsters and fighting them.<br /> <br /> Myself and MP also addressed the previous issues, giving them a religious angle to make them more distinct from the people's guard and a more defined origin for their Endowment.<br /> <br /> My vote: Include them.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Overall</b></u><br /> <br /> I understand your worry about going in every direction at once, but I do not think there's a problem here.<br /> <br /> Vent0's version of the Cold Guard, the People's Guard, and the Church of the Valley are all different groups that fill different niches. Rather than think of it as the redevelopment of the old Cold Guard being confused and pulled in different directions, treat it as three independent groups being developed side by side. Unlike official products you have no wordcount limits. I could see a 4/4 spread of<br /> <br /> Compacts: #Ammit, The Light Company, Character Risk Analysis, Star of Bethlehem.<br /> <br /> Conspiracies: Magisters, People's Guard, Cold Guard, Church of the Valley.<br /> <br /> Working fine.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1130630#post1130630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll try specify that. Like once per day, or given motivating circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd have a second, longer, interval for exceptional successes. Once every three months maybe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1130630#post1130630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Issue with Channel Spite is that the damage could get crazy high, fast.<br /> For Devouring Dark, I could. I was thinking of that. Though Shadows can get pretty high, making it almost unfair.</div> </div> </div> </div> True. But I still favour soft limits over hard. Maybe tie it into Breaking Points. If you're over the safe limit you get a different, and nastier set of Conditions, from a Breaking Point roll; even a success is bad news.<br /> <br /> If you're over Safe Limit +5 a Success on a breaking point roll could trigger a mechanic like Werewolf's Death Rage, locking you out from making full use of your power surge. While a failure could lead to your cell outright being forced to put you down, if they can't afford to take the risk of locking you up until the tempoary shadows fade.<br /> <br /> You could also use Shadows / 2 in some cases, especially for direct damage effects. Since the safe limit can go up to 10 and I don't think Endowments will be pushing damage above five in most cases.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1130630#post1130630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Good point on Veil of Corruption. So make it a more stealth and Dark World excursion power?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1130630#post1130630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other than the Monster Lord Dread Power?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, something that lets them not only order the Lurker, but also leash it's evil impulses. So if you order it to meet you outside a nest, it wont walk around the area spreading fear and mayhem until you arive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1130630#post1130630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, when they exceed their safe limit, they now start counting as creatures of Darkness (technically Darkened).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oops missed that. But more emphasis on how the Conspiracy thinks of this drawback, and a few roleplaying hints, would be helpful.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T04:45:11-07:00","id":1130771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1130759#post1130759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">???: Not sure about the &quot;Cleaners&quot; as they seem to be under revision.</div> </div> </div> </div>The revision is pretty much done, or done enough for them to be reviewed. I'd be interested to hear what you think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1130759#post1130759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crown Jewels: I think they should still be a Conspiracy, their Endowment being Bequests separate from need Princesses. The arguments that they would need to be loyal to Nobles to exist isn't as convincing in a Hunter book. They can still be an organization that employs former Sworn to their own independent, monster hunting ends - without being a fawning Princess Sworn-recruitment agency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to clarify a point: It's not that Sworn need to be loyal to Princesses. It's that the Crown Jewels directly compete with Princesses for a Sworn's loyalty.<br /> <br /> A group that employs Sworn who've lost the Princess they used to work with to peruse an independent goal could work.<br /> <br /> However a Conspiracy that employs Sworn, while those Sworn are retainers for a Princess, and expects those Sworn to be more loyal to the Conspiracy than the Princess has no chance of making it work. Hunters win by exploiting supernaturals' weaknesses, not by going against their strongest front. At best the Conspiracy could win the loyalty of some Sworn, but not enough to stop the Princess community learning their secrets.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm under the impression that Darinas specifically wanted a group of Nobles who worked along side Princesses; which is why I designed the Light Company so that they wouldn't need to compete with Princesses for their members loyalty. An independent group of Sworn could work, but it would still need a complete re-write from the current write up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T18:29:49-07:00","id":1131049,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hoH6av4_H3OpWFvIpsigGacqHxPo7F7dfj4x2E9Lwtc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> is my ongoing doc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1130767#post1130767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <u><b>The Crown Jewels / Free Company</b></u><br /> <br /> The issue I have with the Crown Jewels is that they go against a core principal of Hunter: the Vigil: Hunters defeat supernatural opponents by using numbers, tactics, and exploiting their weaknesses. As written the Crown Jewels are the exact opposite. By trying to manipulate and manage Princesses, and compete for the loyalty of sworn they're going against Princesses on their strengths, not their weaknesses.<br /> <br /> The closest analogue would be the Bear Lodge who compete with Werewolves against their strength of hunting; but note that the Bear Lodge do exploit Werewolves' weaknesses with silver weapons, the Crown Jewels don't have an equivalent, and the Bear Lodge canonically have taken major losses. As a decentralised Compact they can afford those losses, but Princesses are much better at sharing information than Werewolves. If the Crown Jewels had a similar attrition rate to the Bear Lodge their secret would be exposed to the Noble community and it's game over.<br /> <br /> The Free Company is an attempt to take the core concept of a hunter group of Sworn who work with and support Princesses, but avoid the above flaws. For example, rather than competing with Princesses for the Sworn's loyalty; I made it a win-win situation if a Princess recruits a member to be her retainer.<br /> <br /> My vote is to use the Free Company.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'd argue that the Crown Jewels target isn't the Princesses, but the Darkness. Given the mercenary spin, they wouldn't try to manipulate Princesses, just get Bequests from them. As for loyalty, they'd be more to pick up the Princess's Sworn once the Noble ends up dead (via other means/foes, of course).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1130767#post1130767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>The Cold Guard (Vent0's version)</b></u><br /> <br /> It's still early days so it's hard to say too much. I like the Endowment. I like the philosophical opposition to nobles based on overcoming your sins / managing your sins and drawing strength from them; and I'd like to see their methods of fighting the Darkness thematically embody that philosophy. Bleak Oubliette is a good start (I did say it was my favourite <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).<br /> <br /> I'm less keen on the bit about opposing nobles because nobles want to make people dependent upon them. It's not exactly wrong, but I think it's less interesting than \u201c overcoming your sins / drawing strength from them\u201d.<br /> <br /> My vote: It's really too early to say. But it shows promise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I'll try to work on the fluff elements this weekend.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1130767#post1130767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>The Church of the Valley</b></u><br /> <br /> (The new name for the Sanitation Workers Collective. <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1t7U_sglV9RXTBc3oU3J-bJFSRVbEAobbFEwyxPrD838/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Link is here</a>)<br /> <br /> Thus far I think they're the only group we have who fit the morally white/grey Conspiracy niche. The People's Guard are grey/grey at best because of their fanaticism, and Vent0's Cold Guard are powered by the physical embodiment of evil and can be corrupted by it so grey/grey at best; their philosophy of accepting and drawing strength from their own sins also strikes me as anti-heroic (I recommend embracing that, who doesn't like a good anti-hero?).<br /> <br /> And I think this group has a lot going for it. They have a philosophical objection to Princesses and a modus operandi that can result in the two groups working together or working against each other depending on the situation. There's a nice \u201cprotect the world that looks down on you vibe\u201d to it. They explore parts of Hunter that rarely get explored \u2013 which is to say they put a lot of focus on actually acting like a conspiracy, infiltrating the corridors of power and manipulating them. But at the same time you can still run them in the classic hunter style of finding monsters and fighting them.<br /> <br /> Myself and MP also addressed the previous issues, giving them a religious angle to make them more distinct from the people's guard and a more defined origin for their Endowment.<br /> <br /> My vote: Include them.</div> </div> </div> </div>They still seem very similar. Their Endowment looks unchanged, last I saw. Where are they getting their powers from, again?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1130767#post1130767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd have a second, longer, interval for exceptional successes. Once every three months maybe.<br /> <br /> True. But I still favour soft limits over hard. Maybe tie it into Breaking Points. If you're over the safe limit you get a different, and nastier set of Conditions, from a Breaking Point roll; even a success is bad news.<br /> <br /> If you're over Safe Limit +5 a Success on a breaking point roll could trigger a mechanic like Werewolf's Death Rage, locking you out from making full use of your power surge. While a failure could lead to your cell outright being forced to put you down, if they can't afford to take the risk of locking you up until the tempoary shadows fade.<br /> <br /> You could also use Shadows / 2 in some cases, especially for direct damage effects. Since the safe limit can go up to 10 and I don't think Endowments will be pushing damage above five in most cases.<br /> <br /> Sounds good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incorporated some of the suggestions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1130767#post1130767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, something that lets them not only order the Lurker, but also leash it's evil impulses. So if you order it to meet you outside a nest, it wont walk around the area spreading fear and mayhem until you arive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I left open the ability to acquire Dread Powers so I wouldn't have to retread powers. If you don't want your pet monsters to cause a scene, keep them away from polite company and give them strict orders. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1130767#post1130767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oops missed that. But more emphasis on how the Conspiracy thinks of this drawback, and a few roleplaying hints, would be helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I did update it in a post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T00:06:16-07:00","id":1131143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1131049#post1131049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'd argue that the Crown Jewels target isn't the Princesses, but the Darkness. Given the mercenary spin, they wouldn't try to manipulate Princesses, just get Bequests from them. As for loyalty, they'd be more to pick up the Princess's Sworn once the Noble ends up dead (via other means/foes, of course).</div> </div> </div> </div> That's very different from the current write-up; who do target and try to manipulate Princesses. Nobody's written an interpretation like that yet.<br /> <br /> It could work, I think it would need an explanation as to why the members want to be part of an all Sworn group rather than work directly with Princesses. Sworn might not need to be loyal to a Princess, but the internal consistency of a charachter is still important. When the group's membership used to work directly with Princesses, remained loyal to those Princesses' cause after their death, you have to ask why they'd reject Princesses who try to join the group. And if you have a mixed group of Sworn and Princesses who promotes based on merit Princesses have supernaturally high levels of merit. This might be a hunter book, but Princesses are still team players who like to join organisations and are supernaturally skilled, which is all it takes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1131049#post1131049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their Endowment looks unchanged, last I saw. Where are they getting their powers from, again?</div> </div> </div> </div> Religious rites discovered by combining African folklore and Christianity.<br /> <br /> &quot;The slaves brought powerful stories and myths with them on the arduous trip from Africa, and they combined these with Christian ideals to create a new faith, manifesting in a strange power that let them survive&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-19-2017, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T13:23:49-07:00","id":1131414,"title":"","content":"So a few ideas for fiction pieces.<br /> <br /> 1: A Medieval pieces about a princess of Tears being countered by the Knights of St. George, only for them to find their Goetic Gospels aren't working as they should against a woman that by all logic says should be a witch.<br /> <br /> 2: Age of Exploration involving a group of &quot;merchants&quot; discussing their latest deal with the &quot;Wardens&quot;<br /> <br /> 3: ORAS paper on a strange cryptid from North Africa that seemed to be some kind of &quot;corrupter&quot;.<br /> <br /> 4: People's Guard &quot;meeting notes&quot; from the 1930s when they were fighting against a princess of storms in Chicago, with TFV stamps stating they broke up a group of &quot;paranormal-equipped communists&quot;.<br /> <br /> 5: Malleus notes on a 1990s rise of sightings of a &quot;new type of witch&quot;.<br /> <br /> 6: Transcript of a discussion between a Union hunter and a princess of Clubs over how to best deal with a Nest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T13:37:17-07:00","id":1131425,"title":"","content":"Number two is my favourite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T15:08:51-07:00","id":1131464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1131143#post1131143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Religious rites discovered by combining African folklore and Christianity.<br /> <br /> &quot;The slaves brought powerful stories and myths with them on the arduous trip from Africa, and they combined these with Christian ideals to create a new faith, manifesting in a strange power that let them survive&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, there's a real-world West African/Christian syncretic religion. It's called <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santer%C3%ADa\" target=\"_blank\">Santeria</a>, and it's very similar to voodoo, on which the Les Mysteres conspiracy is based. I would expect an Endowment developed by syncretism of West African myth and Christianity to look like the Rites du Cheval, not like your &quot;Cleansing&quot;, which is focused on stealth and infiltration and has nothing from either of its putative religious sources in it.<br /> <br /> Since there isn't much point to creating another Les Mysteres, the Church of the Valley looks like a mix of them and the People's Guard, and the Guard's Endowment isn't developed yet ... I suggest that you just combine the Church of the Valley and the Guard. Drop Vox Populi, give the Guard Cleansing, and refocus the Guard as a conspiracy of spies and thieves working to subvert the powerful, not lead uprisings against them. (Is there a compact or conspiracy that works like real spy networks?) Add in the idea that the Guard secretly cleans up the corruption that the powerful and careless leave behind them (the virtuous side of the Church of the Valley) and you have a solid concept: hunters who try to do good by stealth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T15:12:53-07:00","id":1131465,"title":"","content":"The closest I can really think of are TFV Suits, though Kings did write MI18.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T15:17:32-07:00","id":1131467,"title":"","content":"I approve of all the notes, Flyboy. We need as many fictions as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T15:49:23-07:00","id":1131484,"title":"","content":"Okay then, first off.<br /> <br /> KINGS! *Kicks door open* What the hell can a princess of Tears do to a group of Knights of St. George?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T18:33:15-07:00","id":1131549,"title":"","content":"Drain their Willpower when she attacks them, hit them with a moment of bad luck, stop them from using Willpower to boost a dice pool, drain their Willpower by <i>talking</i> to them to the point where they'll automatically obey one order, blight any of their Resistance Attributes, read their minds to discover just how to persuade them to do her favors (and what favors they can do her), force them to serve Alhambra for a month or go slowly mad (though that takes a few hours), set ghosts on them, plant a ghost in their safehouse ... and those are just Charms specific to Tears.<br /> <br /> By the way, which Goetic Gospel powers would actually work against a Noble?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T01:05:03-07:00","id":1131650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1131464#post1131464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, there's a real-world West African/Christian syncretic religion. It's called <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santer%C3%ADa\" target=\"_blank\">Santeria</a>, and it's very similar to voodoo, on which the Les Mysteres conspiracy is based. I would expect an Endowment developed by syncretism of West African myth and Christianity to look like the Rites du Cheval, not like your &quot;Cleansing&quot;, which is focused on stealth and infiltration and has nothing from either of its putative religious sources in it.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's also <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Umbanda\" target=\"_blank\">Umbanda</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winti\" target=\"_blank\">Winti,</a> and probably several more. not all Cast African / Christian syncretic religions are going to look the same.<br /> <br /> The focus on stealth and infultration comes from worship on the plantations itself. Such as the use of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prayer_kettle\" target=\"_blank\">prayer kettles</a> to hide items of value, and the need to hold prayer <a href=\"http://www.christianitytoday.com/history/issues/issue-33/secret-religion-of-slaves.html\" target=\"_blank\">meetings in secret</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1131464#post1131464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suggest that you just combine the Church of the Valley and the Guard. Drop Vox Populi, give the Guard Cleansing, and refocus the Guard as a conspiracy of spies and thieves working to subvert the powerful, not lead uprisings against them. (Is there a compact or conspiracy that works like real spy networks?) Add in the idea that the Guard secretly cleans up the corruption that the powerful and careless leave behind them (the virtuous side of the Church of the Valley) and you have a solid concept: hunters who try to do good by stealth.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be a massive change to the guard, less so to the Church of the Valley - who's modus operandi of stealth and infultration - is the core of the concept; rather than their backstory of faith. So long as the struggles of poverty angle remains I can support this, but I think we should ask <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar483_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"483\" data-vbnamecard=\"483\">Flyboy254</a> about this. Since the Guard would be changing more than the Church.<br /> <br /> If we merged the two we could keep the French Revolution origin, but with more focus on the failures of the revolution; they would see it as the replacement of one tyrant with another tyrant and as a result they soured on the idea of revolutions and supported various reform movements instead, before they came to believe that reforms only work for a while before society returns to inequality (pick a last straw, it could be as late as collapse of manufacutring and the growing rust belt) and decided to work in the shadows themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1131464#post1131464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Is there a compact or conspiracy that works like real spy networks?)</div> </div> </div> </div>TF:V has elements of it, but it's closer to the NSA data mining the entire internet than going undercover. Certainly Advanced Armory doesn't have much to help with infultration. I wrote MI:18, but they're more like James Bond with weird gadgets and snappy one liners. The church's style of spying and theving is a yet unfilled niche.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1131484#post1131484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">KINGS! *Kicks door open* What the hell can a princess of Tears do to a group of Knights of St. George?</div> </div> </div> </div>The most likely thing is actually just shoot them. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PZ2xnHOJmO0\" target=\"_blank\">Princess combat magic is very direct</a>.<br /> <br /> Other possibilities include subverting the demons the Knights summon (this is <i>really</i> playing fast and loose with the setting, since Tears can manipulate Darkness not demons, and the Knights might be summoning Abyssal intruders not demons).<br /> <br /> The Princess could just blow up a ton of medieval gunpowder in the knowledge that she's tough enough to survive it but her opponents aren't. Tears believe that there is no price too high for their continued survival; so when backed into a corner they're likely to pull of stunts like this.<br /> <br /> The Princess' magic could be nullified by the Goetic Gospels, only for her to demonstrate that unlike conjuring fire with arcane chanting, her skill with a magic sword works just as well with a regular sword.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1131549#post1131549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, which Goetic Gospel powers would actually work against a Noble?</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO, most of them. If it specifically refers to Source or Paradox it won't work on Princesses. But anything that refers to a spell could affect a Charm. And anything that refers to a Mystery could translate to a Charm Tree.<br /> <br /> But Holy Shield and Transformations aren't spells, so at the very least a Princess will still have significant power and her enhanced attributes and skills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-20-2017, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T09:20:12-07:00","id":1131743,"title":"","content":"I honestly don't see the Guard's style being changed like that without losing their core themes of how I wrote them. We're talking about guys who would tear down the system damn how well the powers that be claim to be working. Merging them with a syncretic religion doesn't seem like something they would do in my own mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T11:16:36-07:00","id":1131792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1131650#post1131650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's also <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Umbanda\" target=\"_blank\">Umbanda</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winti\" target=\"_blank\">Winti,</a> and probably several more. not all Cast African / Christian syncretic religions are going to look the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, there are differences; but the key element - ritual dances intended to invite possession by spirits - is shared across all the syncretic West African religions, and it's that which inspired the Rites du Cheval Endowment. I'm saying a conspiracy with a religious backstory should have an Endowment based on the religion; and also that Les Mysteres already occupies the niche of &quot;conspiracy based on West African syncretism&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1131650#post1131650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be a massive change to the guard, less so to the Church of the Valley - who's modus operandi of stealth and infultration - is the core of the concept; rather than their backstory of faith. So long as the struggles of poverty angle remains I can support this, but I think we should ask <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar483_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"483\" data-vbnamecard=\"483\">Flyboy254</a> about this. Since the Guard would be changing more than the Church.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1131743#post1131743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don't see the Guard's style being changed like that without losing their core themes of how I wrote them. We're talking about guys who would tear down the system damn how well the powers that be claim to be working. Merging them with a syncretic religion doesn't seem like something they would do in my own mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was suggesting that the People's Guard take over the Cleansing Endowment, not the Church of the Valley's backstory. The arc I envision is the Guard starting as leaders of popular revolts against supernatural aristocrats (the current writeup), then developing a clandestine branch that prepares for the revolution by watching monsters in secret (and finding the Endowment), and finally realizing that popular revolts aren't good tools for taking down most monsters, and striking from anonymity works a lot better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1131650#post1131650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Princess' magic could be nullified by the Goetic Gospels, only for her to demonstrate that unlike conjuring fire with arcane chanting, her skill with a magic sword works just as well with a regular sword.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's the thing. What does &quot;spell&quot; mean in the rules for Goetic Gospels? Certainly it includes Supernal magic and thaumaturgy ala Second Sight, because those are what the Gutter Magic rules in Witch Finders cover. Just as certainly, it doesn't include all supernatural powers - psychics are specifically excluded, for instance. But there's no clear rule, or even indication, saying what powers are affected and what aren't. For example, are powers from spirits - Numina, werewolf Gifts, the Rites du Cheval - vulnerable to the Goetic Gospels? Are ghosts? Wyrd-based magic? The God-Machine and its servants? If any of those are covered, I can see Charms being vulnerable too; but I could easily make a case that none of them are. (Princess actually has a notion of &quot;spell&quot; in the Arcane Embassy, but by that definition most Charms are <i>not</i> Arcane.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T11:30:31-07:00","id":1131800,"title":"","content":"Isn't that more the Ascending Ones with the Knife of Paradise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T06:04:47-07:00","id":1132172,"title":"","content":"There is similarities. But we haven't seen the Knife of Paradise manipulating politics from the shadows, and it's members seem to have better more stable jobs (i.e. they're usually clergy) than the Valley.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1131792#post1131792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that's the thing. What does &quot;spell&quot; mean in the rules for Goetic Gospels? Certainly it includes Supernal magic and thaumaturgy ala Second Sight, because those are what the Gutter Magic rules in Witch Finders cover. Just as certainly, it doesn't include all supernatural powers - psychics are specifically excluded, for instance. But there's no clear rule, or even indication, saying what powers are affected and what aren't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. So I'm using the following rule of thumb:<br /> <br /> 1) It's a Gift/Contract/Charm or some other power and not an innate template ability like a Pledge or Transformation<br /> 2) The relevant gameline describes it as magic.<br /> <br /> The various Thamaturge traditions are fairly diverse, so I think Charms can fit in there too.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T15:15:22-07:00","id":1132409,"title":"","content":"What if we had the Cleaners as a faction within the People's Guard?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T17:00:50-07:00","id":1132436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1132409#post1132409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if we had the Cleaners as a faction within the People's Guard?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the &quot;REVOLUTION!&quot; firebrands are one faction, the &quot;Infiltrate the halls of power as janitors&quot; are another faction? Maybe a third as academics and sociologists, who identify the driving forces of society? Or general researchers who found the secret of the Conspiracies Endowment? Or just a general &quot;talk-y&quot; Logistics and negotiator faction that keeps the other two supplied?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T17:49:12-07:00","id":1132451,"title":"","content":"Yep, sounds good to me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T19:06:24-07:00","id":1132466,"title":"","content":"I'm good with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T02:31:01-07:00","id":1132535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1132436#post1132436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the &quot;REVOLUTION!&quot; firebrands are one faction, the &quot;Infiltrate the halls of power as janitors&quot; are another faction? Maybe a third as academics and sociologists, who identify the driving forces of society? Or general researchers who found the secret of the Conspiracies Endowment? Or just a general &quot;talk-y&quot; Logistics and negotiator faction that keeps the other two supplied?</div> </div> </div> </div>That leaves out Valley faction of people who's jobs are so bad they need an Endowment just to make it to quitting time (e.g. the cleaning crew who're forced to work in Nests). That was the core of the group, and I wouldn't want to see them go.<br /> <br /> Obviously there's no reason why we can't have more than three groups, The Malleus has six thanks to extras in the Compacts and Conspiracies book. But thinking about it. Having some groups based on a big picture philosophy and others based on their situation, it feels like some groups fit the leadership but other groups are more appropriate to the front line. Les Mysteries introuduced a tweaked setup by combining factions with the crossroads.<br /> <br /> What if we were to introduce our own tweak? Where we have seperate groups for low status and high status members. The low status groups would be based on the current ones in the Church of the Valley. The high status groups will be the &quot;REVOLUTION!&quot; faction and the &quot;Infiltrate the halls of power&quot; faction. For the third, of the proposals in your post I prefer logistics. Researchers and socieologists should be distributed between the groups; so that all the groups their favoured accademics arguing that their group is correct.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T14:22:13-07:00","id":1134609,"title":"","content":"Back from vacay with some stereotypes of the People's Guard from the core Compacts and Conspiracies. You can tell me if I missed any of them.<br /> <br /> <b>Loyalists of Thule</b>: Mob rule can just as disastrous as fascism, especially when its hatred has so singular a focus.<br /> <br /> <b>Aegis Kai Doru</b>: Wonderful allies in the war against the Mages and their Shifter Servants. Now if only they would stop destroying the relics we need.<br /> <br /> <b>Ascending Ones</b>: Call them if an Empath is disrupting funding operations, but make sure to make it worth their while<br /> <br /> <b>Ashwood Abbey</b>: Fucking commies who want to take away all our neat toys. But handy if you can convince a cell to go hunting Nobles with you.<br /> <br /> <b>Task Force: Valkyrie</b>: A useful but tentative ally against the invasion. But learn all you can for when they turn on us next.<br /> <br /> <b>Cheiron Group</b>: Protests led by them have disrupted operations minimally before, but they are more useful than not. Standing orders are to tail them and grab the leftovers. <br /> <br /> <b>Union</b>: We're not in this for their revolution, but when you've got to go up against an Empath, there's no one I trust more.<br /> <br /> <b>Malleus Maleficarum</b>: They deny all authority, even the divine. They must be brought to heel.<br /> <br /> <b>Long Night</b>: Hypocrites who use atheism and their own damned brand of magic to lead the flock astray.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T14:59:49-07:00","id":1134628,"title":"","content":"Slight edit to VALKYRIE to make it more &quot;government&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;Reactionary movement to P/S-ENE forces attempting sedition against government. Utilize as disposable assets in eventual hostilities between personnel; recommend domestic law enforcement.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T15:05:21-07:00","id":1134633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1134628#post1134628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slight edit to VALKYRIE to make it more &quot;government&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;Reactionary movement to P/S-ENE forces attempting sedition against government. Utilize as disposable assets<b>. In eventual hostilities between personnel</b>; recommend domestic law enforcement.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine, but jolly good","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T15:55:10-07:00","id":1134646,"title":"","content":"I suggest we change either the People's Guard's or the Cold Guard's name. Having both names with &quot;Guard&quot; feels a bit redundant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T16:58:37-07:00","id":1134663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1134646#post1134646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suggest we change either the People's Guard's or the Cold Guard's name. Having both names with &quot;Guard&quot; feels a bit redundant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Vanguard different enough?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T22:08:52-07:00","id":1134754,"title":"","content":"I guess it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T00:18:42-07:00","id":1134775,"title":"","content":"So what's happening with the discussion on the direction for compacts/conspiracies? It feels like the conversation just stopped half way through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T19:55:12-07:00","id":1135040,"title":"","content":"still not sure. I guess we <i>might</i> follow your suggestion, but I'm waiting for the other conspiracy to be completed...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T15:39:55-07:00","id":1136405,"title":"","content":"For a reminder, the People's Guard still has missing informations regarding status and other sections, by the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T15:18:38-07:00","id":1137063,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11745_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11745\" data-vbnamecard=\"11745\">Darinas</a> asked me to put the Church of the Valley into the main document so it's all in one place. But we still need to think of a future direction for them.<br /> <br /> When the discussion on the subject ended we were discussing the possibility of merging them with the People's Guard. And I said that if we did that we'd probably want to do something unique with the factions (look at Les Mysteries' crossroad for an example of tweaked factions). That way we could represent both the split between the &quot;Vive la r\u00e9volution&quot; faction who want radical change, and the &quot;Robin Hood political blackmail&quot; faction who think tearing down the system will hurt the poor who're they're supposed to protect and want to manipulate the system instead; along with the inevitable stop arguing and get on with the job faction. While having a second axis to cover the split between thieves, spies, and hunters dealing with nests that's in the current Church write up.<br /> <br /> The backstory for this could keep the origins in the French revolution but have the excesses and failures of the revolution lead to the conspiracy becoming moderates, only for two world wars and growing awareness of the cultural underpinnings of racism leading to the revolutionaries growing again; only for the moderates to re-asscend after the fall of the Iron Curtain and more knowledge about what the Soviets were up too. This would put the moderates in charge, but the revolutionaries start picking up steam after the 2008 crash. With both sides blaming each other for Trump, Brexit, and the rise of populism in continental Europe (you moderates are turning a blind eye to the system being broken enough to elect Trump vs Trump is a populist who riles up the working class, who does that remind me off?) and the possibility of it going either way in the player's game.<br /> <br /> (The idea is that if players want to be revolutionaries, having a vulnerable but still in charge moderate faction makes the perfect target for players to have fun overthrowing without upending the storyteller's setting. But if the Storyteller is ok with them overthrowing major world governments they can press on anyway) <hr /><br /> Alternatively if we don't merge the two we should probably nail down what exactly the Church of the Valley's theology is, and how much of their behaviour is driven by faith and how much is driven by political pragramtism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-03-2017, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T22:48:14-07:00","id":1137610,"title":"","content":"Got another art piece. Clubs and the Malleus try to work out what to do about an interesting tome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://sta.sh/01d55zks3t3v\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://st.deviantart.net/minish/main/logo/card_black_large.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a hr