195132\" target=\"_blank\"> https://erinptah.deviantart.com/art/Commission-Priests-and-Clubs-704195132 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Commission - Priests and Clubs &mdash; artwork by ErinPtah on DeviantArt. Published: 2017-09-15 &middot; Likes: 13 &middot; Views: 1172 &middot; Comments: 2 &middot; Tags: commission, princessthehopeful, demmonhunters </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T06:04:06-07:00","id":1140785,"title":"","content":"Saw it already^^ We REALLY should start putting them on the document.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T10:17:28-07:00","id":1142201,"title":"","content":"Just posting to ask if everyone is fine (thinking in particular of people who were waiting for Irma).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T10:47:28-07:00","id":1142216,"title":"","content":"Same answer as last time, I'm waiting to know what direction we're taking the Church of the Valley. Are we merging them in the People's Guard? Going more religious? Revert to the old secular group?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T14:10:21-07:00","id":1142298,"title":"","content":"I am also waiting for answers personally. If people show up, I'm listening to their suggestions. And please don't move to a different topic until we have solved that issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T14:54:49-07:00","id":1142310,"title":"","content":"Tagging in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar483_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"483\" data-vbnamecard=\"483\">Flyboy254</a> (what's mp's forum account again?) - and no worries, I have no plans to drift off topic.<br /> <br /> My suggestion is to merge them with the People's Guard. The Church's theme of being the invisible people fits well with the peasant's revolt of the guard, and the two group's differing methods can be made into an internal division. My idea for the backstory:<ul><li>They still formed in the French Revolution with a stronger tie to Princesses. They were directly oppressed by a Princess of Tears as basically Wisp farming serfs. The revolution inspired them to rise up, and they claimed some magical stuff as spoils of victory before marching on Paris.</li> <li>The reign of terror disillusioned the group, and many had to flee abroad. Some started joining more reformist rather than revolutionary working class groups.</li> <li>WWI hits and the reformists are discredited - their soft approach allowed the elite to start a World War. WWII hits and discredits them further. The group aligns itself with communism leaving behind a rump of reformists.</li> <li>Around this time they develop Clensings as an Endowment.</li> <li>Stalin happens and the revolutionaries are discredited. The reformists meanwhile scored a major victory through protecting the suffragette movement (they took down a Seer of the Throne or a Beast); this puts them back in power, and align themselves with the American Civil Rights movement. Further successes cement their control.</li> <li>The financial crash hits once again damaging the reformists credibility. The current status is that the reformists are in charge but there's two competing movements, egalitarians and separatists.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> I was also thinking of doing an X/Y split for subfactions. Les mysteries did something similar. X is what you do from the Conspiracy and would include the current factions of the Church of the Valley. Y would be your political creed.<ul><li>Reformists - the domiment creed. They point to the French revolution and communism as proof that tearing down the system hurts those at the bottom. Reformists believe it's better to work with the system to change it for the better. But their idea of working with the system involves lots of blackmail and some political assassinations. A cross between Robin Hood and Professor Moriarty. A lot of low status members are Reformist by default, being unaware that there even is a Conspiracy above them.</li> <li>Egalitarians - the oldest creed. They're fundamentalists about equality, to the point they don't like the fact innate magic talents places some people above others. They also really don't like the hierarchical conspiracy the Reformists built. Communism is still popular.</li> <li>Separatists - the newest creed and a middle ground. They agree with the Egalitarians on morality, but also agree with the Reformists that revolutions don't work. They want to live in small societies, small enough for equality to be achievable. Hippy communes are an inspiration.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-20-2017, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T18:07:59-07:00","id":1142365,"title":"","content":"I'm in favor of the suggestions Kings, so long as we keep the theme of revolution and egalitarian ethos as their core ideal.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT: </b>Also that their endowment is an anti-magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 09-20-2017, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T01:43:33-07:00","id":1142439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1142365#post1142365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm in favor of the suggestions Kings, so long as we keep the theme of revolution and egalitarian ethos as their core ideal.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT: </b>Also that their endowment is an anti-magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a no then - since the suggestion was to make reformists/standing up for the little guy the current domimant ethos. Since the church cannot function without a hirarchical structure akin to a real criminal conspiracy; and since it would give the revolutionaries someone to revolt against (I figured a lot of storytellers would be more open to overthrowing a Conspiracy than overthrowing the government).<br /> <br /> But if you're set against that, the other option is to make the reformists/church a splinter faction of the guard. We'd drop the religious stuff. During the reign of terror the guard fled France to keep their heads attached, part of them went north to England, joined with groups like Chartists/Luddites (actual Luddites, not anti-technology) and eventually became a conspiracy manipulating politics to protect the little guy. Part of the Guard went East and eventually became communists, keeping their belief in revolution and equality.<br /> <br /> Making them splinter groups would neatly solve the problem of them having (some) similarities in theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-21-2017, 04:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T03:14:59-07:00","id":1142447,"title":"","content":"I am not sure about this approach to be frank; I am not sure these two groups merge that well. I mean, you realize both the Communists and a good chunk of the French Revolution were deeply anti-religious, right? In the case of the Revolution, they might have started out preaching freedom of cult, but the Terror was NOT nice to Catholicism. Heck, it's been centuries and some left-wing people in France <i>still</i> have issues with religion. So mixing them with a group based on a Church seem... kinda contradictory.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Mhm... upon re-reading, I realize King Raven did address that. My bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T05:18:41-07:00","id":1142469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1142447#post1142447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Mhm... upon re-reading, I realize King Raven did address that. My bad.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> the religious aspect was just a way to differentiate them from the Guard. It's tangenical to the core concept of a politics manipulating conspiracy among society's invisible people.<br /> <br /> IMO, if we make the two groups splinters of each other then we don't need to avoid similarities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T08:53:41-07:00","id":1142543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1142201#post1142201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just posting to ask if everyone is fine (thinking in particular of people who were waiting for Irma).</div> </div> </div> </div>I am, just busy with deadlines. I'll try to get some more ideas ironed out for the CG in the GDoc. If anyone has input or content, feel free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T08:59:51-07:00","id":1142547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1142469#post1142469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yep <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> the religious aspect was just a way to differentiate them from the Guard. It's tangenical to the core concept of a politics manipulating conspiracy among society's invisible people.<br /> <br /> IMO, if we make the two groups splinters of each other then we don't need to avoid similarities.</div> </div> </div> </div>So they deviated near inception? Would they have the same Endowment? Or separately discovered ones? How do they feel about each other now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T00:45:34-07:00","id":1142826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1142547#post1142547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So they deviated near inception? Would they have the same Endowment? Or separately discovered ones?</div> </div> </div> </div> I imagine that their Endowment has a common origin but they've taken it in such different directions that they're funtionally seperate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1142547#post1142547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do they feel about each other now?</div> </div> </div> </div>The People's Guard: You're trators who've got too comfortable with stolen wealth and power and now defend the oppressive symptom that feeds you.<br /> <br /> The other one: You're not even the downtrodden. You're comfortable enough to waste your time playing at revolution without a care to the lower classes who'll starve from chaos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T06:36:51-07:00","id":1144735,"title":"","content":"Sooo, I'll be frank, I get the impression nobody really knows what to do with the Cleansers. Am I the only one feeling like this?<br /> <br /> Regardless, unless we can figure out something to do with them, I'm thinking of something: we could merge them to the People's Guard and make them a subfaction (peharps one who is less concerned about hunting Princesses and more about fighting the Darkness itself). Then, either we create a new Conspiracy to fill its slot, or we add similar subfactions for the Cold Guard and the Magisters who are more reasonable. That way, we get less Conspiracies (which should be more manageable) AND we make some of them more sympathetic.<br /> <br /> Any opinion?<br /> <br /> Also, starting to wonder, wouldn't the People's Guard fit better as a Compact? Unlike the original Cold Guard, I get the feeling their Endowment doesn't bring much to their identity, not to mention it's a bit too vaguely defined to my tastes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 09-28-2017, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T08:09:28-07:00","id":1144778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1144735#post1144735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sooo, I'll be frank, I get the impression nobody really knows what to do with the Cleansers. Am I the only one feeling like this?<br /> <br /> Regardless, unless we can figure out something to do with them, I'm thinking of something: we could merge them to the People's Guard and make them a subfaction (peharps one who is less concerned about hunting Princesses and more about fighting the Darkness itself). Then, either we create a new Conspiracy to fill its slot, or we add similar subfactions for the Cold Guard and the Magisters who are more reasonable. That way, we get less Conspiracies (which should be more manageable) AND we make some of them more sympathetic.<br /> <br /> Any opinion?<br /> <br /> Also, starting to wonder, wouldn't the People's Guard fit better as a Compact? Unlike the original Cold Guard, I get the feeling their Endowment doesn't bring much to their identity, not to mention it's a bit too vaguely defined to my tastes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I haven't read all of the thread but have read the google doc, so I might be uninformed, but yeah, I think folding the Cleansers into the People's Guard and turning the People's Guard into a Compact are both great ideas. Maybe thinking up a new Conspiracy still focused on combating the Darkness would also be good, since most of the Conspiracies in this seem too focused on Princesses as the enemy.<br /> <br /> As for the Cold Guard and the Magisters, leave them that way. They aren't the only Hunters to make terrible, uninformed decisions (looking at you, Les Mysteres and Keepers of the Source).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T12:04:21-07:00","id":1144876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1144735#post1144735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sooo, I'll be frank, I get the impression nobody really knows what to do with the Cleansers. Am I the only one feeling like this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Um?<br /> <br /> I know exactly what to do with them. I'm planning to change the backstory to make them and the people's guard siblings when I find the time. But even right now they feel they are a complete and solid organisation.<br /> <br /> Princesses might suffer for their mission, but they get lots of luxuries too: They get appreciation, respect, privileges. Princesses are, after all, nobility.<br /> <br /> The Cleansers serve as a foil to this. They fight the same fight as Princesses but they get no recognition and no reward unless they take it for themselves.<br /> <br /> Most of all, Princesses have the ultimate luxury. The luxury of choice. With their magic they could easily escape and live comfortably in the wilderness away from danger and in blissfull ignorance of the world's ills. The Cleansers don't have that choice.<br /> <br /> Add to that that they explore an area not normally touched by hunter. There's lots of Conspiracies, but the idea of being a literal conspiracy who's agents are hidden among the corridors of power is pretty much untouched.<br /> <br /> All in all I think they're a unique group who fit well and can be used in many different ways.<br /> <br /> <br /> Darinas what exactly are you having trouble getting? You've said you don't understand them, but you dropped the topic as soon as you started it.<br /> <br /> As for for merging them with the People's Guard. I could do it, but Flyboy said he wants to keep the Guard in a direction that's incompatible with the Cleansers. Making them siblings with a shared origin seems like a safer option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-28-2017, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T13:03:37-07:00","id":1144905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1144876#post1144876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for for merging them with the People's Guard. I could do it, but Flyboy said he wants to keep the Guard in a direction that's incompatible with the Cleansers. Making them siblings with a shared origin seems like a safer option.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could also have them as an ancient conspiracy (as opposes to as recent as the French Revolution), I'm just saying...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T14:38:11-07:00","id":1144967,"title":"","content":"Yes, I figure you do have an idea, King Raven, since (no offense intended) you created that group to begin with. I meant the others, because whereas I got tons of suggestions for the other groups, I get the impression little to no one is suggesting anything for them.<br /> <br /> As for me personally, I admit I am still having a hard time figuring out what their deal really is. I get what you're trying to do with them as a foil for Princesses, but doesn't making them a Conspiracy goes against that? I mean, yeah, being a Conspiracy allows them to have agents everywhere, which serves your ideas, but it also means they have an Endowment. AKA Supernatural powers. AKA what you say they aren't supposed to have in contrast with Princesses. Hence why I feel they serve their foil purpose better as a Compact.<br /> <br /> Which leads me to my next problem: their Endowment. Not sure if you'll see what I mean, but I feel there is an issue similar to the Cainite Heresy here, in that their Endowment doesn't feel integral to the group; it doesn't really have a defined source (yet), it's just something allowing them to fight the Darkness which felt like it was added just to respect the rules of Conspiracies having Endowments.<br /> To illustrate, compare the core Conspiracies' Endowments: the Malleus Maleficarum are Church militants -&gt; blessed powers from prayers; the Lucifuge are half-demons -&gt; satanic powers; Task Force VALKYRIE is a MiB style government branch-&gt; high tech. The Aegis Kai Doru are Relic hunters -&gt; Relics which they collected. The Cheiron Group are mad scientists experimenting on supernaturals-&gt; chirurgical implants recovered from dissected monsters.<br /> Each time the Endowment has a clear concept and origin that feels really integral to what the organization is about, something I don't get with the Cleanser or the Cainite. And before you point it out, yes, I have the same issue with the People's Guard, just not as badly.<br /> <br /> Now, I won't deny I might be wrong. If you feel I am, by all mean show me how, that would avoid us retooling the whole thing yet again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T15:45:39-07:00","id":1144992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1144967#post1144967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for me personally, I admit I am still having a hard time figuring out what their deal really is. I get what you're trying to do with them as a foil for Princesses, but doesn't making them a Conspiracy goes against that? I mean, yeah, being a Conspiracy allows them to have agents everywhere, which serves your ideas, but it also means they have an Endowment. AKA Supernatural powers. AKA what you say they aren't supposed to have in contrast with Princesses.</div> </div> </div> </div> Pay no attention to the man behind the curtain!<br /> <br /> I mean. You have a point here. Partly there is a distinction - if you look at the magic Princesses get, it's full of potential to use it for yourself. Sure flying is a useful way to get to wherever Darkspawn are attacking before they do too much harm, but you can also fly for fun (flying is awesome!) or fly to visit your friends. Cleansings don't have these alternative uses unless you want to embark on a life of crime. Metaphorically speaking Princesses get the fancy dinner, Cleansers get the table scraps while they're at work.<br /> <br /> But the real reason they have this power. It's to justify the fact they even exist. An international conspiracy needs lots of money to function. You need training for your agents. You need to set up a communication infrastructure and keep the NSA out of it. The only way I could justify to myself that they haven't been busted by now is if they had a supernatural edge.<br /> <br /> So basically there's trade-offs. Giving them the Endowment did dilute the thematic purity, but it was nessacary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1144967#post1144967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which leads me to my next problem: their Endowment. Not sure if you'll see what I mean, but I feel there is an issue similar to the Cainite Heresy here, in that their Endowment doesn't feel integral to the group</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you mean, but I'm not sure I agree.<br /> <br /> I would argue that their specific powers are all exagerations of traits that reflect their role in society. Domestic staff are often overlooked, Invisible Servant lets them become almost outright invisible. The underpaid security guard watching the cameras is the guy who really knows what everyone's up too. With Guest List nobody can ever escape his sight.<br /> <br /> This could be made more explicit though. With the write ups referring to jobs by name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T16:26:48-07:00","id":1145004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would argue that their specific powers are all exagerations of traits that reflect their role in society. Domestic staff are often overlooked, Invisible Servant lets them become almost outright invisible. The underpaid security guard watching the cameras is the guy who really knows what everyone's up too. With Guest List nobody can ever escape his sight. </div> </div> </div>Yes, and<i> conceptually</i> it fits, much like the vampire-hating Cainites have rites allowing them to injure vampires in all sorts of creative ways. But again, the Endowment lacks a clear source that would tie to their origin; and I feel that gives them less of an identity; I prefer when Conspiracies have at least a vague idea of WHERE they got their Endowments. Since you said they get the scrap, again I think a cool idea could be to have gained their powers from recovered vestiges from the Kingdom. That would tie with the theme.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Okay, upon re-reading it, you DID give a source to the Cleansing Rites as a combination of african rites and Christian faith, my bad. Still not sure how that tie to their concept, but that's something, and I admit that conceptually it could be cool. So I don't know, maybe these rites don't need a retool after all. Maybe just play up that mixed religion angle by giving them names based on African folkfore and christian rites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 09-28-2017, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T18:33:45-07:00","id":1145045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1144992#post1144992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the real reason they have this power. It's to justify the fact they even exist. An international conspiracy needs lots of money to function. You need training for your agents. You need to set up a communication infrastructure and keep the NSA out of it. The only way I could justify to myself that they haven't been busted by now is if they had a supernatural edge.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know there are Conspiracies that don't have complicated infrastructure, deep pockets to fund operations, or indeed any global organization at all, right? Les Mysteres is described as a loose network of shamanistic cults that trade information occasionally. Then there's the Merrick Institute in &quot;Tooth &amp; Nail&quot; - a few hundred teenagers who escaped from a series of mysterious black labs, and have to steal most of their tech from the labs that experiment on kids like them. They're both Conspiracies because they have Endowments, which are absolutely central to their concepts. Neither one has anything like the global reach and coordination that, say, a US government task force, a European pharmaceutical firm, or an office in the Vatican bureaucracy does.<br /> <br /> The difference between a Compact and a Conspiracy isn't one of scale - it's clearly just &quot;does this group need cool powers to be credible monster hunters?&quot; And it's not obvious that the Cleansers <i>do</i> need an Endowment to work. Their concept is &quot;the people no one notices or thinks about&quot; - the janitor, the trash collector, the junkyard owner; the people who spend their lives cleaning up the dirt and stink left by their careless social superiors. They are the pariahs, the untouchables; their job is to take away filth and refuse that others don't want near them. You don't need an Endowment to make a hunter out of that concept. You just need to see monsters as corruption given flesh, dirt and filth that will breed more filth unless it's properly cleaned away.<br /> <br /> Which, incidentally, gives another plausible origin for the Cleansers, if you're willing to consider it. Equating moral and spiritual evil with impurity and corruption is central to Japanese Shinto, and the people who had to work in impure occupations formed a social caste (now called <i>burakumin</i>) who were generally avoided and lived apart from other Japanese. The concept of a group of <i>burakumin</i> monster hunters whose self-concept revolves around purifying physical and spiritual uncleanness shares an obvious affinity with your original idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T01:42:49-07:00","id":1145131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1145004#post1145004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a cool idea could be to have gained their powers from recovered vestiges from the Kingdom. That would tie with the theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's part of the plan for when I rewrite their backstory to link to the Guard. They raided that Alhambran enclave before the split.<br /> <br /> You misunderstand MB. When I said an international conspiracy I used a small 'c'. I was drawing a distinction between groups like the Clensers, who spy on and blackmail politicians, titans of industry, and big-C Hunter Conspiracies, who generally don't. (I should have been explicit).<br /> <br /> Staying one step ahead of Werewolves is possible for a Tier 2 group e.g. the Bear Lodge. You don't need that much resources to do it. But if you're spying on senators you need to stay one step ahead of the NSA, the CIA, maybe even VALKYRIE. I think that's significantly harder and requires way more resources if you don't have a relevent Endowment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1145045#post1145045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which, incidentally, gives another plausible origin for the Cleansers, if you're willing to consider it. Equating moral and spiritual evil with impurity and corruption is central to Japanese Shinto, and the people who had to work in impure occupations formed a social caste (now called <i>burakumin</i>) who were generally avoided and lived apart from other Japanese. The concept of a group of <i>burakumin</i> monster hunters whose self-concept revolves around purifying physical and spiritual uncleanness shares an obvious affinity with your original idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something too fitting not to use. Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm getting ideas already. Their Endowment combines from a Alhambran tomes (this is hunter, it doesn't need to match the Princess setting 100%) &quot;libertated&quot; from an Alhambran enclave but they only managed to unlock it by getting help from the burakumin. This means that Shinto ideas of spiritual/moral purity crop up in their endowment (e.g. the powers to cleanse nests) and it's a big part of the reason why their Endowment looks different from the Guard .<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-29-2017, 04:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T05:49:47-07:00","id":1145182,"title":"","content":"Okay, I will wait to see where this goes, then. Glad we are getting somewhere with this^^<br /> <br /> On a note, I know this probably won't get answers, but I am still looking for fictions to insert in the supplement, so if anyone feels like writing interactions between the Hopeful and Compacts/Conspiracies (be it fighting or collaborating), go crazy.<br /> <br /> Also, unrelated to this, I was curious about one thing, King Raven: does Princess the Hopeful has an official skull symbol?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T05:59:06-07:00","id":1145185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1145182#post1145182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, unrelated to this, I was curious about one thing, King Raven: does Princess the Hopeful has an official skull symbol?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hot pink skull with a flower or tiara on it? \u263a","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T06:05:56-07:00","id":1145189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1145182#post1145182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a note, I know this probably won't get answers, but I am still looking for fictions to insert in the supplement, so if anyone feels like writing interactions between the Hopeful and Compacts/Conspiracies (be it fighting or collaborating), go crazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure about full write-ups, but one scene popped into my head:<br /> <br /> A mixed cell of Hunters finally takes down the Princess that was causing them trouble. She de-Transforms and is revealed to be a teenager. One of the more ruthless ones is going to finish her off when the <i>Ashwood Abbey</i> member