enhorn? I've fought these witches before and let me tell you who else wore a stupid outfit. Superman with his underwear outside his tights. This is not a cakewalk and if you don't shape up you wont be coming home. I've seen skilled veterans empty entire clips and hit nothing but air. I've seen little girls walk of bullets at point blank range. And rookie, you will never ever laugh at a Barbie magic wand once you've seen rainbows melt the flesh off a man's bones. Oh god, I can still smell it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T06:00:27-07:00","id":1147982,"title":"","content":"Love it^^ who knew you could make a wand that shoots rainbows sound horrifying?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T07:15:12-07:00","id":1147997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1147982#post1147982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Love it^^ who knew you could make a wand that shoots rainbows sound horrifying?</div> </div> </div> </div>You've never been subjected to Prismatic Spray, have you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T08:06:56-07:00","id":1148008,"title":"","content":"And I've revised the Sanitation Workers Committee as an offshoot of the People's Guard (new source of the Endowment is looted Alhambran stuff from before the split) <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1t7U_sglV9RXTBc3oU3J-bJFSRVbEAobbFEwyxPrD838/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...yxPrD838/edit#</a><br /> <br /> Also, there's a tactic in Dream Catchers: Checkmate. You might want to copy it. Defence against firearms is standard for combat Princesses.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-08-2017, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T08:49:26-07:00","id":1148022,"title":"","content":"Mhm... I just finished reading. So far, my feelings are mixed. On one hand, I like the integration to the past and the fact that they now have a clear explanation of where their Endowment came from. On the other hand, I don't really see what motivated them into fighting the Darkness or how the Darkness even played a role in their creation. Maybe I read too fast, though. Wouldn't be the first time.<br /> <br /> I do really like their relationship with Princesses, though. It's an interesting dynamic, and definitely lighter than the People's Guard, while still not being blatantly pro-Princess like the Light Company.<br /> <br /> Not sure how I feel about the new name, though. I get the idea, but I don't know if it really works as an actual name...<br /> <br /> Haven't fully read the Endowment yet due to time limitation. I'll check it later.<br /> <br /> As for Checkmate, is it really right to copy it when it already exists in a previous fan-supplement?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 10-08-2017, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T11:20:38-07:00","id":1148064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1148022#post1148022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mhm... I just finished reading. So far, my feelings are mixed. On one hand, I like the integration to the past and the fact that they now have a clear explanation of where their Endowment came from. On the other hand, I don't really see what motivated them into fighting the Darkness or how the Darkness even played a role in their creation. Maybe I read too fast, though. Wouldn't be the first time.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's covered under The Enemy. They don't have a philosophical reason to focus on the Darkness above all, it's just the most consistent threat their membership face.<br /> <br /> I think something could be added based on the burakumin and their ideas of physical&amp;moral cleanliness, but IMO it should be a support to the self-defence angle and not the prime motive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1148022#post1148022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haven't fully read the Endowment yet due to time limitation. I'll check it later.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's mostly rewording things. Removing religious references and being more explicit that these are servant abilities turned up to 11.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1148022#post1148022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Checkmate, is it really right to copy it when it already exists in a previous fan-supplement?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wrote it for Dream Catchers.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T14:46:04-07:00","id":1148127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's mostly rewording things. Removing religious references and being more explicit that these are servant abilities turned up to 11. </div> </div> </div>I would have actually increased that instead of removing but okay.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well I wrote it for Dream Catchers and I suggested it <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but it's already in Dream Catchers, isn't it? Aren't we supposed to bring in only new material?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T15:12:19-07:00","id":1148134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1148127#post1148127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would have actually increased that instead of removing but okay.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sadly I don't know enough Shinto to create a halfway plausible fictional folk-Shinto.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1148127#post1148127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but it's already in Dream Catchers, isn't it? Aren't we supposed to bring in only new material?</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but on the hand it's a really useful Tactic against Princesses.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T15:58:58-07:00","id":1148152,"title":"","content":"Ive been experimenting with shinto last 3 or 4 years, mostly to add religious zeal to my recycling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T10:56:15-07:00","id":1148631,"title":"","content":"Okay, guys, I found an artist of my own and got her start sketches as well. She just finished doing a Dreamland Warden pic... could someone tell me how to put the pic here so everyone can see it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T11:27:17-07:00","id":1148640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1148631#post1148631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, guys, I found an artist of my own and got her start sketches as well. She just finished doing a Dreamland Warden pic... could someone tell me how to put the pic here so everyone can see it?</div> </div> </div> </div>[img]ImageURL[/img]. Optionally inside of [spoiler][/ spoiler] like this: [spoiler][img]ImageURL[/img][/ spoiler] (without the space behind the/), if you don't want it to take up the whole page.<br /> <br /> *Goes back to lurking*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T12:02:23-07:00","id":1148650,"title":"","content":"Thanks. Here we go:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://img00.deviantart.net/5e83/i/2017/283/f/9/img_20171010_0001_by_kayas_kosmos-dbq5kkt.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Hope you guys like it^^ She's still hesitating for the colors, though. Would you prefer disgusting bruised and pale human skin colours, or just blacks and reds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T17:46:26-07:00","id":1148711,"title":"","content":"WOAH UGLY! I thought these things guarded the <i>Dreamlands</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T18:33:47-07:00","id":1148717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1148711#post1148711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WOAH UGLY! I thought these things guarded the <i>Dreamlands</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nightmares are dreams too...<br /> <br /> That said, yeah. I hate to criticize such ghoolishly cool sketches, but I thought the Wardens were more the honey trap that suckered you in by dulling your senses and presenting you with the perfect world. I don't see such masters of deception appearing like this to the Magisters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T18:37:30-07:00","id":1148719,"title":"","content":"speaking of Dreamlanders, does Princess use the 2e or 1e rules for ephemeral beings? cause I only understand the latter. I'm assuming 2e since the book mentions Integrity, but I want to be certain","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T18:37:30-07:00","id":1148720,"title":"","content":"double post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 10-10-2017, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T00:48:13-07:00","id":1148772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nightmares are dreams too...<br /> <br /> That said, yeah. I hate to criticize such ghoolishly cool sketches, but I thought the Wardens were more the honey trap that suckered you in by dulling your senses and presenting you with the perfect world. I don't see such masters of deception appearing like this to the Magisters. </div> </div> </div>Wardens are shapeshifters and illusionists, they can appear as whatever they want, so really there's nothing wrong with their true form being ugly. If anything it <i>adds</i> to the creepyness when you consider they can spend an entire illusion showing up as your loved one, until you finally break through the illusion and realize THIS is what you've been interacting with. Moreover, according to the book they <i>were</i> created by the Darkness, so I wouldn't expect them to look nice in their true form.<br /> <br /> As for the rules regarding Dreamlanders, the book indeed isn't very clear; from my understanding, they use the 2e rules, only they don't have Corpus (they use Willpower instead) and ignore Manifestations while in the Dreamlands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T13:53:55-07:00","id":1149230,"title":"","content":"And here comes the complete Warden pic^^ What do you guys think?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://pre00.deviantart.net/b707/th/pre/i/2017/285/2/5/trapped_in_the_illusion__by_kayas_kosmos-dbqd5q7.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T14:09:50-07:00","id":1149235,"title":"","content":"Looks cool.<br /> <br /> Would the person it is puppeteering be a Princess, or what the Warden is presenting as?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T14:46:11-07:00","id":1149241,"title":"","content":"A Princess^^ How do you like her design? If I remember correct she is supposed to be a Princess of Diamond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T20:37:27-07:00","id":1149299,"title":"","content":"Tell the artist, damn good job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T01:57:46-07:00","id":1149347,"title":"","content":"Amazing artwork.<br /> <br /> To confirm what Darinas said, the inspiration for Wardens is the Other Mother from Coraline - that's why the Warden in their microfiction calls their prisoner &quot;button&quot; - and the Other Mother certainly got creepy looking as her desguise wore away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1148772#post1148772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the rules regarding Dreamlanders, the book indeed isn't very clear; from my understanding, they use the 2e rules, only they don't have Corpus (they use Willpower instead) and ignore Manifestations while in the Dreamlands.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was written before Mage 2E. I should probably revise that to ensure it matches Mage's astral travel, and if nothing else it could be clearer.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T02:12:20-07:00","id":1149348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1148152#post1148152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ive been experimenting with shinto last 3 or 4 years, mostly to add religious zeal to my recycling.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have any suggestions please don't hesitate.<br /> <br /> The doc is here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1t7U_sglV9RXTBc3oU3J-bJFSRVbEAobbFEwyxPrD838/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...yxPrD838/edit#</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T02:14:11-07:00","id":1149349,"title":"","content":"Personally really looking forward to CtL2e to be released with rules for oneiromancy and Dreaming Roads. <br /> Would be fascinating to homebrew Changeling perspective on Dreamland and Princesses, and I already have some ideas bouncing around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":". 10-13-2017, 05:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T04:41:53-07:00","id":1149361,"title":"","content":"Thanks a lot, guys^^ I'll make sure to transmit your compliments to the artist (who, by the way, is the same person who did the skull logo and Princess the Hopeful cover I sent you, King Raven).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That was written before Mage 2E. I should probably revise that to ensure it matches Mage's astral travel, and if nothing else it could be clearer. </div> </div> </div>That would make things much easier, yeah. As much as I love Princess the Hopeful, the whole &quot;Willpower as health in the Dreamlands&quot; things kinda proved troublesome when I tried to apply it in my campaign, as it meant you could &quot;die&quot; much faster (since there is no distinction between the types of damages), recovered much more slowly, and Dreamlanders would have limited Health (since Willpower cannot go above 10 with Ephemeral beings). And that's not even talking about that time I tried to have a Beast enter the Dreamlands. Using Dream Health instead would be much easier to handle, and make sense in the context of the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you have any suggestions please don't hesitate.<br /> <br /> The doc is here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1t7U_sglV9RXTBc3oU3J-bJFSRVbEAobbFEwyxPrD838/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...yxPrD838/edit#</a> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of which, feel free to add it to the main doc. I believe almost everyone feels comfortable with this version by now. Personally I would maybe change their name, but aside from that, I think they are solid and any refinement we will add no longer requires keeping them in a separate doc^^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Personally really looking forward to CtL2e to be released with rules for oneiromancy and Dreaming Roads.<br /> Would be fascinating to homebrew Changeling perspective on Dreamland and Princesses, and I already have some ideas bouncing around. </div> </div> </div>Oh, really? You got me intrigued now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 10-13-2017, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T05:29:53-07:00","id":1149369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1149361#post1149361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I love Princess the Hopeful, the whole &quot;Willpower as health in the Dreamlands&quot; things kinda proved troublesome when I tried to apply it in my campaign, as it meant you could &quot;die&quot; much faster (since there is no distinction between the types of damages), recovered much more slowly, and Dreamlanders would have limited Health (since Willpower cannot go above 10 with Ephemeral beings). And that's not even talking about that time I tried to have a Beast enter the Dreamlands. Using Dream Health instead would be much easier to handle, and make sense in the context of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vocation converted Dreamlanders to Dream Health shortly after Beast came out, for compatibility reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T10:50:40-07:00","id":1149469,"title":"","content":"Looks like Beast and Mage share Dream Health. So that makes things simpler.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1149361#post1149361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks a lot, guys^^ I'll make sure to transmit your compliments to the artist (who, by the way, is the same person who did the skull logo and Princess the Hopeful cover I sent you, King Raven).</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh that was you. Digs through emails... for those who don't know. Darinas is <a href=\"https://kayas-kosmos.deviantart.com/art/CM-WOD-Princess-The-Hopeful-fan-cover-639221505\" target=\"_blank\">referring to this.</a><br /> <br /> It's a great piece, but it feels more fantasy than urban fantasy. More suitable for the Dreamlands chapter than the front cover. I think the front cover needs to look grittier and clearly set in the modern world. Something like <a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/fa/34/1d/fa341d4ffb5685e4dc067f0780e83704.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. The scars really complete the piece.<br /> <br /> I feel bad being critical when it's obvious how much effort went into it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1149361#post1149361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of which, feel free to add it to the main doc. I believe almost everyone feels comfortable with this version by now. Personally I would maybe change their name, but aside from that, I think they are solid and any refinement we will add no longer requires keeping them in a separate doc^^</div> </div> </div> </div>Doing that now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-13-2017, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T12:33:49-07:00","id":1149496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1149469#post1149469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh that was you. Digs through emails... for those who don't know. Darinas is <a href=\"https://kayas-kosmos.deviantart.com/art/CM-WOD-Princess-The-Hopeful-fan-cover-639221505\" target=\"_blank\">referring to this.</a></div> </div> </div> </div><i>Why have I never seen this before?</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1149469#post1149469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a great piece, but it feels more fantasy than urban fantasy. More suitable for the Dreamlands chapter than the front cover. I think the front cover needs to look grittier and clearly set in the modern world. Something like <a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/fa/34/1d/fa341d4ffb5685e4dc067f0780e83704.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. The scars really complete the piece.<br /> <br /> I feel bad being critical when it's obvious how much effort went into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. The official games' covers aren't pictures of actual scenes, modern world or otherwise, but abstract art. The fantasy feel of this piece is a good fit for a game about magical girls, IMO. Grittier pictures like the &quot;Sailor Jupiter in the girders&quot; picture would work well as interior illustrations, especially in contrast to this as the cover, but not for the cover itself.<br /> <br /> I mean, if I'd been designing a cover I'd have done something like a spotlit still life of a crown and sceptre on display, maybe with a few unsettling outlines in shadows behind them - no human figures at all. But I think this is better.<br /> <br /> Darinas, you commissioned this specifically as a cover for Princess: the Hopeful, right? Not just for your personal use? You have the rights to contribute it to the project? Because <i>I</i> want to use it, even if Kings Raven turns up his nose at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T12:34:14-07:00","id":1149497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh that was you. Digs through emails... for those who don't know. Darinas is <a href=\"https://kayas-kosmos.deviantart.com/art/CM-WOD-Princess-The-Hopeful-fan-cover-639221505\" target=\"_blank\">referring to this.</a><br /> <br /> It's a great piece, but it feels more fantasy than urban fantasy. More suitable for the Dreamlands chapter than the front cover. I think the front cover needs to look grittier and clearly set in the modern world. Something like <a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/fa/34/1d/fa341d4ffb5685e4dc067f0780e83704.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. The scars really complete the piece.<br /> <br /> I feel bad being critical when it's obvious how much effort went into it. </div> </div> </div>Thank you for giving an opinion on it^^ I can try to have her do another cover more like what you described, if you wish. Not right now, though. She is unfortunately gonna be busy for a while^^ But I can try later. And don't worry^^ I'm glad you think it's great.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Doing that now <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> </div> </div> </div>Good^^ And since I'm at it, that goes for whoever is working on the new Cold Guard as well (sorry, forgot who was in charge of that). Feel free to add this to the document as well. Any progress made is good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I disagree. The official games' covers aren't pictures of actual scenes, modern world or otherwise, but abstract art. The fantasy feel of this piece is a good fit for a game about magical girls, IMO. Grittier pictures like the &quot;Sailor Jupiter in the girders&quot; picture would work well as interior illustrations, especially in contrast to this as the cover, but not for the cover itself.<br /> <br /> I mean, if I'd been designing a cover I'd have done something like a spotlit still life of a crown and sceptre on display, maybe with a few unsettling outlines in shadows behind them - no human figures at all. But I think this is better.<br /> <br /> Darinas, you commissioned this specifically as a cover for Princess: the Hopeful, right? Not just for your personal use? You have the rights to contribute it to the project? Because <i>I</i> want to use it, even if Kings Raven turns up his nose at it. </div> </div> </div>Thanks^^ and no, I didn't commissionned it for personal use; I just felt it was sad Princess the Hopeful had no illustrations nor fanarts, so I asked my friend to do a fan cover to fix that. And we both agreed we'd be fine with creators of the game using it, so feel free to use it if you wish^^ I would be honored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 10-13-2017, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T13:21:27-07:00","id":1149509,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what your reasoning is MB. Both pieces of art depict a magical girl posed against a location, on a scale of abstract art to actual scenes they're exactly the same. The important thing about a front cover is that it gives a feeling of the contents within, which for princess is gritty. But no matter, you do whatever you like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1149497#post1149497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can try to have her do another cover more like what you described, if you wish. Not right now, though. She is unfortunately gonna be busy for a while^^ But I can try later. And don't worry^^ I'm glad you think it's great.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love it if you did <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> and while i'm on the subject, if she has the origonal source image pre-text I could put it in the dreamlands chapter.<br /> <br /> It might look a bit odd having exactly one piece of art but *shrug* you got to start somewhere.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-13-2017, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T22:51:18-07:00","id":1149858,"title":"","content":"Third art piece finished and up. *Dings bell*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://sta.sh/0k9dln5gha9\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://st.deviantart.net/minish/main/logo/card_black_large.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://sta.sh/0k9dln5gha9\" target=\"_blank\"> DeviantArt: 404 </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://sta.sh/0k9dln5gha9\" target=\"_blank\"> https://sta.sh/0k9dln5gha9 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> DeviantArt is the world's largest online social community for artists and art enthusiasts, allowing people to connect through the creation and sharing of art. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T02:40:39-07:00","id":1149885,"title":"","content":"Looks pretty good^^ I'll add it to the doc as soon as it's in the gallery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T07:27:07-07:00","id":1149914,"title":"","content":"Anyway, just to clarify, so far we have 4 Compacts and 3 Conspiracies. Which leads me to 2 questions:<br /> <br /> 1) Do we add the new Cold Guard, or not? If yes, I'd appreciate that whoever was in charge of developping them add them to the doc.<br /> 2) Do we keep the Star of Bethlehem? Apparently some people we in favour of removing them, though personally I'd rather keep them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T08:37:03-07:00","id":1149933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1149914#post1149914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Do we add the new Cold Guard, or not? If yes, I'd appreciate that whoever was in charge of developping them add them to the doc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm stalled on actually writing anything substantial. I have ideas, but I can't put them to words. If someone wants to handle the fluff and just use the Endowment I wrote, that would be great.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1149914#post1149914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Do we keep the Star of Bethlehem? Apparently some people we in favour of removing them, though personally I'd rather keep them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just don't see any great need for them? The Talbot group and Habibti Ma both cover what they do conceptually, they just are limited by their Splat-focus. It's fine for including them, it is just if they need to get trimmed, they could be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T14:28:55-07:00","id":1150206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm stalled on actually writing anything substantial. I have ideas, but I can't put them to words. If someone wants to handle the fluff and just use the Endowment I wrote, that would be great. </div> </div> </div>I see. Anyone interested in working on it, then?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just don't see any great need for them? The Talbot group and Habibti Ma both cover what they do conceptually, they just are limited by their Splat-focus. It's fine for including them, it is just if they need to get trimmed, they could be. </div> </div> </div>I respectfully disagree. Granted, they are all social groups with no liking of violence, but Habibit Ma deals with Cultists, which does NOT match Princesses, and the Tabolt Group focuses specifically on Werewolves, so they wouldn't deal with Princesses. Plus by this logic, Yuri's Group and Searchlight wouldn't exist either. So yeah, personally I am for keeping them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T16:23:03-07:00","id":1150232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1150206#post1150206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I respectfully disagree. Granted, they are all social groups with no liking of violence, but Habibit Ma deals with Cultists, which does NOT match Princesses, and the Tabolt Group focuses specifically on Werewolves, so they wouldn't deal with Princesses. Plus by this logic, Yuri's Group and Searchlight wouldn't exist either. So yeah, personally I am for keeping them.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's fine. We don't need to trim anything (no word-count limits - yay!), so they are fine.<br /> <br /> Though I could point out that Princesses behavior may seem like cult-ish brainwashing from far enough outside, and the Werewolf focus limiting Talbot is exactly what I was referring to.<br /> <br /> Some more differentiation (on how a member would play) would be nice, but not needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T19:51:40-07:00","id":1150257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1150206#post1150206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. Anyone interested in working on it, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>I may have time. What's the Endowment?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T02:15:09-07:00","id":1150287,"title":"","content":"I think it was something about channeling the Powers of the Darkness as a mean to fight the Darkness itself, so I guess they should have Umbrae/Caligines-like Endowments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T02:33:03-07:00","id":1150291,"title":"","content":"My real issue with the Star of Bethlehem is that anyone who plays them, barring a large change to the setting, is setting their charachter up for outright failure. Their goal is to make war on the Queens, but to invade a nation state, overcome it's armies, and then defeat it's demigod ruler you'd need to be a Tier 4 group. However the theme of concerned parents only works at Tier 1 or 2. So basically, they can't win.<br /> <br /> Maybe that's not a problem for other people, but I've never liked Hunter groups who can't win.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1150257#post1150257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may have time. What's the Endowment?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1150287#post1150287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it was something about channeling the Powers of the Darkness as a mean to fight the Darkness itself, so I guess they should have Umbrae/Caligines-like Endowments.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always liked the idea that the Cold Guard are more about managing the darkness rather than fighting it. The idea that they believe (not without some justification) that this is the &quot;world of darkness&quot;. By cosmic law will always be darkness.<br /> <br /> So rather than try to kill the monsters and wait for them to inevitably be replaced by more monsters somewhere else who'll eat innocents before the Cold Guard find them again. They use their Endowment to trap the monsters, so they always know where they are and it's somewhere far from people.<br /> <br /> Mix this in with a philosophy that they don't try to overcome their darker personality traits, but accept them and put them to good use and you have a foil to Princesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-17-2017, 05:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T03:24:08-07:00","id":1150293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1150291#post1150291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My real issue with the Star of Bethlehem is that anyone who plays them, barring a large change to the setting, is setting their charachter up for outright failure. Their goal is to make war on the Queens, but to invade a nation state, overcome it's armies, and then defeat it's demigod ruler you'd need to be a Tier 4 group. However the theme of concerned parents only works at Tier 1 or 2. So basically, they can't win.<br /> <br /> Maybe that's not a problem for other people, but I've never liked Hunter groups who can't win.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think failure is the expectation with any Hunter that has ambitious end goals. Realistically, none of them has any chance of affecting sweeping change - but they can affect the Here and Now.<br /> <br /> I just think there isn't much range of character types to play that haven't already been covered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1150291#post1150291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always liked the idea that the Cold Guard are more about managing the darkness rather than fighting it. The idea that they believe (not without some justification) that this is the &amp;quot;world of darkness&amp;quot;. By cosmic law will always be darkness.<br /> <br /> So rather than try to kill the monsters and wait for them to inevitably be replaced by more monsters somewhere else who'll eat innocents before the Cold Guard find them again. They use their Endowment to trap the monsters, so they always know where they are and it's somewhere far from people.<br /> <br /> Mix this in with a philosophy that they don't try to overcome their darker personality traits, but accept them and put them to good use and you have a foil to Princesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>You would probably find a mix of either. Yeah long term containment over temporary dispersal is good, but sometimes you need to stop harm now and find a use for it later.<br /> <br /> I can send a list of what I have written on the Endowment so far, once I get to a PC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T08:38:56-07:00","id":1150365,"title":"","content":"After little bit of thinking I realized my Changeling Entitlement could function as Hunter Conspiracy/Compact as well: Knight Order of Circle of Rem, medieval order that dedicated itself to study and defense of dreams. Dreamlanders, Princesses, Beasts, Eidolons (I speculate this is new name of Oneroi), and Gentry's Dream Plagues fall under their zone of interest. Endowments could let them benefit from Changeling dream shaping and dream combat, and bring some of the dream into reality in fight against bodysnatching dreams, Beasts, and &quot;rogue&quot; Radiant Princesses.<br /> <br /> They would most likely have connection to Changeling Entitlement of Family of the Silent Night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T08:52:18-07:00","id":1150367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My real issue with the Star of Bethlehem is that anyone who plays them, barring a large change to the setting, is setting their charachter up for outright failure. Their goal is to make war on the Queens, but to invade a nation state, overcome it's armies, and then defeat it's demigod ruler you'd need to be a Tier 4 group. However the theme of concerned parents only works at Tier 1 or 2. So basically, they can't win.<br /> <br /> Maybe that's not a problem for other people, but I've never liked Hunter groups who can't win. </div> </div> </div>That's their endgoal? I was under the impression it was more something they wanted to do as a potential long-term goal, and their true priority was protecting Princesses from the danger they expose themselves too (which while difficult is a bit more realistic). I mean, that's like saying Searchlight is trying to go on war with Arcadia.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After little bit of thinking I realized my Changeling Entitlement could function as Hunter Conspiracy/Compact as well: Knight Order of Circle of Rem, medieval order that dedicated itself to study and defense of dreams. Dreamlanders, Princesses, Beasts, Eidolons (I speculate this is new name of Oneroi), and Gentry's Dream Plagues fall under their zone of interest. Endowments could let them benefit from Changeling dream shaping and dream combat, and bring some of the dream into reality in fight against bodysnatching dreams, Beasts, and &quot;rogue&quot; Radiant Princesses.<br /> <br /> They would most likely have connection to Changeling Entitlement of Family of the Silent Night. </div> </div> </div>I guess that could make a cool idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T09:17:07-07:00","id":1150376,"title":"","content":"They would be one of the groups who would be distrustful of Princesses but often find themselves fighting on same side. <br /> Their antagonistic attitude towards Radiant stems from their long standing internal disputes whether &quot;Dreamland Phenomenon&quot; should be considered a threat. Now that it suddenly has started to spill over into reality? They are very concerned.<br /> <br /> I think they might have two Endowment lines to present their dual duty: Lucid Deep Dream Dive, that lets them &quot;patrol&quot; dreams and act more efficiently within them, and Cape and Daggers of DayDreams, that let them benefit from some Dream combat features in reality.<br /> <br /> Possible further annoyance for Princess, Rem-nites are suckers for byzantine chivalry and lineage crap and tend to be stupidly public about it (Daggers of DayDreams lets them gloss over some of this stuff).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T21:04:44-07:00","id":1150537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1150291#post1150291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've always liked the idea that the Cold Guard are more about managing the darkness rather than fighting it. The idea that they believe (not without some justification) that this is the &quot;world of darkness&quot;. By cosmic law will always be darkness.<br /> <br /> So rather than try to kill the monsters and wait for them to inevitably be replaced by more monsters somewhere else who'll eat innocents before the Cold Guard find them again. They use their Endowment to trap the monsters, so they always know where they are and it's somewhere far from people.<br /> <br /> Mix this in with a philosophy that they don't try to overcome their darker personality traits, but accept them and put them to good use and you have a foil to Princesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, the wardens of evil. I like that. They're the people who go about putting evils into cans, because they don't think it's possible to kill them (and sometimes, it's the safer and less costly option-a Dethroned will reincarnate if killed, barring some specific circumstances, so they honestly have the smart plan barring a Noble willing to be symbiotically possessed after fighting a posthuman demigod of despair.).<br /> <br /> Once I see the Endowment, I'll see what I can do. Also, idea-their &quot;pseudo-Caliganes&quot; (which I'll call the Malebranches for now, after the demonic guards of Malebolge-the Evil Claws) use their prisoners as a &quot;filter&quot; of sorts to draw on the Dark without being corrupted by it; the self-same act of developing a Malebranche is simultaneously an act of defilement and purification, since it is done by using the entropic aspects of the Dark to make their prisoners suffer for what they have done. They do not expect their prisoners to mend their ways (especially because, as creatures of the Dark, they <i>can't</i>), but on the rare occasions it <i>does </i>happen (because they...aren't creatures of the Dark, say a powerful vampire in semi-permanent torpor or a godlike Amanojaku), it is a time of great celebration, since that both means they can divert resources somewhere else and because they have proven their philosophy-&quot;Only once one knows the darkness of self can one truly find the light.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which also flips their portrayal from unthinking zealots to conflicted, well-intentioned philosophers, but I consider that a benefit, the previous Cold Guard didn't even strike me as love-to-hate scummy like the Magisters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 10-18-2017, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T23:25:40-07:00","id":1150551,"title":"","content":"Thank you, Leliel. I can't wait.<br /> <br /> Though speaking of the evolution regarding the Cold Guard, I would like to remind you all the People's Guard STILL has an entire section empty-- namely the &quot;The Enemy&quot;, &quot;Hunters&quot;, &quot;Factions&quot; and &quot;Status&quot; parts. Someone actually filling these would be appreciated. Writing down something with their Endowment would be appreciated as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T00:51:42-07:00","id":1150565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1150537#post1150537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, the wardens of evil. I like that. They're the people who go about putting evils into cans, because they don't think it's possible to kill them (and sometimes, it's the safer and less costly option-a Dethroned will reincarnate if killed, barring some specific circumstances, so they honestly have the smart plan barring a Noble willing to be symbiotically possessed after fighting a posthuman demigod of despair.).</div> </div> </div> </div> Just a minor point. Dethroned are pretty rare and when they are around they're more likely to sit around in a pit of self-loathing than actively do evil. The worldwide reach of a Conspiracy means the Cold Guard are bound to met at least one. What I'm saying is, I'd suggest making sure that they don't rely entirely on the Dethroned for proof of their philosophy but also talk about regular Darkspawn and why they believe imprisoning them is better than killing them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1150537#post1150537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They do not expect their prisoners to mend their ways (especially because, as creatures of the Dark, they <i>can't</i>), but on the rare occasions it <i>does </i>happen (because they...aren't creatures of the Dark, say a powerful vampire in semi-permanent torpor or a godlike Amanojaku), it is a time of great celebration, since that both means they can divert resources somewhere else and because they have proven their philosophy-&quot;Only once one knows the darkness of self can one truly find the light.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> What happens if the prisoner is merely a Darkened? Presumably as a Conspiracy focused on the Darkness they can tell the difference between a Darkened and more perment cases of corruption?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T03:15:41-07:00","id":1150588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1150565#post1150565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Just a minor point. Dethroned are pretty rare and when they are around they're more likely to sit around in a pit of self-loathing than actively do evil. The worldwide reach of a Conspiracy means the Cold Guard are bound to met at least one. What I'm saying is, I'd suggest making sure that they don't rely entirely on the Dethroned for proof of their philosophy but also talk about regular Darkspawn and why they believe imprisoning them is better than killing them.<br /> <br /> What happens if the prisoner is merely a Darkened? Presumably as a Conspiracy focused on the Darkness they can tell the difference between a Darkened and more perment cases of corruption?</div> </div> </div> </div>Heck, they may even recruit a few. Baring intentions and their Endowment that let them get away with it, there was little surface difference between them.<br /> <br /> Though from solely the Hunter-book perspective, since Darkened and Mnemosyne are both Infiltrators, as far as other Hunters (and the book) are concerned, they actually have Infiltrators in their ranks as accepted members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 10-18-2017, 06:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T05:48:05-07:00","id":1150614,"title":"","content":"Well, if they use the Darkness, it'd make sense they know more about it than most hunters.<br /> <br /> You know, I am getting a Grey Warden vibe from these guys (for those familiar with Dragon Age). And I love it^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T07:51:58-07:00","id":1150641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1150565#post1150565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Just a minor point. Dethroned are pretty rare and when they are around they're more likely to sit around in a pit of self-loathing than actively do evil. The worldwide reach of a Conspiracy means the Cold Guard are bound to met at least one. What I'm saying is, I'd suggest making sure that they don't rely entirely on the Dethroned for proof of their philosophy but also talk about regular Darkspawn and why they believe imprisoning them is better than killing them.<br /> <br /> What happens if the prisoner is merely a Darkened? Presumably as a Conspiracy focused on the Darkness they can tell the difference between a Darkened and more perment cases of corruption?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Good point. My mind honestly slipped a gear there and forgot they like to cocoon themselves away. Still, I have the answer for Cataphractoi, at least: They believe the &quot;Court of the Black&quot; is actually a genus of immortal spirits that replace the souls of the newborn Infiltrator-killing one just banishes the Courtier, which is a temporary solution at best. Sooner or later, it will find a new host. The only real solution is to turn their armor into their cell and seal them in human form.<br /> <br /> 2) One would have to be very, very alien in form before they sent a Darkened to the permanent prisons (I have them making specialized seal talismans and the like, they're fans of underground, heavily warded catacombs under the working title of Bolgias), but they know containment and isolation from the opportunity to perform evil or be traumatized halts the corruption, and gives them a chance to &quot;vitrify&quot; it (ie, halt the decay permanently through full purification or successful initiation into the Guard). Permanent prisoners are those the [Commanders] feel are lost causes and/or too dangerous for a loose leash.<br /> <br /> Basically, I'm looking at the Cold Guard as the people who put evil in cans of some shape or another that often end up being unleashed later for whatever reason (with the caveat that they are actually really good at can design and maintenance).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T10:20:15-07:00","id":1150683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1150641#post1150641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) Good point. My mind honestly slipped a gear there and forgot they like to cocoon themselves away. Still, I have the answer for Cataphractoi, at least: They believe the &quot;Court of the Black&quot; is actually a genus of immortal spirits that replace the souls of the newborn Infiltrator-killing one just banishes the Courtier, which is a temporary solution at best. Sooner or later, it will find a new host. The only real solution is to turn their armor into their cell and seal them in human form.<br /> <br /> 2) One would have to be very, very alien in form before they sent a Darkened to the permanent prisons (I have them making specialized seal talismans and the like, they're fans of underground, heavily warded catacombs under the working title of Bolgias), but they know containment and isolation from the opportunity to perform evil or be traumatized halts the corruption, and gives them a chance to &quot;vitrify&quot; it (ie, halt the decay permanently through full purification or successful initiation into the Guard). Permanent prisoners are those the [Commanders] feel are lost causes and/or too dangerous for a loose leash.<br /> <br /> Basically, I'm looking at the Cold Guard as the people who put evil in cans of some shape or another that often end up being unleashed later for whatever reason (with the caveat that they are actually really good at can design and maintenance).</div> </div> </div> </div>Liking it so far.<br /> <br /> Did you get to Bleak Oubilette yet? It can easily be modified to be based/focused on a seal (like the Focus of a Nest, but a lock to the Focus's anchor).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 10-18-2017, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T10:28:54-07:00","id":1150690,"title":"","content":"One nice thing about Bleak Oubilette (basically requiring a Nest as a foundation for their prisons) is that has a built in moral dilemma:<br /> <br /> Do we kidnap some innocents and kill them in a purpose built bunker in the Australian Outback to create an inescapable prison surrounded by a vast desert. Or do we just acquire that serial killer's cabin in the woods which means <i>we</i> don't have to do anything evil but it's in walking distance from a town.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1150641#post1150641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but they know containment and isolation from the opportunity to perform evil or be traumatized halts the corruption, and gives them a chance to &quot;vitrify&quot; it (ie, halt the decay permanently through full purification or successful initiation into the Guard).</div> </div> </div> </div>How they pitch membership to former victims and train them in the Endowment is definitely an area where any weird parts of their philosophy, and the obligatory moral greyness of a Conspiracy, could get a chance to shine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T10:45:03-07:00","id":1150696,"title":"","content":"I admit I like these ideas more and more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T11:10:28-07:00","id":1150707,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://MTG.gamepedia.com/The_Helvault\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;What cannot be destroyed, must be bound.&quot;</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T14:31:18-07:00","id":1150781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1150690#post1150690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One nice thing about Bleak Oubilette (basically requiring a Nest as a foundation for their prisons) is that has a built in moral dilemma:<br /> <br /> Do we kidnap some innocents and kill them in a purpose built bunker in the Australian Outback to create an inescapable prison surrounded by a vast desert. Or do we just acquire that serial killer's cabin in the woods which means <i>we</i> don't have to do anything evil but it's in walking distance from a town.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good call. I'll be sure to remember that, when I'm making the write-up. Right now, I'm using the lull in homework to do some obligations to my co-author on a fanfic. Also because we plan to do a CofD crossover soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T22:26:40-07:00","id":1151866,"title":"","content":"Okay, lemme start with the beginnings of backstory:<br /> <br /> <b>The Cold Guard </b>(The Tenebrous Gaol)<br /> <br /> <i>Through shadow and day, through pain and empty promises, I will not falter. I am the line, and I will hold.</i><br /> <br /> Once there was a Kingdom. More accurately, there were several Kingdoms, each who loved the Light. One saw Light in searing brightness of knowledge, another in the warm glow of a hearth, a third in the clarion call of destiny, among others. Together, they sealed away the Dark of the Void, a hungry, empty nothing that wished to devour all that was, or ruin it so that all others may share its pain.<br /> <br /> This is not their story. This is the story of what lay between the borders of the Kingdom, the wild lands where Light did not shine. There, away from the insular civilizations that denied them, lay the Dark, eternally mustering for the moment the borders would falter and they would destroy the hideous brightness that drove it away in shame of what it was. And it was there that the Cold Guard lived, watching the Dark to ensure it never had the chance-not because the borders could not falter, but because the Dark would not be free to do so. <br /> <br /> The Cold Guard does not keep a long history of its founding-part of that is due to their incredible age, but mostly it's because the space their dedicate to their records are mostly rolls of various prisoners and the locations of the Bolgia curse-pits they keep them in over the eons, and the security measures they must take to prevent escape or release, with a significant portion of the remainder dedicated to medical procedures and meditative techniques they use to ensure their own Endowment does not devour them. But they do have a myth; the Cold Guard was founded by an alliance of the subordinate nations of the Kingdom as an exiled force of wardens and prison keepers, meant to contain those aspects and children of the Dark too powerful to defeat without great loss of life. Ancient monster-gods of sorrow and rage, powerful demons born from the unholy union of black magic and corrupt human flesh, but above all else was the Hollow Court, a reflection of the very rulers of the Kingdom itself. <br /> <br /> Modern Guards like to use the analogy of a vacuum-whenever a Noble Blossoms, the Light that gives them power is taken out of the world, and the gap tries to fill itself with existence. Because the Light is at least partially intelligent, so is the vacuum, and it seeks its own embodiments to give power to, equal and opposite; whereas the Nobility seems concerned with bringing hope, the unfortunates possessed by the Hollow become embodiments of existential despair, semi-living monsters brimming with hunger for what they were and seeking to spread the Dark as far as possible to strip the world of the Light they need to feed their insatiable emptiness. Only the Light being returned to them, however, can sate them, and until then they would rampage eternally until the host was given a merciful end and the Hollow returned to the Dark World. Except then, of course, the Hollow is still free to seek another host and become an even greater menace than before. Thus, the Cold Guard, exiled from the Kingdom to not only track the Court, but to imprison them within their own stolen bodies within great prison complexes so that they would trouble the world no more, until it was finally time for their corresponding Noble to pass on to the next life and fill the void.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the Nobility, however heroic they might seem, are human. And humans fear death, to the point where comparing their own life to that of the world, some will chose their life.<br /> <br /> The Cold Guard has many theories, each more vehement then the last, about who betrayed the mission of the Guard and humanity itself to save themselves. Generally, however, the gist is that some individuals chose to invert the relationship between Light and Noble, choosing to become magic rather than filtering it into the world. How varies on the particular (from enclosing themselves in great cocoons, fleeing to the &quot;world beyond sleep&quot;, or to consume their own bodies to power a self-sustaining spell with their minds for hearts), but what is known is that this stole even more Light than their allotted share, and their Hollows became as gods from the newfound emptiness. Even worse, lesser Hollows could be sustained by the all-consuming emptiness of the Hunger Kings, even beyond the deaths of their Nobles. Soon, all that was left of the Kingdom were its exiles-the Guard included.<br /> <br /> In the confusion, hundreds of prisoners escaped, some of which menace the world to this day. Worse, the Traitors had learned to donate their bloated Light to fools and madwomen who stole more Light to support their corrupt lieges for eternity, to haphazardly burn out the Dark in some parody of controlling the consequences of their selfishness, or indulge in childish, parodic passion plays of the ancient nations. None accepted the Cold Guard the few times they presented themselves and asked for help to resume their duties, and in many cases the Guard was even attacked due to suspicion of contamination by their own prisoners. <br /> <br /> But the Cold Guard did not learn how to contain evil by being unimaginative. In this new world, they noticed, there was no small amount of magic that did not draw from Light or Dark-not directly. This was in complete contradiction to how they were taught in the days of the Kingdom, and so, the Guard developed a theory that the rift torn by the Hunter Kings had corrupted the Dark itself; no longer was it simply a disincarnate force of consumption, but it had turned to the primal, fertile proto-energy of the dark Void that existed before time, when Light and Darkness had not become disparate. These new powers were atavisms to that time, neither good nor evil, inherently creative or destructive. The most easily available magic, however, was still the Dark, seeing as how most of it was still pure-and thus, pure evil. But, just as the Empty Kings corrupted it from pure malevolence to amoral power, could not the Cold Guard do the same by understanding-and <i>controlling</i>-the parts of them most like the Kings?<br /> <br /> And so the Tenebrous Gaol learned to turn the Dark upon itself, and transform its own Shadows into its bars, a hell of its own making.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T02:45:30-07:00","id":1151886,"title":"","content":"Pretty good. A few spelling/grammar issues to iron out, but very flavorful.<br /> <br /> If the Guard had a function in the ancient Kingdom(s), how does Alhambra (which dates back to then) treat them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T03:12:38-07:00","id":1151890,"title":"","content":"Like it so far. Good foil to Princesses, interesting ideas, and kinda reminds me of the Aegis Kai Doru. Keep up the good work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T18:00:34-07:00","id":1152078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1151886#post1151886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty good. A few spelling/grammar issues to iron out, but very flavorful.<br /> <br /> If the Guard had a function in the ancient Kingdom(s), how does Alhambra (which dates back to then) treat them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Guard hates Alhambra, because to them, Tears is replicating their mythical Original Sin, for the same motive, every time they drill for lamp oil. They have a shoot-on-sight order for Princesses of Tears, and that has led to them being referred to in Alhambra as having been corrupted by the Dark, driven mad by the Queen &quot;needing&quot; to abandon them. To Alhambra, they are rebels from the Provinces who are aware they are rebels, and willingly spurn the Light out of hatred for its perfect user.<br /> <br /> Naturally, this view would make them even angrier if they knew it, because they don't hate the Light at all. They regard themselves as martyrs trying to stabilize the balance between it and the Dark, while Tears is a parasite who ruins it not because it is her nature, but because she <i>wants </i>to. In many ways, they're what Alhambra could have been if it wasn't so self-centered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T07:46:29-07:00","id":1152198,"title":"","content":"So just warning, I moved all the new Conspiracy Endowments to the New Endowments section rather than right after their respective conspiracies. I thought it'd be easier for everyone.<br /> <br /> I also take the opportunity to 1) Thank Leliel on his progress on the New Cold Guard, and 2) Remind everyone the People's Guard also still has some stuff missing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T08:39:15-07:00","id":1152208,"title":"","content":"So... what about something dealing heavily with the topic of reincarnation? It's a minor footnote even in Princess, but sets the backstory as all (well at least most) Nobles are the reincarnations of previous beings.<br /> <br /> A conspiracy or compact that hypothetically deals with reincarnation maybe? A disdain and a desire to &quot;end the cycle&quot;, perhaps guided by Hindu beliefs of history following a wheel of ages that perpetuates ad infinitum? If a Conspiracy, perhaps hypocritically, they use reincarnation themselves, though justify it as being being not &quot;real&quot; reincarnation. Maybe a form of duping or cloning. It would make a whole lot more sense and fit more within the context of Princess than previous suggestions I made.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, I'd just to say I think the Magisters are probably... unhealthy. Lots of abuse there. Are they supposed to be an entire conspiracy made up of Disney villians who prey on Royalty? I am not really saying that's bad, but I for some reason keep thinking of Jaffar and the Queen from Snow White.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T09:25:59-07:00","id":1152214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyways, I'd just to say I think the Magisters are probably... unhealthy. Lots of abuse there. Are they supposed to be an entire conspiracy made up of Disney villians who prey on Royalty? I am not really saying that's bad, but I for some reason keep thinking of Jaffar and the Queen from Snow White. </div> </div> </div>Well, they were designed with the idea of playing as Lex Luthor or David Xanathos, sooo.... yeah, they ARE meant to be villainous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T11:42:07-07:00","id":1152248,"title":"","content":"While not being villainously stupid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T03:35:22-07:00","id":1152450,"title":"","content":"If you think about it. Disney's Jaffar is a highly intelligent political schemer and statesman who has the apparatus of state twisted around his thumb while technically being a mere servant and successfully gained near godlike powers. I get the feeling that <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z7YbpeIvQSw\" target=\"_blank\">Jaffar was less interested in power and more in getting revenge for a lifetime of indignities and being overlooked</a>. The sultan is a nice person, but he seems like he'd be a horribly annoying boss who ignores your advice and then blames you for it &quot;excellent judge of charachter&quot; indeed. Put Jaffar in the modern world with public education and opportunities other than sucking up to royalty for the lower classes I imagine he'd be happy as a very highly paid &amp; respected professional like a lawyer in some technical field like mergers and acquisitions where the MBAs do what he tells them and pay fat sacks of cash for the privilege of doing so.<br /> <br /> In short, the difference between Jaffar and Xanatos is how seriously they're portrayed. Drop the kid-appeal comedy humiliations like having the door slamed on him, remember that he actually succeeded in his evil plot and became both Sultan and the most powerful sorcerer in the world, and Jaffar is as much of a threat as Xanatos or Luther.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-24-2017, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T12:22:14-07:00","id":1152586,"title":"","content":"Huh, new Hunter playtest rules. If Code stays as is, it will clash rather badly with some fan-Conspiracy concepts. I know it clashes with original pitch for mine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T14:16:17-07:00","id":1152611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1152586#post1152586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, new Hunter playtest rules. If Code stays as is, it will clash rather badly with some fan-Conspiracy concepts. I know it clashes with original pitch for mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Code stays as is, it is the first thing I am ditching/house-ruling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T06:41:15-07:00","id":1153461,"title":"","content":"@Leliel: For Factions, what about Wardens (keeps guard over the prisons), Rangers (hunts down monsters to throw into their &quot;jails&quot;), and a scribe or recruiter group?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T12:10:38-07:00","id":1153550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1153461#post1153461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Leliel: For Factions, what about Wardens (keeps guard over the prisons), Rangers (hunts down monsters to throw into their &amp;quot;jails&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, and a scribe or recruiter group?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good.<br /> <br /> Though probably slow, school comes first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T16:35:16-07:00","id":1154013,"title":"","content":"Hate to repeat myself, but the People's Guard still have an entire part of its sections empty. I'd rather not be forced to remove them entirely solely because they are incomplete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T17:25:09-07:00","id":1154020,"title":"","content":"Courtesy of google translate: &quot;L'avant-garde populaire&quot; as a potential alternative name?<br /> <br /> Hunters:<br /> -A hard-core revolutionary, eager to strike at the ruling class no matter what form they take. Maybe subject to oppression in one of the current despotic regimes.<br /> -A more mild-mannered anarchist, possible social worker,or hacker.<br /> -Someone who wasn't really gung-ho with the cause at first, just seeing them as allies, but proceeding to take up the fight more and more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 10-29-2017, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T17:44:35-07:00","id":1154025,"title":"","content":"I kinda like the idea of giving them a french word like Les Myst\u00e8res^^ Not sure about l'Avant-Guard Populaire, but being french, I would find it comfortable to find a name. I am almost tempted to call them &quot;les Insoumis&quot;, but that would be petty of me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (for those who don't know, that's the name of an extreme left-wing party in France. For those who kept track of recent political events in my country, Melenchon is their leader).<br /> <br /> As for the hunters, I approve^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T22:08:07-07:00","id":1154058,"title":"","content":"A few suggestions (please forgive me if these are a little bastardized.):<ul><li>Les Populistes (the Populists): The word &quot;populist&quot; may be too much of a political connotation, but given the themes of Princess, that might be a plus.</li> <li>La Garde Populiste (The Populist Guard): Keeps the &quot;guard&quot; part of the name, and is close to &quot;the people's guard.&quot;</li> <li>Les Incorrompus (The Uncorrupted): Might be good as a name if they choose to defy the idea of their use of darkness corrupting them.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T05:12:25-07:00","id":1154091,"title":"","content":"Nope, you got all three right^^'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T05:34:57-07:00","id":1154099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1154025#post1154025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda like the idea of giving them a french word like Les Myst\u00e8res^^ Not sure about l'Avant-Guard Populaire, but being french, I would find it comfortable to find a name. I am almost tempted to call them &quot;les Insoumis&quot;, but that would be petty of me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (for those who don't know, that's the name of an extreme left-wing party in France. For those who kept track of recent political events in my country, Melenchon is their leader).<br /> <br /> As for the hunters, I approve^^</div> </div> </div> </div>I know you're joking, but unless I misunderstand them, they could have some libertarians on their staff too","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T05:35:58-07:00","id":1154101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1154058#post1154058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Les Incorrompus (The Uncorrupted): Might be good as a name if they choose to defy the idea of their use of darkness corrupting them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought they were a separate group from the Cold Guard now?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T09:14:40-07:00","id":1154734,"title":"","content":"Yes, they are.<br /> <br /> Also, after talking with Raven, he confirmed me the Stormwracked were intended to be hunter, so I added small rules to play them as a Hunter compact. Feel free to check them and judge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T22:10:43-07:00","id":1155948,"title":"","content":"Okay, here are the factions (called Postings) of the Cold Guard. For the Clerks, their thing is that they rely a bit much on precedence and what the Guard already knows to make judgements-good for stability, not so good for speedy decisions or adapting:<br /> <br /> <b>Bondsmen: </b>To inter a prisoner, they must be captured. This is the duty of the Bondsmen, the most traditional hunters of the Cold Guard. In truth, their name is something of a relic to a time before the Queens betrayed them; in the days of the Kingdom, the Bondsmen gave up the safety of civilization out of loyalty to their Nobles, and so were entrusted as their most devoted servants. Now the name is something of a pun-they are both the ones who forge bonds, and when the other Postings fail in keeping their prisoners, it is they who retrieve the escapees. This duty is perhaps the most dangerous, with great bounties and acclaim being offered to those who succeed. After all, the escapees know what's coming for them. Specialty: Athletics (Foot Chase).<br /> <br /> <b>Overseers: </b>The Tenebrous Gaol needs a gaol, it's kind of hinted at by the nickname. And wherever there is a Malebolge, there are guards to keep it. The Overseers are those guards, both from prisoners escaping and from fools who would see them set free. While the Guard isn't numerous enough to post an Overseer to every site where they keep a monster or Dark place sealed, they maintain regular patrols and are the designers of the wards by which the Dark is kept in. In many ways, the Overseers are also the research wing, as it is from their cells that new purified distillations of Dark energies are derived; in seeking lore of the Dark and Malebranches, one could do worse than peruse the writings of the Overseers. Specialty: Occult (Darkness).<br /> <br /> <b>Clerks: </b>Perhaps once, they were attached to an actual justice system, but that was part of the damage the Betrayal did to the fabric of the world. Today, the Cold Guard's Clerks are a combination scribe and psychologist, serving as both the collectors of information needed to pursue their mission, and monitors of their fellows' well-being as part of a broad interpretation of their writ to monitor the internal affairs of the other Postings. It is by the Clerks that the Guard keeps track of its many Malebolges and ensures they are not forgotten in the confusion and secrecy, and it is they who judge whether an edge case is deserving of being locked away in the pits. It's also they alone who possess the right of pardon-if a monster is judged to have sufficiently reformed, then the Clerks have the privilege to order a precautionary release for the sake of neutralizing a greater evil. Specialty: Academics (Cold Guard Convict Lore)<br /> <br /> [Art: A grave-looking man of indeterminate ethnicity is walking by a cell in a prison guard uniform, hitting the bars with a nightstick. Tentacles and claws are reaching out towards him.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T03:17:48-08:00","id":1155990,"title":"","content":"All work for me^^ I validate them.<br /> <br /> Also thanks for confirming there are still progress being made here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T17:31:56-08:00","id":1156523,"title":"","content":"Hey, they set up a PtH Discord so if you want to hang out or talk with people, feel free.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/pc7ZzJt\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/pc7ZzJt\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/pc7ZzJt\" target=\"_blank\"> https://discord.gg/pc7ZzJt </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5387-peteman","name":"Peteman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T00:25:59-08:00","id":1156602,"title":"","content":"Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Just joined.<br /> <br /> And since I am at it, any progress on the Cold Guard or any other material?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 11-10-2017, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T15:57:25-08:00","id":1156820,"title":"","content":"Okay, I started completing the People's Guard section a bit. Feel free to add stuff of your own, or improve/correct what I wrote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T06:27:30-08:00","id":1157513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1156602#post1156602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Just jointed.<br /> <br /> And since I am at it, any progress on the Cold Guard or any other material?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a good idea of what I want with the enemy section. I want to say the Cold Guard does not hate most of its prey. They recognize the Dark is a cancer, but it isn't the cancers fault it wants to kill you, it's just how it is. Properly balanced, it is a part of the world and the source of much...well, not good, but morally neutral power. <br /> <br /> Of course, the Nests cannot be balanced, because the people whose jobs that was abandoned it to protect their own lives. They can work with Nobles, but they have long memories, and beyond the Betrayal the Cold Guard has been used, backstabbed, and repeatedly abandoned all over again when it became convenient for the Twilight Courts (especially Tears, who is the most prone to accept the Malebranches and the most likely to view the Guard as disposable pawns due to they being lower priority than Alhambra). To get them to trust a Noble instead of just kill them to fill a Hollow, one has to atone for, or prove innocence in, a library of crimes the Guard has on file.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T06:39:51-08:00","id":1157515,"title":"","content":"I like it so far^^<br /> <br /> As for me, trying to write down a The Enemy section for the People's Guard, but I am struggling so far. Here's what I've been able to do until now:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Aside from possibly Task Force VALKYRIE, the People\u2019s Guard might well be the most hostile Hunter organization toward Princesses. Most Compacts and Conspiracies don\u2019t necessarily trust or work with Princesses, but they at least feel uncomfortable openly using lethal force against them. But the Egalitarians have nothing but disdain for these so-called Nobles, and do not think twice before using lethal force against them. To them, each kind of Noble represent a facet of the old aristocracy they rose to fight. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Weeping are elitism and oppression, trying to dominate the people and drain their will to live for their own end; </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Selfish, meanwhile, are vanity and arrogance, convinced of their own superiority from birth.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Wrathful are the violent knights from medieval times, the ones who go on pointless crusades against a random enemy as an excuse to slaughter innocents in their blood thirst.</span></span><br /> <br /> Still not sure what to make them think in details about the Radiant Nobles. Anyone feels like helping me out here ?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, for Lelial, someone made a doc for his take on the Cold Guard, if you want to work with him:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OkCR9ZANKOqQ8dDA7EC7-O0YEg7hQbh39ExECi7cKdk/edit\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OkCR9ZANKOqQ8dDA7EC7-O0YEg7hQbh39ExECi7cKdk/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OkCR9ZANKOqQ8dDA7EC7-O0YEg7hQbh39ExECi7cKdk/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OkCR9ZANKOqQ8dDA7EC7-O0YEg7hQbh39ExECi7cKdk/edit </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 11-10-2017, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T04:41:05-08:00","id":1157906,"title":"","content":"Final pic up!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://erinptah.deviantart.com/art/Commission-Shopkeepers-and-Swords-714478757\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://images-wixmp-ed30a86b8c4ca887773594c2.wixmp.com/f/8fabbc7c-436b-4716-94c9-1a42d5d879d2/dbtdrc5-bfc51ca3-7464-47f6-90ae-684c6b77244b.png/v1/fill/w_600,h_650,q_80,strp/commission_shopkeepers_and_swords_by_erinptah_dbtdrc5-fullview.jpg?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..ysi8WRF3YcKCgQTRKkA17yeFuJs3wsybWRptSwQMgrc\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://erinptah.deviantart.com/art/Commission-Shopkeepers-and-Swords-714478757\" target=\"_blank\"> Commission - Shopkeepers and Swords by ErinPtah on DeviantArt </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://erinptah.deviantart.com/art/Commission-Shopkeepers-and-Swords-714478757\" target=\"_blank\"> https://erinptah.deviantart.com/art/Commission-Shopkeepers-and-Swords-714478757 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Commission - Shopkeepers and Swords &mdash; artwork by ErinPtah on DeviantArt. Published: 2017-11-11 &middot; Likes: 17 &middot; Views: 1327 &middot; Comments: 1 &middot; Tags: commission, sailormoon, princessthehopeful </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T06:45:03-08:00","id":1157923,"title":"","content":"Okay I REALLY like this one. Added it to the supplement.<br /> <br /> Also, completed the Enemy section for the People's Guard with a help from someone. An opinion, please? Here it is:<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The hostility of the People\u2019s Guard against Princesses surprises all but the most militant Hunter organizations.. Most Compacts and Conspiracies don\u2019t necessarily trust or work with Princesses, but they at least feel uncomfortable openly using lethal force against them. But the Egalitarians have nothing but disdain for these so-called Nobles, and do not think twice before using lethal force against them. To them, each kind of Noble represent a facet of the old aristocracy they rose to fight. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Weeping are elitism and oppression, trying to dominate the people and drain their will to live for their own end.The Selfish are vanity and arrogance, convinced of their own superiority from birth. The Wrathful are the violent knights from medieval times, the ones who go on pointless crusades against a random enemy as an excuse to slaughter innocents in their blood thirst.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As for the younger ones, these so-called \u201cgood\u201d Nobles? They may consider themselves a well-meaning aristocracy, but they still consider themselves aristocracy, taught by detached and presumptuous \u201cQueens\u201d, and they have the power and the privilege to impose their views of a better world on the people. The People\u2019s Guard will never allow humanity to submit to such would-be monarchs.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Of course, this struggle against oppression doesn\u2019t limit itself to Nobles, though they are by far the primary target. The People\u2019s Guard has no particular qualm against being supernatural, but their hatred burns for anyone who sees themselves as meant to rule over those they see as beneath them. If magic won\u2019t keep the People\u2019s Guard from warring against the Nobility, neither will it prevent the People\u2019s Guard from striking at Vampires, Beasts, or any others who have turned into tyrants.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Needless to say, you don\u2019t stay in the Vigil that long without learning about the creatures of the Darkness, especially when you focus on fighting Princesses. The Egalitarians have a very specific modus operanti when it comes to these; they fight Spawns out of necessity, but usually restrain from immediately destroying Nests, for they realized such places acted as perfect honey traps for the Hopeful. As such, they typically leave agents patrolling around the Nests, taking down any Noble coming to deal with the Nest; once they stop coming, the Guard destroy their trap and move on.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T17:46:17-08:00","id":1162292,"title":"","content":"(finally a moment to myself. Have the beginnings of the Enemy section!)<br /> <br /> <b>The Enemy</b><br /> <br /> Let's be clear: The Guard does not hate the target it was meant to contain.<br /> <br /> That may sound odd, but let's reiterate: <i>the Cold Guard does not hate the Dark.</i> Fear it, despise its effects, and loathe the fools who drink of its unfiltered power and so become monsters...but they don't hate the Dark itself. Hating the Dark is like hating death; pointless, and often leads one down the path that ends with one becoming its embodiment. Fear the Dark, but recognize it is a part of nature, one that seeks to imbalance nature and create the unnatural by its very existence, but a &quot;natural&quot; humanity would still be a desperate prey animal, not even organized enough to form proper tribes of hunter-gatherers; no tools, no fire, no hope. In practice, this byline isn't as followed as strictly as it is said to be (most of the Tenebrous Gaol came to their grim profession out of lethal encounters with the Dark), but it informs everything they do. They do not hunt, they quarantine. They do not kill, they capture. They do not purge, they filter. In that last case, frequently the difference is purely semantic, but it all ties into their cosmological view of the world. To them, the Dark is a force of chaos and change, frequently entropic, but also the ultimate source of &quot;low magic&quot; (low as in lowly, aka <i>humble</i>); it asks nothing, it repays what you sacrifice, and it leads to the weak becoming the strong. Of course, in its excessive state is seeks to devour that which is associated with the Light-kindness, order, happiness, but in its balanced state it accepts less cruel sacrifices than your soul. The gifts it gives are also less vicious (and frequently less directly powerful-you get what you pay for) in balance. Malebranches aren't <i>quite </i>born from balance, and in time, the Cold Guard accepts, the cancerous part of the Dark will inevitably devour their lives-but that is the point. A successful initiation and Decathexis rite is all about sacrificing the darkest potential of the Empty Court and the belief you, personally, will live forever to the Dark, taming the corruption in your soul and making its hungers a tool of virtue. From the moment she first manifests the Wicked Claws, a Cold Guard has in some sense won; she will never be consumed in total by the Dark and made a body of the Court or one of their Viziers (the same cannot be said of her body, but her soul is safe).<br /> <br /> The same cannot be said of the hypocrites that made true balance nigh-impossible and stole the Light. The Cold Guard <i>hates </i>the Nobility, and for all of their recorded history they keep on accumulating new justifications for their vitriol.<br /> <br /> (Not nearly complete yet).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T17:55:29-08:00","id":1162296,"title":"","content":"Aaaaah, finally, a new post. I was worried this thread was dying down. You know, I'm considering removing the People's Guard now. Every time I ask for an opinion or help about it, nobody answers. Maybe the group isn't very well-liked.<br /> <br /> Anyway that's a nice beginning, Lelial. But I'd suggest really trying to coordinate with Mp12, because so far we'll end up with two completely different versions of the group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T17:57:42-08:00","id":1162298,"title":"","content":"Okay. I honestly did not see that.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I like. I have a few things to suggest as well, especially a particular power that is both a source of their strength and their worst trait:<br /> <br /> <b>Consult the Forgotten Martyrs</b>:<br /> <br /> The (Guard/Pact) knows that reincarnation exists. Those who pass on, and do not leave ghosts behind, are washed free of memories and reborn. Supposedly, only the Light allows viewing of one's own past selves-and that's true. That's nature. The Dark, of course, is all about the unnatural-by bringing its power against the nature of the kharmic wheel itself, the hunter is able to ask the discarded memories of her predecessors for advice in saving their current lives.<br /> <br /> (system isn't there as of yet, but the idea is that someone with this has a set of bonus to access in mental and social challenges, and a way to ask about old Bleak Oubliettes and monster lore than a particular hunter of the Conspiracy knew, but it only works on people who are dead, not active as ghosts in any realm-the Underworld has claimed more memories than they like to think-and have never been Mnemosynes, which the Conspiracy instinctively renounces along with their memories. Curiously, it works on dead Cataphracts and dead Spawn, which they claim is because their souls have not embraced the worst aspects of the Dark.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 11-24-2017, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T03:10:31-08:00","id":1162412,"title":"","content":"Understandable, given he dislikes coming on that forum. Glad you were able to see it.<br /> <br /> And I like this idea for an Endowment^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T12:04:59-08:00","id":1162526,"title":"","content":"So does anyone have any suggestions for further Philadelphia NPCs/segments?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T15:27:07-08:00","id":1162560,"title":"","content":"Not really at the moment. As I said, city appendixes aren't something I'm familiar with; I tend to not read them most of the time. Even though I probably should, given they seem to contain plenty of interesting stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T14:36:00-08:00","id":1164641,"title":"","content":"Just posting to remind you guys this thread isn't dead. Here's an opening fiction I did for the People's Guard:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cDeath to the witch! Death to the witch!\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The men and women in the assembly enthusiastically repeated their mantra as the Noble stepped through the crowd, her face low. She was in her human form, her hand tied behind her back, scratches and cuts all over their body; the jailors had not bothered being kind to her. Most people would probably have felt sorry for this young woman; but all the crowd saw was the sinister, veiled witch who had corrupted their home these last weeks, and taken the life of six men before they finally managed to get her. And now, they wanted payback.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>They finally reached the scaffold, and forced her to knee. The leader approached her and forced her to look at him.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cAny last word, my lady?\u201d he sarcastically asked.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>She gave him a cold, arrogant stare.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cThe Last Empress won\u2019t tolerate this barbary,\u201d she whispered, her voice filled with hatred and disdain. \u201cMore will come to crush your little rebellion.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cOh, but we are counting on it,\u201d the man snickered. \u201cAnd when they do, we will send them your head as a message. Maybe then, your Queen will finally understand her time in this world is over.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>He stood up and turned to the crowd.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cAnd let this be the fate of all those who dare step on the people!\u201d He screamed.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The crowd cheered once again. The Noble was pushed ahead, and her executioner raised his axe. She closed her eyes as the blade fell on her neck.&quot;</i></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T15:42:52-08:00","id":1164666,"title":"","content":"I love it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T06:14:53-08:00","id":1164768,"title":"","content":"Thanks^^ Did my best. I don't know why, but I felt the scene of them executing a Princess would be particularly strong and establish well what they are about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T07:33:12-08:00","id":1164785,"title":"","content":"What was The People's Guard's Endowment, again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T07:59:58-08:00","id":1164791,"title":"","content":"Vox Populis. I didn't fully understood it, but basically it's something that allows them to channel their collective will into supernatural effects such as blocking supernatural powers to an extent, summoning spectre-like creatures to attack Nobles, and increase their ability in Teamwork. The current version leaves it ambiguous where they got these abilities from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T08:36:49-08:00","id":1164795,"title":"","content":"Has it been codified yet, or is it just general ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T10:55:35-08:00","id":1164832,"title":"","content":"There are some mechanics on the doc for it, motly based on the 2E rules for Edowments. It might get modified though, given the 2E Hunter book isn't up yet. Plus it only has the three basic powers I just described you.<br /> <br /> Why are you asking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T13:15:39-08:00","id":1164867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1164832#post1164832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are some mechanics on the doc for it, motly based on the 2E rules for Edowments. It might get modified though, given the 2E Hunter book isn't up yet. Plus it only has the three basic powers I just described you.<br /> <br /> Why are you asking?</div> </div> </div> </div>Had more ideas for specific powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T15:27:14-08:00","id":1164904,"title":"","content":"Then feel free to add them to the doc. God knows I need more attention for the People's Guard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T06:41:15-08:00","id":1166082,"title":"","content":"Since we are at it, I am thinking... should we add a section on Shikigami in the book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T10:08:27-08:00","id":1166118,"title":"","content":"Alright, since nobody bother with the People's Guard hunter section, i'll try starting. Here's my first try:<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You used to be a cheerleader in high school. But then one day, something happened to someone in your squad. She suddenly got more successful, and started becoming more selfish, more arrogant. At first, you thought it was just popularity going to her head, but soon you realize something was wrong, with your classmates worshipping her as if they had been brainwashed. It was when you discovered she was using some weird magic powers to peel other girls\u2019 beauty off their faces that you realized the kind of monster she had become. It wasn\u2019t easy stabbing someone you had known for so long in her sleep, but when people around you started turning back to normal, you knew you had done the right thing. The People\u2019s Guard found and recruited you soon after.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T10:38:11-08:00","id":1166123,"title":"","content":"Pretty solid. Add it?<br /> <br /> Should this project be finalized April 2nd, 2018, one year after the thread's start? (Anniversary?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T10:45:38-08:00","id":1166126,"title":"","content":"Added it^^ Thanks.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I guess that'd be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T15:34:01-08:00","id":1166349,"title":"","content":"And here's a new opening fiction, this time for the Light Company:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The creature rushed on Julian, snapping its monstrous jaws at him. Dodging the bite at the last minute, the man slashed at its neck; the Spawn\u2019s horrible head fell off, rolling a few meter away. With their leader dead, the other beast hesitated, allowing the other to finish them off with a few well-placed gunshot. Juliann sighed in relief as his strange, glowing sword reverted to the form of an ordinary machete.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>With all the creatures dead, the Princess turned in his direction. She seemed to have been injured as well in the fight, albeit not to the same degree; a few cuts and bruises were visible on her face and knees, and chunks of her dress had been torn apart by the monsters\u2019 teeth.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cAre they all dead?\u201d she asked.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Julian nodded. \u201cWe already took care of the ones in the basement before joining you here. My men are taking control the Nest as we speak.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>A radiant smile appeared on the Noble\u2019s bruised face. \u201cThank you so much.\u201d she said. \u201cI couldn\u2019t have done it without you.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cIt was a honor, my lady. I trust you have our payment, though?\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cOf course. Just give me a moment\u2026\u201d she grabbed her purse, eventually pulling a small book out. \u201cHere it is. I had a hard time crafting it, but it was worth all the effort.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cIs it the one we asked for?\u201d Julian politely asked.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cYes. That should be all you need to purify a Nest. I trust you will use it well.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cIndeed we will,\u201d the captain answered with a smile. \u201cPleasure doing business with you, my lady.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>He saluted her, promptly imitated by all his men.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Opinions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T07:47:48-08:00","id":1167607,"title":"","content":"Nice fluff. Julian makes me think he's royalty because of Madagascar<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I had a derp moment where I thought that Princess's main document was elsewhere, the link was weird","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 12-14-2017, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T14:57:01-08:00","id":1167778,"title":"","content":"Thanks^^<br /> <br /> Weird? How so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T21:03:18-08:00","id":1167831,"title":"","content":"No clue. I went into some other document.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T19:40:25-08:00","id":1168102,"title":"","content":"I like it too.<br /> <br /> Also, my term is Finally. Freaking. Over. I'm ready to start working on the Cold Guard/Remnants' Pact again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T03:05:28-08:00","id":1168146,"title":"","content":"Glad to hear^^<br /> <br /> On a note, if some of you feel like building profiles for characters, there are some sample characters in the appendix. I started one of them, but having a hard time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 12-16-2017, 08:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T21:35:33-08:00","id":1168715,"title":"","content":"Okay, looking over the Remnant's Pact, and not knowing how to get in contact with its author, I'll just say there are some pretty big gaps in the Endowments.<br /> <br /> As in, there needs to be more than three. As mentioned, I think there should be a &quot;contact ancestors&quot; Endowment to show just how much their age and mythology affects them, but it seems like their big thing should be environmental control. Off the top of my head-<br /> <br /> -Change curses in a Nest, altering it so that it effects things that don't hurt the Warden as much, and hopefully effects an enemy more. More meant for Nobility when used offensively, as they're the ones who act selfless in a Nest.<br /> <br /> -Change spatial relationships to create a &quot;shelter&quot; for themselves or others, or a &quot;pit&quot; to trap opponents; it imposes bonuses to hiding from combat or ambushing in a warded area, as threats become nearer or farther depending on uses.<br /> <br /> -Inflict a Tilt that invokes bloody karma on anyone who tries to violate a rule the Warden defines when she buys the Endowment, causing a debilitating sickness that usually takes the violator out of the fight. Major weakness is that it flows both ways-if the Warden breaks her own rule, it's going to be even worse for her as she can't measure up to her own moral code.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T03:25:35-08:00","id":1168749,"title":"","content":"So... no one wants to use the CG Endowment material I wrote up? Too complicated?","signature":"<hr class=