ted":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5387-peteman","name":"Peteman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T14:08:15-08:00","id":1173576,"title":"","content":"Done. Thanks^^<br /> <br /> Anyway, what remains to be done, now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T16:26:46-08:00","id":1173610,"title":"","content":"Sample Setting? Finishing up the Cold Guard/Remnants Pact (since there are still references). Have the sample NPCs/monsters and Dread Powers been reviewed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T18:00:08-08:00","id":1173646,"title":"","content":"Thank you, Vent0.<br /> <br /> the Remnant Pact/Cold Guard, I'll leave to the ones working on it. On a note, I feel like Remnant Pact probably is the best name, to avoid confusion with the Cold Guard, but that remains to be decided.<br /> <br /> I think the sample NPCs/monsters and Dread Powers haven't been reviewed, so it'd be a good idea.<br /> <br /> As for the sample setting... does anyone here know how to make a proper appendix? I admit I'm not that good at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T10:23:42-08:00","id":1173785,"title":"","content":"Oh, I don't recall if this has been covered in detail - since Princesses come from people, what about when people the Hunter knows (or, rarely, the Hunter themselves) Blossom?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T11:25:42-08:00","id":1173797,"title":"","content":"... That's a pretty good question actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T23:19:47-08:00","id":1173970,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I'd honestly expect certain Hunter groups to have a higher-than-average rate of Blossoming, especially ones like Habibti Ma'at, the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood, or the Union, given their specific proclivities toward various types of activism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T10:51:00-08:00","id":1175798,"title":"","content":"What about Yuri's Group?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T21:53:05-08:00","id":1175913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1175798#post1175798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Yuri's Group?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This makes Princesses' opinion of Beasts make even more sense...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T03:18:37-08:00","id":1175945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This makes Princesses' opinion of Beasts make even more sense... </div> </div> </div>One: I fail to see how.<br /> <br /> Two: How does that answer my question?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T03:49:43-08:00","id":1175947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1175945#post1175945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One: I fail to see how.<br /> <br /> Two: How does that answer my question?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yuri's Group really doesn't like Beasts, having seen their depredations.<br /> <br /> Yuri's Group Hunters that Blossom are going to carry those prejudices with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T04:06:24-08:00","id":1175951,"title":"","content":"I was asking if you'd say Yuri's Group has a lot of Blossoming, not how this would shape their opinions on Beasts. Also, Yuri's Group actually has a more complicated relationship with Beasts than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T06:56:16-08:00","id":1175967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1175951#post1175951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was asking if you'd say Yuri's Group has a lot of Blossoming, not how this would shape their opinions on Beasts. Also, Yuri's Group actually has a more complicated relationship with Beasts than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, I was being a smartass while tired. I realize only now I forgot to answer it.<br /> <br /> I would think there's a high percentage (if only in comparison to other Hunters) of Yuri's Group Blossomings. The ideology draws people who are already primed for it, and the crucible of well, being a hunter catalyzes those who retain their idealism-which is something they promote and encourage. Of them, many tend to be Menders for obvious reasons, and many of those align themselves with Diamonds, Swords...and often enough, Mirrors, since they already often think they can fix the world, personally. Being told they have a destiny to is simply confirmation bias.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T08:31:13-08:00","id":1175978,"title":"","content":"Okay, thank you^^<br /> <br /> We got to consider something though; do Hunters KNOW how Blossoming works, and if they do, how much?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T10:01:55-08:00","id":1175989,"title":"","content":"Actually, here's an important question if you're going to address a Hunter's Blossoming odds: does twisting your Integrity into knots the way most Hunters are assumed to affect that in any way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T10:05:01-08:00","id":1175993,"title":"","content":"One thing to keep in mind is that the most important trait that leads to Blossoming is being the reincarnation of a Princess. Onceborn are a minority and require significantly more to Blossom. (This is why Princesses tend to come from backgrounds that resemble an anime protagonist; rather than adults who go to Cambodia and dig up landmines).<br /> <br /> As a rule of thumb a Onceborn should have the Virtueous merit, strong beliefs, and be proactive about putting their beliefs into practice, and have that unquantifiable WoD mystery-secret-sauce that First Changes, Awakenings, and Blossomings all require. All of that certainly could be found in a member of Yuri's group. But I'd say Yuri's group are more likely to see newbies with past lives Blossom on their first hunt than veterans blossom after a long career builds up enough Light.<br /> <br /> BTW, I'd actually say the most likely organisations to have members Blossoming are Network Zero and the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood, simply because they recruit younger and are thus there are more reincarnated Princesses who haven't Blossomed yet in their recruiting pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T15:22:37-08:00","id":1176083,"title":"","content":"Thank you, King Raven. And how much would you say hunter should know about Blossoming in itself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T02:05:04-08:00","id":1176220,"title":"","content":"I'd say it should be common knowledge that Blossomings exist but beyond that it should be a mass of speculation and blind guessing. Is Blossoming something you build up internally or being chosen from above. Is it really your past life or some sort of possession. Are they aware that Blossoming and creating a Sworn are entirely different things. If they are aware, do they thing a Blossoming is the Queen's equivalent of creating a Sworn.<br /> <br /> Some of these questions are things Princesses can't answer; so Hunters definitely shouldn't be able to.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T16:00:51-08:00","id":1181834,"title":"","content":"Sooo would like opinions; which are your favourite Compacts and Conspiracies introduced in this supplement?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T16:31:42-08:00","id":1181844,"title":"","content":"#Ammit and (honestly) the Magisters.<br /> <br /> <b>#Ammit </b><br /> They are a slightly different take on Hacktivism (as opposed to the more AV take of Network Zero). That they are a former violent cult (which is what Stormwracked Cells <i>are</i>) which realized the incidental harm they were doing and strive to better themselves, covers ground I don't think other groups do. They also seem to be one of the more understanding groups, so long as the target in question hasn't proven themselves a danger.<br /> <br /> <b>Magisters of the Economie/Unlimited</b><br /> These are some genuine a**-holes, but they are <i>understandable</i> a-holes. You can easily see the privileged crowd re-appropriating other's powers for what they see as better management. They still do uphold the Vigil, even with their warped motives, and any they actually self-analyze would make great drama to act out in character. They also let you use the powers of the Light for possibly darker purposes (without throwing Twilight Princesses around all the time).<br /> <br /> <b>Review of the others</b>:<br /> <b>Star of Bethlehem</b> - They certainly serve a role, but not one I can see using very much.<br /> <b>The Light Company</b> - The mercenary aspect is nice, but they seem a little less <i>mercenary</i> than I'd use. They seem a little sycophantic (in a harsher light), though it does still support the closed-off Ronin-type character.<br /> <b>Character Risk Analysis </b>- PR Hunters-for-Hire are nice, and would probably be my choice after #Ammit, but there is a little character-type overlap with the SRO Hunter that I am still working through. (More my issue than theirs)<br /> <b>The Sanitation Workers Collective</b> - They are a little held back (for me) by confusion of what they actually are. A &quot;poor-man's conspiracy&quot; of various Help-types wielding jumped up folk-magic rituals. Okay...? There's nothing particularly wrong with them, they just aren't catching my interest at the moment.<br /> <b>The People's Guard</b> - Ah, Revolutionaries. There is something to like in their fire and desire for equality, but they hew a bit to closely to Zealotry for me to love. Still, a group I can see using.<br /> (<b>The Cold Guard/The Remnants Pact</b> - Well, they aren't done/in the document, so they aren't an option. I do like the Grey Warden feel, and &quot;turn Darkness against Darkness&quot; aspects.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 02-03-2018, 09:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T08:34:56-08:00","id":1181997,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Vent0. Glad to see someone likes #Ammit. Would you mind handling their opening fiction, please? I know absolutely nothing about Hacktivists, so I feel kinda out of my element with them.<br /> <br /> I agree with you on the Magister, the Cold Guard and the People's Guard. I am also confused one what the Sanitation Workers Collective is, though. As for the Light Company... I personally like them fine as they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T17:13:20-08:00","id":1183099,"title":"","content":"Okay, just looked over the Doc again, and I'd have to say, my favorites are as follows:<br /> <br /> <b>#Ammit</b><br /> \u200bYou get to be a hacktivist and an obnoxious internet troll! How can I not find this compact interesting?<br /> <br /> <b>The Light Company</b><br /> \u200bSupernatural mercenaries sounds like a very interesting idea to me. Kind of wish there was something like this in Hunter<br /> <br /> <b>\u200bStar of Bethlehem</b><br /> \u200bA cool concept, even if it is rather narrow and niche in scope. Makes me feel like I'd be playing the parents of a super hero; and the sheer adult fear of it all could make for great roleplaying.<br /> <br /> <b>\u200bThe Cold Guard / The Remnants Pact</b><br /> \u200bLike Vent0, I'm liking the Grey Warden-esque feel they give off, but they aren't a finished concept. They are also making me think of SCP (not SPC) Foundation in their methods.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs for what groups I honestly dislike... I'd pick CRA, People's Guard and The Magisters, but that's more because of personally views than anything to do with their concepts. If you want specifics, here you go:<br /> <br /> <i>\u200bCharacter Risk Analysis</i><br /> This group of character assassins just rubs me the wrong way. The fact that they specialize in hitting a Princess where it hurts just makes me think they'd one day create a mass of Dethroned...<br /> <br /> <i>People's Guard</i><br /> \u200bYeah... a group that just loves killing little girls; that's not disturbing in the least...<br /> <br /> <i>The Magisters</i><br /> A group of people who believe in mind raping people for profit... I like the idea of these people as much as I like Les Mysteres... I.E. not at all.<br /> <br /> \u200bThen again, I'm the guy who also believes all Hunters are doomed to make the world worse by killing the wrong monster, by accidentally breaking some kind of seal, or by being in the wrong place at the wrong time... So what do I know?<br /> <br /> ==Edit==<br /> \u200bAdded a bit more detail, and included some dislikes and why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":17107,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","user":"Mangaholic13","date":". 02-06-2018, 09:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T18:02:20-08:00","id":1183111,"title":"","content":"My favorites is the Star of Bethlehem when it comes to princess specific compact. It has a really unique niche that fits well with princess's theme. They are indeed memorable and understandable.<br /> <br /> I like Character Risk Analysis as well, although it is somewhat generic. They could serve as dangerously effective right hands to villans of any chronicles. And could be used as grey helpers of the heros, or can even become protagonists on their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","name":"tg0098","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23621_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T01:31:48-08:00","id":1183200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bThen again, I'm the guy who also believes all Hunters are doomed to make the world worse by killing the wrong monster, by accidentally breaking some kind of seal, or by being in the wrong place at the wrong time... So what do I know? </div> </div> </div>Welcome to the club <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I feel the same way about the large majority of them, to be frank. Though I think it's possible for some of them to be reasonable every now and then, but... yeaaaaah, more often than not they tend to make things worse. In fact, that was a theme I tried to keep in mind when writing this supplement.<br /> <br /> I honestly take no offense in your reasons to dislike these groups, and in fact sympathize, since I feel the same way about many of them (ESPECIALLY the People's Guard). Personally my opinion about these three groups is similar to what I think of the Ashwood Abbey: I like them in a Love to Hate kind of way, but I wouldn't want to play as them. I'd mostly use them as antagonists in a Princess Chronicle.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T11:20:56-08:00","id":1183319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangaholic13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1183099#post1183099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Light Company</b><br /> \u200bSupernatural mercenaries sounds like a very interesting idea to me. Kind of wish there was something like this in Hunter</div> </div> </div> </div>Dogs of War does go into this a little bit. Though it tends to be more for &quot;mortal soldiers/fighters&quot;, the line kinda blurs when you have a literal army backing you up. It basically says &quot;here is how a Mercenary group works, an example and some story hooks, and how Vampires/Werewolves/Mages/Other Supernaturals into this.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bThen again, I'm the guy who also believes all Hunters are doomed to make the world worse by killing the wrong monster, by accidentally breaking some kind of seal, or by being in the wrong place at the wrong time... So what do I know? </div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> No such thing as the &quot;Wrong Monster&quot; #MDC!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T12:40:17-08:00","id":1183352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1181997#post1181997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, Vent0. Glad to see someone likes #Ammit. Would you mind handling their opening fiction, please? I know absolutely nothing about Hacktivists, so I feel kinda out of my element with them.</div> </div> </div> </div> Okay...<br /> <br /> What should I write? I'm going to throw out options.<br /> Perspective<br /> * Hunter's<br /> * Outsider's<br /> * Target's<br /> <br /> #Ammit Group<br /> * Research<br /> * Outreach<br /> * Onsite<br /> <br /> Target<br /> * Corrupt Human<br /> * Monster<br /> * Another Hunter<br /> * No target - peaceful interaction","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 02-07-2018, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T15:17:24-08:00","id":1183405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1183319#post1183319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No such thing as the &quot;Wrong Monster&quot; #MDC!</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bA werewolf/sin-eater in the middle of a ritual sealing away a dangerous spirit/ghost.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, Vent0, how about from the perspective of a Darkness worshiper who's skeletons have been exposed by Ammit?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T16:17:28-08:00","id":1183417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bA werewolf/sin-eater in the middle of a ritual sealing away a dangerous spirit/ghost. </div> </div> </div>I think Ruger was joking, Mangaholic^^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, Vent0, how about from the perspective of a Darkness worshiper who's skeletons have been exposed by Ammit? </div> </div> </div>That could work. Alternatively, I thought having it written as a mail conversation between two #Ammit members would have worked as well. Your call on which you prefer, Vent.<br /> <br /> As for the target, I'd say Corrupt human; I am fine with and even encourage mentioning other monsters in the Hunters and The Enemy sections, but I feel the opening Fictions need to stay in the theme of the supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T16:25:20-08:00","id":1183420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangaholic13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1183405#post1183405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bA werewolf/sin-eater in the middle of a ritual sealing away a dangerous spirit/ghost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a two-for-one sale at the supernatural supermarket! Just bring salt with your silver and season to taste. Both should be distracted and possibly exhausted, so its the perfect time to take 'em out ^_^.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T16:32:00-08:00","id":1183424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sounds like a two-for-one sale at the supernatural supermarket! Just bring salt with your silver and season to taste. Both should be distracted and possibly exhausted, so its the perfect time to take 'em out ^_^. </div> </div> </div>Oooooor you either kill the werewolf/sin-eater first, accidentally freeing the spirit/ghost in the process, or the latter first, leaving the former alive and pissed off against you. Not even taking the whole thing about Sin-Eaters resurrecting by killing someone close by upon death or a Spirit/Ghost's tendency to come back if not taken care of properly.<br /> <br /> And this is the primary reason why Hunter is a hobby with a high mortality rate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T16:50:19-08:00","id":1183427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1183424#post1183424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oooooor you either kill the werewolf/sin-eater first, accidentally freeing the spirit/ghost in the process, or the latter first, leaving the former alive and pissed off against you. Not even taking the whole thing about Sin-Eaters resurrecting by killing someone close by upon death or a Spirit/Ghost's tendency to come back if not taken care of properly.<br /> <br /> And this is the primary reason why Hunter is a hobby with a high mortality rate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, if it were easy, this would be the &quot;Chronicles of Completely Mundane People&quot;, since all the spooky stuff would be dead already. But I digress <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T02:46:03-08:00","id":1183525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hey, if it were easy, this would be the &quot;Chronicles of Completely Mundane People&quot;, since all the spooky stuff would be dead already. But I digress </div> </div> </div>Oooor still the Chronicles of Darkness only with few to little humans at all. Remember, Hunters are the <i>exception</i> here; most games are about playing these monsters <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yeah, we're digressing. Let's get back on topic.<br /> <br /> Are there any progress on the Remnant's Pact, for starter? The more I think about them, the more I like them. Grey Warden-like hunters indeed make a nice foil to Princesses.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T03:11:44-08:00","id":1183529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1183525#post1183525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are there any progress on the Remnant's Pact, for starter? The more I think about them, the more I like them. Grey Warden-like hunters indeed make a nice foil to Princesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like them, in abstract. We'll need to see where the flavor goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T15:16:20-08:00","id":1183722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1183525#post1183525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oooor still the Chronicles of Darkness only with few to little humans at all. Remember, Hunters are the <i>exception</i> here; most games are about playing these monsters <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yeah, we're digressing. Let's get back on topic.<br /> <br /> Are there any progress on the Remnant's Pact, for starter? The more I think about them, the more I like them. Grey Warden-like hunters indeed make a nice foil to Princesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bActually, I had a thought about that... Why not model them after Buddhism and other real-world religions that believe in balance and harmony, using strange dedications and meditative techniques that allow them to manipulate Light and Darkness as a means of restoring balance? Like turning a Nest into a prison or forcing a Noble out of their transformation?<br /> <br /> Let me know what you think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T16:34:52-08:00","id":1183757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ^Actually, I had a thought about that... Why not model them after Buddhism and other real-world religions that believe in balance and harmony, using strange dedications and meditative techniques that allow them to manipulate Light and Darkness as a means of restoring balance? Like turning a Nest into a prison or forcing a Noble out of their transformation?<br /> <br /> Let me know what you think. </div> </div> </div>I don't know, forcing a Princess out of her Transformation feels a bit overpowered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T17:01:25-08:00","id":1183766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1183757#post1183757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know, forcing a Princess out of her Transformation feels a bit overpowered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah, you're right... maybe to dispel a charm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T17:51:23-08:00","id":1183777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangaholic13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1183722#post1183722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bActually, I had a thought about that... Why not model them after Buddhism and other real-world religions that believe in balance and harmony, using strange dedications and meditative techniques that allow them to manipulate Light and Darkness as a means of restoring balance? Like turning a Nest into a prison or forcing a Noble out of their transformation?<br /> <br /> Let me know what you think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well.... Buddhism's balance and harmony isn't about keeping light and darkness equal. Light is balance and harmony, dark is unharmonius and must be cleansed from mind. Buddhism preaches the middle way between thoughtless mortification and and unchained hedonism, not between good and evil.<br /> <br /> But other than that, they do have the unfilled niche of hunter organizations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","user":"tg0098","date":".  Typo. 02-08-2018, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","name":"tg0098","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23621_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T18:49:51-08:00","id":1183790,"title":"","content":"It won\u2019t be the first time a hunter group operated on skewed, warped, or downright wrong interpretations of a given philosophy or religion.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, a Taoist group would fit better for the Light-Dark balance powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T12:54:45-08:00","id":1184050,"title":"","content":"Honestly, a dark (heh) version of Balance is what I was going for with them. I was genuinely invoking Taoist ideas of balance-to the Pact, Light and Dark need each other, otherwise it imbalances and wrecks the world. In fact, it HAS wrecked the world. Without human control, then, both forces become destructive, inhuman, and cruel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T13:37:16-08:00","id":1184060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1184050#post1184050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, a dark (heh) version of Balance is what I was going for with them. I was genuinely invoking Taoist ideas of balance-to the Pact, Light and Dark need each other, otherwise it imbalances and wrecks the world. In fact, it HAS wrecked the world. Without human control, then, both forces become destructive, inhuman, and cruel.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b...You make a very good, and scary, point Leliel. And yeah, dark Taoists sounds awesome. Do you have any idea's for how their endowment works?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T14:49:57-08:00","id":1184093,"title":"","content":"Wil these Taoist be religous, believing in alchemy and gods? Or will they be philosophical, following the works of Laozi and Zhuangzi? It will determine what kind of endowments they use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","name":"tg0098","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23621_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T15:11:56-08:00","id":1184103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangaholic13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1184060#post1184060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200b...You make a very good, and scary, point Leliel. And yeah, dark Taoists sounds awesome. Do you have any idea's for how their endowment works?</div> </div> </div> </div>I already posted a couple, and rules-wise environmental control and binding is the name of the game.<br /> <br /> Binding, here, meaning binding an entity together with something else. In fact, let's say it's the source of their nullification Endowment-they take an ability from an enemy and bind it to a trinket, rendering it unusable.<br /> <br /> Symbolically, they are turning the binding trinket into the antithesis of that power and making a static equilibrium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T00:02:18-08:00","id":1189794,"title":"","content":"Just posting to confirm that yes, this project is still in-work. I just had a lot of things to keep me busy lastly.<br /> <br /> Also still waiitng progress on the Remnant's Pact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T05:55:01-08:00","id":1189843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1189794#post1189794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just posting to confirm that yes, this project is still in-work. I just had a lot of things to keep me busy lastly.<br /> <br /> Also still waiitng progress on the Remnant's Pact.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry! I have project ADD a lot of the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T06:08:11-08:00","id":1190235,"title":"","content":"No problem, we have all been busy.<br /> <br /> Here's the beginning of a fiction I am writing for the supplement. This'll be a long one for the intro, so I am posting it in multiple part. Feel free to give opinions.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cI don\u2019t like this place.\u201d </i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cShut the fuck up, Luigi.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cI\u2019m just telling you, man, we shouldn\u2019t have gone that far. At least waited for back-up.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The others sighted. Of course, they all knew he was right. But did they really have the choice?</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>It had been month now. Month since they started tracking down the insane cult that had been rising in the area. These maniacs had been capturing and torturing living beings to fuel their unholy sorcery. They had started small, with pets and errand cats; but they had soon grown daring and moved to homeless men and women. When they started kidnapping children, the Cell had become more determined than ever to take their down.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Eventually, after several weeks of investigation, they had managed to locate their hideout, and led an assault against it. They had been prepared for a fight, but when they arrived, someone had apparently preceded them; all the cultists at the entrance were either dead or unconscious. They had ended up following the trace of bodies to the cave below the building. And this was how they ended up here, in the dark, walking through something wet and they really didn\u2019t want to identify.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cWe still don\u2019t know who took down these witches up there,\u201d Vera answered. \u201cAnd we need to see if we can find rescapees.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cWe saw what they do with their prisoners\u201d, Luigi protested. \u201cYou guys really think they suddenly kept the last one alive for some reason?\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cIt\u2019s worth checking,\u201d Jack answered. \u201cIf we could bring back just one kid safe, then our effort won\u2019t have been in vain...\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cWait!\u201d Very suddenly said, causing her comrades to stop with an interrogative look. \u201cI think I saw something move.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The three of them raised their flashlight in the direction she pointed at. Eventually, they did reveal someone sitting against the corner. It was a child, a girl who looked barely older than thirteen. Jack noticed with surprised how she seemed in fairly good shape for a prisoner. Not perfect, of course; her clothes were still ripped, her hair wet, and her face marked with bruises. But considering where they had found him, he had expected her to have worse.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cSee? We told you it\u2019d pay off!\u201d Vera triumphantly told Lugi, before bring her attention back to the girl. \u201cIt\u2019s okay, sweety. We\u2019re here to help you.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The girl stood up, and Jack couldn\u2019t help but be unsettled by how calm she appeared. He had expected to find someone crying, or terrorized. But the way she stared at them\u2026 this wasn\u2019t the look of scared kidnapped child. In fact, if she had been taken by them, why was she even free?</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cYou shouldn\u2019t be there,\u201d she suddenly said.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cWhat?\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cYou shouldn\u2019t be there,\u201d she repeated. \u201cIt\u2019s dangerous. Leave while you still can.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Before they could answer anything, she turned her back to them and ran deeper in the cave.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cEh! Wait!\u201d Vera yelled.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>They rushed after her.</i></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T12:46:53-08:00","id":1192033,"title":"","content":"Okay, thinking about the Remnant's Pact again. I'm thinking, what kind of other Endowments should they have? Big thing with them is environemtnal control, but given their almost Taoist theme of balance, perhaps neutralization as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T13:37:11-08:00","id":1192041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1192033#post1192033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, thinking about the Remnant's Pact again. I'm thinking, what kind of other Endowments should they have? Big thing with them is environemtnal control, but given their almost Taoist theme of balance, perhaps neutralization as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe something for leveraging an environment they &quot;own&quot; for additional effects? Back in Penumbrae, I had one where the Hunter could inflict a Nest's curses upon a target. If the Pact neutralized a Nest, maybe they could &quot;relieve&quot; the suppression for a target or small area. Temporarily let the existing effects take place, but upon subjects of the Hunter's choosing.<br /> <br /> This would, of course, require that they &quot;correct&quot; an area before-hand.<br /> <br /> Another option is &quot;spreading the poison&quot; - leech the curses of Nests and blessings of [Light-places] into items, and weaken/balance them via controlled dispersion. Example - store some of the health and sanity reducing curses of a Nest into a special blade (or bullet). The Nest is reduced (albeit slightly), and that curse can be turned against more deserving monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T10:04:38-07:00","id":1208047,"title":"","content":"Im curious is it safe to say &quot;star of Bethlehem&quot;'s goal of attacking the queens even with the dream travel merit is laughably impossible? And will probaly do more to amuse the queen's then anything?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T10:46:50-07:00","id":1208060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1072110-hunter-the-vigil-supplement-for-princesses?p=1208047#post1208047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im curious is it safe to say &quot;star of Bethlehem&quot;'s goal of attacking the queens even with the dream travel merit is laughably impossible? And will probaly do more to amuse the queen's then anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>With their &quot;protect the children&quot; tactics and resources? Yes. If they pair up with Task Force: Valkyrie? Dream-Nukes*. Might cause the Queens to take notice.<br /> <br /> * These don't exist. Yet. That's what Endowment R&amp;D is for. And Beasts provide a clearer use and research subject for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T11:26:15-07:00","id":1208083,"title":"","content":"another thing a question I have on hunter's in general?<br /> <br /> Is it inappropiate if you have the book in question for Vampires, werewolves beasts, whatever, to use it?<br /> <br /> and the thing Hunter has, with dread powers is mostly for convenience if you LACK the books?<br /> <br /> <br /> Was thinkiing safe to say if a member of Star of Bethlehem is trying to keep her safe against her will Belief will force her to use gentle restraint, or evasion , not lethal force?<br /> <br /> Oh!?<br /> <br /> Why does the notion of one of the peoples Guard at the Mercy of a Brat bring a smile to my face?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 04-17-2018, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T03:15:46-07:00","id":1208382,"title":"","content":"''Is it inappropiate if you have the book in question for Vampires, werewolves beasts, whatever, to use it? And the thing Hunter has, with dread powers is mostly for convenience if you LACK the books?''<br /> <br /> All these supplement books, including this one, have a section adressing this. The dread powers and other are just a mean to play monsters in a Hunter game without having to buy all the other corebooks. If you DO have the Princess/Vampire/Werewolf/other corebook, you can perfectly use them in your hunter game.<br /> <br /> And the Star of Bethlehem typically tries to go for gentle methods first. Remember, they see Nobles as children to be loved and protected.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T06:37:45-07:00","id":1208423,"title":"","content":"Oh on Knight of Mirror's.<br /> <br /> <br /> Can a Princess's Nakama or Familiar intervene on her behalf? harrying the well meaning fool's? or using connect charms to get them to leave?<br /> <br /> How do you think Star of Bethlehem will react if the Tactic doesnt work or She shows herself quite able to transform even with the penalty?<br /> <br /> or if it drive's her to run away from home?<br /> <br /> or she get's assasinated while she's vulnerable?<br /> <br /> Blame it all on the queens?<br /> <br /> Oh another Thought!?<br /> <br /> Worth a sidebar?<br /> <br /> how do you think they'd react if told the truth?<br /> <br /> That the blossoming comes from within, not from an act by the queens, and all deposing them would do even if it <i>could </i>somehow be done, is leave the 'child soldier's' Generalless, causing far more to die.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;This is a lie coming from him&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;He's been decieved! He has to have been!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;We need to look into it! Have to be sure we know what were doing&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Even if their not Conscripting them, they are using them! That alone is worth tackling them over!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh on my comment towards the begining of the thread that PTH is monomythic, I meant simply it isnt like Vampire that leaves the true origins of the kindred up in the air<br /> <br /> WTF: had a bar in one bookm that its possible Father wolf was just a myth.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: One more idea!? A tactic aimed at identifying an either confiscatting or stealing a nobles phylactery?<br /> <br /> I could see the star of Bethlehem wanting to do it to keep the sensitives out of danger.<br /> <br /> And Task force Zero wanting to do so to have them securely in custody.<br /> <br /> but it should be DIFFICULT.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh something else that may matter on Valkyrie<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/52/30121\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/52/30121<br /> <br /> o</a>h on investigation? Might explicitly state you only get one roll per incident As you need to peice it together slowly but surely. with each appearance being another chance to put facts together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 04-28-2018, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T03:50:55-07:00","id":1216028,"title":"","content":"Sorry I've not been there for a while, been really busy with studies and everything lastly. Anyway, just would like to confirm this project isn't dead - though I'm still wondering if we should wait for Hunter 2E to come out in order to properly adapt it.<br /> <br /> Now to answer Prince of the Night the best I can....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can a Princess's Nakama or Familiar intervene on her behalf? harrying the well meaning fool's? or using connect charms to get them to leave? </div> </div> </div>In theory, I'd say yes. Remember, the book is mostly written from a Hunter's perspective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How do you think Star of Bethlehem will react if the Tactic doesnt work or She shows herself quite able to transform even with the penalty? or if it drive's her to run away from home? or she get's assasinated while she's vulnerable? Blame it all on the queens? Oh another Thought!? Worth a sidebar? </div> </div> </div>Good question. I don't know, what do the other think about that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How do you think they'd react if told the truth? That the blossoming comes from within, not from an act by the queens, and all deposing them would do even if it <i>could </i>somehow be done, is leave the 'child soldier's' Generalless, causing far more to die.&quot; </div> </div> </div>I'd say the answer is the same than if, say, Werewolves tried to tell the Talbot Group their condition isn't truly possession and isn't natural; most likely it'd be seen as a lie, but overall it depends on the Cell or person. Not every hunter will have the same reaction to that discovery, and even if they do believe them, their comrads might not. Basically, all your suggested answers are valid depending on the situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One more idea!? A tactic aimed at identifying an either confiscatting or stealing a nobles phylactery? I could see the star of Bethlehem wanting to do it to keep the sensitives out of danger. And Task force Zero wanting to do so to have them securely in custody. but it should be DIFFICULT. </div> </div> </div>Sure, but how would they go around the Nobles' ability to summon them back in their hand (which we have established in the supplement by the way?)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T04:38:31-07:00","id":1216043,"title":"","content":"Also, just finished this opening fiction for the supplement. I would very much appreciate opinions please:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cI don\u2019t like this place.\u201d </i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cShut the fuck up, Luigi.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cI\u2019m just telling you, man, we shouldn\u2019t have gone that far. At least waited for back-up.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The others sighted. Of course, they all knew he was right. But did they really have the choice?</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>It had been month now. Month since they started tracking down the insane cult that had been rising in the area. These maniacs had been capturing and torturing living beings to fuel their unholy sorcery. They had started small, with pets and errand cats; but they had soon grown daring and moved to homeless men and women. When they started kidnapping children, the Cell had become more determined than ever to take their down.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Eventually, after several weeks of investigation, they had managed to locate their hideout, and led an assault against it. They had been prepared for a fight, but when they arrived, someone had apparently preceded them; all the cultists at the entrance were either dead or unconscious. They had ended up following the trace of bodies to the cave below the building. And this was how they ended up here, in the dark, walking through something wet and they really didn\u2019t want to identify.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cWe still don\u2019t know who took down these witches up there,\u201d Vera answered. \u201cAnd we need to see if we can find rescapees.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cWe saw what they do with their prisoners\u201d, Luigi protested. \u201cYou guys really think they suddenly kept the last one alive for some reason?\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cIt\u2019s worth checking,\u201d Jack answered. \u201cIf we could bring back just one kid safe, then our effort won\u2019t have been in vain...\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cWait!\u201d Very suddenly said, causing her comrades to stop with an interrogative look. \u201cI think I saw something move.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The three of them raised their flashlight in the direction she pointed at. Eventually, they did reveal someone sitting against the corner. It was a child, a girl who looked barely older than thirteen. Jack noticed with surprised how she seemed in fairly good shape for a prisoner. Not perfect, of course; her clothes were still ripped, her hair wet, and her face marked with bruises. But considering where they had found him, he had expected her to have worse.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cSee? We told you it\u2019d pay off!\u201d Vera triumphantly told Lugi, before bring her attention back to the girl. \u201cIt\u2019s okay, sweetie. We\u2019re here to help you.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The girl stood up, and Jack couldn\u2019t help but be unsettled by how calm she appeared. He had expected to find someone crying, or terrorized. But the way she stared at them\u2026 this wasn\u2019t the look of scared kidnapped child. In fact, if she had been taken by them, why was she even free?</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cYou shouldn\u2019t be there,\u201d she suddenly said.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cWhat?\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cYou shouldn\u2019t be there,\u201d she repeated. \u201cIt\u2019s dangerous. Leave while you still can.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Before they could answer anything, she turned her back to them and ran deeper in the cave.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cEh! Wait!\u201d Vera yelled.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>They rushed after her. However, she run fast, and they could barely see her in the dark. After a few minutes, they had lost her.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cWell, that\u2019s just great\u201d, Jack groaned. \u201cHow are we supposed to save her if she runs away?\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cMaybe she is with them,\u201d Luigi suggested. \u201cMaybe she\u2019s a monster in disguise.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cIf she is, we will deal with her,\u201d Vera answered. \u201cRight now, let\u2019s focus on\u2026\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>A strange noise interrupted her, and the three hunters froze. They had been doing this for a few years, now, and experience had taught them to immediately identify the meaning behind a few specific sounds. And in that case, the meaning clearly was \u201csomething ugly is lurking in the dark\u201d.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cStay together\u201d, Vera whispered to them.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>As she was talking, a snarl was heard, and creatures emerged from the dark. at first, Jack thought they were human, as the shape was roughly the same; but as they got closer, he saw differences; their skin was grey and dirty, their arms disturbingly long with claws and blades on the elbows; their eyes were glowing and hungry; and they opened their mouth, revealing several sharp, broken teeths.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The three hunters opened fire. Several of the monsters fell, hit by the bullets as they were rushing at them with beastly shrieks. But they outnumbered them two to one; eventually one of them reached Luigi. The poor man screamed in terror as the thing threw in on the ground and prepared to sink its teeth into him.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>That was when, out of nowhere, a ray of light hit the monster in the head. It\u2019s horrible, now half-burnt maw let out of a disgusting noise before the thing collapsed, allowing Luigi to get up. Monsters and hunters alike stopped their fight and turned around to look where the ray had come from.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Then someone step out of the darkness.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>It was a teenage girl again. Not the same, it seemed; she look slightly older, with a slender body shape, darker skin, and a brighter, slightly long hair, with a red tint to it. Her blue eyes also seem to glow in the dark. But the strangest part about her was her outfit; she wore something that look like a strange mix between a pink dress and a golden samurai armor, with a kimono, plate shoulderpads, a form-fitting breastplate and a big bow in the back. And finally, she was wielding a spear-like weapon with a strange, glowing gem in the middle of the blade.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Her arrival appeared to enrage the monsters; shrieking, they all rushed toward her with the clear intention of ripping her apart. With an agility that seemed absurd for someone that small wearing armor, the girl stepped aside and stabbed one of them in the flank, killing it instantly. She then immediately removed her weapon from the corpse with surreal ease and used it to block an assault from another of the beasts, before striking back, cutting the creature\u2019s head in half. Three of them tried to attack her simultaneously, only to be obliterated by another ray of light she somehow generated from her spear. Another tried to bite her arm, only to be stopped by some strange glowing barrier before she grabbed it, threw it on the ground and pierced its heart.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Then suddenly there was a disgusting tearing sound, and she screamed in pain. The last monster standing had just reached her, and its arm had suddenly turned into a blade, catching her by surprise and stabbing through her lower back. The girl spat some blood, then raised her spear at the creature\u2019s head. The gem glowed, and a fireball emerged from it, turning the disgusting creature to ashes.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Her last opponent gone, the girl almost collapsed, only barely clinging to the closest wall. The three hunters could hear her cough as she started vomiting blood. They couldn\u2019t help but stand and look at this strange kid who had just single-handedly slaughtered an entire group of monsters. Eventually, she got up and look at them.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cThe children you are looking for are a bit further to the right,\u201d she told them. \u201cYou should reach for them soon. Please make sure they get back home. Don\u2019t worry about the other monsters, I took care of them. Good night.\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>She then walked back into the shadow, disappearing in the tunnel. Once she was gone, Jack finally managed to articulate something:</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201c... The fuck was that?!\u201d</i></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T05:05:10-07:00","id":1216051,"title":"","content":"thought of an idea for a star of bethlehem fiction<br /> <br /> a high school aged princess outright gift wrapping a grade school aged prince to them before going off on what she knows is probaly a suicide mission not wanting him killed too.<br /> <br /> oh anything on my idea that investigation rolls to find a princessess's identity, should only get one roll per appearance<br /> <br /> To be clear this issue driving me insane is why I started this thread<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1213031-investigation-rules-when-to-add-complications\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-complications</a><br /> <br /> If a princess finds out a hunter is trying to figure out her identity, its very relevant when she does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 05-09-2018, 08:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T05:10:45-07:00","id":1217337,"title":"","content":"That could be a cool fiction. Do you plan to write that?<br /> <br /> Also, currently having a friend of mine working on a cover for the supplement. i'll show it soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T08:47:32-07:00","id":1217416,"title":"","content":"Am ready to get started doing so.<br /> <br /> just out morbid curiousity... what rating a belief vioation should it be if you believe a betrayal to be for the betrayeds &quot;Own good&quot;<br /> <br /> have to go to a doctor's appointment how's what I finished so far look?<br /> <br /> C<i>hristina sighed and looked down. She did not fear her iminent death, in spite of being pretty much , she was a princess, blessed by the Queen of Diamonds, a Grace, she did not fear death, she almost welcomed it, the peace of death.</i><br /> <br /> <i>But she could not, would not take another innocent with her.</i><br /> <br /> <i>He\u2026 he was young, and had a lot of potential</i><br /> <br /> <i>Kelby, was a 9 year old Troubadour of Hearts always ready with grand tales, of courage and romance.</i><br /> <br /> <i>He didnt really understand death at his age, and she didnt fancy him gaining too intimate an understanding.</i><br /> <br /> <i>She thought of him she\u2019d trained him as best she could taught him formality and protocol as best as she understood it. Along with ways to combat the darkness, Using physical violence or diplomacy or occultism. Teaching him and when to use all of the above.</i><br /> <br /> <i>It had brought out the mother in her as well as the general.</i><br /> <br /> <i>And today she was thinking as a mother not a general.</i><br /> <br /> <i>The last month they\u2019d been tracking a mighty Cataphract down. He seemed to be the local general of the Darkness And needed taken out, at least that would ensure any more darkspawn attacks were uncoordinated and performed only out of base instincts,rather then part of any strategy, people would die yes and that was tragic, but it was better then the darkness conducting a strategic war in the region.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>She accepted it was a suicide mission not with despair or even resignation but would not let kelby\u2019s life be ended with her\u2019s</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>she had thought of the optians to find another hopeful who she\u2019d trust with the dutie\u2019s of De Facto guardian of a boy like kelby she would have to leave the city.</i><br /> <i>Allowing the cataphract to engage who knows what kinds of evil.</i><br /> <i>The vampires and m ages she trusted not at all.</i><br /> <br /> <i>The only choice\u2026 she hated herself for even thinking of for a half second\u2026 she already felt the telltale warning of sensitivity just from thinking it\u2026</i><br /> <br /> <i>but it was the only path to his survival</i><br /> <br /> <i>************** ******</i><br /> <br /> <i>The 3 of them had worked hard to make things work</i><br /> <br /> <i>They were undermanned and underfunded\u2026 But they worked tirelessly to protect children from all danger\u2019s.</i><br /> <br /> <i>They had a strong sense of right and wrong but werent philosopher\u2019s</i><br /> <br /> <i>Justin was a gifted investigator, Rodrigo, handled the bulk of combat, Melissa tended the Mundane front for their cell And tended to be their spokes person.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Christina sighed, she felt the telltale hint of Kelby\u2019s presence She had told him they needed to launch an all out attack\u2026 he trusted her she thought sadly and well he shouldnt.</i><br /> <br /> <i>They were hiding on the ceiling ready to jump down and try scaring these loser\u2019s out of town\u2026 or so he thought.</i><br /> <br /> <i>He was waiting for her to go in She usualy took the lead making him Follow from the sidelines Wanting him \u201cKept safe\u201d so he was surprised and delighted when she invited him to charge in harrying away these fool\u2019s reasoning his talent for music should be enough</i><br /> <br /> <i>She sighed she wished it would have a chance but the Well meaning fool\u2019s were looking more puzzled then anything.</i><br /> <br /> <i>he\u2019d gone down and was using inspire to try making them know what fools they were.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>She came down two behind him he smiled knowing she was there to back him up\u2026</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>He knew wrong</i><br /> <br /> <i>She gathered her resolve and with one motion grabbed the ring from his finger with one swift motion</i><br /> <br /> <i>he screamed in pain and betrayal as he forcefully detransformed</i><br /> <br /> <i>They blinked</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cWhat is going on?</i><br /> <br /> <i>Christina sighed feeling the shadow\u2019s born of her betrayal of a member of her Nakama who had trusted her</i><br /> <br /> <i>Even in death this stain will follow me she thought acridly. Feeling her sensitivity flare\u2026 she could still make it right all it would cost was letting kelby put himself in deadly danger\u2019s</i><br /> <i>What are you his mother? Some internal censor criticized her.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Let him put himself in whatever danger he see\u2019s fit you\u2019ve already instructed him for 2 year\u2019s he lives or he dies, why should you worry overmuch about it, all too often its a hopeful\u2019s fate.</i><br /> <br /> <i>She shook her head she\u2019d come this far she couldnt second guess herself.</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cWe\u2019ve investigated a monster for week\u2019s that need\u2019s to be taken out, for year\u2019s I\u2019ve been in de Facto guardianship of him, his own parents dont know he\u2019s a royal. Even if they did, I dont think they could keep him safe\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>she handed the ring to them with a sigh</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cTake this its his phylactery\u201d she shook her head</i><br /> <br /> <i>Dumbfounded justin accepted it locking it away in a safe.</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cEventually he\u2019ll be able to recover it, and escape, but it will take weeks or months\u201d she said</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cand maybe longer if you keep him occupied and make him not want to escape too soon\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>Melissa began firmly</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cYoung lady while we appreciate your desire to keep him safe if you think were going to let you go out to get killed-\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>Christina shook her head \u201cI have another thing coming? I think we both know your not ready to subdue me on this short of notice\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>they sighed unfortunately she was right</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cI hate you!\u201d kelby blubbered \u201cI hate you!!! I hate you!!! dont you see I want the honor of dieing for my queen\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>Christina shook her head sadly</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cSomeday I am sure you will have that privilege of dieing for your queen, but I\u2019ve put it off for a few years, only one of us need\u2019s to die today Pluss I want your death to have meaning ok sweetheart?\u201d she said with a tenderness the 3 onlooker\u2019s found difficult to understand since they had bizzare views on the hopeful.\u201dfor your death to have meaning you have to learn study grow\u2026 and become\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>She looked at him with sadness \u201cI know what I\u2019ve done, regardless of my motivation is unforgivable\u201d she said with a sigh. \u201cBut I want you to live to adulthood</i><br /> <br /> <i>as she was saying this Rodrigo was reaching for something some kind of weapon or alarm</i><br /> <br /> <i>she glanced at him and commanded him to kneel and he could not help but obey.</i><br /> <br /> <i>She looked to kelby one last time with maternal affection and sighed \u201cI had best be on my wat\u201d she said \u201cAgain one day you will die for your queen\u201d She assured him and jumped out. Of the building</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cShe used us\u201d Rodrigo snarled \u201cShe used us as a dumping ground for another sensitive she didnt want running underfoot\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>Justin nodded \u201cIts such a shame, she so rationally contemplates dangers to another\u2019s life And tried to prevent them\u201d shook his head \u201cBut her own life was just an asset of her queen\u2019s to dispose of as she saw fit\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>Melissa shook her head</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cSomehow I think she just wanted him to mature enough so his death can have some meaning remember what she told him\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>Justin shook his head</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cHopefully, by the time he grow\u2019s up their wont be a queen to die for anymore\u201d</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 05-19-2018, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T17:22:49-07:00","id":1217533,"title":"","content":"I honestly don't know; My guess is that it's depends on the context, the Princess' personal moral code and various other factors. But if you're curious, you should ask either Brazier or King Raven.<br /> <br /> As for that beginning of fiction, like it so far. Keep going^^<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"